  aRacing fans with a knack for design can enjoy the best of both worlds as they create original racetracks and then speed around them with as many as three friends in Build'n Race. There are a number of included courses from which to choose, each filled with jumps, ramps, and hairpin turns designed to encourage fast-paced, stunt-filled races, and players can tackle any of the tracks in "Solo Race," "Time Trial," "Championship," "Race Challenge," and "Time Challenge" modes. The design function lets gamers place hundreds of different track pieces, buildings, and environmental objects, and then join up to three players for split-screen multiplayer races.  i2009kDestination Software / Zoo Games / KSSsGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext01003na  a2200133   4500001000700000245004700007264002800054300002300082500064600105542003100751655002500782655002800807655003400835RJOEXJ00aJu-on: The Grudge: Haunted House Simulator 1bXseed Gamesc2009-10-13  a1 Wii optical disc  aIf you stumbled upon an actual haunted house, how far in would you be willing to go? Find out in this spine-chilling game inspired by the hit horror film The Grudge. Enter a virtual haunted house with only your Wiimote flashlight to guide you. Who knows what lurks in the darkness? Think you're brave enough to explore an abandoned warehouse, a mannequin factory, or a dimly lit hospital? What about when the furniture suddenly moves or footprints appear in the dust? Two-player play is more creep-out than co-op. A friend can grab a second Wiimote and trigger haunted happenings on-screen. But a real friend wouldn't do that to you...right?  i2009kXseed GamessGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext 7aSurvival horror games2wiiext00344na  a2200133   4500001000700000245002400007264003000031300002300061500000500084542003400089655002500123655002800148655003400176RJOJJ900aKyoufu Taikan: Juon 1bAQ Interactivec2009-7-30  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2009kAQ InteractivesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext 7aSurvival horror games2wiiext00990na  a2200133   4500001000700000245002200007264003400029300002300063500064600086542003700732655002500769655002800794655003400822RJOP9900aJu-on: The Grudge 1bRising Star Gamesc2009-10-25  a1 Wii optical disc  aIf you stumbled upon an actual haunted house, how far in would you be willing to go? Find out in this spine-chilling game inspired by the hit horror film The Grudge. Enter a virtual haunted house with only your Wiimote flashlight to guide you. Who knows what lurks in the darkness? Think you're brave enough to explore an abandoned warehouse, a mannequin factory, or a dimly lit hospital? What about when the furniture suddenly moves or footprints appear in the dust? Two-player play is more creep-out than co-op. A friend can grab a second Wiimote and trigger haunted happenings on-screen. But a real friend wouldn't do that to you...right?  i2009kRising Star GamessGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext 7aSurvival horror games2wiiext00293na  a2200121   4500001000700000245003600007264002200043300002300065500000500088542002600093655002500119655002700144RJPJA400aJikkyou Powerful Pro Yakyuu Wii 1bKonamic2007-7-19  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2007kKonamisGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aBaseball games2wiiext00397na  a2200109   4500001000700000245003600007264003600043300002300079500011600102542004100218655002800259RJQE5G00aPajama Sam: Don't Fear the Dark 1bMajesco Entertainmentc2008-8-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe award-winning best-selling Humongous children’s property made popular on the PC is now available for Wii!  i2008kMajesco EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aAdventure games2wiiext00300na  a2200109   4500001000700000245005500007264003400062300002300096500000500119542003800124655002800162RJQP7000aPajama Sam: No Need to Hide When It's Dark Outside 1bAtari (Infogrames)c2009-5-29  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2009kAtari (Infogrames)sGameTDB 7aAdventure games2wiiext00817na  a2200133   4500001000700000245004400007264002300051300002300074500048800097542002600585655002400611655002400635655002400659RJREA400aDance Dance Revolution: Hottest Party 3 1bKonamic2009-10-27  a1 Wii optical disc  aDanceDanceRevolution Hottest Party 3 is a dance/party game for Wii that takes the long-running DDR party to the next level. Bundled with the game's iconic floor peripheral, and including controller support for the Wii Remote/nunchuck controller configuration, and for the first time the Wii Balance Board, it is sure to be the life of the party and get you into shape. Game also include local 2-4 player multiplayer support, a diverse 60-song soundtrack, entirely new modes and more.  i2009kKonamisGameTDB 7aMusic games2wiiext 7aParty games2wiiext 7aDance games2wiiext01023na  a2200133   4500001000700000245003800007264002200045300002300067500070100090542002600791655002400817655002400841655002400865RJRJA400aDance Dance Revolution: Music Fit 1bKonamic2010-1-28  a1 Wii optical disc  aWork out to the beat using your Dance Dance Revolution Wii Dance Pad Controller or the Wii balance board for Dance Dance Revolution: Hottest Party 3. Players will be able to dance to the beat of an expansive library of over 40 great songs, including a string of top hits recorded by the original artists. Debuting in Hottest Party 3 is the Balance Board Mode. In this high energy, low impact mode, players trade their feet to utilize their hips, waist and hands with the Wii Balance Board and Nunchuk. This all new mode will be sure to add a whole new level of gameplay to Dance Dance Revolution. Players still will be able to use their Dance Dance Revolution controller mat for classic gameplay.  i2010kKonamisGameTDB 7aMusic games2wiiext 7aParty games2wiiext 7aDance games2wiiext01029na  a2200133   4500001000700000245004400007264002100051300002300072500070100095542002600796655002400822655002400846655002500870RJRPA400aDance Dance Revolution: Hottest Party 3 1bKonamic2010-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aWork out to the beat using your Dance Dance Revolution Wii Dance Pad Controller or the Wii balance board for Dance Dance Revolution: Hottest Party 3. Players will be able to dance to the beat of an expansive library of over 40 great songs, including a string of top hits recorded by the original artists. Debuting in Hottest Party 3 is the Balance Board Mode. In this high energy, low impact mode, players trade their feet to utilize their hips, waist and hands with the Wii Balance Board and Nunchuk. This all new mode will be sure to add a whole new level of gameplay to Dance Dance Revolution. Players still will be able to use their Dance Dance Revolution controller mat for classic gameplay.  i2010kKonamisGameTDB 7aMusic games2wiiext 7aDance games2wiiext 7aRhythm games2wiiext00408na  a2200121   4500001000700000245002100007264003300028300002300061500010400084542003700188655002500225655003600250RJSENR00aKawasaki Jet Ski 1bDestineer Studiosc2008-1-22  a1 Wii optical disc  aGrab your Kawasaki Jet Ski, pull off insane tricks, win races, and leave your friends in your wake!  i2008kDestineer StudiossGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext 7aWatercraft racing games2wiiext01594na  a2200121   4500001000700000245002100007264003800028300002300066500128000089542004201369655002501411655003601436RJSPUG00aKawasaki Jet Ski 1bMetro 3D / Data Designc2008-4-25  a1 Wii optical disc  aOfficially recreated under Kawasaki license, Jet Ski offers a level of playability that allows players to easily get into the roll of things. Players can utilise the Wii control system allowing both precision and easy movement of the Jet Ski. A wide array of impressive tracks from famous location from around the world, including The Thames (London), Taiwanese Islands, Canadian Rookies and the Canals of Venice. There is really no way one could find this title lacking in the long-term. With the vigorous challenges that await in the Championship mode to the more self-improving challenges of Time Trial, and of course the all out mayhem of the Two-Player mode. However as impressive as these modes are, Stunt mode is certainly a stand out. Master a wide range of cool tricks available to perfectly control the Jet Ski during air. The sheer level of addictiveness the Wii Remote provides, it is really just all here. Impressive sound delivering a number of ambient effects as well as the more brutal engine sounds, metal clashes and of course character voices and grunts. Kawasaki Jet Ski is perfect for the Wii, not only with gameplay, playability and challenge but also showing what the Wii hardware is capable of amassing huge, clean 3D worlds with mind-blowing effects.  i2008kMetro 3D / Data DesignsGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext 7aWatercraft racing games2wiiext01522na  a2200109   4500001000700000245002100007264002600028300002300054500128000077542003001357655002501387RJSXUG00aKawasaki Jet Ski 1bKOCH Mediac2008-4-25  a1 Wii optical disc  aOfficially recreated under Kawasaki license, Jet Ski offers a level of playability that allows players to easily get into the roll of things. Players can utilise the Wii control system allowing both precision and easy movement of the Jet Ski. A wide array of impressive tracks from famous location from around the world, including The Thames (London), Taiwanese Islands, Canadian Rookies and the Canals of Venice. There is really no way one could find this title lacking in the long-term. With the vigorous challenges that await in the Championship mode to the more self-improving challenges of Time Trial, and of course the all out mayhem of the Two-Player mode. However as impressive as these modes are, Stunt mode is certainly a stand out. Master a wide range of cool tricks available to perfectly control the Jet Ski during air. The sheer level of addictiveness the Wii Remote provides, it is really just all here. Impressive sound delivering a number of ambient effects as well as the more brutal engine sounds, metal clashes and of course character voices and grunts. Kawasaki Jet Ski is perfect for the Wii, not only with gameplay, playability and challenge but also showing what the Wii hardware is capable of amassing huge, clean 3D worlds with mind-blowing effects.  i2008kKOCH MediasGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext00772na  a2200145   4500001000700000245003100007264002300038300002300061500040700084542002800491655002400519655002500543655002500568655003300593RJTJ0100aMinna no Joushiki Ryoku TV 1bNintendoc2008-3-6  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis family game tests and raises a person or a family's level of common sense and knowledge of world events. Various topics are covered, such as geography, sports, even daily tasks such as cooking. Detailed explanations come with the answers and there is an encyclopedia to reference to after being asked an interesting question. Make use of the Wi-Fi function and consult the web for further answers.  i2008kNintendosGameTDB 7aParty games2wiiext 7aPuzzle games2wiiext 7aTrivia games2wiiext 7aEducational software2wiiext00537na  a2200109   4500001000700000245003800007264004800045300002300093500023000116542005200346655002900398RJVEGN00aHysteria Hospital: Emergency Ward 1bOxygen Interactive Software (UK)c2009-6-19  a1 Wii optical disc  aA usual day in Hysteria Hospital – another torrent of patients threatens to turn the emergency ward into chaos. Only one person can control the frantic situation - can you keep your patients happy when your ward is overrun?  i2009kOxygen Interactive Software (UK)sGameTDB 7aSimulation games2wiiext00495na  a2200109   4500001000700000245003800007264002800045300002300073500023000096542003200326655002700358RJVPGN00aHysteria Hospital: Emergency Ward 1bOxygen Gamesc2009-7-17  a1 Wii optical disc  aA usual day in Hysteria Hospital – another torrent of patients threatens to turn the emergency ward into chaos. Only one person can control the frantic situation - can you keep your patients happy when your ward is overrun?  i2009kOxygen GamessGameTDB 7aStrategy games2wiiext00292na  a2200121   4500001000700000245003700007264002000044300002300064500000500087542002500092655002500117655002800142RJWJEL00aJawa: Mammoth to Himitsu no Ishi 1bSpikec2008-7-3  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2008kSpikesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00666na  a2200121   4500001000700000245002500007264003200032300002300064500037100087542003700458655002500495655002400520RJXE5G00aGo Play: Lumberjacks 1bMajesco Sales Incc2009-6-9  a1 Wii optical disc  aGo Play Lumberjacks pits a cast of wacky lumberjacks in four-player competition as they climb, chop, saw and logroll their way to victory! Use your Wii Remote as the all-in-one timber-cutting contest tool. Saw dust will fly from your chainsaw in the Hot Saw; test your balance on the waterlogged Log Roll, ascend towering tree trunks in the Pole Climb and much more!  i2009kMajesco Sales IncsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aParty games2wiiext00673na  a2200121   4500001000700000245002500007264003600032300002300068500037100091542004000462655002500502655002400527RJXXFR00aGo Play: Lumberjacks 1bdtp Entertainment AGc2011-7-15  a1 Wii optical disc  aGo Play Lumberjacks pits a cast of wacky lumberjacks in four-player competition as they climb, chop, saw and logroll their way to victory! Use your Wii Remote as the all-in-one timber-cutting contest tool. Saw dust will fly from your chainsaw in the Hot Saw; test your balance on the waterlogged Log Roll, ascend towering tree trunks in the Pole Climb and much more!  i2011kdtp Entertainment AGsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aParty games2wiiext00702na  a2200133   4500001000700000245003800007264004100045300002300086500034100109542004400450655002500494655002400519655002500543RJYE5Z00aDoctor Fizzwizzle's Animal Rescue 1bConspiracy Entertainmentc2009-10-27  a1 Wii optical disc  aWhy has everyone fled the islands? There’s not a person in sight! Who will feed the animals and find out what scared the people away? Doctor Fizzwizzle, of course! Bounce bubbles, rescue hungry animals, and solve a mystery, all at the same time! Over 180 levels of thrilling brick-busting action, and over 60 animal species to rescue!  i2009kConspiracy EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aArcade games2wiiext 7aParty games2wiiext 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00680na  a2200121   4500001000700000245003100007264003800038300002300076500036700099542004200466655002500508655002500533RJZP7U00aSNK Arcade Classics Vol. 1 1bIgnition Entertainmentc2008-7-22  a1 Wii optical disc  aCelebrate the history of SNK with the ultimate collection of arcade classic hits. Featuring the following 16 NEOGEO games: Art of Fighting, Baseball Stars 2, Burning Fight, Fatal Fury, KOF 94, King of the Monsters, Last Resort, Magician Lord, Metal Slug, Neo Turf Masters, Samurai Shodown, Sengoku, Shock Troopers, Super Sidekicks 3, Top Hunter and World Heroes.  i2008kIgnition EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aArcade games2wiiext 7aCompilations2wiiext00665na  a2200121   4500001000700000245002900007264002200036300002300058500038300081542002500464655002900489655002500518RK2EEB00aTrauma Center: New Blood 1bAtlusc2007-11-20  a1 Wii optical disc  aAt a remote hospital in Alaska, Dr. Markus Vaughn quietly toils, a surgeon who has forsaken the politics and power struggles of his former ward. He is content to use the power he has discovered within himself, the Healing Touch, to positively affect the lives of those in need. His partner is Valerie Blaylock, a promising young doctor eager to unlock her own dormant abilities.  i2007kAtlussGameTDB 7aSimulation games2wiiext 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00622na  a2200109   4500001000700000245002400007264002100031300002300052500038300075542002500458655002900483RK2JEB00aCaduceus: New Blood 1bAtlusc2008-1-17  a1 Wii optical disc  aAt a remote hospital in Alaska, Dr. Markus Vaughn quietly toils, a surgeon who has forsaken the politics and power struggles of his former ward. He is content to use the power he has discovered within himself, the Healing Touch, to positively affect the lives of those in need. His partner is Valerie Blaylock, a promising young doctor eager to unlock her own dormant abilities.  i2008kAtlussGameTDB 7aSimulation games2wiiext00633na  a2200109   4500001000700000245002900007264002400036300002300060500038300083542002800466655002900494RK2P0100aTrauma Center: New Blood 1bNintendoc2008-11-7  a1 Wii optical disc  aAt a remote hospital in Alaska, Dr. Markus Vaughn quietly toils, a surgeon who has forsaken the politics and power struggles of his former ward. He is content to use the power he has discovered within himself, the Healing Touch, to positively affect the lives of those in need. His partner is Valerie Blaylock, a promising young doctor eager to unlock her own dormant abilities.  i2008kNintendosGameTDB 7aSimulation games2wiiext00319na  a2200133   4500001000700000245001600007264002400023300002300047500000500070542002800075655002400103655002500127655003300152RK3J0100aAnd-Kensaku 1bNintendoc2010-4-29  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2010kNintendosGameTDB 7aParty games2wiiext 7aTrivia games2wiiext 7aEducational software2wiiext00250na  a2200109   4500001000700000245003400007264002100041300002300062500000500085542002500090655002500115RK4JAF00aKekkaishi: Kokubourou no Kage 1bNamcoc2007-9-27  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2007kNamcosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00767na  a2200145   4500001000700000245002200007264002500029300002300054500040400077542002800481655002500509655002800534655002700562655003200589RK5E0100aKirby's Epic Yarn 1bNintendoc2010-10-17  a1 Wii optical disc  aKirby’s first console platform game since the Nintendo 64™ days introduces an amazing new look based on animated yarn and a world of cloth and textiles. The creative approach is woven directly into the game play and allows the ever-morphing Kirby™ to take on a variety of new forms. It’s a one-of-a-kind platformer that lets players explore high and low for hidden objects and fun adventure.  i2010kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext 7aHidden object games2wiiext00764na  a2200145   4500001000700000245001900007264002500026300002300051500040400074542002800478655002500506655002800531655002700559655003200586RK5J0100aKeito no Kirby 1bNintendoc2010-10-14  a1 Wii optical disc  aKirby’s first console platform game since the Nintendo 64™ days introduces an amazing new look based on animated yarn and a world of cloth and textiles. The creative approach is woven directly into the game play and allows the ever-morphing Kirby™ to take on a variety of new forms. It’s a one-of-a-kind platformer that lets players explore high and low for hidden objects and fun adventure.  i2010kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext 7aHidden object games2wiiext00963na  a2200145   4500001000700000245002400007264002300031300002300054500060000077542002800677655002500705655002800730655002700758655003200785RK5K0100aTeolsil Kirby Iyagi 1bNintendoc2011-9-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aKirby's Epic Yarn is a 2D platformer for Wii that blends classic Kirby gameplay with new abilities, functionality and more. Kirby's first console platform game since the Nintendo 64 days, Kirby's Epic Yarn introduces an amazing new look based on animated yarn and a world of cloth and textiles. The creative approach is woven directly into the gameplay and allows the ever-morphing Kirby to take on a variety of new forms. It's a one-of-a-kind platformer that lets players explore high and low for hidden objects, experience fun adventure and even join with a second player in a co-op play mode.  i2011kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext 7aHidden object games2wiiext00962na  a2200145   4500001000700000245002200007264002400029300002300053500060000076542002800676655002500704655002800729655002700757655003200784RK5P0100aKirby's Epic Yarn 1bNintendoc2011-2-25  a1 Wii optical disc  aKirby's Epic Yarn is a 2D platformer for Wii that blends classic Kirby gameplay with new abilities, functionality and more. Kirby's first console platform game since the Nintendo 64 days, Kirby's Epic Yarn introduces an amazing new look based on animated yarn and a world of cloth and textiles. The creative approach is woven directly into the gameplay and allows the ever-morphing Kirby to take on a variety of new forms. It's a one-of-a-kind platformer that lets players explore high and low for hidden objects, experience fun adventure and even join with a second player in a co-op play mode.  i2011kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext 7aHidden object games2wiiext00653na  a2200121   4500001000700000245002700007264004200034300002300076500033300099542004600432655002800478655002500506RK6E1800aMarble Saga: Kororinpa 1bHudson Entertainment, Inc.c2009-3-17  a1 Wii optical disc  aSet out on an adventure with Anthony the Ant on his quest through the Ant World. Gather essential items along the way in the ultimate goal to reach the Golden Sunflower and save Anthony's colony. Face treacherous mazes, use awesome gadgets and balance the world (literally) with fun and intuitive controls only available on Wii.  i2009kHudson Entertainment, Inc.sGameTDB 7aAdventure games2wiiext 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00876na  a2200109   4500001000700000245005300007264002600060300002300086500060100109542003100710655002500741RK6J1800aKororinpa 2: Anthony to Kin'iro Himawari no Tane 1bHudson Softc2009-8-6  a1 Wii optical disc  aMarbles! Balance Challenge is a skill-based action title where the player helps an Ant called Anthony save his colony via a series of physical tests. Wii Balance Board users can access Marbles! Balance Challenge?s 100 specially-created stages where the players steer a ball using the shifting weight of their physical movements. This unique way to control the game offers a new experience and combines fun and physical exercise. Players can also use gentle movements of the Wii Remote, with steering the ball through 200 different stages in a quest to locate the mythical ?Golden Sunflower Seed.?  i2009kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00845na  a2200109   4500001000700000245003100007264002200038300002300060500060100083542002600684655002500710RK6P1800aMarbles! Balance Challenge 1bKonamic2009-4-23  a1 Wii optical disc  aMarbles! Balance Challenge is a skill-based action title where the player helps an Ant called Anthony save his colony via a series of physical tests. Wii Balance Board users can access Marbles! Balance Challenge?s 100 specially-created stages where the players steer a ball using the shifting weight of their physical movements. This unique way to control the game offers a new experience and combines fun and physical exercise. Players can also use gentle movements of the Wii Remote, with steering the ball through 200 different stages in a quest to locate the mythical ?Golden Sunflower Seed.?  i2009kKonamisGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00244na  a2200109   4500001000700000245002000007264002200027300002300049500000500072542002600077655003100103RK7J0A00aOugon no Kizuna 1bJalecoc2009-5-28  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2009kJalecosGameTDB 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00806na  a2200121   4500001000700000245003000007264002400037300002300061500051900084542002900603655002500632655002700657RK8E5400aMajor League Baseball 2K8 1b2K Sportsc2008-3-3  a1 Wii optical disc  aMajor League Baseball® 2K8 returns to the diamond with the most complete MLB® experience available on every major video game console. Revolutionizing your control of the 5 tools in baseball are brand new pitching, fielding and baserunning controls and completely overhauled batting interface. Featuring a totally unique trading card mode, robust Minor League™ system, all-new Signature Style™ animations for 2008, and more, Major League Baseball® 2K8 brings a new level of fun to the virtual baseball world.  i2008k2K SportssGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aBaseball games2wiiext00600na  a2200121   4500001000700000245002300007264002200030300002300052500032700075542002600402655002400428655002600452RK9EA400aKaraoke Revolution 1bKonamic2009-12-7  a1 Wii optical disc  aKaraoke Revolution returns with an all-new lineup of music, characters, and venues! Get the party started with friends or perform solo and rise to the top of the charts. Tailor your game experience with customizable characters, wild outfits and accessories, and create your own custom venues! Can you handle the spotlight?  i2009kKonamisGameTDB 7aMusic games2wiiext 7aKaraoke games2wiiext00340na  a2200121   4500001000700000245002300007264002200030300002300052500006700075542002600142655002400168655002600192RK9PA400aKaraoke Revolution 1bKonamic2010-2-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aKonami reveals the ultimate party game as Karaoke Revolution's  i2010kKonamisGameTDB 7aMusic games2wiiext 7aKaraoke games2wiiext00630na  a2200121   4500001000700000245003300007264003800040300002300078500031500101542004100416655002500457655002600482RKAE6K00aUltimate Shooting Collection 1bUFO Interactive Gamesc2008-12-15  a1 Wii optical disc  aPacking three great titles into one disc, this collection of shoot em ups contain some never before seen titles that are sure to please casual and hardcore fans of this genre! The Ultimate Shooting Collection is a