Publisherc2008-9-25  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2008kD3 PublishersGameTDB00653na  a2200109   4500001000700000245003300007264003800040300002300078500037600101542004200477655002400519RZ9EG900aFamily Party: 30 Great Games 1bD3Publisher of Americac2008-12-2  a1 Wii optical disc  aOptimized for the Wii Remote, Family Party: 30 Great Games has more than 30 fun games to play as players tackle obstacle courses, plate spin, fire laser guns, test their wit at memory games and more. The game offers a wide variety of fun and addictive party games for up to 4 players featuring everything from track n' field, to playground games, to brain games and more.  i2008kD3Publisher of AmericasGameTDB 7aParty games2wiiext00650na  a2200109   4500001000700000245005000007264002800057300002300085500037600108542003200484655002400516RZ9JG900aSimple 2000 Series Wii Vol. 2: The Party Game 1bD3 Publisherc2008-8-28  a1 Wii optical disc  aOptimized for the Wii Remote, Family Party: 30 Great Games has more than 30 fun games to play as players tackle obstacle courses, plate spin, fire laser guns, test their wit at memory games and more. The game offers a wide variety of fun and addictive party games for up to 4 players featuring everything from track n' field, to playground games, to brain games and more.  i2008kD3 PublishersGameTDB 7aParty games2wiiext00633na  a2200109   4500001000700000245003300007264002800040300002300068500037600091542003200467655002400499RZ9PG900aFamily Party: 30 Great Games 1bD3 Publisherc2009-1-23  a1 Wii optical disc  aOptimized for the Wii Remote, Family Party: 30 Great Games has more than 30 fun games to play as players tackle obstacle courses, plate spin, fire laser guns, test their wit at memory games and more. The game offers a wide variety of fun and addictive party games for up to 4 players featuring everything from track n' field, to playground games, to brain games and more.  i2009kD3 PublishersGameTDB 7aParty games2wiiext00478na  a2200109   4500001000700000245006200007264003800069300002300107500016300130542004200293655003300335RZAPTV00aLernerfolg Grundschule Power Mathe: Der Kopfrechentrainer 1bTivola Publishing GmbHc2010-9-23  a1 Wii optical disc  aQuizzes and mini-games designed for children. This game is playable in six languages. Fun for kids of all ages or anyone who may want to sharpen there skills.  i2010kTivola Publishing GmbHsGameTDB 7aEducational software2wiiext00736na  a2200121   4500001000700000245001000007264003600017300002300053500044600076542004100522655002500563655002600588RZCE6K00aSaint 1bUFO Interactive Gamesc2009-6-7  a1 Wii optical disc  aGamers shoot their way through more than 20 fast-paced side-scrolling levels in this modern re-imagining of the classic Chinese epic Journey to the West. Players take on the role of the Saint, who must use his godlike powers to destroy hordes of mythical enemies. Players can select from more than a dozen upgradable weapons in "Story" mode, and the "Co-op" mode lets two players join forces to take out the swarming beasts. ~ All Game Guide  i2009kUFO Interactive GamessGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00764na  a2200121   4500001000700000245004300007264002500050300002300075500046300098542002800561655002500589655002800614RZDE0104aThe Legend of Zelda: Twilight Princess 1bNintendoc2006-11-19  a1 Wii optical disc  aWhen an evil darkness enshrouds the land of Hyrule, a young farm boy named Link must awaken the hero – and the animal – within. When Link travels to the Twilight Realm, he transforms into a wolf and must scour the land with the help of a mysterious girl named Midna. Besides his trusty sword and shield, Link will use his bow and arrows by aiming with the Wii Remote controller, fight while on horseback and use a wealth of other items, both new and old.  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00761na  a2200121   4500001000700000245004100007264002400048300002300072500046300095542002800558655002500586655002800611RZDJ0100aZelda no Densetsu: Twilight Princess 1bNintendoc2006-12-2  a1 Wii optical disc  aWhen an evil darkness enshrouds the land of Hyrule, a young farm boy named Link must awaken the hero – and the animal – within. When Link travels to the Twilight Realm, he transforms into a wolf and must scour the land with the help of a mysterious girl named Midna. Besides his trusty sword and shield, Link will use his bow and arrows by aiming with the Wii Remote controller, fight while on horseback and use a wealth of other items, both new and old.  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00763na  a2200121   4500001000700000245004300007264002400050300002300074500046300097542002800560655002500588655002800613RZDK0104aThe Legend of Zelda: Twilight Princess 1bNintendoc2009-8-27  a1 Wii optical disc  aWhen an evil darkness enshrouds the land of Hyrule, a young farm boy named Link must awaken the hero – and the animal – within. When Link travels to the Twilight Realm, he transforms into a wolf and must scour the land with the help of a mysterious girl named Midna. Besides his trusty sword and shield, Link will use his bow and arrows by aiming with the Wii Remote controller, fight while on horseback and use a wealth of other items, both new and old.  i2009kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00763na  a2200121   4500001000700000245004300007264002400050300002300074500046300097542002800560655002500588655002800613RZDP0104aThe Legend of Zelda: Twilight Princess 1bNintendoc2006-12-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aWhen an evil darkness enshrouds the land of Hyrule, a young farm boy named Link must awaken the hero – and the animal – within. When Link travels to the Twilight Realm, he transforms into a wolf and must scour the land with the help of a mysterious girl named Midna. Besides his trusty sword and shield, Link will use his bow and arrows by aiming with the Wii Remote controller, fight while on horseback and use a wealth of other items, both new and old.  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00914na  a2200109   4500001000700000245001700007264002600024300002300050500066800073542003000741655003300771RZEE5200aScience Papa 1bActivisionc2009-7-21  a1 Wii optical disc  aScience Papa is the world's most renowned scientist. You've just joined his elite team, and it's time for you to prove your worth! Explore chemistry, physics, paleontology, and biology in over 30 different experiments. You'll be competing against rival scientists who are out to steal prizes from under your nose. There are records to beat, lab equipment to unlock, and people to impress!  Mix chemicals, heat solutions, unearth dinosaur bones, and rewire electronic gadgets, all using the innovative control scheme. Take on the challenge of the Solo Mode, or attempt to sabotage your friends and family as you race to successfully complete different experiments!  i2009kActivisionsGameTDB 7aEducational software2wiiext00956na  a2200121   4500001000700000245001700007264002700024300002300051500066800074542003000742655002900772655003300801RZEP5200aScience Papa 1bActivisionc2009-10-30  a1 Wii optical disc  aScience Papa is the world's most renowned scientist. You've just joined his elite team, and it's time for you to prove your worth! Explore chemistry, physics, paleontology, and biology in over 30 different experiments. You'll be competing against rival scientists who are out to steal prizes from under your nose. There are records to beat, lab equipment to unlock, and people to impress!  Mix chemicals, heat solutions, unearth dinosaur bones, and rewire electronic gadgets, all using the innovative control scheme. Take on the challenge of the Solo Mode, or attempt to sabotage your friends and family as you race to successfully complete different experiments!  i2009kActivisionsGameTDB 7aSimulation games2wiiext 7aEducational software2wiiext00954na  a2200121   4500001000700000245003500007264002600042300002300068500063800091542003100729655002800760655004400788RZFPKM00aSecret Files 2: Puritas Cordis 1bDeep Silverc2009-5-7  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe world is on the brink of disaster. By the time Nina Kalenkow realizes that the recent catastrophes were caused not by nature, but by an unscrupulous secret society known as Puritas Cordis, it is almost too late. While her ex-boyfriend Max, a scientist, witnesses the brutal methods of Puritas Cordis at the excavation site of an ancient Indonesian temple complex, Nina joins forces with a priest in France to investigate the connection between the secret society's sinister prophesies and the creepy leader of an ancient order. A dramatic race against time begins. Will the protagonists be able to avert the impending apocalypse?  i2009kDeep SilversGameTDB 7aAdventure games2wiiext 7aPoint-and-click adventure games2wiiext00820na  a2200121   4500001000700000245001700007264003600024300002300060500051500083542004100598655002900639655003000668RZHE5G00aZoo Hospital 1bMajesco Entertainmentc2008-9-2  a1 Wii optical disc  aYou've graduated from Veterinary College not a moment too soon--your Aunt Lucy just called from the world famous Zoo Hospital she manages because she needs your help! A local property magnate, Gordon Grimm, is eying the zoo's land as the potential site for a profitable mini-golf course. Under Aunt Lucy's tutelage it's now up to you to help restore the zoo to its former glory by treating its ailing inhabitants, improving its Zoo Rating and attracting new exotic animals that will in turn attract the crowds!  i2008kMajesco EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aSimulation games2wiiext 7aVirtual pet games2wiiext00772na  a2200109   4500001000700000245001700007264003300024300002300057500051600080542003700596655002900633RZHX5G00aZoo Hospital 1bMajesco Sales Incc2008-12-4  a1 Wii optical disc  aYou've graduated from Veterinary College not a moment too soon--your Aunt Lucy just called from the world famous Zoo Hospital she manages because she needs your help! A local property magnate, Gordon Grimm, is eyeing the zoo's land as the potential site for a profitable mini-golf course. Under Aunt Lucy's tutelage it's now up to you to help restore the zoo to its former glory by treating its ailing inhabitants, improving its Zoo Rating and attracting new exotic animals that will in turn attract the crowds!  i2008kMajesco Sales IncsGameTDB 7aSimulation games2wiiext00996na  a2200121   4500001000700000245004200007264002500049300002300074500069800097542002900795655002500824655002500849RZIE2000aWinter Sports 3: The Great Tournament 1bZoo Gamesc2010-9-25  a1 Wii optical disc  aWinter Sports 2010 brings home the Olympic spirit by delivering the thrill of competition on a true worldwide stage. Compete in eight of the most popular winter sports events: snowboardcross, alpine skiing, free ride skiing, short track speedskating, ski jump, biathalon, figure skating, and bobsled. Play a Campaign, Quick Cup, Free Cup, Career, or vie with friends in four-person split-screen and online multiplayer. Play against anyone, anywhere; rise to the top of the global leaderboard, and become a true world champion. You'll feel like you're right on the snow and ice with high-impact graphics, real-life physics, and an up-close presentation style designed to deliver maximum impact.  i2010kZoo GamessGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aSkiing games2wiiext00704na  a2200109   4500001000700000245004500007264002600052300002300078500043900101542002900540655002500569RZIPRT00aWinter Sports 2010: The Great Tournament 1bRTL Gamesc2009-11-12  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn the story-based career mode, players can invest any experience points they collect in improved skills and equipment for their characters, and work their way up from beginners to world-class athletes. All of this takes place within a gripping story in which the player takes part in 16 competitions against four national teams. As an added challenge, one of those teams is the player's ultimate rival, and particularly hard to beat.  i2009kRTL GamessGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext00635na  a2200121   4500001000700000245002700007264003200034300002300066500033800089542003500427655002500462655002600487RZJD6900aDead Space: Extraction 1bElectronic Artsc2009-11-10  a1 Wii optical disc  aDead Space Extraction is a prequel that reveals the events leading up to Isaac Clarke’s mission on the USG Ishimura in Visceral Games’ award-winning Dead Space. Dead Space Extraction marries the innovative motion controls of the Wii Remote with a frenetic first person perspective to create a new action-packed horror experience.  i2009kElectronic ArtssGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00937na  a2200157   4500001000700000245002700007264003100034300002300065500051500088542003500603655002500638655002500663655002600688655003100714655003400745RZJE6900aDead Space: Extraction 1bElectronic Artsc2009-9-29  a1 Wii optical disc  aDead Space Extraction tells the story of a handful of space colonists desperately struggling to escape from a horrific infection on the Aegis VII mining colony deep in the furthest regions of space. The game introduces a new heroine to the fiction and as the crew fall victim to a mysterious contagion aboard the ship, it becomes clear that protecting her may be their only hope for survival. Dead Space Extraction introduces all new characters, weapons, enemies, puzzles and co-operative multiplayer gameplay.  i2009kElectronic ArtssGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aHorror games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext 7aRail shooter games2wiiext 7aSurvival horror games2wiiext00313na  a2200121   4500001000700000245002700007264003700034300002300071500000500094542004100099655002500140655002600165RZJJ1300aDead Space: Extraction 1bElectronic Arts Japanc2009-10-1  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2009kElectronic Arts JapansGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00634na  a2200121   4500001000700000245002700007264003100034300002300065500033800088542003500426655002500461655002600486RZJP6900aDead Space: Extraction 1bElectronic Artsc2009-9-24  a1 Wii optical disc  aDead Space Extraction is a prequel that reveals the events leading up to Isaac Clarke’s mission on the USG Ishimura in Visceral Games’ award-winning Dead Space. Dead Space Extraction marries the innovative motion controls of the Wii Remote with a frenetic first person perspective to create a new action-packed horror experience.  i2009kElectronic ArtssGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00518na  a2200109   4500001000700000245002000007264002500027300002300052500027900075542002900354655002500383RZKE2000aPuzzle Kingdoms 1bZoo Gamesc2009-4-13  a1 Wii optical disc  aFrom the acclaimed designer of Puzzle Quest, Steve Fawkner of Infinite Interactive, comes Puzzle Kingdoms. Deep, classic turn based empire gameplay tells an incredible story. Instead of auto-resolved conflict, a unique puzzle mechanic makes each battle unique and addictive.  i2009kZoo GamessGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00746na  a2200109   4500001000700000245002000007264002500027300002300052500050700075542002900582655002500611RZKP7J00aPuzzle Kingdoms 1bZoo Gamesc2009-4-14  a1 Wii optical disc  aPuzzle Kingdoms challenges players to plan out strategic attacks in order to defeat their opponents. Order troops across the map, conquering cities through innovative puzzle gameplay. Players build and manage armies led by heroic commanders to save the world of Etheria from the brink of destruction. By matching corresponding gems on the game board, players will both inflict damage on enemy forces while building mana that can be used to perform devastating attacks that will cripple their opponents.  i2009kZoo GamessGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00973na  a2200145   4500001000700000245001400007264003900021300002300060500059800083542004200681655002500723655002900748655002400777655002600801RZLE4100aCook Wars 1bUbi Soft Entertainmentc2009-11-24  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis is a cooking game in which players compete with other chefs to become the best in the world. Players move around a game board, collect coins, and perform a variety of cooking tasks (e.g., chopping, slicing, grating, and heating). Some recipes may include ingredients such as wine, liqueur, and sherry. A few cutscenes contain humurous antics: A chef falls into a fish tank full of lobsters; another chef coughs fire after tasting something hot; and a chef on the ground gets stepped on and says, "owww!" One female chef occasionally winks at the camera and dances in a flirtatious manner.  i2009kUbi Soft EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aSimulation games2wiiext 7aParty games2wiiext 7aCooking games2wiiext00327na  a2200109   4500001000700000245001800007264003900025300002300064500006400087542004200151655002400193RZLP4100aCooking Party 1bUbi Soft Entertainmentc2009-11-19  a1 Wii optical disc  aGet ready to be grilled. Become the best chef in the world!  i2009kUbi Soft EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aParty games2wiiext00504na  a2200109   4500001000700000245002500007264002400032300002300056500026200079542002800341655002500369RZNJ0100aZangeki no Reginleiv 1bNintendoc2010-2-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe story, heavily influenced by Norse mythology, paints Asgard gods Freyr and Freya cooperating with mortals in their war against a race of giants attacking a village to the north -- the first skirmish in what will ultimately escalate into Ragnarok itself.  i2010kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00325na  a2200121   4500001000700000245001700007264002000024300002300044500005400067542002300121655002900144655003000173RZOE7800aWorld of Zoo 1bTHQc2009-10-27  a1 Wii optical disc  aWhat would you do if you had the keys to the zoo?  i2009kTHQsGameTDB 7aSimulation games2wiiext 7aVirtual pet games2wiiext00337na  a2200109   4500001000700000245001700007264001900024300002300043500010900066542002300175655002900198RZOP7800aWorld of Zoo 1bTHQc2009-11-6  a1 Wii optical disc  aWorld of Zoo is the only life sim game that pushes you past the fences and into a world of your own zoo.  i2009kTHQsGameTDB 7aSimulation games2wiiext00672na  a2200121   4500001000700000245002900007264002500036300002300061500038700084542002800471655002500499655002600524RZPE0100aLink's Crossbow Training 1bNintendoc2007-11-19  a1 Wii optical disc  aAnyone can pick up the Wii Zapper and become a master marksman in the quick-play shooting galleries of Link's Crossbow Training. Dozens of fast-paced stages offer a wide variety of game play, from shooting stationary targets to defending a supply wagon from onrushing hordes of enemies. Multiplayer modes let players and their friends share a Wii Zapper to shoot for the high score.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00712na  a2200133   4500001000700000245002800007264002300035300002300058500038700081542002800468655002500496655002600521655003100547RZPJ0100aLink no Bowgun Training 1bNintendoc2008-5-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aAnyone can pick up the Wii Zapper and become a master marksman in the quick-play shooting galleries of Link's Crossbow Training. Dozens of fast-paced stages offer a wide variety of game play, from shooting stationary targets to defending a supply wagon from onrushing hordes of enemies. Multiplayer modes let players and their friends share a Wii Zapper to shoot for the high score.  i2008kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext 7aRail shooter games2wiiext00669na  a2200121   4500001000700000245002800007264002300035300002300058500038700081542002800468655002500496655002600521RZPK0100aLinkui Sagyeok Training 1bNintendoc2010-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aAnyone can pick up the Wii Zapper and become a master marksman in the quick-play shooting galleries of Link's Crossbow Training. Dozens of fast-paced stages offer a wide variety of game play, from shooting stationary targets to defending a supply wagon from onrushing hordes of enemies. Multiplayer modes let players and their friends share a Wii Zapper to shoot for the high score.  i2010kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00671na  a2200121   4500001000700000245002900007264002400036300002300060500038700083542002800470655002500498655002600523RZPP0100aLink's Crossbow Training 1bNintendoc2007-12-7  a1 Wii optical disc  aAnyone can pick up the Wii Zapper and become a master marksman in the quick-play shooting galleries of Link's Crossbow Training. Dozens of fast-paced stages offer a wide variety of game play, from shooting stationary targets to defending a supply wagon from onrushing hordes of enemies. Multiplayer modes let players and their friends share a Wii Zapper to shoot for the high score.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00587na  a2200121   4500001000700000245002500007264002400032300002300056500030400079542002900383655002500412655002800437RZREGT04aThe Destiny of Zorro 1b505 Gamesc2009-5-5  a1 Wii optical disc  aPlayers will make an incredible action-packed journey through the sun-scorched coast and desert landscape of early 1800’s Spanish California playing as the infamous Zorro – the swashbuckling defender of the oppressed whose secret identity is the fictional wealthy caballero Don Diego de la Vega.  i2009k505 GamessGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00588na  a2200121   4500001000700000245002500007264002500032300002300057500030400080542002900384655002500413655002800438RZRPGT04aThe Destiny of Zorro 1b505 Gamesc2009-2-27  a1 Wii optical disc  aPlayers will make an incredible action-packed journey through the sun-scorched coast and desert landscape of early 1800’s Spanish California playing as the infamous Zorro – the swashbuckling defender of the oppressed whose secret identity is the fictional wealthy caballero Don Diego de la Vega.  i2009k505 GamessGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00690na  a2200109   4500001000700000245001500007264002700022300002300049500045200072542003100524655002500555RZSEGJ00aSpeed Zone 1bDetn8 Gamesc2009-8-14  a1 Wii optical disc  aA futuristic racing game for the Wii home video game system. Players can choose from three modes of play: Solo, Race, and Battle. In Race mode, players compete against seven computer-controlled AI cars, while Battle mode is an all-out, futuristic demolition derby, using spectacular weapon. In Solo mode, players try to ignite jet thrusters with boost pads to accelerate "into the zone," with phantom cars and racing lines to help set lap records.  i2009kDetn8 GamessGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext00583na  a2200121   4500001000700000245001400007264003500021300002300056500028300079542003800362655002500400655003600425RZSP6800aWheelspin 1bBethesda Softworksc2009-11-27  a1 Wii optical disc  aWheelspin is a futuristic racing game developed by Archer Maclean’s studio, Awesome Play, for Wii. Wheelspin is a high-energy racing, high-impact game spread across a wide range of inter-planetary tracks and features three engaging modes as well as robust multiplayer options.  i2009kBethesda SoftworkssGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext 7aFuturistic racing games2wiiext01472na  a2200157   4500001000700000245002200007264002400029300002300053500108300076542002801159655002501187655002401212655002901236655002601265655002301291RZTE0100aWii Sports Resort 1bNintendoc2009-7-26  a1 Wii optical disc  aWii Sports Resort takes the inclusive, fun and intuitive controls of the original Wii Sports to the next level, introducing a whole new set of entertaining and physically immersive activities. With the deep control enhancements of Wii MotionPlus, veteran Wii users and newcomers alike can enjoy unprecedented gaming precision as they cruise on a water scooter, duel with swords, throw a Frisbee® and much more. This sequel to the popular Wii Sports makes use of the Wii MotionPlus accessory, which gives players the most responsive and realistic experience possible. The Wii MotionPlus accessory, which is included with Wii Sports Resort, plugs into the base of the Wii Remote™ controller and, combined with the accelerometer and sensor bar, provides an experience that gives players an even greater sense of immersion. Just as with Wii Sports, people will love competing against friends and family. As the competition heats up, Wii Sports Resort is as much fun to watch as it is to play. First-time players will find it easy to pick up a Wii Remote and jump into the action.  i2009kNintendosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aParty games2wiiext 7aBasketball games2wiiext 7aBowling games2wiiext 7aGolf games2wiiext01480na  a2200157   4500001000700000245002200007264002400029300002300053500108300076542002801159655002501187655002401212655002901236655002601265655003101291RZTJ0100aWii Sports Resort 1bNintendoc2009-6-25  a1 Wii optical disc  aWii Sports Resort takes the inclusive, fun and intuitive controls of the original Wii Sports to the next level, introducing a whole new set of entertaining and physically immersive activities. With the deep control enhancements of Wii MotionPlus, veteran Wii users and newcomers alike can enjoy unprecedented gaming precision as they cruise on a water scooter, duel with swords, throw a Frisbee® and much more. This sequel to the popular Wii Sports makes use of the Wii MotionPlus accessory, which gives players the most responsive and realistic experience possible. The Wii MotionPlus accessory, which is included with Wii Sports Resort, plugs into the base of the Wii Remote™ controller and, combined with the accelerometer and sensor bar, provides an experience that gives players an even greater sense of immersion. Just as with Wii Sports, people will love competing against friends and family. As the competition heats up, Wii Sports Resort is as much fun to watch as it is to play. First-time players will find it easy to pick up a Wii Remote and jump into the action.  i2009kNintendosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aParty games2wiiext 7aBasketball games2wiiext 7aBowling games2wiiext 7aTable tennis games2wiiext01321na  a2200109   4500001000700000245002200007264002300029300002300052500108300075542002801158655002501186RZTK0100aWii Sports Resort 1bNintendoc2010-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aWii Sports Resort takes the inclusive, fun and intuitive controls of the original Wii Sports to the next level, introducing a whole new set of entertaining and physically immersive activities. With the deep control enhancements of Wii MotionPlus, veteran Wii users and newcomers alike can enjoy unprecedented gaming precision as they cruise on a water scooter, duel with swords, throw a Frisbee® and much more. This sequel to the popular Wii Sports makes use of the Wii MotionPlus accessory, which gives players the most responsive and realistic experience possible. The Wii MotionPlus accessory, which is included with Wii Sports Resort, plugs into the base of the Wii Remote™ controller and, combined with the accelerometer and sensor bar, provides an experience that gives players an even greater sense of immersion. Just as with Wii Sports, people will love competing against friends and family. As the competition heats up, Wii Sports Resort is as much fun to watch as it is to play. First-time players will find it easy to pick up a Wii Remote and jump into the action.  i