g the series in a new direction, while also introducing elements that would go on to become standard in future Zelda games. In Zelda II™: The Adventure of Link™, Link is on a quest to seek the Triforce of Courage and awaken Princess Zelda from a sleeping spell placed upon her by an evil wizard. Meanwhile, Ganon’s minions are attempting to resurrect their master.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00747na  a2200121   4500001000500000245004100005264002300046300002300069500045200092542002800544655002500572655002800597FA9J00aZelda no Densetsu 2 - Link no Bouken 1bNintendoc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis direct sequel to the original The Legend of Zelda™ is famous for taking the series in a new direction, while also introducing elements that would go on to become standard in future Zelda games. In Zelda II™: The Adventure of Link™, Link is on a quest to seek the Triforce of Courage and awaken Princess Zelda from a sleeping spell placed upon her by an evil wizard. Meanwhile, Ganon’s minions are attempting to resurrect their master.  i2014kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00742na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003600005264002300041300002300064500045200087542002800539655002500567655002800592FA9P00aZelda II: The Adventure of Link 1bNintendoc2007-2-9  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis direct sequel to the original The Legend of Zelda™ is famous for taking the series in a new direction, while also introducing elements that would go on to become standard in future Zelda games. In Zelda II™: The Adventure of Link™, Link is on a quest to seek the Triforce of Courage and awaken Princess Zelda from a sleeping spell placed upon her by an evil wizard. Meanwhile, Ganon’s minions are attempting to resurrect their master.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00427na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001600005264002500021300002300046500019500069542002800264655002500292FAAE00aDonkey Kong 1bNintendoc2006-11-19  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe classic that launched the careers of Donkey Kong™ and Mario. Climb all the way to the top and save the beautiful Pauline from the paws of the giant ape in this colourful platform game.  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aArcade games2wiiext00462na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001600005264002300021300002300044500019500067542002800262655002500290655002500315FAAJ00aDonkey Kong 1bNintendoc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe classic that launched the careers of Donkey Kong™ and Mario. Climb all the way to the top and save the beautiful Pauline from the paws of the giant ape in this colourful platform game.  i2014kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext00463na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001600005264002400021300002300045500019500068542002800263655002500291655002500316FAAP00aDonkey Kong 1bNintendoc2006-12-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe classic that launched the careers of Donkey Kong™ and Mario. Climb all the way to the top and save the beautiful Pauline from the paws of the giant ape in this colourful platform game.  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext00460na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001600005264002100021300002300042500019500065542002800260655002500288655002500313FAAT00aDonkey Kong 1bNintendoc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe classic that launched the careers of Donkey Kong™ and Mario. Climb all the way to the top and save the beautiful Pauline from the paws of the giant ape in this colourful platform game.  i2014kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext00786na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002000005264002400025300002300049500055100072542002800623655002500651FABE00aDonkey Kong Jr. 1bNintendoc2006-12-4  a1 Wii optical disc  aBased on the popular arcade game, Donkey Kong Jr. is the sequel to the immensely successful Donkey Kong. Play as Donkey Kong's son, Junior, and rescue your dad who has been kidnapped and imprisoned in a cage by Mario. Use your jumping and climbing abilities to clamber up vines and chains, gather vital fruit and keys, and open the cage to free your father. Make sure you avoid the pesky birds, nasty electric sparks, and creepy chompers! Four different worlds filled with numerous climbing and jumping puzzles await you in this timeless classic.  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aArcade games2wiiext00455na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002000005264002300025300002300048500018400071542002800255655002500283655002500308FABJ00aDonkey Kong Jr. 1bNintendoc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aDonkey Kong™ has finally been captured by Mario! Reverse roles and help his son Junior avoid many dangers to save the giant ape. Here is another smash hit of the early Eighties.  i2014kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext00457na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002000005264002500025300002300050500018400073542002800257655002500285655002500310FABP00aDonkey Kong Jr. 1bNintendoc2006-12-22  a1 Wii optical disc  aDonkey Kong™ has finally been captured by Mario! Reverse roles and help his son Junior avoid many dangers to save the giant ape. Here is another smash hit of the early Eighties.  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext00822na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001200005264002500017300002300042500059300065542002800658655002600686FACE00aPinball 1bNintendoc2006-11-19  a1 Wii optical disc  aHit various targets and rack up points in this classic pinball game. Featuring a bonus mode starring Nintendo's legendary character, Mario, you control our hero as he holds a platform used to keep the ball in the air. And don't forget—you also have to save Pauline. If she falls and hits the ground, you lose a ball, but if you save her and lead her to the exit, you'll get a nice little surprise! This game is fun and easy to learn, and includes bonus balls for high scorers. On top of that, it features a two-player alternating mode. Both pinball fans and novices alike will enjoy it!  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aPinball games2wiiext00516na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001200005264002300017300002300040500025200063542002800315655002600343655002500369FACJ00aPinball 1bNintendoc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis cute pinball simulator was one of the first video games of the genre and still holds dear to many NES owners. Just as on a real pinball table, your goal is to flip the ball up and never let it fall off the bottom. How many points can you get?  i2014kNintendosGameTDB 7aPinball games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext00518na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001200005264002500017300002300042500025200065542002800317655002500345655002600370FACP00aPinball 1bNintendoc2006-12-15  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis cute pinball simulator was one of the first video games of the genre and still holds dear to many NES owners. Just as on a real pinball table, your goal is to flip the ball up and never let it fall off the bottom. How many points can you get?  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aArcade games2wiiext 7aPinball games2wiiext00186na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002400005264001300029300002300042500000500065542001800070FADJ00aGomoku Narabe Renju 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00780na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001600005264002500021300002300046500054800069542002800617655002500645FAFE00aMario Bros. 1bNintendoc2006-11-19  a1 Wii optical disc  aMario and Luigi are doing some underground plumbing when all sorts of strange creatures come flying out of the pipes. Help the two brothers clear stages by collecting coins and avoiding getting hit by enemies. Crabs, turtles and fighter flies must be cleared out by jumping underneath the platform they sit on, then kicking them away. But beware! Just when you think you got rid of them, they come back for more! Play against the computer or with a friend. Either way, this is one underground classic you will want to play time and time again.  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00536na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001600005264002300021300002300044500026900067542002800336655002500364655002500389FAFJ00aMario Bros. 1bNintendoc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aPlumbers Mario and Luigi must dispose of all the critters coming out of pipes in the action-packed arcade game that initiated the most popular video game franchise of all time. Two players can cooperate and compete in one of the first multiplayer hits of Nintendo.  i2014kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext00537na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001600005264002400021300002300045500026900068542002800337655002500365655002500390FAFP00aMario Bros. 1bNintendoc2006-12-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aPlumbers Mario and Luigi must dispose of all the critters coming out of pipes in the action-packed arcade game that initiated the most popular video game franchise of all time. Two players can cooperate and compete in one of the first multiplayer hits of Nintendo.  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext00534na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001600005264002100021300002300042500026900065542002800334655002500362655002500387FAFQ00aMario Bros. 1bNintendoc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aPlumbers Mario and Luigi must dispose of all the critters coming out of pipes in the action-packed arcade game that initiated the most popular video game franchise of all time. Two players can cooperate and compete in one of the first multiplayer hits of Nintendo.  i2014kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext00534na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002200005264002500027300002300052500029600075542002800371655002500399FAGE00aSuper Mario Bros. 1bNintendoc2006-12-25  a1 Wii optical disc  aFor more than twenty years, Mario and Luigi have been tirelessly running and jumping across these caves and castles to put a smile on every player's face. Squash goombas and crawl down pipes. Swallow mushrooms and Fire Flowers. Discover or rediscover the most popular video game of all time.  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00571na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002200005264002300027300002300050500029600073542002800369655002500397655002700422FAGJ00aSuper Mario Bros. 1bNintendoc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aFor more than twenty years, Mario and Luigi have been tirelessly running and jumping across these caves and castles to put a smile on every player's face. Squash goombas and crawl down pipes. Swallow mushrooms and Fire Flowers. Discover or rediscover the most popular video game of all time.  i2014kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00571na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002200005264002300027300002300050500029600073542002800369655002500397655002700422FAGP00aSuper Mario Bros. 1bNintendoc2007-1-5  a1 Wii optical disc  aFor more than twenty years, Mario and Luigi have been tirelessly running and jumping across these caves and castles to put a smile on every player's face. Squash goombas and crawl down pipes. Swallow mushrooms and Fire Flowers. Discover or rediscover the most popular video game of all time.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00569na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002200005264002100027300002300048500029600071542002800367655002500395655002700420FAGQ00aSuper Mario Bros. 1bNintendoc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aFor more than twenty years, Mario and Luigi have been tirelessly running and jumping across these caves and castles to put a smile on every player's face. Squash goombas and crawl down pipes. Swallow mushrooms and Fire Flowers. Discover or rediscover the most popular video game of all time.  i2014kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00806na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001100005264002500016300002300041500054200064542002800606655002500634655002500659FAHE00aTennis 1bNintendoc2006-12-18  a1 Wii optical disc  aPlayers slam a serve, fire a blazing backhand and smash a forehand volley on their way to winning the victory cup. Players can choose between five different levels of difficulty, ranging from Beginner all the way up to Advanced. If players want to become true champs, they should be ready to show off their most brilliant lobs and most powerful smashes. Play a singles match or grab a partner for doubles, and then choose an opponent. Players control the moves in tennis action so intense, they'll almost believe they're at center court.  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aTennis games2wiiext00621na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001100005264002300016300002300039500035900062542002800421655002500449655002500474FAHJ00aTennis 1bNintendoc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aIt was the first tennis game on the NES and allowed to play singles or doubles against five different levels of enemies. Although there aren't many moves to remember, it actually takes time to master the game and defeat the toughest and fastest opponents. Practicing volleys and smashes might help you tremendously if you want to win the last tournament.  i2014kNintendosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aTennis games2wiiext00623na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001100005264002500016300002300041500035900064542002800423655002500451655002500476FAHP00aTennis 1bNintendoc2006-12-22  a1 Wii optical disc  aIt was the first tennis game on the NES and allowed to play singles or doubles against five different levels of enemies. Although there aren't many moves to remember, it actually takes time to master the game and defeat the toughest and fastest opponents. Practicing volleys and smashes might help you tremendously if you want to win the last tournament.  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aTennis games2wiiext00823na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001100005264002500016300002300041500055900064542002800623655002500651655002500676FAIE00aSoccer 1bNintendoc2006-11-19  a1 Wii optical disc  aEnjoy 'real football' as you direct your team up and down the field. Pick from seven international teams—USA, Great Britain, France, Germany, Brazil, Japan, and Spain—and perform all the kickoffs, throw-ins, goal kicks, and corner kicks seen in a real friendly match. You can choose the skill level of the opposing team on a scale from one to five, so as your team improves, so do your opponents. Select a computer team or play against a friend. You even choose the length of the match, and as time ticks down, do your best to score the winning goal!  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aSoccer games2wiiext00551na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001100005264002100016300002300037500028900060542002800349655002500377655002700402FAIJ00aSoccer 1bNintendoc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe first football game of the NES offered a choice between seven national teams (Brazil, Germany, Spain, France, England, Japan and the U.S.A.) and five different difficulty levels. The real attraction of the game came from the possibility for two friends to play against each other.  i2014kNintendosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aFootball games2wiiext00555na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001100005264002500016300002300041500028900064542002800353655002500381655002700406FAIP00aSoccer 1bNintendoc2006-12-22  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe first football game of the NES offered a choice between seven national teams (Brazil, Germany, Spain, France, England, Japan and the U.S.A.) and five different difficulty levels. The real attraction of the game came from the possibility for two friends to play against each other.  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aFootball games2wiiext00334na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001500005264002500020300002300045500006600068542002800134655002500162655002500187FAJE00aIce Hockey 1bNintendoc2006-12-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aSharpen your skates and skills and shoot your way to victory.  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aHockey games2wiiext00525na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001500005264002100020300002300041500026100064542002800325655002500353655002500378FAJJ00aIce Hockey 1bNintendoc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aIce Hockey is one of the most acclaimed sports games on the NES. The reason for its popularity is that it offered a fun and straightforward experience, yet also required some tactician skills from players who had to compose their own team before the match.  i2014kNintendosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aHockey games2wiiext00529na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001500005264002500020300002300045500026100068542002800329655002500357655002500382FAJP00aIce Hockey 1bNintendoc2006-12-29  a1 Wii optical disc  aIce Hockey is one of the most acclaimed sports games on the NES. The reason for its popularity is that it offered a fun and straightforward experience, yet also required some tactician skills from players who had to compose their own team before the match.  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aHockey games2wiiext00792na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002400005264002500029300002300054500054900077542002800626655002800654FAKE04aThe Legend of Zelda 1bNintendoc2006-11-19  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe brave Link begins his hazardous journey in the fantastic world of Hyrule. Using your sword, your shield and your wit, retrieve the eight fragments of the Triforce and save the princess Zelda from the evil Gannon. This is the best-selling adventure game that initiated one of the most successful series of all time. Created by Shigeru Miyamoto, it introduced many innovative features that Zelda games are still associated with today. Not only is the adventure action-packed, it also features puzzling dungeons and myriads of secret passages.  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aAdventure games2wiiext00871na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002200005264002300027300002300050500059500073542002800668655002500696655002800721FAKJ00aZelda no Densetsu 1bNintendoc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe brave Link begins his hazardous journey in the fantastic world of Hyrule. Using your sword, your shield and your wit, retrieve the eight fragments of the Triforce and save the princess Zelda from the evil Gannon. This is the best-selling adventure game that initiated one of the most successful series of all time. Created by Shigeru Miyamoto, it introduced many innovative features that Zelda games are still associated with today. Not only is the adventure action-packed, it also features puzzling dungeons and myriads of secret passages. Discover or rediscover this timeless classic.  i2014kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00874na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002400005264002400029300002300053500059500076542002800671655002500699655002800724FAKP04aThe Legend of Zelda 1bNintendoc2007-2-16  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe brave Link begins his hazardous journey in the fantastic world of Hyrule. Using your sword, your shield and your wit, retrieve the eight fragments of the Triforce and save the princess Zelda from the evil Gannon. This is the best-selling adventure game that initiated one of the most successful series of all time. Created by Shigeru Miyamoto, it introduced many innovative features that Zelda games are still associated with today. Not only is the adventure action-packed, it also features puzzling dungeons and myriads of secret passages. Discover or rediscover this timeless classic.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00871na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002400005264002100029300002300050500059500073542002800668655002500696655002800721FAKT04aThe Legend of Zelda 1bNintendoc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe brave Link begins his hazardous journey in the fantastic world of Hyrule. Using your sword, your shield and your wit, retrieve the eight fragments of the Triforce and save the princess Zelda from the evil Gannon. This is the best-selling adventure game that initiated one of the most successful series of all time. Created by Shigeru Miyamoto, it introduced many innovative features that Zelda games are still associated with today. Not only is the adventure action-packed, it also features puzzling dungeons and myriads of secret passages. Discover or rediscover this timeless classic.  i2014kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00575na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001300005264002300018300002300041500030900064542002800373655002500401655002700426FALE00aBaseball 1bNintendoc2007-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aBaseball was a very successful title in Japan and North America, two regions where the sport is highly popular. At the time, it was considered one of the best sports simulations available because of its accessibility and cute graphics. It remains a good introduction to the rules of this enjoyable sport.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aBaseball games2wiiext00575na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001300005264002300018300002300041500030900064542002800373655002500401655002700426FALJ00aBaseball 1bNintendoc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aBaseball was a very successful title in Japan and North America, two regions where the sport is highly popular. At the time, it was considered one of the best sports simulations available because of its accessibility and cute graphics. It remains a good introduction to the rules of this enjoyable sport.  i2014kNintendosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aBaseball games2wiiext00577na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001300005264002500018300002300043500030900066542002800375655002500403655002700428FALP00aBaseball 1bNintendoc2006-12-29  a1 Wii optical disc  aBaseball was a very successful title in Japan and North America, two regions where the sport is highly popular. At the time, it was considered one of the best sports simulations available because of its accessibility and cute graphics. It remains a good introduction to the rules of this enjoyable sport.  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aBaseball games2wiiext00485na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264002500023300002300048500025100071542002800322655002500350FAME00aWario's Woods 1bNintendoc2006-11-19  a1 Wii optical disc  aWario's Woods™ is a puzzle game in which Toad piles up falling creatures and bombs in order to make them all disappear, collect gold coins and reach the next level. Setting up chain reactions is a very effective strategy to go far in this game.  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00483na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264002300023300002300046500025100069542002800320655002500348FAMJ00aWario no Mori 1bNintendoc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aWario's Woods™ is a puzzle game in which Toad piles up falling creatures and bombs in order to make them all disappear, collect gold coins and reach the next level. Setting up chain reactions is a very effective strategy to go far in this game.  i2014kNintendosGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00484na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264002400023300002300047500025100070542002800321655002500349FAMP00aWario's Woods 1bNintendoc2006-12-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aWario's Woods™ is a puzzle game in which Toad piles up falling creatures and bombs in order to make them all disappear, collect gold coins and reach the next level. Setting up chain reactions is a very effective strategy to go far in this game.  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00292na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001900005264002300024300002300047500005700070542002800127655002700155FANE00aUrban Champion 1bNintendoc2007-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe mean streets have a new force to deal with: you!  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00329na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001900005264002300024300002300047500005700070542002800127655002500155655002700180FANJ00aUrban Champion 1bNintendoc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe mean streets have a new force to deal with: you!  i2014kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext00331na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001900005264002500024300002300049500005700072542002800129655002500157655002700182FANP00aUrban Champion 1bNintendoc2006-12-15  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe mean streets have a new force to deal with: you!  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext00327na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001900005264002100024300002300045500005700068542002800125655002500153655002700178FANT00aUrban Champion 1bNintendoc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe mean streets have a new force to deal with: you!  i2014kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext00867na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264002200023300002300045500063900068542002500707655002500732FAOE00aSolomon's Key 1bTecmoc2006-11-19  a1 Wii optical disc  aA classic arcade title first released by Tecmo, Solomon's Key defined the 1980s puzzle-strategy genre. As Dana, a skilled and talented hero, you must strategically maneuver through over 40 stages using mysterious block-creation skills and other magical powers. Free the captive Fairy in each stage by finding the Bell, and escape by grabbing the Magic Key. Use quick thinking and magical firepower to discover hidden items and evade numerous enemies as you race against the clock! Solomon's Key also features over 10 secret levels and multiple endings you can unlock! Do you have what it takes to unravel the secrets of Solomon's Key?  i2006kTecmosGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00792na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002000005264002000025300002300045500056400068542002500632655002500657FAOJ00aSolomon no Kagi 1bTecmoc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aTo save his world from rampaging demons, Dana goes on a dangerous quest to find Solomon's Key and seal the monsters away. An audacious mix between an action game and a giant puzzle, Solomon's Key™ is one of the toughest challenges on the NES, but also one of its most endearing adventures. The player is required to combine logic and cunning reflexes to unravel all the mysteries of each room. Several secrets ought to be unlocked by the brightest minds, and only a few have been deemed worthy of seeing all the different endings. Will you be clever enough?  i2014kTecmosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00792na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264002200023300002300045500056400068542002500632655002500657FAOP00aSolomon's Key 1bTecmoc2006-12-15  a1 Wii optical disc  aTo save his world from rampaging demons, Dana goes on a dangerous quest to find Solomon's Key and seal the monsters away. An audacious mix between an action game and a giant puzzle, Solomon's Key™ is one of the toughest challenges on the NES, but also one of its most endearing adventures. The player is required to combine logic and cunning reflexes to unravel all the mysteries of each room. Several secrets ought to be unlocked by the brightest minds, and only a few have been deemed worthy of seeing all the different endings. Will you be clever enough?  i2006kTecmosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00943na  a2200133   4500001000500000245002900005264002400034300002300058500062700081542002800708655002500736655002500761655002300786FAPE00aNES Open Tournament Golf 1bNintendoc2007-6-18  a1 Wii optical disc  aWe all knew that Mario was a top-notch plumber, but did you know that he could also be a world-class golfer? You can challenge another player in Stroke, Match and Tournament modes. Play on three fantasy courses in the USA, the UK and Japan and try to win a million dollars. Make sure you keep an eye on the wind and distance to the hole before selecting your club, or else you'll be racking up some high scores - which is exactly what you don't want to do in this game. Whether you're a beginner or an experienced golfer, NES Open Tournament Golf is perfect for those days when you just can't get to the local golf course.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext 7aGolf games2wiiext00376na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002000005264002300025300002300048500010700071542002800178655002500206655002300231FAPJ00aMario Open Golf 1bNintendoc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aTee off with Mario (and Luigi, too, in two-player mode) in this classic sporting simulation from 1992.  i2014kNintendosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aGolf games2wiiext00386na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002900005264002400034300002300058500010700081542002800188655002500216655002300241FAPP00aNES Open Tournament Golf 1bNintendoc2007-5-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aTee off with Mario (and Luigi, too, in two-player mode) in this classic sporting simulation from 1992.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aGolf games2wiiext00383na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002900005264002100034300002300055500010700078542002800185655002500213655002300238FAPT00aNES Open Tournament Golf 1bNintendoc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aTee off with Mario (and Luigi, too, in two-player mode) in this classic sporting simulation from 1992.  i2014kNintendosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aGolf games2wiiext01103na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002300005264004600028300002300074500082200097542004900919655002500968FAQJ00aNinja JaJaMaru-kun 1bJaleco / Jaleco Entertainmentc2006-11-26  a1 Wii optical disc  aTake on the role of a ninja called JaJaMaru and rescue the captured Princess Sakura from the evil Namazu Dayuu in this action-packed game, never before released outside of Japan. JaJaMaru must use his throwing stars to defeat the monsters lurking in each of Dayuu’s many hideouts. JaJaMaru has to be careful though, as each monster has its own unique weapon and method of attacking. The only way for him to advance is to break the floor bricks above him and move up and down between the levels of each round, defeating monsters as he goes. To help him, broken bricks sometimes reveal items that JaJaMaru can use to his advantage, possibly leading to him getting the ultimate power-up—a ride on Gamapakun, the giant frog! Take all this, throw in some bonus stages, and you’ve got a game with a style all its own!  i2006kJaleco / Jaleco EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00579na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002300005264004500028300002300073500029900096542004900395655002500444FAQL00aNinja JaJaMaru-kun 1bJaleco / Jaleco Entertainmentc2007-9-21  a1 Wii optical disc  aNinja JaJaMaru-kun (meaning 'determined little ninja') was originally released for the Japanese Famicom (NES) in Japan in 1985. This action game features a ninja called JaJaMaru, who uses his shuriken (ninja throwing stars) to defeat monsters and save Princess Sakura from the evil Lord Namazu.  i2007kJaleco / Jaleco EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext01103na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002300005264004600028300002300074500082200097542004900919655002500968FAQN00aNinja JaJaMaru-kun 1bJaleco / Jaleco Entertainmentc2007-10-22  a1 Wii optical disc  aTake on the role of a ninja called JaJaMaru and rescue the captured Princess Sakura from the evil Namazu Dayuu in this action-packed game, never before released outside of Japan. JaJaMaru must use his throwing stars to defeat the monsters lurking in each of Dayuu’s many hideouts. JaJaMaru has to be careful though, as each monster has its own unique weapon and method of attacking. The only way for him to advance is to break the floor bricks above him and move up and down between the levels of each round, defeating monsters as he goes. To help him, broken bricks sometimes reveal items that JaJaMaru can use to his advantage, possibly leading to him getting the ultimate power-up—a ride on Gamapakun, the giant frog! Take all this, throw in some bonus stages, and you’ve got a game with a style all its own!  i2007kJaleco / Jaleco EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00883na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001200005264002100017300002300038500062300061542002600684655002500710655002600735FARE00aGradius 1bKonamic2007-1-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aAcross the galaxy, there exists a distant planet known as Gradius. Gradius' peaceful existence has been brought to an end by an intense space invasion by a race known as the Bacterion. To save the planet, the hyperspace fighter Vic Viper has been deployed to fight the Bacterion invasion. Players pilot the Vic Viper through seven stages, shooting and dodging through deadly obstacles, while using various power-ups, including missiles, lasers, options and shields. The Vic Viper's target is the enemy fortress, Xaerous. The only way to end the war is to plunge deep through the enemy forces and destroy its very core.  i2007kKonamisGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00367na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001200005264001900017300002300036500014700059542002600206655002500232FARJ00aGradius 1bKonamic2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aYou are the last hope of the gentle people of Gradius™. You’ve just lifted off to confront the invading forces of the amoeboid Bacterions.  i2014kKonamisGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00369na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001200005264002100017300002300038500014700061542002600208655002500234FARP00aGradius 1bKonamic2007-2-2  a1 Wii optical disc  aYou are the last hope of the gentle people of Gradius™. You’ve just lifted off to confront the invading forces of the amoeboid Bacterions.  i2007kKonamisGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00692na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001200005264002100017300002300038500047100061542002500532655002500557FASE00aXevious 1bNamcoc2007-1-15  a1 Wii optical disc  aControl your Solvalou ship and destroy the Xevious forces! Fire the zapper missiles against air-based enemies and drop the blaster bombs down upon ground-based targets. Destroy Andor Genesis to earn bonus points! Unique enemies, interesting background music, a variety of vertically scrolling background environments and many hidden game play features differentiated Xevious from the other shooting games released at the time. Are you devious enough to beat Xevious?  i2007kNamcosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00488na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001200005264003300017300002300050500020400073542003800277655002500315655002600340FASJ00aXevious 1bNamco Bandai Gamesc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aControl your Solvalou ship and destroy the Xevious™ forces! Use zapper missiles against air-based enemies and blaster bombs against ground-based targets. Destroy Andor Genesis to earn bonus points!  i2014kNamco Bandai GamessGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00489na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001200005264003400017300002300051500020400074542003800278655002500316655002600341FASP00aXevious 1bNamco Bandai Gamesc2007-1-12  a1 Wii optical disc  aControl your Solvalou ship and destroy the Xevious™ forces! Use zapper missiles against air-based enemies and blaster bombs against ground-based targets. Destroy Andor Genesis to earn bonus points!  i2007kNamco Bandai GamessGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00486na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001200005264003100017300002300048500020400071542003800275655002500313655002600338FAST00aXevious 1bNamco Bandai Gamesc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aControl your Solvalou ship and destroy the Xevious™ forces! Use zapper missiles against air-based enemies and blaster bombs against ground-based targets. Destroy Andor Genesis to earn bonus points!  i2014kNamco Bandai GamessGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00712na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002300005264002100028300002300049500048000072542002500552655002500577FATE04aThe Legend of Kage 1bTaitoc2007-2-19  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis classic ninja-action game first appeared in arcades in 1985 and became instantly popular. As the Iga ninja named "Kage," players embark on an action-packed quest as they move toward a magic castle where the Princess "Kiri" is held captive by "Yohshirou Yukikusa." To stay alive, players move vertically and horizontally through forest and castle environments and execute massive jumps, all the while using throwing-star knives and a sword to take down hordes of enemies.  i2007kTaitosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00709na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002100005264002000026300002300046500048000069542002500549655002500574FATJ00aKage no Densetsu 1bTaitoc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis classic ninja-action game first appeared in arcades in 1985 and became instantly popular. As the Iga ninja named "Kage," players embark on an action-packed quest as they move toward a magic castle where the Princess "Kiri" is held captive by "Yohshirou Yukikusa." To stay alive, players move vertically and horizontally through forest and castle environments and execute massive jumps, all the while using throwing-star knives and a sword to take down hordes of enemies.  i2014kTaitosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00326na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001500005264002100020300002300041500006300064542002500127655002500152655002700177FAVE00aTecmo Bowl 1bTecmoc2007-3-12  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe king of the retro pigskin reigns over Virtual Console!  i2007kTecmosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aFootball games2wiiext00323na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001500005264001800020300002300038500006300061542002500124655002500149655002700174FAVJ00aTecmo Bowl 1bTecmoc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe king of the retro pigskin reigns over Virtual Console!  i2014kTecmosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aFootball games2wiiext00673na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002000005264002000025300002300045500044500068542002500513655002500538FAWE00aElevator Action 1bTaitoc2007-3-5  a1 Wii optical disc  aA blast from the past! In this multidirectional scrolling action game, you control a spy and sneak alone into a building to steal the secret papers hidden there. Use a pistol, kicks, an elevator, and even the lights to take out the building’s guards. The gun-fighting action is full of thrills! You will need speed and timing to get on the elevators, move between floors, steal the secret papers, and escape from the basement parking lot.  i2007kTaitosGameTDB 7aArcade games2wiiext00671na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002000005264001800025300002300043500044500066542002500511655002500536FAWJ00aElevator Action 1bTaitoc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aA blast from the past! In this multidirectional scrolling action game, you control a spy and sneak alone into a building to steal the secret papers hidden there. Use a pistol, kicks, an elevator, and even the lights to take out the building’s guards. The gun-fighting action is full of thrills! You will need speed and timing to get on the elevators, move between floors, steal the secret papers, and escape from the basement parking lot.  i2014kTaitosGameTDB 7aArcade games2wiiext00810na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001200005264004700017300002300064500053700087542005100624655002500675FAXE00aPac-Man 1bNAMCO BANDAI Games America Inc.c2007-5-14  a1 Wii optical disc  aMove Pac-Man through the maze, avoiding ghosts and eating all the Pac-Dots. Beware, each of the ghosts behave differently! When Pac-Man chomps a Power Pellet, he becomes invincible and is able to eat the blue ghosts. The more ghosts Pac-Man eats in a row, the higher the score. Don't forget to eat the bonus fruit, too! Released in 1980, Pac-Man is the most well-known video game on Earth and is also commonly acknowledged as one of the most successful coin-operated games in history. Enjoy this masterpiece of gaming history today!  i2007kNAMCO BANDAI Games America Inc.sGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00587na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001200005264003300017300002300050500034100073542003800414655002500452FAXJ00aPac-Man 1bNamco Bandai Gamesc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aMove Pac-Man® through the maze, avoiding ghosts and eating all the Pac-Dots. Beware though, each of the ghosts behaves differently! When Pac-Man® chomps a Power Pellet, he becomes invincible, and is able to eat the blue ghosts. The more ghosts Pac-Man® eats in a row, the higher the score. Don’t forget to eat the bonus fruit, too!  i2014kNamco Bandai GamessGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00588na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001200005264003400017300002300051500034100074542003800415655002500453FAXP00aPac-Man 1bNamco Bandai Gamesc2007-4-13  a1 Wii optical disc  aMove Pac-Man® through the maze, avoiding ghosts and eating all the Pac-Dots. Beware though, each of the ghosts behaves differently! When Pac-Man® chomps a Power Pellet, he becomes invincible, and is able to eat the blue ghosts. The more ghosts Pac-Man® eats in a row, the higher the score. Don’t forget to eat the bonus fruit, too!  i2007kNamco Bandai GamessGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00585na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001200005264003100017300002300048500034100071542003800412655002500450FAXT00aPac-Man 1bNamco Bandai Gamesc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aMove Pac-Man® through the maze, avoiding ghosts and eating all the Pac-Dots. Beware though, each of the ghosts behaves differently! When Pac-Man® chomps a Power Pellet, he becomes invincible, and is able to eat the blue ghosts. The more ghosts Pac-Man® eats in a row, the higher the score. Don’t forget to eat the bonus fruit, too!  i2014kNamco Bandai GamessGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00171na  a2200097   4500001000500000245000900005264001300014300002300027500000500050542001800055FAYJ00aIkki 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00179na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001700005264001300022300002300035500000500058542001800063FAZJ00aField Combat 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00219na  a2200097   4500001000500000245005700005264001300062300002300075500000500098542001800103FAZQ00aDowntown Nekketsu Koushinkyoku: Soreyuke Daiundoukai 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB01217na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002400005264002300029300002300052500097900075542002801054655002501082FB2J00aSuper Mario Bros. 2 1bNintendoc2010-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aOriginally released in Japan as Super Mario Bros.® 2, this game has previously made only brief cameo appearances in the Western hemisphere. Now available on the Virtual Console in all of its original splendor, Mario fans will appreciate the familiar look and feel of the game, while finding that its updated game play creates an entirely new challenge. No longer content just to wear different-colored overalls, Mario and Luigi also possess different skill sets (Mario can stop quicker, while Luigi can jump higher). In addition to the classic enemies already known to fans worldwide, there are also Poison Mushrooms, backward Warp Zones, and the occasional wind gust (which can help or hinder your progress) to take into account. And if that’s somehow not enough, expert players can go looking for the game’s secret worlds. So get ready to put your Mario skills to the ultimate test, and save the Princess again. Just don’t be surprised if she’s in another castle!  i2010kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00453na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003900005264002400044300002300068500016000091542002800251655002500279655002700304FB2L00aSuper Mario Bros.: The Lost Levels 1bNintendoc2008-8-22  a1 Wii optical disc  aIt's time for a blast from the past! Now, on Virtual Console, you can once again experience the original sequel to the best-selling video game of all time!  i2008kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext01234na  a2200109   4500001000500000245004000005264002400045300002300069500097900092542002801071655002501099FB2N00aSuper Mario Bros. - The Lost Levels 1bNintendoc2007-10-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aOriginally released in Japan as Super Mario Bros.® 2, this game has previously made only brief cameo appearances in the Western hemisphere. Now available on the Virtual Console in all of its original splendor, Mario fans will appreciate the familiar look and feel of the game, while finding that its updated game play creates an entirely new challenge. No longer content just to wear different-colored overalls, Mario and Luigi also possess different skill sets (Mario can stop quicker, while Luigi can jump higher). In addition to the classic enemies already known to fans worldwide, there are also Poison Mushrooms, backward Warp Zones, and the occasional wind gust (which can help or hinder your progress) to take into account. And if that’s somehow not enough, expert players can go looking for the game’s secret worlds. So get ready to put your Mario skills to the ultimate test, and save the Princess again. Just don’t be surprised if she’s in another castle!  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00209na  a2200097   4500001000500000245004700005264001300052300002300065500000500088542001800093FB3J00aValkyrie no Bouken - Toki no Kagi Densetsu 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00841na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001500005264003000020300002300050500056000073542003300633655002500666655002800691FB4E00aLunar Pool 1bD4 Enterprisec2007-10-22  a1 Wii optical disc  aLunar Pool takes the historical ball game of billiards and reinvents it with a unique and futuristic flair. The rules are simple. All you need to do is use your cue stick to hit the white cue ball, causing it to hit the other numbered balls and make them go into the pockets. You can enjoy nearly unlimited game play with 30 tables, 2 different ball arrangements, and the ability to change the degree of friction on the table. You can also play against a computer or another human player, so try challenging someone once you’ve got the hang of the game.  i2007kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aBilliards games2wiiext00493na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001500005264003400020300002300054500020200077542003900279655002500318655002800343FB4J00aLunar Ball 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aLunar Pool, out now on Virtual Console, is a pool game with a difference. Instead of using a standard rectangular table, this NES game features 30 differently-shaped tables and adjustable friction.  i2014kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aBilliards games2wiiext00494na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001500005264003500020300002300055500020200078542003900280655002500319655002800344FB4P00aLunar Pool 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2007-7-24  a1 Wii optical disc  aLunar Pool, out now on Virtual Console, is a pool game with a difference. Instead of using a standard rectangular table, this NES game features 30 differently-shaped tables and adjustable friction.  i2007kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aBilliards games2wiiext00796na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001000005264002900015300002300044500052300067542003300590655002500623655002600648FB5E00aZanac 1bD4 Enterprisec2007-12-3  a1 Wii optical disc  aZANAC is a vertically scrolling shoot-‘em-up game that was released in November 1986. Take control of the state-of-the-art fighter, ZANAC, with the objective of destroying the bases of the mechanized enemy forces. Use your full array of regular weapons as well as 8 special weapons to clear the 12 intense areas of the game. Be careful, though, as the game changes the degree of difficulty in real time based on how well you play. This ensures that it feels like you’re experiencing a new game every time you play!  i2007kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00795na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001000005264002800015300002300043500052300066542003300589655002500622655002600647FB5J00aZanac 1bD4 Enterprisec2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aZANAC is a vertically scrolling shoot-‘em-up game that was released in November 1986. Take control of the state-of-the-art fighter, ZANAC, with the objective of destroying the bases of the mechanized enemy forces. Use your full array of regular weapons as well as 8 special weapons to clear the 12 intense areas of the game. Be careful, though, as the game changes the degree of difficulty in real time based on how well you play. This ensures that it feels like you’re experiencing a new game every time you play!  i2014kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00177na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001500005264001300020300002300033500000500056542001800061FB6J00aFront Line 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00178na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001600005264001300021300002300034500000500057542001800062FB7J00aNuts & Milk 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00177na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001500005264001300020300002300033500000500056542001800061FB8J00aChallenger 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00173na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001100005264001300016300002300029500000500052542001800057FB9J00aPooyan 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00450na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002000005264002100025300002300046500017500069542002800244655002500272655003100297FBAJ00aSmash Ping Pong 1bNintendoc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis speedy table tennis game was originally released only in Japan for the Famicom Disk System. Now, over 20 years later, it makes its European debut on Virtual Console!  i2014kNintendosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aTable tennis games2wiiext00456na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002300005264002400028300002300052500017500075542002800250655002500278655003100303FBAL00aSmash Table Tennis 1bNintendoc2009-7-17  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis speedy table tennis game was originally released only in Japan for the Famicom Disk System. Now, over 20 years later, it makes its European debut on Virtual Console!  i2009kNintendosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aTable tennis games2wiiext00784na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001500005264002300020300002300043500051800066542002800584655002500612655002500637FBBE00aMach Rider 1bNintendoc2007-7-7  a1 Wii optical disc  aIt's the year 2112. Earth has been invaded by the forces of evil. Battle the invaders as you race from sector to sector on your motorcycle, searching for survivors. Feel the incredible sense of speed as you zip past evil Quadrunners and zigzag between treacherous rocks, oil spills and other obstacles on the course. For a different challenge, create your own course in Design Mode, using the various twists, turns and straightaways the game has to offer. Remember, you are Earth's only hope—you are Mach Rider.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext00469na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001500005264002300020300002300043500024000066542002800306655002500334FBBJ00aMach Rider 1bNintendoc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aIt is the year 2112 and Earth has been taken over by evil forces. As a lone motorcycle warrior, you must battle the invaders while racing from sector to sector in search of survivors. You are Earth’s last hope. You are Mach Rider™!  i2014kNintendosGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext00470na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001500005264002400020300002300044500024000067542002800307655002500335FBBP00aMach Rider 1bNintendoc2007-5-25  a1 Wii optical disc  aIt is the year 2112 and Earth has been taken over by evil forces. As a lone motorcycle warrior, you must battle the invaders while racing from sector to sector in search of survivors. You are Earth’s last hope. You are Mach Rider™!  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext00792na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001500005264002400020300002300044500051400067542002800581655002500609655003600634FBCE00aExcitebike 1bNintendoc2007-3-19  a1 Wii optical disc  aFace crazy curves, hairpin turns, and daredevil jumps as you race toward the checkered flag and the Excitebike championship. Race against the clock or challenge an opponent. You must keep your bearings as you fly through the air, and avoid getting clipped by other racers. Stay cool under pressure or your bike will overheat. If you get tired of racing on the circuit, create your own course in Design mode. There you have access to all the ramps, mounds, bridges, and other obstacles Excitebike has to offer.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext 7aMotorcycle racing games2wiiext00565na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001500005264002100020300002300041500029000064542002800354655002500382655003600407FBCJ00aExcitebike 1bNintendoc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aLong before Excite Truck™ for Wii, there was Excitebike™ for NES; a wheelie-poppin’, mud-flingin’, side-scrollin’ motocross masterpiece. Roar across the dirt and take down rival riders to claim victory in the main event, or design your own monster motocross track to race on!