NABE00aMario Kart 64 1bNintendoc2007-1-29  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe crazy power slides and vicious red shells are back! Mario Kart 64™ was one of the earliest hits of the Nintendo 64 and is still considered by many as one of the best episodes of Nintendo's classic kart series. Several reasons justify such a high reputation. The 4-player multiplayer provides some of the most entertaining sessions ever. The driving experience has been refined with the addition of several advanced techniques. And the various tracks are filled with clever ideas and hidden shortcuts.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext 7aKart racing games2wiiext00822na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001800005264002400023300002300047500051100070542002800581655002500609655002400634655003000658NABJ00aMario Kart 64 1bNintendoc2007-1-30  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe crazy power slides and vicious red shells are back! Mario Kart 64™ was one of the earliest hits of the Nintendo 64 and is still considered by many as one of the best episodes of Nintendo's classic kart series. Several reasons justify such a high reputation. The 4-player multiplayer provides some of the most entertaining sessions ever. The driving experience has been refined with the addition of several advanced techniques. And the various tracks are filled with clever ideas and hidden shortcuts.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext 7aParty games2wiiext 7aKart racing games2wiiext00822na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001800005264002400023300002300047500051100070542002800581655002500609655002400634655003000658NABP00aMario Kart 64 1bNintendoc2007-1-26  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe crazy power slides and vicious red shells are back! Mario Kart 64™ was one of the earliest hits of the Nintendo 64 and is still considered by many as one of the best episodes of Nintendo's classic kart series. Several reasons justify such a high reputation. The 4-player multiplayer provides some of the most entertaining sessions ever. The driving experience has been refined with the addition of several advanced techniques. And the various tracks are filled with clever ideas and hidden shortcuts.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext 7aParty games2wiiext 7aKart racing games2wiiext00783na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264002100023300002300044500051100067542002800578655002500606655003000631NABT00aMario Kart 64 1bNintendoc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe crazy power slides and vicious red shells are back! Mario Kart 64™ was one of the earliest hits of the Nintendo 64 and is still considered by many as one of the best episodes of Nintendo's classic kart series. Several reasons justify such a high reputation. The 4-player multiplayer provides some of the most entertaining sessions ever. The driving experience has been refined with the addition of several advanced techniques. And the various tracks are filled with clever ideas and hidden shortcuts.  i2014kNintendosGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext 7aKart racing games2wiiext00437na  a2200109   4500001000500000245004100005264002400046300002300070500017800093542002800271655002800299NACE04aThe Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time 1bNintendoc2007-2-26  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased to an eager audience in 1998, The Legend of Zelda™: Ocarina of Time became an instant smash and quickly established itself as one of the greatest games ever made.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aAdventure games2wiiext00472na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003900005264002400044300002300068500017800091542002800269655002500297655002800322NACJ00aZelda no Densetsu: Toki no Okarina 1bNintendoc2007-2-27  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased to an eager audience in 1998, The Legend of Zelda™: Ocarina of Time became an instant smash and quickly established itself as one of the greatest games ever made.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00474na  a2200121   4500001000500000245004100005264002400046300002300070500017800093542002800271655002500299655002800324NACP04aThe Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time 1bNintendoc2007-2-23  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased to an eager audience in 1998, The Legend of Zelda™: Ocarina of Time became an instant smash and quickly established itself as one of the greatest games ever made.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00942na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001600005264002300021300002300044500063100067542002800698655002500726655003100751655002600782NADE00aStar Fox 64 1bNintendoc2007-4-2  a1 Wii optical disc  aPlayers take the controls of their Arwing and complete 15 missions to reach the final objective: a showdown on Venom, the home planet of the interplanetary tyrant, Andross. Throughout the adventure, players have to accomplish challenging objectives in order to reach and conquer every mission. Skim over the surface of an alien sea, weave through the concrete canyons of a futuristic metropolis or dodge planetoids the size of mountains. Between missions, players will be treated to real-time 3-D movies that progress the story of the Star Fox team of space mercenaries in their struggle against the evil ape emperor, Andross.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aRole-playing games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00502na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001600005264002400021300002300045500023300068542002800301655002500329655002600354NADJ00aStar Fox 64 1bNintendoc2007-4-17  a1 Wii optical disc  aAndross has launched an all-out attack on the Lylat System, and only Fox McCloud and the Star Fox team stand in his way. Jump into your Arwing fighter, Landmaster tank or Blue Marine sub, and blast Andross’s forces into atoms!  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00501na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001500005264002400020300002300044500023300067542002800300655002500328655002600353NADP00aLylat Wars 1bNintendoc2007-4-20  a1 Wii optical disc  aAndross has launched an all-out attack on the Lylat System, and only Fox McCloud and the Star Fox team stand in his way. Jump into your Arwing fighter, Landmaster tank or Blue Marine sub, and blast Andross’s forces into atoms!  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00499na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001600005264002100021300002300042500023300065542002800298655002500326655002600351NADT00aStar Fox 64 1bNintendoc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aAndross has launched an all-out attack on the Lylat System, and only Fox McCloud and the Star Fox team stand in his way. Jump into your Arwing fighter, Landmaster tank or Blue Marine sub, and blast Andross’s forces into atoms!  i2014kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00926na  a2200145   4500001000500000245001600005264002400021300002300045500057300068542002800641655002500669655002800694655003100722655002700753NAEE00aPaper Mario 1bNintendoc2007-7-16  a1 Wii optical disc  aPaper Mario is a graphically innovative game that breaks the confines of the RPG genre. Now slimmed down, everyone's favorite plumber flips, spins, jumps, and hammers his way through scads of exotic worlds that teem with a huge and hugely entertaining supporting cast. Players control numerous characters, both old and new, in a complex, nonlinear story that follows different scenarios depending on player choices. A dizzying collection of spells, attacks, skills, and special items can be collected by players willing to thoroughly explore the lush 3-D environments!  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext 7aRole-playing games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00482na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001600005264002400021300002300045500024500068542002800313655003100341NAEJ00aMario Story 1bNintendoc2007-7-10  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn this sprawling action-RPG, Mario may be two-dimensional but his adventure is anything but thin! Paper Mario brilliantly blends the heroic plumber’s platform antics with a hilarious quest full of offbeat characters and wacky challenges.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00522na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001600005264002400021300002300045500024500068542002800313655002800341655003100369NAEP00aPaper Mario 1bNintendoc2007-7-13  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn this sprawling action-RPG, Mario may be two-dimensional but his adventure is anything but thin! Paper Mario brilliantly blends the heroic plumber’s platform antics with a hilarious quest full of offbeat characters and wacky challenges.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aAdventure games2wiiext 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00993na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001300005264002400018300002300042500071700065542002800782655002500810655003600835NAFE00aF-Zero X 1bNintendoc2007-6-25  a1 Wii optical disc  aChoose from 30 different hover-car racers, including updated versions of the Blue Falcon and other vehicles from the original F-Zero, and get ready to play one of the fastest racers ever! Race to the finish line on tracks that twist and turn through the air. However, you will have to avoid the other 29 cars on the track or else face the consequences! If you're in a competitive mood, try to win a Grand Prix Cup, get the fastest lap time in a Time Trial, or destroy the competition in a Death Race. You can also challenge three friends in the Versus mode. With five separate play modes, hidden vehicles and courses, and an excellent sound track, F-Zero X still represents one of the best racing titles to date!  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext 7aFuturistic racing games2wiiext00486na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001300005264002400018300002300042500021000065542002800275655002500303655003600328NAFJ00aF-Zero X 1bNintendoc2007-5-29  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe fastest racing game in the universe returns! F-Zero X is the stunning Nintendo 64 sequel to the Super Nintendo smash hit, featuring more sound barrier-breaking, gravity-defying action than ever before.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext 7aFuturistic racing games2wiiext00486na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001300005264002400018300002300042500021000065542002800275655002500303655003600328NAFP00aF-Zero X 1bNintendoc2007-6-15  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe fastest racing game in the universe returns! F-Zero X is the stunning Nintendo 64 sequel to the Super Nintendo smash hit, featuring more sound barrier-breaking, gravity-defying action than ever before.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext 7aFuturistic racing games2wiiext00217na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001400005264001400019300002300033500000500056542002100061655002500082NAGJ00aAerogauge 1bASCIIc--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  ikASCIIsGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext01134na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264002400023300002300047500086200070542002800932655002500960655002700985NAHE00aYoshi's Story 1bNintendoc2007-9-17  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe evil Baby Bowser has cast a spell turning Yoshi’s Island into a picture book. Worse yet, the Super Happy Tree has been stolen, making the island dark and gloomy. Players must take control of six Yoshis, each a different color, and travel through six pages (worlds) of platforming adventure to recover the tree and return the island to normal! Featuring huge character models and bright, vibrant colors, the game’s various environments (such as woods, caves, mountains, and oceans) come alive in a uniquely gorgeous 2½-D look. Eat fruit, avoid enemies and obstacles, and throw eggs from the Yoshis’ never-ending supply in your quest to stop Baby Bowser’s plan from succeeding. If you’re good enough, you can aim for higher scores by being picky about the fruit you eat. And who knows, you might even find the mysterious black and white Yoshis!  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00493na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264002500023300002300048500022000071542002800291655002500319655002700344NAHJ00aYoshi's Story 1bNintendoc2007-10-30  a1 Wii optical disc  aBaby Bowser has snatched the Super Happy Tree and cast a spell on Yoshi’s Island, turning it into a picture book! Only six Yoshis remain, so it falls to them to reclaim the tree and restore happiness to the world.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00493na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264002500023300002300048500022000071542002800291655002500319655002700344NAHP00aYoshi's Story 1bNintendoc2007-10-26  a1 Wii optical disc  aBaby Bowser has snatched the Super Happy Tree and cast a spell on Yoshi’s Island, turning it into a picture book! Only six Yoshis remain, so it falls to them to reclaim the tree and restore happiness to the world.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00999na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001700005264002300022300002300045500072000068542002800788655002500816655003600841NAIE00aWave Race 64 1bNintendoc2007-8-6  a1 Wii optical disc  aTake to the waves on your own personal watercraft and experience some of the best water effects in video-game history! Choose one of four characters, each with his/her own unique abilities and style, and master the game’s excellent controls. Make your way through nine courses, each with its own challenges. If the ramps, mines, and hairpin turns aren’t enough, you’ll also have to deal with varying weather conditions that can make the water choppy or cover the course with fog. And if you ever feel like taking a break from racing, then try out Stunt Mode to polish your skills pulling off handstands, rolls, and more! Get good enough and you might even be able to ride a dolphin—just don’t get seasick!  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext 7aWatercraft racing games2wiiext00465na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001700005264002400022300002300046500018500069542002800254655002500282655003600307NAIJ00aWave Race 64 1bNintendoc2007-7-31  a1 Wii optical disc  aOriginally a launch game for Nintendo 64, Wave Race 64 immediately blew the competition out of the water with its impressive 3D graphics and gameplay that was anything but shallow!  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext 7aWatercraft racing games2wiiext00465na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001700005264002400022300002300046500018500069542002800254655002500282655003600307NAIP00aWave Race 64 1bNintendoc2007-8-17  a1 Wii optical disc  aOriginally a launch game for Nintendo 64, Wave Race 64 immediately blew the competition out of the water with its impressive 3D graphics and gameplay that was anything but shallow!  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext 7aWatercraft racing games2wiiext00557na  a2200121   4500001000500000245004100005264002400046300002300070500026300093542002800356655002500384655002600409NAJJ00aTsumi to Batsu - Hoshi no Keishousha 1bNintendoc2007-9-20  a1 Wii optical disc  aEarth is under threat from Ruffians – mutants bred to boost dwindling food stocks who have turned against their masters. As a young resistance fighter, face an onslaught of bio-genetic monsters and corrupt military forces in your battle to save the planet.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00537na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264002400026300002300050500026300073542002800336655002500364655002600389NAJL00aSin & Punishment 1bNintendoc2007-9-28  a1 Wii optical disc  aEarth is under threat from Ruffians – mutants bred to boost dwindling food stocks who have turned against their masters. As a young resistance fighter, face an onslaught of bio-genetic monsters and corrupt military forces in your battle to save the planet.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00537na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264002400026300002300050500026300073542002800336655002500364655002600389NAJN00aSin & Punishment 1bNintendoc2007-10-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aEarth is under threat from Ruffians – mutants bred to boost dwindling food stocks who have turned against their masters. As a young resistance fighter, face an onslaught of bio-genetic monsters and corrupt military forces in your battle to save the planet.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext01082na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264002500023300002300048500084800071542002800919655002500947NAKD00aPokémon Snap 1bNintendoc2007-12-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aAs one of the most unique games in a renowned series, Pokémon Snap was the first truly 3-D Pokémon game and introduced the phenomenon to the Nintendo 64. Travel to Pokémon Island and meet Professor Oak to begin a safari to take the best possible photographs of 63 different Pokémon as they exist in the wild, undisturbed by humans. This is not as easy as it sounds—the island has many types of climates and environments to explore, along with secret activities and hidden passages to discover. Plus, some of the Pokémon can be a little shy and won’t pose for the camera unless you tease them with special items! After you’re done, submit one picture of each Pokémon to Professor Oak, and he’ll judge it based on size, pose, technique, and number of Pokémon captured. Better start practicing if you want to snap the perfect shot!  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00509na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264002500023300002300048500023100071542002800302655002500330655003200355NAKE00aPokémon Snap 1bNintendoc2007-12-10  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn Pokémon Snap, you capture Pokémon not with a Poké Ball but with a camera! As budding young photographer Todd, help Professor Oak research Pokémon by taking pictures of them from your purpose-built vehicle, the ZERO-ONE.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aMultimedia software2wiiext01082na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264002500023300002300048500084800071542002800919655002500947NAKF00aPokémon Snap 1bNintendoc2007-12-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aAs one of the most unique games in a renowned series, Pokémon Snap was the first truly 3-D Pokémon game and introduced the phenomenon to the Nintendo 64. Travel to Pokémon Island and meet Professor Oak to begin a safari to take the best possible photographs of 63 different Pokémon as they exist in the wild, undisturbed by humans. This is not as easy as it sounds—the island has many types of climates and environments to explore, along with secret activities and hidden passages to discover. Plus, some of the Pokémon can be a little shy and won’t pose for the camera unless you tease them with special items! After you’re done, submit one picture of each Pokémon to Professor Oak, and he’ll judge it based on size, pose, technique, and number of Pokémon captured. Better start practicing if you want to snap the perfect shot!  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext01082na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264002500023300002300048500084800071542002800919655002500947NAKI00aPokémon Snap 1bNintendoc2007-12-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aAs one of the most unique games in a renowned series, Pokémon Snap was the first truly 3-D Pokémon game and introduced the phenomenon to the Nintendo 64. Travel to Pokémon Island and meet Professor Oak to begin a safari to take the best possible photographs of 63 different Pokémon as they exist in the wild, undisturbed by humans. This is not as easy as it sounds—the island has many types of climates and environments to explore, along with secret activities and hidden passages to discover. Plus, some of the Pokémon can be a little shy and won’t pose for the camera unless you tease them with special items! After you’re done, submit one picture of each Pokémon to Professor Oak, and he’ll judge it based on size, pose, technique, and number of Pokémon captured. Better start practicing if you want to snap the perfect shot!  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext01081na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264002400023300002300047500084800070542002800918655002500946NAKJ00aPokémon Snap 1bNintendoc2007-12-4  a1 Wii optical disc  aAs one of the most unique games in a renowned series, Pokémon Snap was the first truly 3-D Pokémon game and introduced the phenomenon to the Nintendo 64. Travel to Pokémon Island and meet Professor Oak to begin a safari to take the best possible photographs of 63 different Pokémon as they exist in the wild, undisturbed by humans. This is not as easy as it sounds—the island has many types of climates and environments to explore, along with secret activities and hidden passages to discover. Plus, some of the Pokémon can be a little shy and won’t pose for the camera unless you tease them with special items! After you’re done, submit one picture of each Pokémon to Professor Oak, and he’ll judge it based on size, pose, technique, and number of Pokémon captured. Better start practicing if you want to snap the perfect shot!  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00465na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264002500023300002300048500023100071542002800302655002500330NAKP00aPokémon Snap 1bNintendoc2007-12-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn Pokémon Snap, you capture Pokémon not with a Poké Ball but with a camera! As budding young photographer Todd, help Professor Oak research Pokémon by taking pictures of them from your purpose-built vehicle, the ZERO-ONE.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext01082na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264002500023300002300048500084800071542002800919655002500947NAKS00aPokémon Snap 1bNintendoc2007-12-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aAs one of the most unique games in a renowned series, Pokémon Snap was the first truly 3-D Pokémon game and introduced the phenomenon to the Nintendo 64. Travel to Pokémon Island and meet Professor Oak to begin a safari to take the best possible photographs of 63 different Pokémon as they exist in the wild, undisturbed by humans. This is not as easy as it sounds—the island has many types of climates and environments to explore, along with secret activities and hidden passages to discover. Plus, some of the Pokémon can be a little shy and won’t pose for the camera unless you tease them with special items! After you’re done, submit one picture of each Pokémon to Professor Oak, and he’ll judge it based on size, pose, technique, and number of Pokémon captured. Better start practicing if you want to snap the perfect shot!  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext01043na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002200005264002500027300002300052500080300075542002800878655002700906NALE00aSuper Smash Bros. 1bNintendoc2009-12-21  a1 Wii optical disc  aChoose from an all-star cast of Nintendo characters in a frantic melee to prove who will be the ultimate brawler. Utilize the easy to learn, but hard to master controls to battle it out in the single-player mode, earning point bonuses and unlocking hidden characters along the way, or enter VS Mode to take on up to three other players simultaneously. Inflict damage using each character's unique set of special moves or familiar items and power-ups, eventually winning by knocking your opponents off the screen in one of the interactive stages, each with a Nintendo theme. Need a moment to catch your breath? Polish your skills in Training Mode or destroy targets in Bonus Stages specific to each character. Are you ready to test your mettle against all comers, including the powerful Master Hand?  i2009kNintendosGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00549na  a2200109   4500001000500000245004800005264002400053300002300077500028400100542002800384655002700412NALJ00aNintendo All-Star! Dairantou Smash Brothers 1bNintendoc2009-1-20  a1 Wii optical disc  aSo who's your favourite Nintendo character of all time? Mario? Link? Samus Aran? Maybe Pikachu? All of these and more star in Super Smash Bros. – a riotous 3D fighting game that pits the skills of your best-loved characters against each other in thrilling tournament match-ups!  i2009kNintendosGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00523na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002200005264002400027300002300051500028400074542002800358655002700386NALP00aSuper Smash Bros. 1bNintendoc2009-6-12  a1 Wii optical disc  aSo who's your favourite Nintendo character of all time? Mario? Link? Samus Aran? Maybe Pikachu? All of these and more star in Super Smash Bros. – a riotous 3D fighting game that pits the skills of your best-loved characters against each other in thrilling tournament match-ups!  i2009kNintendosGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00462na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003300005264002400038300002300062500017500085542002800260655002500288655002700313NAME00aKirby 64: The Crystal Shards 1bNintendoc2008-2-25  a1 Wii optical disc  aKirby’s first 3D adventure takes the powerful pink puffball beyond Dream Land and into the stars, as he fights to save his friends from a deadly new enemy: Dark Matter.  i2008kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00451na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002200005264002400027300002300051500017500074542002800249655002500277655002700302NAMJ00aHoshi no Kirby 64 1bNintendoc2008-4-15  a1 Wii optical disc  aKirby’s first 3D adventure takes the powerful pink puffball beyond Dream Land and into the stars, as he fights to save his friends from a deadly new enemy: Dark Matter.  i2008kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00461na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003300005264002300038300002300061500017500084542002800259655002500287655002700312NAMP00aKirby 64: The Crystal Shards 1bNintendoc2008-3-7  a1 Wii optical disc  aKirby’s first 3D adventure takes the powerful pink puffball beyond Dream Land and into the stars, as he fights to save his friends from a deadly new enemy: Dark Matter.  i2008kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00460na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003400005264002100039300002300060500017500083542002800258655002500286655002700311NAMT00aKirby 64 - The Crystal Shards 1bNintendoc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aKirby’s first 3D adventure takes the powerful pink puffball beyond Dream Land and into the stars, as he fights to save his friends from a deadly new enemy: Dark Matter.  i2014kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext01180na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002700005264002400032300002300056500093800079542002801017655002501045NAND00aPokémon Puzzle League 1bNintendoc2008-5-30  a1 Wii optical disc  aGet ready for a new kind of Pokémon battle where the power and speed of your brain are just as important as the strength of your Pokémon! Join Ash, Brock, Misty and many more characters from the Pokémon animated series as they gather in Puzzle Village to compete for the title of Pokémon Puzzle Master. Just match three or more blocks of the same color in any direction. Sounds simple, right? But the actual game-play is surprisingly deep (chains and combos anyone?) and addictive, especially when you’re facing off against a human opponent. Choose from six different modes offering a wide range of action, from a story mode or solving preset puzzles to continuous play or timed play. If that’s not enough, take on the challenge in 3D and get ready for more blocks than ever before. Featuring animated cut scenes combined with bright, fun graphics, there’s enough to satisfy anyone who is a fan of Pokémon or puzzle games!  i2008kNintendosGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00282na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002700005264002300032300002300055500004100078542002800119655002500147NANE00aPokémon Puzzle League 1bNintendoc2008-5-5  a1 Wii optical disc  aGet ready for a new kind of Pokémon  i2008kNintendosGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext01180na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002700005264002400032300002300056500093800079542002801017655002501045NANF00aPokémon Puzzle League 1bNintendoc2008-5-30  a1 Wii optical disc  aGet ready for a new kind of Pokémon battle where the power and speed of your brain are just as important as the strength of your Pokémon! Join Ash, Brock, Misty and many more characters from the Pokémon animated series as they gather in Puzzle Village to compete for the title of Pokémon Puzzle Master. Just match three or more blocks of the same color in any direction. Sounds simple, right? But the actual game-play is surprisingly deep (chains and combos anyone?) and addictive, especially when you’re facing off against a human opponent. Choose from six different modes offering a wide range of action, from a story mode or solving preset puzzles to continuous play or timed play. If that’s not enough, take on the challenge in 3D and get ready for more blocks than ever before. Featuring animated cut scenes combined with bright, fun graphics, there’s enough to satisfy anyone who is a fan of Pokémon or puzzle games!  i2008kNintendosGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00531na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002700005264001700032300002300049500030000072542002400372655002500396NANJ00aPokémon Puzzle League 1bNintendoc--  a1 Wii optical disc  aPut your Pokémon-battling and puzzling skills to the test against the best Trainers in Puzzle League Village! To succeed, you’ll need quick wits and fast fingers to clear puzzle pieces by matching like-coloured blocks. The more pieces you clear at the same time, the more points you'll score.  ikNintendosGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00542na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002700005264002400032300002300056500030000079542002800379655002500407NANP00aPokémon Puzzle League 1bNintendoc2008-5-30  a1 Wii optical disc  aPut your Pokémon-battling and puzzling skills to the test against the best Trainers in Puzzle League Village! To succeed, you’ll need quick wits and fast fingers to clear puzzle pieces by matching like-coloured blocks. The more pieces you clear at the same time, the more points you'll score.  i2008kNintendosGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext01259na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002200005264002400027300002300051500097900074542002801053655002501081655003101106NAOE00a1080 Snowboarding 1bNintendoc2008-1-28  a1 Wii optical disc  aHit the slopes for some serious shredding in one of the first truly realistic snowboarding games ever created! Start in the lodge and select from five characters, each with his/her own particular attributes and special tricks. Then take a look at the wide assortment of available boards and choose one that best suits your rider and style. Once you’ve got the gear, six different modes of play, including Match Race, Trick Attack, and 2-Player Versus, await. Pick a course and get ready to experience a sensation of speed that’ll make you forget all about the cold—but it might just send a shiver down your spine. Throw in hidden characters and boards, varying weather and snow conditions, multiple paths through each course, and a variety of tricks to master—topped off with rock-solid play control—and you’ve got a recipe for winter fun that you can enjoy any time of the year. It’s all the fun and excitement of the sport, without the bruises and frostbite!  i2008kNintendosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aSnowboarding games2wiiext00543na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002200005264002400027300002300051500026300074542002800337655002500365655003100390NAOJ00a1080 Snowboarding 1bNintendoc2008-1-15  a1 Wii optical disc  aPrepare to experience the thrills and chills of the ultimate extreme sport in 1080°: TenEighty Snowboarding. This Nintendo 64 classic offers one of the most accurate yet accessible snowboarding simulations around – all from the warmth of your living room!  i2008kNintendosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aSnowboarding games2wiiext00545na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002400005264002400029300002300053500026300076542002800339655002500367655003100392NAOP00a1080° Snowboarding 1bNintendoc2008-1-18  a1 Wii optical disc  aPrepare to experience the thrills and chills of the ultimate extreme sport in 1080°: TenEighty Snowboarding. This Nintendo 64 classic offers one of the most accurate yet accessible snowboarding simulations around – all from the warmth of your living room!  i2008kNintendosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aSnowboarding games2wiiext00540na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002200005264002100027300002300048500026300071542002800334655002500362655003100387NAOT00a1080 Snowboarding 1bNintendoc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aPrepare to experience the thrills and chills of the ultimate extreme sport in 1080°: TenEighty Snowboarding. This Nintendo 64 classic offers one of the most accurate yet accessible snowboarding simulations around – all from the warmth of your living room!  i2014kNintendosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aSnowboarding games2wiiext00282na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001900005264002400024300002300048500000500071542002800076655002500104655003100129NAPJ00aCustom Robo V2 1bNintendoc2008-2-19  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2008kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00440na  a2200109   4500001000500000245003900005264002400044300002300068500018300091542002800274655002800302NARE04aThe Legend of Zelda: Majora's Mask 1bNintendoc2009-5-18  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe countdown has begun! You have just three days to save the land of Termina from destruction by its own moon, which is being pulled out of its orbit by a mysterious evil force!  i2009kNintendosGameTDB 7aAdventure games2wiiext00476na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003900005264002300044300002300067500018300090542002800273655002500301655002800326NARJ00aZelda no Densetsu: Mujura no Kamen 1bNintendoc2009-4-7  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe countdown has begun! You have just three days to save the land of Termina from destruction by its own moon, which is being pulled out of its orbit by a mysterious evil force!  i2009kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00476na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003900005264002300044300002300067500018300090542002800273655002500301655002800326NARP04aThe Legend of Zelda: Majora's Mask 1bNintendoc2009-4-3  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe countdown has begun! You have just three days to save the land of Termina from destruction by its own moon, which is being pulled out of its orbit by a mysterious evil force!  i2009kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext01189na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001600005264002400021300002300045500095800068542002801026655002501054NASE00aCruis'n USA 1bNintendoc2008-3-31  a1 Wii optical disc  aEver felt like driving to the Golden Gate Bridge, Mount Rushmore, and the White House in one day? Well then, gear up to put your racing skills to the test in a frantic trip across the United States, following a route that you won’t find on any map! Whether it’s the rolling hills of Appalachia, the flowing corn fields of Iowa, or the crowded tunnels below Chicago, you’ll find yourself too focused on the intense racing action to worry about the scenery. Get started by picking from a garage full of cars to find the one that best suits your style—if you’re good enough, you’ll even find a few hidden ones to round out your selection. Then choose one of three different playing perspectives and get ready to hang on tight! With five difficulty levels, the ability to remove traffic or other racers, and two- player simultaneous racing, it’s enough to make you forget all about finding that next rest stop. Just watch out for the cows, OK?  i2008kNintendosGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext00541na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001600005264001700021300002300038500032100061542002400382655002500406NASJ00aCruis'n USA 1bNintendoc--  a1 Wii optical disc  aPut pedal to metal and hang on for a wild ride across the highways of America! Race along LA freeways, across the deserts of Arizona and to the nation’s capital Washington DC, experiencing the thrills of street racing while taking in famous sights like the Golden Gate Bridge, the Grand Canyon and the White House.  ikNintendosGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext00552na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001600005264002400021300002300045500032100068542002800389655002500417NASP00aCruis'n USA 1bNintendoc2008-3-28  a1 Wii optical disc  aPut pedal to metal and hang on for a wild ride across the highways of America! Race along LA freeways, across the deserts of Arizona and to the nation’s capital Washington DC, experiencing the thrills of street racing while taking in famous sights like the Golden Gate Bridge, the Grand Canyon and the White House.  i2008kNintendosGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext01222na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001700005264002400022300002300046500095300069542002801022655002501050655002501075NATE00aMario Tennis 1bNintendoc2010-6-28  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe Mushroom Kingdom welcomes another sport to its lineup in the Nintendo 64 smash, Mario Tennis. In addition to the bright graphics and intuitive, but incredibly tight, controls that all Mario games are known for, a cast of 16 Nintendo characters (including the introduction of Waluigi) is ready to take to the court. Along with the ability to unnerve an opponent by varying shots and precisely target their destination, each character has specific attributes in categories such as speed, power, and control, all of which combines to offer multiple play styles to choose from. A variety of game modes ranging from a standard tournament to the crazy, item-filled Bowser Stage will keep you—and up to three of your friends—running around the court for quite some time. Whether trying to unlock all the secrets in single-player mode or challenging friends with some intense fun in multiplayer mode, this is a game that definitely holds its serve!  i2010kNintendosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aTennis games2wiiext00393na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002000005264002400025300002300049500012100072542002800193655002500221655002500246NATJ00aMario Tennis 64 1bNintendoc2010-8-31  a1 Wii optical disc  aAcclaimed as one of the most addictively fun games on the Nintendo 64, Mario Tennis has returned on Virtual Console!  i2010kNintendosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aTennis games2wiiext00390na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001700005264002400022300002300046500012100069542002800190655002500218655002500243NATP00aMario Tennis 1bNintendoc2010-6-18  a1 Wii optical disc  aAcclaimed as one of the most addictively fun games on the Nintendo 64, Mario Tennis has returned on Virtual Console!  i2010kNintendosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aTennis games2wiiext00971na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001500005264002400020300002300044500070600067542002800773655002500801655002300826NAUE00aMario Golf 1bNintendoc2008-10-6  a1 Wii optical disc  aMario takes a well-deserved break from his role as the Mushroom Kingdom’s busiest hero and returns to the links for some world-class golfing action. Since no one likes to hit the fairways alone, he’s brought along a group of friends—both familiar characters and brand-new ones. Choose from ten different modes of play and six 18-hole courses in a variety of environments for a golfing experience with endless replay value. Add in fun, colorful graphics with a Mario touch (a Boo indicates wind direction), intuitive controls, incredibly deep game play, and multiplayer support (taunt your opponents!), and you have a game anyone will enjoy—even if they’ve never played a round of golf. Fore!  i2008kNintendosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aGolf games2wiiext00476na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264002500023300002300048500020700071542002800278655002500306655002300331NAUJ00aMario Golf 64 1bNintendoc2008-10-30  a1 Wii optical disc  aTee off with Mario and friends as they put a new spin on golf! Choose from 14 different characters, each with their own power and swing styles. You can even taunt opponents to break their concentration!  i2008kNintendosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aGolf games2wiiext00472na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001500005264002400020300002300044500020700067542002800274655002500302655002300327NAUP00aMario Golf 1bNintendoc2009-1-23  a1 Wii optical disc  aTee off with Mario and friends as they put a new spin on golf! Choose from 14 different characters, each with their own power and swing styles. You can even taunt opponents to break their concentration!  i2009kNintendosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aGolf games2wiiext01102na  a2200109   4500001000500000245004500005264002700050300002300077500083000100542003100930655003100961NAYE00aOgre Battle 64: Person of Lordly Caliber 1bSquare Enixc2010-3-29  a1 Wii optical disc  aOgre Battle 64: Person of Lordly Caliber is a tactical RPG originally released for the Nintendo 64 system. Featuring a gripping storyline with multiple possible endings, and a genre-defining character class system, this strategic epic has rightly retained its place in the hearts of tactical RPG fans for over a decade. The game tells the story of Magnus Gallant, a recently graduated officer of the Palatinean Army who is assigned to the troubled southern region of his native land. There he witnesses the plight of the lower classes – the victims of a tyrannical ruling elite whose only thought is for the preservation of their own lofty status. With civil war brewing, Magnus is faced with a terrible choice: to betray his own noble origins in the name of liberty, or turn a blind eye to the evils of his rotten society.  i2010kSquare EnixsGameTDB 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00609na  a2200121   4500001000500000245004600005264002700051300002300078500029700101542003100398655003100429655002700460NAYJ00aOgre Battle 64 - Person of Lordly Caliber 1bSquare Enixc2010-1-26  a1 Wii optical disc  aOgre Battle 64: Person of Lordly Caliber is a tactical RPG for the Nintendo 64. Featuring a gripping storyline with multiple possible endings, and a genre-defining character class system, this strategic epic has rightly retained its place in the hearts of tactical RPG fans for over a decade.  i2010kSquare EnixsGameTDB 7aRole-playing games2wiiext 7aStrategy games2wiiext00608na  a2200121   4500001000500000245004500005264002700050300002300077500029700100542003100397655003100428655002700459NAYM00aOgre Battle 64: Person of Lordly Caliber 1bSquare Enixc2010-3-26  a1 Wii optical disc  aOgre Battle 64: Person of Lordly Caliber is a tactical RPG for the Nintendo 64. Featuring a gripping storyline with multiple possible endings, and a genre-defining character class system, this strategic epic has rightly retained its place in the hearts of tactical RPG fans for over a decade.  i2010kSquare EnixsGameTDB 7aRole-playing games2wiiext 7aStrategy games2wiiext00779na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264002500023300002300048500050900071542002800580655002500608655002400633NAZE00aMario Party 2 1bNintendoc2010-12-20  a1 Wii optical disc  aGet ready to party like it’s the year 2000 all over again, complete with fancy costumes, bags of surprises, and games galore! Mario and his Mushroom Kingdom friends return for a brand-new round of Bowser-bashing board game action in Mario Party 2. Each of your favorite characters don different themed outfits to take part in five fun-packed Adventure Boards: Pirate Land, Western Land, Space Land, Mystery Land, and Horror Land. Then battle Bowser on his own specific board...if you’re brave enough.  i2010kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aParty games2wiiext00777na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264002400023300002300047500050900070542002800579655002400607655002400631NAZJ00aMario Party 2 1bNintendoc2010-11-2  a1 Wii optical disc  aGet ready to party like it’s the year 2000 all over again, complete with fancy costumes, bags of surprises, and games galore! Mario and his Mushroom Kingdom friends return for a brand-new round of Bowser-bashing board game action in Mario Party 2. Each of your favorite characters don different themed outfits to take part in five fun-packed Adventure Boards: Pirate Land, Western Land, Space Land, Mystery Land, and Horror Land. Then battle Bowser on his own specific board...if you’re brave enough.  i2010kNintendosGameTDB 7aParty games2wiiext 7aBoard games2wiiext00778na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264002500023300002300048500050900071542002800580655002400608655002400632NAZP00aMario Party 2 1bNintendoc2010-12-24  a1 Wii optical disc  aGet ready to party like it’s the year 2000 all over again, complete with fancy costumes, bags of surprises, and games galore! Mario and his Mushroom Kingdom friends return for a brand-new round of Bowser-bashing board game action in Mario Party 2. Each of your favorite characters don different themed outfits to take part in five fun-packed Adventure Boards: Pirate Land, Western Land, Space Land, Mystery Land, and Horror Land. Then battle Bowser on his own specific board...if you’re brave enough.  i2010kNintendosGameTDB 7aParty games2wiiext 7aBoard games2wiiext00180na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001800005264001300023300002300036500000500059542001800064LAAJ00aHokuto no Ken 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00842na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001700005264003100022300002300053500059600076542003500672655002500707LABE00aFantasy Zone 1bSEGA of Americac2008-4-14  a1 Wii optical disc  aTake command of the spaceship Opa-Opa and blast your way through various fantastical levels as you try to take out all the enemy bases in each stage. Once you’ve destroyed the bases, you’ll have to beat the stage boss in order to move on to the next level. By using your guns and bombs wisely, you’ll be able to take down your enemies and explore each of the crazy environments in this side-scroller. You can also buy upgraded weapons for your ship by accessing the shop. Various SEGA games through the years have referenced the Opa-Opa—now you can play the game that started it all!  i2008kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aArcade games2wiiext00520na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001700005264001700022300002300039500026100062542002400323655002500347655002600372LABJ00aFantasy Zone 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aTake command of the spaceship Opa-Opa and blast your way through various fantastical levels as you try to take out all the enemy bases in each stage. Once you've destroyed the bases, you'll have to beat the stage boss in order to move on to the next level.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00523na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001700005264002000022300002300042500026100065542002400326655002500350655002600375LABP00aFantasy Zone 1bSegac2008-4-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aTake command of the spaceship Opa-Opa and blast your way through various fantastical levels as you try to take out all the enemy bases in each stage. Once you've destroyed the bases, you'll have to beat the stage boss in order to move on to the next level.  i2008kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00898na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001500005264003100020300002300051500065100074542003500725655002800760LACE00aWonder Boy 1bSEGA of Americac2008-3-31  a1 Wii optical disc  aAs Tom-Tom the Wonder Boy, it’s up to you to rescue your girlfriend, Tanya, from the vile clutches of the monster that has kidnapped her. To do so, you must navigate through a series of worlds in a race against time to reach your goal. Along the way, you’ll battle foes and collect fruit that will add to the amount of time you have to complete your mission. You can also receive helpful power-ups from various eggs, but make sure to avoid the bad eggs and poisonous mushrooms that sap your precious vitality. Find the magic doll in each level to open up hidden areas, and make it to the very end of your journey to rescue your one true love!  i2008kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAdventure games2wiiext00496na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264001700026300002300043500023200066542002400298655002500322655002700347LACJ00aSuper Wonder Boy 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aAs Tom-Tom the Wonder Boy, it’s up to you to rescue your girlfriend Tanya from the vile clutches of the monster that has kidnapped her. To do so, you must navigate a series of worlds in a race against time to reach your goal.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00493na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001500005264002000020300002300040500023200063542002400295655002500319655002700344LACP00aWonder Boy 1bSegac2008-4-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aAs Tom-Tom the Wonder Boy, it’s up to you to rescue your girlfriend Tanya from the vile clutches of the monster that has kidnapped her. To do so, you must navigate a series of worlds in a race against time to reach your goal.  i2008kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00835na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264003100023300002300054500058200077542003500659655003100694LADE00aPhantasy Star 1bSEGA of Americac2009-8-31  a1 Wii optical disc  aOriginally released on the Sega Master System, Phantasy Star is a pioneer in the role-playing game genre. Relive this classic, where you play as Alis, the fearless female protoganist out to avenge her brother's death by the cruel dictator King Lassic. Guide Alis and her troop through the sprawling environments of the Agol solar system, in an attempt to defeat King Lassic and liberate the people of Agol. Engage in dynamic turn-based combat with dragons, ghouls, giants, and magicians by using unique weapons such as glowing daggers, crossbows, and of course... magic spells.  i2009kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00353na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264001700023300002300040500012500063542002400188655003100212LADJ00aPhantasy Star 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aOriginally released on the SEGA MASTER SYSTEM, Phantasy Star was and still is, a pioneer of the role-playing game genre.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00356na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264002000023300002300043500012500066542002400191655003100215LADP00aPhantasy Star 1bSegac2009-8-14  a1 Wii optical disc  aOriginally released on the SEGA MASTER SYSTEM, Phantasy Star was and still is, a pioneer of the role-playing game genre.  i2009kSegasGameTDB 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00798na  a2200109   4500001000500000245003100005264003100036300002300067500053500090542003500625655002800660LAEE00aAlex Kidd in Miracle World 1bSEGA of Americac2008-6-23  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn this platformer from the 1980s, you’re Alex Kidd, looking for your lost brother Egle. In order to find your brother, you’ll have to contend with the evil Janken the Great, who will send his henchmen and monsters at you to thwart your progress. One aspect of this adventure is that you’ll have to play the classic game of “rock, paper, scissors” against the henchmen in order to defeat them. With 16 different levels to conquer in order to save Egle, this classic is sure to test your skills and wits at the same time!  i2008kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAdventure games2wiiext00525na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003100005264001700036300002300053500025100076542002400327655002500351655002700376LAEJ00aAlex Kidd no Miracle World 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn this platformer from the 1980s, you're Alex Kidd, looking for your lost brother Egle. In order to find your brother, you'll have to contend with the evil Janken the Great, who will send his henchmen and monsters at you to thwart your progress.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00528na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003100005264002000036300002300056500025100079542002400330655002500354655002700379LAEP00aAlex Kidd in Miracle World 1bSegac2008-6-13  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn this platformer from the 1980s, you're Alex Kidd, looking for your lost brother Egle. In order to find your brother, you'll have to contend with the evil Janken the Great, who will send his henchmen and monsters at you to thwart your progress.  i2008kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00438na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001100005264001700016300002300033500018300056542002400239655002500263655002800288LAFJ00aAshura 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aWhether you recognise this game by its US title (Rambo: First Blood II) or its European title of Secret Command, this SEGA MASTER SYSTEM classic lives on through Virtual Console!  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00867na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001900005264003100024300002300055500058100078542003500659655002500694655002600719LAFN00aSecret Command 1bSEGA of Americac2009-7-13  a1 Wii optical disc  aPlay as a lone warrior, armed to the teeth, sent on a top-secret commando mission behind enemy lines to liberate your comrades at arms. Released on the SEGA Master System in Europe as Secret Command, players will battle frenzied attacks from enemy soldiers, rocket troops, tanks, and other enemies doing everything they can to stop you from saving the hostages. Use your trusty machine gun and a compound bow, equipped with explosive-tipped arrows, to pave the way to victory. Let nothing stand in your path! Play it with a friend in two-player mode for double the fire power!  i2009kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00449na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001900005264002000024300002300044500018300067542002400250655002500274655002800299LAFP00aSecret Command 1bSegac2009-4-17  a1 Wii optical disc  aWhether you recognise this game by its US title (Rambo: First Blood II) or its European title of Secret Command, this SEGA MASTER SYSTEM classic lives on through Virtual Console!  i2009kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00423na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002300005264003000028300002300058500013300081542003500214655002500249655002700274LAGE00aSonic The Hedgehog 1bSEGA of Americac2008-8-4  a1 Wii optical disc  aGet ready for a second helping of the original Sonic the Hedgehog with the SEGA MASTER SYSTEM remake of Sonic's debut adventure!  i2008kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00399na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002300005264001700028300002300045500013300068542002400201655002500225655002700250LAGJ00aSonic The Hedgehog 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aGet ready for a second helping of the original Sonic The Hedgehog with the SEGA MASTER SYSTEM remake of Sonic's debut adventure!  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00402na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002300005264002000028300002300048500013300071542002400204655002500228655002700253LAGP00aSonic The Hedgehog 1bSegac2008-9-19  a1 Wii optical disc  aGet ready for a second helping of the original Sonic The Hedgehog with the SEGA MASTER SYSTEM remake of Sonic's debut adventure!  i2008kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00807na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264003100023300002300054500056000077542003500637655002500672LAHE00aSpace Harrier 1bSEGA of Americac2008-11-3  a1 Wii optical disc  aSpace Harrier was originally released in the arcade in the 1980s, developed by AM2, which also developed OutRun and Afterburner. Space Harrier is widely recognizable by many arcade fans due to its distinctive, colorful art design and its fast-paced action. The SEGA Master System version is considered a solid port of the arcade game, containing 18 levels of intense fun. As the "Space Harrier," you must fight your way through "The Land of Dragons" and defeat the bosses at the end of each level to restore peace to the land. Are you prepared? Get ready!  i2008kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aArcade games2wiiext00539na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264001700023300002300040500027900063542002400342655002500366655002600391LAHJ00aSpace Harrier 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aSpace Harrier was originally released in arcades during the 1980s and was developed by AM2, which also developed OutRun and Afterburner. With its distinctive, colourful graphics and its fast-paced action, Space Harrier is widely recognisable to arcade fans across the world!  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00543na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264002100023300002300044500027900067542002400346655002500370655002600395LAHP00aSpace Harrier 1bSegac2008-10-17  a1 Wii optical disc  aSpace Harrier was originally released in arcades during the 1980s and was developed by AM2, which also developed OutRun and Afterburner. With its distinctive, colourful graphics and its fast-paced action, Space Harrier is widely recognisable to arcade fans across the world!  i2008kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00810na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001700005264003200022300002300054500056300077542003500640655002500675LAIE00aEnduro Racer 1bSEGA of Americac2008-11-15  a1 Wii optical disc  aEnduro Racer, based off the popular SEGA arcade game and redesigned for the SEGA Master System, takes you on an intense set of adrenaline-designed courses containing diverse and rough terrain that will test your skills and reaction times to the limits. Ride as fast as you can to pass as many cars and bikes as possible while also avoiding obstacles and pitfalls such as debris on the road. Take jumps off of ramps and try to keep your speed up, but make sure to keep an eye on your bike so it doesn’t blow up in your face! Are you ready for the challenge?  i2008kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext00462na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001700005264001900022300002300041500023900064542002400303655002500327LAIJ00aEnduro Racer 1bSegac2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aBased on the popular SEGA arcade game and redesigned for the SEGA MASTER SYSTEM, Enduro Racer takes you on an intense journey of adrenaline through diverse and rough terrain that will test your skills and reaction times to the limits!  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext00463na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001700005264002000022300002300042500023900065542002400304655002500328LAIP00aEnduro Racer 1bSegac2009-1-12  a1 Wii optical disc  aBased on the popular SEGA arcade game and redesigned for the SEGA MASTER SYSTEM, Enduro Racer takes you on an intense journey of adrenaline through diverse and rough terrain that will test your skills and reaction times to the limits!  i2009kSegasGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext00432na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002500005264003100030300002300061500017800084542003500262655002500297LAJE00aSonic The Hedgehog 2 1bSEGA of Americac2008-12-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aPlay the popular sequel to Sonic the Hedgehog, made specifically for the SEGA MASTER SYSTEM, which saw the cameo debut of Miles "Tails" Prower, Sonic's high-flying sidekick!  i2008kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00446na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002500005264001700030300002300047500017800070542002400248655002500272655002700297LAJJ00aSonic The Hedgehog 2 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aPlay the popular sequel to Sonic The Hedgehog, made specifically for the SEGA MASTER SYSTEM, which saw the cameo debut of Miles "Tails" Prower, Sonic's high-flying sidekick!  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00450na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002500005264002100030300002300051500017800074542002400252655002500276655002700301LAJP00aSonic The Hedgehog 2 1bSegac2008-12-26  a1 Wii optical disc  aPlay the popular sequel to Sonic The Hedgehog, made specifically for the SEGA MASTER SYSTEM, which saw the cameo debut of Miles "Tails" Prower, Sonic's high-flying sidekick!  i2008kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00976na  a2200109   4500001000500000245003100005264003100036300002300067500071600090542003500806655002500841LAKE00aWonder Boy in Monster Land 1bSEGA of Americac2009-1-26  a1 Wii optical disc  aAfter the defeat of the evil king, the kingdom of Wonder Land was a paradise...for a time. The peace was broken when a ferocious fire-breathing dragon struck without warning and took over Wonder Land with a swarm of evil, monstrous henchmen, turning the once-peaceful land into one of utter chaos; turning it into Monster Land. Unable to fight, the people looked to Wonder Boy. Realizing that he was Wonder Land’s last hope, Wonder Boy set out on an incredible journey to rid the country of the monsters and to ultimately defeat the “invincible” evil dragon. Guide Wonder Boy through various environments and dungeons and defeat enemies, using Special Weapons and Spells during the course of your journey!  i2009kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00624na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003700005264001900042300002300061500034200084542002400426655002500450655002700475LAKJ00aSuper Wonder Boy - Monster World 1bSegac2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aAfter the evil King was defeated, the kingdom of Wonder Land was a paradise... for a time. Then the peace was broken when a ferocious, fire-breathing dragon struck without warning and took over Wonder Land with a swarm of evil, monstrous henchmen - turning the once peaceful land into one of utter chaos. Wonder Land became Monster Land.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00619na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003100005264002000036300002300056500034200079542002400421655002500445655002700470LAKP00aWonder Boy in Monster Land 1bSegac2009-1-23  a1 Wii optical disc  aAfter the evil King was defeated, the kingdom of Wonder Land was a paradise... for a time. Then the peace was broken when a ferocious, fire-breathing dragon struck without warning and took over Wonder Land with a swarm of evil, monstrous henchmen - turning the once peaceful land into one of utter chaos. Wonder Land became Monster Land.  i2009kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00756na  a2200121   4500001000500000245004300005264003100048300002300079500044600102542003500548655002500583655002600608LALE00aFantasy Zone II - The Tears of Opa-Opa 1bSEGA of Americac2009-6-29  a1 Wii optical disc  aTen years have elapsed since Opa-Opa restored peace to the Fantasy Zone™. Now history is repeating itself, and the planets that make up the Fantasy Zone once again find themselves attacked by the mastermind of the Nenon planet forces. This mastermind is secretly constructing a huge fortress in the Fantasy Zone and aims to put an end to their ambitious plans. Just as he did ten years ago, Opa-Opa must do battle to save the Fantasy Zone!  i2009kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00450na  a2200121   4500001000500000245004000005264001700045300002300062500016800085542002400253655002500277655002600302LALJ00aFantasy Zone II - Opa-Opa no Namida 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a10 years have passed since Opa-Opa restored peace to the "Fantasy Zone". Now history is repeating itself and the Fantasy Zone once again finds itself under attack!  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00455na  a2200121   4500001000500000245004300005264001900048300002300067500016800090542002400258655002500282655002600307LALP00aFantasy Zone II - The Tears of Opa-Opa 1bSegac2009-5-8  a1 Wii optical disc  a10 years have passed since Opa-Opa restored peace to the "Fantasy Zone". Now history is repeating itself and the Fantasy Zone once again finds itself under attack!  i2009kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00377na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001600005264003000021300002300051500013300074542003500207655002500242LAME00aSonic Chaos 1bSEGA of Americac2009-2-2  a1 Wii optical disc  aPlay as Sonic or Tails in Sonic Chaos - the first 8-bit Sonic title to feature his loyal sidekick Tails as a playable character!  i2009kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00392na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001600005264001700021300002300038500013300061542002400194655002500218655002700243LAMJ00aSonic Chaos 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aPlay as Sonic or Tails in Sonic Chaos - the first 8-bit Sonic title to feature his loyal sidekick Tails as a playable character!  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00394na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001600005264001900021300002300040500013300063542002400196655002500220655002700245LAMP00aSonic Chaos 1bSegac2009-2-6  a1 Wii optical disc  aPlay as Sonic or Tails in Sonic Chaos - the first 8-bit Sonic title to feature his loyal sidekick Tails as a playable character!  i2009kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00557na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003100005264003000036300002300066500025900089542003500348655002500383655002700408LANE00aAlex Kidd - The Lost Stars 1bSEGA of Americac2009-3-9  a1 Wii optical disc  aRejoin Alex Kidd in this platformer from the 1980s. Help Alex in a race against time to find the twelve missing zodiac signs hidden in six challenging levels including toyland, the robot factory, and an outer-space level, all complete with crazy enemies.  i2009kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00608na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003100005264001700036300002300053500033400076542002400410655002500434655002700459LANJ00aAlex Kidd - The Lost Stars 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aRejoin the heroic Alex Kidd in this platformer from the 1980s! Race against time to recover the twelve Miracle Balls and restore the stars of the Aries Constellation! This title features twelve fast-paced rounds in six challenging levels, including a toy land, robot factory and even outer space, all complete with crazy enemies!  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00611na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003100005264002000036300002300056500033400079542002400413655002500437655002700462LANP00aAlex Kidd - The Lost Stars 1bSegac2009-4-17  a1 Wii optical disc  aRejoin the heroic Alex Kidd in this platformer from the 1980s! Race against time to recover the twelve Miracle Balls and restore the stars of the Aries Constellation! This title features twelve fast-paced rounds in six challenging levels, including a toy land, robot factory and even outer space, all complete with crazy enemies!  i2009kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00782na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001100005264002000016300002300036500052600059542002400585655002500609655002600634LAOE00aR-Type 1bIREMc2009-11-2  a1 Wii optical disc  aR-TYPE is a classic side-scrolling arcade shoot-em up that was developed by Irem in 1987. The game takes place in the 22nd century and you are humanity’s last hope against the evil Bydo Empire. Your ship is called the R-9a “Arrowhead” and it comes with a standard gun, but power ups and upgrades are available in each mission. Navigate through eight challenging levels that will test even the best gamer’s reflexes. The Sega Master System version features an exclusive secret level not found in any other release.  i2009kIREMsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00614na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001100005264001700016300002300033500036100056542002400417655002500441655002600466LAOJ00aR-Type 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis classic side-scrolling arcade shoot-em up developed by Irem, takes place in the 22nd century where you are humanity’s last hope against the evil Bydo Empire. Your ship, the R-9a “Arrowhead”, comes equipped with nothing but a standard laser but never fear! Power-ups and upgrades are available in each mission to keep you fighting the good fight.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00617na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001100005264002000016300002300036500036100059542002400420655002500444655002600469LAOP00aR-Type 1bSegac2009-9-29  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis classic side-scrolling arcade shoot-em up developed by Irem, takes place in the 22nd century where you are humanity’s last hope against the evil Bydo Empire. Your ship, the R-9a “Arrowhead”, comes equipped with nothing but a standard laser but never fear! Power-ups and upgrades are available in each mission to keep you fighting the good fight.  i2009kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00936na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003900005264003100044300002300075500062200098542003500720655002800755655003100783LAPE00aWonder Boy III - The Dragon's Trap 1bSEGA of Americac2009-11-9  a1 Wii optical disc  aWonder Boy III The Dragon’s Trap is widely considered among the best games produced for the Sega Master System, featuring some of the best animations of its time during the original release. Wonder Boy III The Dragon’s Trap is the direct sequel to Wonder Boy in Monster Land, starting in the final lair of the previous game. This game is the first in the series to allow Wonder Boy to roam freely by using various animal forms, but much like previous games in the series, Wonder Boy can also buy various weapons, armor, and items to help him in his quest. Add this gem to your Sega Master System collection today!  i2009kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAdventure games2wiiext 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00780na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003900005264002000044300002300064500049500087542002400582655002500606655002700631LAPP00aWonder Boy III - The Dragon's Trap 1bSegac2009-10-9  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe once quiet town of Xenobia is under attack by fierce, gruesome monsters and no one can stop them! As Leo, it is up to you to save Xenobia and the world from danger as you navigate through several rounds in a race against time to reach your goal. Battle foes with your sword and jumping abilities. Look out for power ups that will increase your health and add to the amount of time you have left to complete each mission. Play alone or with a friend, who will take the role of Priscilla.  i2009kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00844na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003100005264003000036300002300066500054600089542003500635655002500670655002700695LAQE00aAlex Kidd in Shinobi World 1bSEGA of Americac2010-2-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aWhat do you get when you combine the two monumental Sega classics Alex Kidd in Miracle World and Shinobi? Alex Kidd in Shinobi World of course! Though never released in Japan, this game has it all: Alex Kidd, kidnapped princesses, evil Dark Ninjas – and of course it’s all played to a rockin’ remixed Shinobi sound track. Run, jump, swim and slash your way through twelve stages, teeming with monstrous foes from the world of Shinobi, and some more lighthearted ones from Alex Kidd. Just don’t let the barracudas turn you into sushi!  i2010kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00426na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003100005264002100036300002300057500014800080542002400228655002500252655002700277LAQP00aAlex Kidd in Shinobi World 1bSegac2009-12-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aWhat do you get when you combine the two monumental SEGA classics Alex Kidd in Miracle World and Shinobi? Alex Kidd in Shinobi World of course!  i2009kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00180na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001800005264001300023300002300036500000500059542001800064MA2J00aDyna Brothers 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00874na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001600005264003100021300002300052500062900075542003500704655002500739MA3E00aPuyo Puyo 2 1bSEGA of Americac2008-3-10  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe object of this head-to-head puzzle game is to clear your grid of falling patterns, called puyos, by forming chains of four or more same-colored puyos in a straight line or one of several geometric patterns. What makes this a challenging two-player contest is the fact that when you clear a chain of puyos from your grid, it drops a random piece of filler onto your opponent’s grid. The more puyos you clear, the more you fill your opponent’s grid, and if you can clutter up his grid enough to fill it to the top, you’ve won the game. An intriguing backstory makes this an amusing experience for one or two players.  i2008kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00433na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001600005264001700021300002300038500021300061542002400274655002500298MA3J00aPuyo Puyo 2 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe object of this head-to-head puzzle game is to clear your grid of falling patterns called puyos by forming chains of four or more same-colored puyos in a straight line or one of several geometric patterns.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00435na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001600005264001900021300002300040500021300063542002400276655002500300MA3L00aPuyo Puyo 2 1bSegac2008-5-9  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe object of this head-to-head puzzle game is to clear your grid of falling patterns called puyos by forming chains of four or more same-colored puyos in a straight line or one of several geometric patterns.  i2008kSegasGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00180na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001800005264001300023300002300036500000500059542001800064MA4J00aBahamut Senki 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00178na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001600005264001300021300002300034500000500057542001800062MA5J00aRent A Hero 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00956na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002200005264003100027300002300058500066500081542003500746655002500781655002800806MA6E00aStreets of Rage 2 1bSEGA of Americac2007-5-21  a1 Wii optical disc  aTo celebrate their defeat of the Syndicate exactly one year before, Blaze, Adam and Axel met for drinks. The next morning, Axel received a frantic phone call from Eddie "Skate" Hunter, Adam's younger brother, whom he was living with on the edge of the city. Blaze and Axel found Adam and Skate's house wrecked, and a picture showing Adam chained up at the feet of Mr. X. The city then once again returned to its nightmarish state as criminals ran rampant. Unable to contact their old friend in artillery, Axel and Blaze team up with Skate and Max Thunder to free the city and rescue Adam from the Syndicate. It is up to you to take down Mr. X once and for all.  i2007kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00586na  a2200133   4500001000500000245004500005264001700050300002300067500025600090542002400346655002500370655002700395655003000422MA6J00aBare Knuckle II - Shitou he no Chinkonka 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aChoose one of four warriors and slam your enemies to the concrete with dazzling martial arts moves! Bash 'em with pipes or slash 'em with knives and ninja weapons! Get ready for the hottest street combat ever as once more you walk the Streets of Rage!  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext00565na  a2200133   4500001000500000245002200005264001900027300002300046500025600069542002400325655002500349655002700374655003000401MA6P00aStreets of Rage 2 1bSegac2007-6-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aChoose one of four warriors and slam your enemies to the concrete with dazzling martial arts moves! Bash 'em with pipes or slash 'em with knives and ninja weapons! Get ready for the hottest street combat ever as once more you walk the Streets of Rage!  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext00897na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002800005264003100033300002300064500063400087542003500721655003100756MA7E00aShining in the Darkness 1bSEGA of Americac2007-8-13  a1 Wii optical disc  aDark Sol has vowed to reign over the enchanted Kingdom of Thornwood, and only you can stop him. Find the powerful Arms of Light and battle the deadly beasts that keep your people desperate and starving in this epic journey for peace. Roaming the dark Labyrinth, you'll seek out enemies and collect weapons, all of which will help you pass the test of the Ancients and become a shining knight. Get into the adventure with a stunning 3-D perspective, amazing cinematic views and fast-paced scrolling. You'll move from battle to battle, solving puzzles and discovering secret items in this engrossing struggle between good and evil.  i2007kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00360na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002100005264001700026300002300043500012900066542002400195655003100219MA7J00aShining Darkness 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe King of Thornwood is beside himself with worry. His daughter and his most trustworthy knight, Mortred, have disappeared.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00369na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002800005264001900033300002300052500012900075542002400204655003100228MA7P00aShining in the Darkness 1bSegac2007-9-7  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe King of Thornwood is beside himself with worry. His daughter and his most trustworthy knight, Mortred, have disappeared.  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00857na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002900005264003000034300002300064500059700087542003500684655002800719MA8E00aEcco - The Tides of Time 1bSEGA of Americac2007-7-2  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn this sequel to Ecco the Dolphin, everyone’s favorite underwater hero must battle the Vortex Queen and her hive of drones. The wicked queen followed Ecco back to Earth from the future and quickly established her hive. It's up to Ecco to defeat this alien threat by navigating the depths of his side-scrolling world, solving puzzles, and receiving help from his marine-mammal friends. When Ecco used the time machine to save his pod, he split the stream of time in two. He must now restore the rift before the world is permanently changed into a mechanical world, sucked dry by the Vortex!  i2007kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAdventure games2wiiext00457na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002300005264001700028300002300045500019000068542002400258655002500282655002800307MA8J00aEcco the Dolphin 2 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe evil Vortex has returned and Ecco faces a dangerous adventure. With help from the beautiful Trellia, guide Ecco through over 25 levels of aquatic action including amazing 3D scenes.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00465na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002900005264001900034300002300053500019000076542002400266655002500290655002800315MA8P00aEcco - The Tides of Time 1bSegac2007-7-6  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe evil Vortex has returned and Ecco faces a dangerous adventure. With help from the beautiful Trellia, guide Ecco through over 25 levels of aquatic action including amazing 3D scenes.  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00183na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002100005264001300026300002300039500000500062542001800067MA9J04aThe Hybrid Front 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00296na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264003200023300002300055500004800078542003500126655002500161MAAE00aAltered Beast 1bSEGA of Americac2006-11-19  a1 Wii optical disc  aA pawn of the gods shall rise against Neff.  i2006kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aArcade games2wiiext00577na  a2200133   4500001000500000245002800005264001700033300002300050500026400073542002400337655002500361655002700386655003000413MAAJ00aJuuouki - Altered Beast 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aEnter a time when men were warriors and Gods ruled the world. A time of good against evil, a place of danger. Summoned by Zeus to rescue Athena, you will infiltrate the Underworld with the power to transform into mythical creatures with supernatural strenght.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext00570na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001800005264002000023300002300043500026400066542002400330655002500354655002700379655003000406MAAP00aAltered Beast 1bSegac2006-12-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aEnter a time when men were warriors and Gods ruled the world. A time of good against evil, a place of danger. Summoned by Zeus to rescue Athena, you will infiltrate the Underworld with the power to transform into mythical creatures with supernatural strenght.  i2006kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext00298na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001200005264003100017300002300048500005700071542003500128655002500163MABE00aColumns 1bSEGA of Americac2006-12-4  a1 Wii optical disc  aSega's classic puzzle game comes to Virtual Console.  i2006kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00434na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001200005264001700017300002300034500021800057542002400275655002500299MABJ00aColumns 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aDrift back to ancient Phoenicia and challenge yourself with Columns, a game favored by ancient merchants. In this mesmerizing pastime, tinker with your riches to align glittering jewels across, down or diagonally.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00437na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001200005264002000017300002300037500021800060542002400278655002500302MABP00aColumns 1bSegac2006-12-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aDrift back to ancient Phoenicia and challenge yourself with Columns, a game favored by ancient merchants. In this mesmerizing pastime, tinker with your riches to align glittering jewels across, down or diagonally.  i2006kSegasGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00324na  a2200109   4500001000500000245003700005264003200042300002300074500005700097542003500154655002500189MACE00aDr. Robotnik's Mean Bean Machine 1bSEGA of Americac2006-12-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aConnect the colors and pop Dr. Robotnik's evil plans  i2006kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00466na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001400005264001700019300002300036500024800059542002400307655002500331MACJ00aPuyo Puyo 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aYou have to stay calm and think fast to win this highly addictive puzzle game. Play against the timer. Challenge a friend. Or use strategy to battle Dr. Robotnik's wiliest robot minions and save the citizens of Beanville from a horrible fate !  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00492na  a2200109   4500001000500000245003700005264002000042300002300062500024800085542002400333655002500357MACP00aDr. Robotnik's Mean Bean Machine 1bSegac2006-12-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aYou have to stay calm and think fast to win this highly addictive puzzle game. Play against the timer. Challenge a friend. Or use strategy to battle Dr. Robotnik's wiliest robot minions and save the citizens of Beanville from a horrible fate !  i2006kSegasGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00511na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002100005264003200026300002300058500025700081542003500338655002800373MADE00aEcco the Dolphin 1bSEGA of Americac2006-11-27  a1 Wii optical disc  aHelp Ecco the dolphin find his missing friends by exploring his vast ocean world. You must surface for air and keep an eye out for enemies as you search the depths. Ecco's unique sonar ability will give you helpful information from other sea creatures.  i2006kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAdventure games2wiiext00469na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264001700026300002300043500020400066542002400270655002500294655002800319MADJ00aEcco the Dolphin 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aYou are Ecco, a powerful young dolphin. A mysterious storm has swept your family from the sea. The search to find them will take you through vast underwater realms of treachery, beauty and adventure.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00472na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264002000026300002300046500020400069542002400273655002500297655002800322MADP00aEcco the Dolphin 1bSegac2006-12-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aYou are Ecco, a powerful young dolphin. A mysterious storm has swept your family from the sea. The search to find them will take you through vast underwater realms of treachery, beauty and adventure.  i2006kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00578na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001500005264003200020300002300052500029300075542003500368655002500403655002800428MAEE00aGolden Axe 1bSEGA of Americac2006-11-28  a1 Wii optical disc  aThree mighty heroes have a score to settle with the evil Death Adder in this classic action game. As a powerful fighter, a female amazon, or a mighty dwarf, you'll fight through Adder's henchman with weapon and magic attacks, or ride the fearsome, fire-breathing beasts to your advantage.  i2006kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00368na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001900005264001700024300002300041500006400064542002400128655002500152655002700177655003000204MAEJ04aThe Golden Axe 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn Turtle Village the children are fleeing for their lives!  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext00367na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001500005264002000020300002300040500006400063542002400127655002500151655002700176655003000203MAEP00aGolden Axe 1bSegac2006-12-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn Turtle Village the children are fleeing for their lives!  i2006kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext00630na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001900005264003200024300002300056500034300079542003500422655002500457655002600482MAFE00aGunstar Heroes 1bSEGA of Americac2006-12-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe Gunstar 9 planet was peaceful for many years until the vicious dictator, Colonel Red, kidnapped the Gunstar twins' older brother and used mind control to make him his slave. Players face many different enemies and bosses while battling to stop the dictator from unleashing "Golden Silver the Destructor" with apocalyptic consequences.  i2006kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00390na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001900005264001700024300002300041500016700064542002400231655002500255MAFJ00aGunstar Heroes 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aColonel Red and his Empire army have decided to steal the Mystical Gems and power up the Destructor, a robot that almost destroyed the planet Gunstar 9 years ago.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00393na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001900005264002000024300002300044500016700067542002400234655002500258MAFP00aGunstar Heroes 1bSegac2006-12-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aColonel Red and his Empire army have decided to steal the Mystical Gems and power up the Destructor, a robot that almost destroyed the planet Gunstar 9 years ago.  i2006kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00532na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001100005264003100016300002300047500025300070542003500323655002500358655002700383MAGE00aRistar 1bSEGA of Americac2006-12-4  a1 Wii optical disc  aGreedy, an evil space pirate, has corrupted the kings of the Valdi System's seven planets and enslaved the people who live there. The plea for a hero is answered by Ristar, who uses his amazing extendable arms and courage to save Valdi from Greedy.  i2006kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00372na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001100005264001700016300002300033500011800056542002400174655002500198655002700223MAGJ00aRistar 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe evil King of Despair holds the constellation of Valjee under a reign of terror, speading misery and darkness.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00376na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001100005264002100016300002300037500011800060542002400178655002500202655002700227MAGP00aRistar 1bSegac2006-12-15  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe evil King of Despair holds the constellation of Valjee under a reign of terror, speading misery and darkness.  i2006kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00571na  a2200133   4500001000500000245002300005264003100028300002300059500024000082542003500322655002500357655002800382655002700410MAHE00aSonic The Hedgehog 1bSEGA of Americac2007-6-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aRocket Sonic, the fastest blue hedgehog on earth, through hair-raising loop-de-loops and dizzying dives past bubbling lava, waterfalls and on as you gather up Rings and stop Dr. Eggman's (AKA Dr. Robotnik) schemes for world domination!  i2007kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00424na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002300005264001700028300002300045500015800068542002400226655002500250655002700275MAHJ00aSonic The Hedgehog 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aBust the video game speed barrier wide open with Sonic The Hedgehog. Blaze by in a blur using the Super Sonic Spin Attack. Loop the loop defying gravity.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00427na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002300005264002000028300002300048500015800071542002400229655002500253655002700278MAHP00aSonic The Hedgehog 1bSegac2006-12-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aBust the video game speed barrier wide open with Sonic The Hedgehog. Blaze by in a blur using the Super Sonic Spin Attack. Loop the loop defying gravity.  i2006kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00593na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264003200026300002300058500030400081542003500385655002500420655002600445MAIE00aSpace Harrier II 1bSEGA of Americac2006-12-18  a1 Wii optical disc  aFantasyland has been taken over by destructive forces, and a call for help comes from deep in the universe. Space Harrier is quick on the scene, armed with his laser, to defeat wave after wave of destructive forces through 12 thrilling stages, with a dangerous boss waiting at the end of each round.  i2006kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00464na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264001700026300002300043500020100066542002400267655002500291655002600316MAIJ00aSpace Harrier II 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aHelp ! Deep in the 214th sector of the universe, a distress signal is sent from a land in turmoil. Under attack and besieged by countless monstrous beings, Fantasyland is fighting a losing battle.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00468na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264002100026300002300047500020100070542002400271655002500295655002600320MAIP00aSpace Harrier II 1bSegac2006-12-22  a1 Wii optical disc  aHelp ! Deep in the 214th sector of the universe, a distress signal is sent from a land in turmoil. Under attack and besieged by countless monstrous beings, Fantasyland is fighting a losing battle.  i2006kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00296na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264003200023300002300055500004800078542003500126655002500161MAJE00aToeJam & Earl 1bSEGA of Americac2006-12-25  a1 Wii optical disc  aSpend time on Earth with two spaced aliens.  i2006kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00473na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264001700023300002300040500021200063542002400275655002500299655002700324MAJJ00aToeJam & Earl 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aToeJam and Earl, the two baddest "rappers" in the universe, had an accident while out cruisin' the galaxy, and crashed down to Earth. Give these two funky aliens a hand putting their spaceship back together!  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00477na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264002100023300002300044500021200067542002400279655002500303655002700328MAJP00aToeJam & Earl 1bSegac2006-12-22  a1 Wii optical disc  aToeJam and Earl, the two baddest "rappers" in the universe, had an accident while out cruisin' the galaxy, and crashed down to Earth. Give these two funky aliens a hand putting their spaceship back together!  i2006kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext01090na  a2200121   4500001000500000245004200005264003100047300002300078500078000101542003500881655002500916655002700941MAKE00aShadow Dancer - The Secret of Shinobi 1bSEGA of Americac2010-1-18  a1 Wii optical disc  aEasy to play, hard to master, Shadow Dancer: The Secret of Shinobi, first released in 1987, is the sequel to the original Shinobi arcade game, and is one of the only games in the Shinobi series to feature true arcade-style gameplay. Play as Joe Musashi, the master ninja known to his enemies only as “The Shinobi”. This battle is not one you must fight alone, as this is the first game in the Shinobi series to feature your ninja attack dog, Yamoto, who will charge foes on command, leaving them open to a powerful drop kick. Use your mastery of ancient ninja technique to topple the crime syndicate—the Neo Zeed Corporation, and free the foreign dignitaries they have taken hostage in New York City. Good luck, and may the ninja spirits help guide you in your journey.  i2010kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00520na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264001700023300002300040500025900063542002400322655002500346655002700371MAKJ00aShadow Dancer 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aShinobi Joe Musashi, after defeating the Neo Zeed crime syndicate, took a much-needed rest. Now, he has a new cause, revenge ! Union Lizard, an organization bent on world domination, made the mistake of murdering Musashi's good friend, Kato, in New York.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00546na  a2200121   4500001000500000245004200005264001900047300002300066500025900089542002400348655002500372655002700397MAKP00aShadow Dancer - The Secret of Shinobi 1bSegac2010-1-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aShinobi Joe Musashi, after defeating the Neo Zeed crime syndicate, took a much-needed rest. Now, he has a new cause, revenge ! Union Lizard, an organization bent on world domination, made the mistake of murdering Musashi's good friend, Kato, in New York.  i2010kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext01131na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001700005264003100022300002300053500088500076542003500961655002500996MALE00aBonanza Bros 1bSEGA of Americac2007-1-29  a1 Wii optical disc  aMobo and Robo Bonanza are enjoying their favorite television show when the picture crackles and the shadowy figure of a mysterious stranger appears on-screen. This figure asks them to collect certain items that he has placed inside various buildings to test his security force. If they return the items successfully, Mobo and Robo will be rewarded. The two of them state that they will get the job done in just three minutes. However, little do they know that each building is packed with security guards who will raise the alarm if they are caught red-handed. Fortunately both Mobo and Robo are equipped with bullets that can knock the guards unconscious for a few seconds. A huge reward will be given out if Mobo and Robo are apprehended. Help the infamous Bonanza Bros. infiltrate a number of different locations ranging from banks to mansions to casinos, and don't get caught!  i2007kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00377na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001700005264001700022300002300039500015300062542002400215655002800239MALJ00aBonanza Bros 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aRobo and Mobo, the Bonanza Bros., are the clumsiest thieves around. They're in deep trouble now, and they need to help to avoid becoming jailbirds !  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAdventure games2wiiext00379na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001700005264001900022300002300041500015300064542002400217655002800241MALP00aBonanza Bros 1bSegac2007-2-2  a1 Wii optical disc  aRobo and Mobo, the Bonanza Bros., are the clumsiest thieves around. They're in deep trouble now, and they need to help to avoid becoming jailbirds !  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aAdventure games2wiiext01166na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002300005264003000028300002300058500090900081542003500990655003101025MAME00aSword of Vermilion 1bSEGA of Americac2007-3-5  a1 Wii optical disc  aSword of Vermilion is about the role of Erik's son, who takes on a quest of revenge to defeat Tsarkon and free the world of Vermilion from evil. In the town of Excalabria, the people went about their business and tended to the fields. One day, vicious fighting broke out everywhere as the army of Cartahena, led by the wizard-king Tsarkon, swarmed all over the town. The townsmen were overwhelmed. The castle of King Erik V collapsed. Erik summoned his bravest, strongest and most faithful warrior, Blade, and gave him his infant son and an ancient family heirloom, the ring of wisdom. He ordered Blade to save himself and the child while the castle burned. Blade traveled to a small village named Wyclif, where he settled down and raised the child as his own son. Eighteen years later, the son of Erik begins his quest. Save the world of Vermilion and fulfill the prophecy of the Malaga fortune-tellers!  i2007kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00441na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002400005264001900029300002300048500016800071542002400239655002500263655003100288MAMJ00aSword of Vermillion 1bSegac2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aEvil threatens the world of Vermilion. Armies of the evil King Tsarkon march in conquest. All hearts look for you, the son of good King Eric V, to end the madness!  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00440na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002300005264001900028300002300047500016800070542002400238655002500262655003100287MAMP00aSword of Vermilion 1bSegac2007-3-2  a1 Wii optical disc  aEvil threatens the world of Vermilion. Armies of the evil King Tsarkon march in conquest. All hearts look for you, the son of good King Eric V, to end the madness!  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aRole-playing games2wiiext01162na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001600005264003000021300002300051500091800074542003500992655002501027MANE00aGain Ground 1bSEGA of Americac2007-2-5  a1 Wii optical disc  aIt's the 31st century, and science and technology have progressed to the point that the human race is approaching perfection: no war, no poverty and no conflict. With nothing to worry about, the human race seems destined to live forever in harmony. But what if Earth came under attack? By this point in time, people did not know how to cope with problems or conflicts, and had completely lost their survival instincts. In response to this, the United Earth Government created the Gain Ground system, a war simulator that would help humans rediscover their lost instincts. After several terrible malfunctions, the creators became prisoners in their own creation. Now it's up to players and two courageous comrades to go into the Gain Ground system, rescue their fellow humans and destroy the system. Players battle through different periods in history as they revive their survival instincts, while trying to live.  i2007kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00456na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001600005264001700021300002300038500019700061542002400258655002500282655002700307MANJ00aGain Ground 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe "Gain Ground" system, a five stage combat-simulation game, became a sensation overnight as a way to release tension. However, one day during a competition, the central computer went crazy!  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aStrategy games2wiiext00458na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001600005264001900021300002300040500019700063542002400260655002500284655002700309MANP00aGain Ground 1bSegac2007-2-2  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe "Gain Ground" system, a five stage combat-simulation game, became a sensation overnight as a way to release tension. However, one day during a competition, the central computer went crazy!  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aStrategy games2wiiext00929na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002100005264003100026300002300057500067900080542003500759655002500794MAOE00aBiohazard Battle 1bSEGA of Americac2007-2-26  a1 Wii optical disc  aAn army of biogenetic mutants has gone haywire, terrorizing the world and putting the future of the planet in jeopardy. In Bio-Hazard Battle, it's up to you to take on the mutant menace and restore order and harmony to the planet Avaron before it's too late! Through eight levels of intense action, you'll be up against some of the nastiest, most vile creatures you've ever seen, including things like mega amoebas, nuclear crabs, electroworms, and gut-grabbing insects. You have four different Bioship fightercraft to choose from, each with unique handling capabilities and weapons systems. Hop into your fightercraft and save Avaron from certain doom in Bio-Hazard Battle.  i2007kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00552na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002800005264001700033300002300050500028200073542002400355655002500379655002600404MAOJ00aCrying - Aseimei Sensou 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aA global biological war has utlerly changed the surface of the planet Avaron. The last human survivors must fly their Bioships to Avaron and search for a safe place to build a colony. You must face all kinds of strange creatures in your search for a new home. To the Bioships !  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00547na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264001900026300002300045500028200068542002400350655002500374655002600399MAOP00aBiohazard Battle 1bSegac2007-3-2  a1 Wii optical disc  aA global biological war has utlerly changed the surface of the planet Avaron. The last human survivors must fly their Bioships to Avaron and search for a safe place to build a colony. You must face all kinds of strange creatures in your search for a new home. To the Bioships !  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00888na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001500005264003100020300002300051500064400074542003500718655002500753MAPE00aComix Zone 1bSEGA of Americac2007-1-29  a1 Wii optical disc  aSketch Turner is an artist in New York City. One day, Sketch is drawing, and then there is a huge thunderstorm in the city. A bolt of lightning hits Sketch's image and brings it to life. That image is Mortus, a megalomaniacal mutant who wants to become real and rule the Earth. Mortus magically transports Sketch into the pages of his comic book so that he can end the creator's life and become real. Inside the comic book, Sketch meets General Alissa Cyan, who believes he is a superhero that came to save their postapocalyptic world from the evil brought by Mortus' bad guys. Instantly, Sketch can fight like a one-man mercenary platoon!  i2007kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00533na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001500005264001700020300002300037500023300060542002400293655002500317655002700342655003000369MAPJ00aComix Zone 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aEnter the Comix Zone... the first truely interactive comic book! Strange events have left Sketch trapped in the pages of his post-apocalyptic comic book, and the drawing pen is in the hands of his most evil creation yet: Mortus.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext00535na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001500005264001900020300002300039500023300062542002400295655002500319655002700344655003000371MAPP00aComix Zone 1bSegac2007-2-2  a1 Wii optical disc  aEnter the Comix Zone... the first truely interactive comic book! Strange events have left Sketch trapped in the pages of his post-apocalyptic comic book, and the drawing pen is in the hands of his most evil creation yet: Mortus.  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext00916na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002000005264003100025300002300056500062800079542003500707655002500742655002700767MAQE00aStreets of Rage 1bSEGA of Americac2007-2-19  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe city was once a happy, peaceful place...until one day, a powerful secret criminal organization took over. This vicious syndicate soon had control of the government and even the police force. The city has become a center of violence and crime where no one is safe. Amid this turmoil, a group of determined young police officers has sworn to clean up the city. Among them are Adam Hunter, Axel Stone and Blaze Fielding. They've decided to put their lives on the line and take back their city through their special hand-to-hand combat abilities. They are willing to risk anything, even their lives, on the Streets of Rage.  i2007kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext00513na  a2200133   4500001000500000245003500005264001700040300002300057500019300080542002400273655002500297655002700322655003000349MAQJ00aBare Knuckle - Ikari no Tekken 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe city has been taken over by a massive crime syndicate. Three young police officers have quit the corrupt Metropolitan police force and set out to topple the organization on their own !  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext00500na  a2200133   4500001000500000245002000005264001900025300002300044500019300067542002400260655002500284655002700309655003000336MAQP00aStreets of Rage 1bSegac2007-3-2  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe city has been taken over by a massive crime syndicate. Three young police officers have quit the corrupt Metropolitan police force and set out to topple the organization on their own !  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext00338na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001700005264003100022300002300053500004900076542003500125655002500160655003100185MARE00aBeyond Oasis 1bSEGA of Americac2007-3-19  a1 Wii optical disc  aFlex the power of the armlet in Beyond Oasis  i2007kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00409na  a2200121   4500001000500000245004500005264001700050300002300067500012000090542002400210655002500234655002800259MARJ04aThe Story of Thor - Hikari wo Tsugu Mono 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aYou are the young Prince Ali in a desperate fight to defeat the evil that is threatening your island empire, Oasis.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00388na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002200005264001900027300002300046500012000069542002400189655002500213655002800238MARP04aThe Story of Thor 1bSegac2007-4-6  a1 Wii optical disc  aYou are the young Prince Ali in a desperate fight to defeat the evil that is threatening your island empire, Oasis.  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00847na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001400005264003100019300002300050500060400073542003500677655002500712MASE00aVectorman 1bSEGA of Americac2008-9-22  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn the year 2049, mankind is forced to abandon an overpolluted Earth and seek out other planets for colonization while the mechanized Orbots stay behind to clean up the mess. When the Orbot leader, WarHead, starts blowing a few circuits and causes a war among the mechanical brethren, a sludge pilot named Vectorman is the only one willing to step up and fight him. You’ll morph into a speeding train, a power drill, a mechanical fish, and a mighty dune buggy in this action-packed adventure. Equip yourself with weapons, pick up morphs and power-ups to defeat WarHead, and restore peace on Earth!  i2008kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00599na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001400005264001700019300002300036500034200059542002400401655002500425655002700450MASJ00aVectorman 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe year is 2043, earth has become a toxic dump being cleaned up by robots. When their leader, Raster, goes haywire and threatens to destroy what's left of the planet, only Vectorman, with his amazing morphing abilities, can stop him. Stunning 3D graphics, and high-speed shooting action makes this simply the best game you'll ever play.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00601na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001400005264001900019300002300038500034200061542002400403655002500427655002700452MASP00aVectorman 1bSegac2007-4-6  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe year is 2043, earth has become a toxic dump being cleaned up by robots. When their leader, Raster, goes haywire and threatens to destroy what's left of the planet, only Vectorman, with his amazing morphing abilities, can stop him. Stunning 3D graphics, and high-speed shooting action makes this simply the best game you'll ever play.  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00495na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001900005264003100024300002300055500024700078542003500325655002500360MATE00aSonic Spinball 1bSEGA of Americac2007-3-12  a1 Wii optical disc  aDr. Eggman (aka Dr. Robotnik) has taken over Mt. Mobius and turned it into a mechanical base. He is using energy from the magma flowing under the volcano to power his Veg-O-Fortress. He has the power to transform helpless animals into robots.  i2007kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00373na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001900005264001700024300002300041500014900064542002400213655002600237MATJ00aSonic Spinball 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aFrom slimy sewers to monstrous machine room, Dr.Robotnik's latest fortress is a giant pinball machine ! Will it whithstand a Sonic spin-vasion ?  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aPinball games2wiiext00375na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001900005264001900024300002300043500014900066542002400215655002600239MATP00aSonic Spinball 1bSegac2007-4-6  a1 Wii optical disc  aFrom slimy sewers to monstrous machine room, Dr.Robotnik's latest fortress is a giant pinball machine ! Will it whithstand a Sonic spin-vasion ?  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aPinball games2wiiext00190na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002800005264001300033300002300046500000500069542001800074MAUJ00aPuzzle Action - Tanto-R 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00920na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003200005264003100037300002300068500061300091542003500704655002800739655003100767MAVE00aWonder Boy in Monster World 1bSEGA of Americac2007-4-23  a1 Wii optical disc  aMonster World was a peaceful, happy place until one dark day when an army of BioMeka monsters invaded. As a young man named Shion, you've vowed to defeat the hostile foes and make the land peaceful again. You'll attack enemies with swords and spears and guard against incoming projectiles with shields and armor. As you travel through the many different regions of Monster World, you'll talk to the townspeople, collect money to buy items, and gather a large variety of weapons and magic. The further you venture, the more powerful your weapons and equipment, including suits of armor and boots, will become.  i2007kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAdventure games2wiiext 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00530na  a2200133   4500001000500000245003700005264001900042300002300061500020800084542002400292655002500316655002800341655002700369MAVJ00aWonder Boy V - Monster World III 1bSegac2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aBattle slimy mushrooms, outspook dangerous spirits, and fight your way through underground caverns filled with creepy creatures. Monster World is in grave danger, come quickly, for Queen Eleanora awaits!  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00525na  a2200133   4500001000500000245003200005264001900037300002300056500020800079542002400287655002500311655002800336655002700364MAVP00aWonder Boy in Monster World 1bSegac2007-5-4  a1 Wii optical disc  aBattle slimy mushrooms, outspook dangerous spirits, and fight your way through underground caverns filled with creepy creatures. Monster World is in grave danger, come quickly, for Queen Eleanora awaits!  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00838na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002100005264003100026300002300057500058600080542003500666655002700701MAWE00aVirtua Fighter 2 1bSEGA of Americac2007-4-16  a1 Wii optical disc  aVirtua Fighter was the very first 3-D fighting game in the industry and introduced six unique characters, each with their own martial-arts style. In Virtua Fighter 2, the intrepid fighters return to the World Fighting Tournament. Take to the stage to see who will claim the championship title. Will it be Lau Chan, Kage-Maru, Wolf Hawkfield, Jeffry McWild, Akira Yuki, Jacky Bryant, Sarah Bryant, or Pai Chan? The answer lies within. Immerse yourself in this technically challenging game and see if you have what it takes to be the champion of the second World Fighting Tournament!  i2007kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00374na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002100005264001700026300002300043500014700066542002400213655002700237MAWJ00aVirtua Fighter 2 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aSelect one of 8 fighters, then pummel the opposition, either computer or friend, who stand in the way of a showdown with the mysterious Dural!  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00376na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002100005264001900026300002300045500014700068542002400215655002700239MAWP00aVirtua Fighter 2 1bSegac2007-5-4  a1 Wii optical disc  aSelect one of 8 fighters, then pummel the opposition, either computer or friend, who stand in the way of a showdown with the mysterious Dural!  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00312na  a2200109   4500001000500000245003800005264003000043300002300073500004600096542003500142655002500177MAXE00aAlex Kidd in the Enchanted Castle 1bSEGA of Americac2007-4-9  a1 Wii optical disc  aCut the bosses down to size with the Kidd  i2007kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00488na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002900005264001900034300002300053500021400076542002400290655002500314655002700339MAXJ00aAlex Kidd - Tenkuu Majou 1bSegac2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aBash! Biff! Pow! Alex Kidd is punching, kicking, and leaping through Paperrock Planet, trying to save his dad ! He's having a tough time, what with scorpions, pufferfish, monkeys and mummies blocking his way !  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00497na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003800005264001900043300002300062500021400085542002400299655002500323655002700348MAXP00aAlex Kidd in the Enchanted Castle 1bSegac2007-5-4  a1 Wii optical disc  aBash! Biff! Pow! Alex Kidd is punching, kicking, and leaping through Paperrock Planet, trying to save his dad ! He's having a tough time, what with scorpions, pufferfish, monkeys and mummies blocking his way !  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00927na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001600005264003200021300002300053500068100076542003500757655002500792MAYE00aAlien Storm 1bSEGA of Americac2007-12-17  a1 Wii optical disc  aShape-shifting aliens have infiltrated the city, creating chaos and panic! Fortunately, a trio of heroes called the Alien Busters has agreed to wipe out the invading creatures. The members of the team wield their own special attacks, and they unload a world of hurt on the Martian menaces from the city streets to the mother ship. Gordon, a tough guy with a bazooka, has a special gunship attack, while Karla has a flamethrower for alien crisping, though she prefers to use her special ballistic-missile attack. Finally, Slammer the robot can self-destruct at will and attacks the intruders with an electric whip and other devices. Take the aliens by storm and save your city!  i2007kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00486na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001600005264001700021300002300038500018500061542002400246655002500270655002700295655003000322MAYJ00aAlien Storm 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aShape-changing alien scum take over your city. Fry the slimy horrors and smash their bid for global conquest. Blast into action with ray guns, flame throwers, power whips and more!  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext00489na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001600005264002000021300002300041500018500064542002400249655002500273655002700298655003000325MAYP00aAlien Storm 1bSegac2008-1-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aShape-changing alien scum take over your city. Fry the slimy horrors and smash their bid for global conquest. Blast into action with ray guns, flame throwers, power whips and more!  i2008kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext00879na  a2200109   4500001000500000245004000005264003000045300002300075500060800098542003500706655002800741MAZE00aToeJam & Earl in Panic on Funkotron 1bSEGA of Americac2007-6-4  a1 Wii optical disc  aDuring ToeJam and Earl’s trip back home, a number of Earthlings hitchhiked on their spaceship and are now infesting planet Funkotron. ToeJam and Earl must track down the Earthlings in order to capture them in large jars and ship them back to Earth in spaceships. It is also their funky mission to find 10 beloved objects belonging to Lamont the "Funkapotamus," the source of all funk in the universe, so they can persuade him to return to his favorite funk-filled planet. ToeJam and Earl must use their "funk powers," such as Funk Move and Funk Scan, to assist in evading and capturing the Earthlings.  i2007kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAdventure games2wiiext00550na  a2200121   4500001000500000245004000005264001900045300002300064500026500087542002400352655002500376655002700401MAZP00aToeJam & Earl in Panic on Funkotron 1bSegac2007-6-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aEarthlings have invaded the peaceful planet of Funkotron, scaring the local natives, and making an awful mess of things! It's up to ToeJam & Earl to track down these pests, send 'em back to Earth and set things right in this super-cool, highly funky adventure!  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00177na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001500005264001300020300002300033500000500056542001800061MB2J00aLangrisser 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00769na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264002000026300002300046500048500069542002400554655003100578655003800609MB3E00aMonster World IV 1bSEGAc2012-5-10  a1 Wii optical disc  aFor the first time outside of Japan, experience the final chapter in the classic Monster World series! One day, a young, green-haired girl names Asha, hears spirits calling out for help. Upon hearing the spirits, she leaves her village and sets forth on a grand adventure into Monster World. One her journey, she comes across a small blue monster named Pepe and a magical Genie. Together they must fight through Monster Land to defeat evil and save the troubled Elemental Spirits.  i2012kSEGAsGameTDB 7aRole-playing games2wiiext 7aAction role-playing games2wiiext00766na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264001700026300002300043500048500066542002400551655003100575655003800606MB3J00aMonster World IV 1bSEGAc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aFor the first time outside of Japan, experience the final chapter in the classic Monster World series! One day, a young, green-haired girl names Asha, hears spirits calling out for help. Upon hearing the spirits, she leaves her village and sets forth on a grand adventure into Monster World. One her journey, she comes across a small blue monster named Pepe and a magical Genie. Together they must fight through Monster Land to defeat evil and save the troubled Elemental Spirits.  i2014kSEGAsGameTDB 7aRole-playing games2wiiext 7aAction role-playing games2wiiext00769na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264002000026300002300046500048500069542002400554655003100578655003800609MB3L00aMonster World IV 1bSEGAc2012-5-10  a1 Wii optical disc  aFor the first time outside of Japan, experience the final chapter in the classic Monster World series! One day, a young, green-haired girl names Asha, hears spirits calling out for help. Upon hearing the spirits, she leaves her village and sets forth on a grand adventure into Monster World. One her journey, she comes across a small blue monster named Pepe and a magical Genie. Together they must fight through Monster Land to defeat evil and save the troubled Elemental Spirits.  i2012kSEGAsGameTDB 7aRole-playing games2wiiext 7aAction role-playing games2wiiext00184na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002200005264001300027300002300040500000500063542001800068MB4J00aParty Quiz Mega Q 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00180na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001800005264001300023300002300036500000500059542001800064MB5J00aLangrisser II 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00807na  a2200109   4500001000500000245003900005264003100044300002300075500053300098542003500631655003100666MB6E00aShining Force II - Ancient Sealing 1bSEGA of Americac2008-10-6  a1 Wii optical disc  aIt’s a dark and stormy night in the kingdom of Granseal, when a thief steals two jewels from the Tower of the Ancients. He sets in motion strange events that lead to the resurrection of Zeon, the Devil King. Granseal’s king falls sick, the princess is kidnapped, and a door to Arc Valley, the Devil King’s home, is opened. The young swordsman, Bowie, realizing the grave danger Granseal faces, must lead the Shining Force to find the Holy Sword, the stolen jewels, and protect Granseal against the invading armies of Zeon.  i2008kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00379na  a2200121   4500001000500000245004000005264001700045300002300062500007700085542002400162655003100186655004000217MB6J00aShining Force II - Inishie no Fuuin 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aAn ancient evil has broken free, and is spreading over the land of Rune.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aRole-playing games2wiiext 7aTactical role-playing games2wiiext00363na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264002000026300002300046500007700069542002400146655003100170655004000201MB6P00aShining Force II 1bSegac2008-10-3  a1 Wii optical disc  aAn ancient evil has broken free, and is spreading over the land of Rune.  i2008kSegasGameTDB 7aRole-playing games2wiiext 7aTactical role-playing games2wiiext00846na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264002400023300002300047500057300070542002800643655002500671655002800696MB7E00aMega Turrican 1bFactor 5c2008-4-14  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe Machine has enslaved the galaxy under its tyrannical rule. As Bren McGuire, the last survivor of the United Freedom Forces, it is your duty to destroy the evil forces of the Machine that have devastated the galaxy. Fight through countless hordes of enemies using everything at your disposal. Use the weapons and power-ups of your Turrican Assault Suit, including the incredible Plasma Rope, to fight back the tide of oncoming enemies and find the health and power-ups that will keep you alive. Fifteen levels of chaos and destruction stand between you and freedom.  i2008kFactor 5sGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00339na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264002000023300002300043500011400066542002400180655002500204MB7P00aMega Turrican 1bSegac2008-3-20  a1 Wii optical disc  aRelentlessly destructive, remorselessly evil "The Machine" once again casts a shadow of fear over the galaxy.  i2008kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00791na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002100005264003100026300002300057500053500080542003500615655003100650MB8E00aPhantasy Star II 1bSEGA of Americac2008-2-18  a1 Wii optical disc  aHailed as one of the greatest games of all time by fans and media alike, Phantasy Star II is an RPG that features an epic story line and turn-based battles. Play as Rolf, Nei, Rudo, or several other characters as you navigate through the Algol star system battling the evil Dark Force. Build your characters, select the right weapons and armor, and take on the forces of evil through various missions as you find the right combination of characters to complete each objective. Experience the magic once again in this great sequel!  i2008kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00398na  a2200109   4500001000500000245005000005264001700055300002300072500013800095542002400233655003100257MB8J00aPhantasy Star II - Kaerazaru Toki no Owari ni 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn the vastness of space the Algo Star System floats like a dust fleck in a sunbeam. Cruise closer. See its three twinkling planets ?  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00372na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002100005264002000026300002300046500013800069542002400207655003100231MB8P00aPhantasy Star II 1bSegac2008-2-15  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn the vastness of space the Algo Star System floats like a dust fleck in a sunbeam. Cruise closer. See its three twinkling planets ?  i2008kSegasGameTDB 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00181na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001900005264001300024300002300037500000500060542001800065MB9J00aPepen ga Pengo 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00927na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001300005264002300018300002300041500065900064542003000723655002500753655002700778MBAJ00aPulseman 1bGame Freakc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aWhen noted 21st-century scientist Doc Yoshimaya fell in love with one of his C-Life artificial-intelligence creations, he uploaded himself into his computer where her program core merged with his DNA, and half-human, half-C-Life, Pulseman was born. Doc Yoshimaya's mind twisted as he emerged back into real life, and he became evil Doc Waruyama. Use Pulseman's ability to harness electricity as a weapon with his Volteccer attack as a means of rapid transport to fight Waruyama's Galaxy Gang across seven crazy stages. Find out why this SEGA Channel classic was widely regarded as one of the best-looking games for SEGA's MEGA DRIVE (Genesis) on release.  i2014kGame FreaksGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00333na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001300005264001900018300002300037500007500060542002400135655002500159655002700184MBAL00aPulseman 1bSegac2009-7-3  a1 Wii optical disc  aYou play Pulseman, a hero power that was created to combat cybercrime.  i2009kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00930na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001300005264002600018300002300044500065900067542003000726655002500756655002700781MBAN00aPulseman 1bGame Freakc2009-7-13  a1 Wii optical disc  aWhen noted 21st-century scientist Doc Yoshimaya fell in love with one of his C-Life artificial-intelligence creations, he uploaded himself into his computer where her program core merged with his DNA, and half-human, half-C-Life, Pulseman was born. Doc Yoshimaya's mind twisted as he emerged back into real life, and he became evil Doc Waruyama. Use Pulseman's ability to harness electricity as a weapon with his Volteccer attack as a means of rapid transport to fight Waruyama's Galaxy Gang across seven crazy stages. Find out why this SEGA Channel classic was widely regarded as one of the best-looking games for SEGA's MEGA DRIVE (Genesis) on release.  i2009kGame FreaksGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00558na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002500005264003100030300002300061500030100084542003500385655002800420MBBE00aSonic The Hedgehog 2 1bSEGA of Americac2007-6-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aDr. Eggman (aka Dr. Robotnik) is searching for the Chaos Emeralds to fuel his new Death Egg engine. One afternoon, he launches a full-scale attack on the island where the Chaos Emeralds are buried, imprisoning all of the helpless animals living there and turning them into mindless worker drones.  i2007kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAdventure games2wiiext00349na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002500005264001700030300002300047500008100070542002400151655002500175655002700200MBBJ00aSonic The Hedgehog 2 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aSonic's back and better than ever. He's a blur in blue ! A blaze in action !  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00351na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002500005264001900030300002300049500008100072542002400153655002500177655002700202MBBP00aSonic The Hedgehog 2 1bSegac2007-7-6  a1 Wii optical disc  aSonic's back and better than ever. He's a blur in blue ! A blaze in action !  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00916na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264003100023300002300054500066600077542003500743655002800778MBCE00aKid Chameleon 1bSEGA of Americac2007-5-28  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe local arcade is packed with kids, all lining up to play the latest, most realistic video game they've ever seen. It's called Wild Side, and it uses holographic images to immerse the player in a strange world. But there's a problem... Kids are literally getting sucked into the game, and now several of them are trapped. Throughout more than 100 levels, you'll take on several different forms, such as a Berzerker, a Micromax, a Maniaxe or a Skycutter, which will make you much more powerful. It's up to you, Kid Chameleon, the best gamer in town, to get yourself inside the game so that you can defeat the game's boss and bring your friends back to reality.  i2007kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAdventure games2wiiext00411na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264001700023300002300040500015000063542002400213655002500237655002700262MBCJ00aChameleon Kid 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aMany of the kids playing Wild Side, the newest game in town, are disappearing. Heady Metal, the game's villain, is capturing them left and right.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00413na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264001900023300002300042500015000065542002400215655002500239655002700264MBCP00aKid Chameleon 1bSegac2007-6-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aMany of the kids playing Wild Side, the newest game in town, are disappearing. Heady Metal, the game's villain, is capturing them left and right.  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00774na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264002000023300002300043500054600066542002400612655002800636MBDE00aGolden Axe II 1bSegac2007-6-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aNot long after the devastating reign of the wicked Death Adder, another evil arose. Dark Guld and his minions invaded and took hold of the prized Golden Axe with plans to destroy it. Once again, as a fierce barbarian named Ax-Battler, a fearless female Amazon known as Tyris-Flare, or a ferocious dwarf named Gilius Thunderhead, you will wield steely swords and powerful magic in an all-out war to recover the sword. Once you slash your way through the six side-scrolling levels, you’ll get the chance to defeat Dark Guld once and for all.  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aAdventure games2wiiext00405na  a2200133   4500001000500000245002200005264001700027300002300044500009800067542002400165655002500189655002700214655003000241MBDJ04aThe Golden Axe II 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aBattle your way through treacherous territory to return the Golden Axe to its rightful place.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext00403na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001800005264001900023300002300042500009800065542002400163655002500187655002700212655003000239MBDP00aGolden Axe II 1bSegac2007-7-6  a1 Wii optical disc  aBattle your way through treacherous territory to return the Golden Axe to its rightful place.  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext00817na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264003100023300002300054500056400077542003500641655003100676MBEE00aShining Force 1bSEGA of Americac2007-7-23  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn ages long forgotten, Light fought Darkness for control of the world. Finally, the Ancients defeated the evil ruler of the dark forces known as Dark Dragon and cast him into another dimension, though he vowed to return in 1,000 years. As time passed, all memory of Dark Dragon was buried, and the land of Rune enjoyed 10 centuries of peace. Yet, as promised, the dark ruler returned, along with hordes of evil creatures that ravaged the land. As chaos erupted, several strongholds of Good still held out, awaiting a hero who could wield the Powers of Light.  i2007kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00401na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003700005264001900042300002300061500011500084542002400199655002500223655003100248MBEJ00aShining Force - Kamigami no Isan 1bSegac2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aYou are the leader of a group of warriors and sorcerers, fighting to save your homeland from an ancient evil !  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00382na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264001900023300002300042500011500065542002400180655002500204655003100229MBEP00aShining Force 1bSegac2007-8-3  a1 Wii optical disc  aYou are the leader of a group of warriors and sorcerers, fighting to save your homeland from an ancient evil !  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00926na  a2200121   4500001000500000245004500005264003100050300002300081500061200104542003500716655002500751655002800776MBFE00aShinobi III - Return of the Ninja Master 1bSEGA of Americac2007-8-22  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn this thrilling sequel to The Revenge of Shinobi, Joe Musashi finds that Neo Zeed – the crime syndicate he believed he had wiped out two years earlier – is indeed still alive and well. The return of Neo Zeed and its leader, the mysterious Shadow Master, forces Musashi to return from exile and confront the growing evil. As the Shinobi, the master of long-forgotten Oboro Ninjitsu martial arts, Musashi must utilize all his powers to overcome his various enemies. Thanks to his considerable combat skills and special Ninjitsu moves, only the Shinobi can thwart Neo Zeed and vanquish the Shadow Master.  i2007kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00422na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002500005264001700030300002300047500015400070542002400224655002500248655002700273MBFJ04aThe Super Shinobi II 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn the mountains of Japan, a lone Ninja stands. He has left the presence of an old enemy once again becoming strong. The Ninja's name is Joe Musashi.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00444na  a2200121   4500001000500000245004500005264001900050300002300069500015400092542002400246655002500270655002700295MBFP00aShinobi III - Return of the Ninja Master 1bSegac2007-8-3  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn the mountains of Japan, a lone Ninja stands. He has left the presence of an old enemy once again becoming strong. The Ninja's name is Joe Musashi.  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00869na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002000005264002000025300002300045500063900068542002400707655002800731MBGE00aDynamite Headdy 1bSegac2007-7-30  a1 Wii optical disc  aHeaddy, a toy with a detachable head, arrives in North Town to find that the evil puppet king Dark Demon is causing serious problems. Dark Demon is gathering up all the puppets in town and turning some into his own evil minions--while eliminating the rest of the puppets that aren’t good enough to join his legions. Headdy is captured and is targeted for the incinerator, but escapes in the nick of time. Now he’s got to save the town. To do so, Headdy will have to take on all manner of bad guys and even has to contend with his lifelong nemesis, Trouble Bruin the bear. Can Headdy overcome all his foes and take down Dark Demon?  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aAdventure games2wiiext00471na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002000005264001700025300002300042500020800065542002400273655002500297655002700322MBGJ00aDynamite Headdy 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe scene is set! This headstrong puppet may be a reject but he's out to prove his worth. 14 zany switchable heads to choose and use as you bite, swing, jump and butt your way to the Dark Demon's castle.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00473na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002000005264001900025300002300044500020800067542002400275655002500299655002700324MBGP00aDynamite Headdy 1bSegac2007-8-3  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe scene is set! This headstrong puppet may be a reject but he's out to prove his worth. 14 zany switchable heads to choose and use as you bite, swing, jump and butt your way to the Dark Demon's castle.  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00195na  a2200097   4500001000500000245003300005264001300038300002300051500000500074542001800079MBHJ00aPuzzle & Action - Ichidant-R 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00918na  a2200121   4500001000500000245004500005264003000050300002300080500058900103542003500692655003100727655003800758MBIE00aLandstalker - The Treasures of King Nole 1bSEGA of Americac2007-9-3  a1 Wii optical disc  aAfter hearing of the legendary treasure of King Nole, the elvish treasure hunter Nigel undertakes a quest to gather various pieces of the famed loot. His journey takes him through Mercator Island's villages, caves and dungeons that hold King Nole's riches. Along the way, he'll have to help the inhabitants of the island while fighting against the treachery of Duke Mercator, who is searching for the treasure as well. A variety of obstacles and foes will try to deter Nigel, who must use all his wits and skills to defeat Duke Mercator and uncover the secret of King Nole's treasure.  i2007kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aRole-playing games2wiiext 7aAction role-playing games2wiiext00585na  a2200133   4500001000500000245003500005264002000040300002300060500026100083542002400344655002500368655003100393655002700424MBIJ00aLandStalker - Koutei no Zaihou 1bSegac2007-9-25  a1 Wii optical disc  aAfter hearing of the legendary treasure of King Nole, the elvish treasure hunter Nigel undertakes a quest to gather various pieces of the famed loot. His journey takes him through Mercator Island's villages, caves and dungeons that hold King Nole's riches.  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aRole-playing games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00595na  a2200133   4500001000500000245004500005264002000050300002300070500026100093542002400354655002500378655003100403655002700434MBIP00aLandstalker - The Treasures of King Nole 1bSegac2007-10-5  a1 Wii optical disc  aAfter hearing of the legendary treasure of King Nole, the elvish treasure hunter Nigel undertakes a quest to gather various pieces of the famed loot. His journey takes him through Mercator Island's villages, caves and dungeons that hold King Nole's riches.  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aRole-playing games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00705na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002100005264002200026300002300048500047000071542002600541655002800567MBJE00aGhouls 'n Ghosts 1bCapcomc2007-8-27  a1 Wii optical disc  aGhouls'n Ghosts is the sequel to the popular action game Ghosts'n Goblins, originally released in the arcades and later ported to the Genesis. One full-moon night, three years after the battle with Astaroth, a ray of light shoots through Princess Prin Prin, and her soul is stolen right in front of Arthur's eyes. To save his bride's soul, Arthur the knight must battle all manner of evil undead creatures with a variety of weapons, powerful magic, and new actions.  i2007kCapcomsGameTDB 7aAdventure games2wiiext00452na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264001700023300002300040500019100063542002400254655002500278655002700303MBJJ00aDai Makaimura 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe time is yesteryear, when knights scoured the countryside in search of the Holy Grail, defended the honor of fair maidens and fought a never ending battle against rampant evil forces.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00457na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264001900026300002300045500019100068542002400259655002500283655002700308MBJP00aGhouls 'n Ghosts 1bSegac2007-9-7  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe time is yesteryear, when knights scoured the countryside in search of the Holy Grail, defended the honor of fair maidens and fought a never ending battle against rampant evil forces.  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00373na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001500005264001700020300002300037500015400060542002400214655002500238MBKJ00aCrack Down 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aBen and Andy, the two top Special Service agents, have accepted a very dangerous assignment, the elimination of Mr. K and his Artificial Life System.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00375na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001500005264001900020300002300039500015400062542002400216655002500240MBKP00aCrack Down 1bSegac2007-9-7  a1 Wii optical disc  aBen and Andy, the two top Special Service agents, have accepted a very dangerous assignment, the elimination of Mr. K and his Artificial Life System.  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00278na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002500005264001700030300002300047500004900070542002400119655002500143MBLJ00aESWAT - Cyber Police 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aEswat is: the toughest fighting force alive!  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00282na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002700005264001900032300002300051500004900074542002400123655002500147MBLP00aESWAT City Under Siege 1bSegac2007-9-7  a1 Wii optical disc  aEswat is: the toughest fighting force alive!  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00500na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002500005264003100030300002300061500020700084542003500291655002500326655002700351MBME00aSonic The Hedgehog 3 1bSEGA of Americac2007-9-10  a1 Wii optical disc  aSonic and Tails are back for another adventure as they again battle the evil Dr. Eggman (AKA Dr. Robotnik), who is desperately trying to collect all the Chaos Emeralds in order to rebuild his Death Egg.  i2007kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00447na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002500005264001700030300002300047500017900070542002400249655002500273655002700298MBMJ00aSonic The Hedgehog 3 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aSonic and Tails must stop Dr.Robotnik from rebuilding his Death Egg, which crash landed on the Floating Island. This island floats because of the power of the Chaos Emeralds.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00449na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002500005264001900030300002300049500017900072542002400251655002500275655002700300MBMP00aSonic The Hedgehog 3 1bSegac2007-9-7  a1 Wii optical disc  aSonic and Tails must stop Dr.Robotnik from rebuilding his Death Egg, which crash landed on the Floating Island. This island floats because of the power of the Chaos Emeralds.  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00174na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001200005264001300017300002300030500000500053542001800058MBNJ00aChelnov 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00802na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001900005264003200024300002300056500051300079542003500592655002500627655002800652MBOE00aGolden Axe III 1bSEGA of Americac2007-10-22  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe once-peaceful kingdom so familiar to fans of the original Golden Axe is under threat once again. The Prince of Darkness has stolen the invaluable Golden Axe, taken over the kingdom, and rendered all its warriors harmless thanks to an evil curse. One warrior, however, breaks free from the curse and must defeat the prince and regain the Golden Axe to save the kingdom. In this one- or two-player action game, play as a giant, a panther, or a sword-wielding human and fight your way to victory once again!  i2007kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00665na  a2200133   4500001000500000245002300005264001700028300002300045500035700068542002400425655002500449655002700474655003000501MBOJ04aThe Golden Axe III 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe once-peaceful kingdom so familiar to fans of the original Golden Axe is under threat once again. The Prince of Darkness has stolen the invaluable Golden Axe, taken over the kingdom and rendered its warriors harmless with an evil curse. One warrior breaks free from the curse and must defeat the prince and regain the Golden Axe to save the kingdom.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext00664na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001900005264002000024300002300044500035700067542002400424655002500448655002700473655003000500MBOP00aGolden Axe III 1bSegac2007-10-5  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe once-peaceful kingdom so familiar to fans of the original Golden Axe is under threat once again. The Prince of Darkness has stolen the invaluable Golden Axe, taken over the kingdom and rendered its warriors harmless with an evil curse. One warrior breaks free from the curse and must defeat the prince and regain the Golden Axe to save the kingdom.  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext00946na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002400005264003100029300002300060500065500083542003500738655002500773655002600798MBPE00aSuper Thunder Blade 1bSEGA of Americac2007-9-17  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn this follow-up to Thunder Blade, you’ll fly a new and improved attack helicopter in a series of attacks against guerilla armies that are bent on taking over the world. Although your aircraft is formidable, your enemies are vast and varied. You’ll have to take on submarines, tanks, fighter planes and more. Your command of this state-of-the-art battle copter must be top notch, as you’ll have to dodge oncoming fire and use your various weapons to eliminate all enemy targets so you can reach the guerilla base and end their nefarious plans once and for all. Put on your flight suit and step into the thrilling action of Super Thunder Blade!  i2007kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00577na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002400005264001700029300002300046500031100069542002400380655002500404655002600429MBPJ00aSuper Thunder Blade 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aOnce known only as Thunder Blade, the ASH-002 is back in action as Super Thunder Blade, model ASH-091B. As part of the Air Force Special Operation Troop, you and Super Thunder Blade must take control of its state-of-the-art artillery to defeat the renegade guerilla armies with plans to dominate the world.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00580na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002400005264002000029300002300049500031100072542002400383655002500407655002600432MBPP00aSuper Thunder Blade 1bSegac2007-10-5  a1 Wii optical disc  aOnce known only as Thunder Blade, the ASH-002 is back in action as Super Thunder Blade, model ASH-091B. As part of the Air Force Special Operation Troop, you and Super Thunder Blade must take control of its state-of-the-art artillery to defeat the renegade guerilla armies with plans to dominate the world.  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00804na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002200005264003100027300002300058500051300081542003500594655002500629655002800654MBQE00aStreets of Rage 3 1bSEGA of Americac2007-9-24  a1 Wii optical disc  aJust when you thought the world was safe from the Syndicate and its shady leader Mr. X, they have returned to torment the city once again. Mr. X has developed lifelike robots to take the place of various city officials so he can be in complete control. Now it’s up to our old heroes Axel, Skate, and Blaze to stop the threat with their amazing fighting skills. With more weapons and combat moves, as well as secret characters and various endings, this return to the streets is one you won’t want to miss.  i2007kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00520na  a2200133   4500001000500000245002100005264001700026300002300043500021400066542002400280655002500304655002700329655003000356MBQJ00aBare Knuckle III 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aStrike a blow for justice! Axel has been falsely arrested, only you can prove his innocence. Fight your way through 8 white-knuckle levels to decide the final outcome. New characters, new moves, new challenge!  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext00524na  a2200133   4500001000500000245002200005264002000027300002300047500021400070542002400284655002500308655002700333655003000360MBQP00aStreets of Rage 3 1bSegac2007-10-5  a1 Wii optical disc  aStrike a blow for justice! Axel has been falsely arrested, only you can prove his innocence. Fight your way through 8 white-knuckle levels to decide the final outcome. New characters, new moves, new challenge!  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext00898na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002200005264004800027300002300075500061400098542005100712655002500763MBRE00aRolling Thunder 2 1bNAMCO BANDAI Games America Inc.c2007-12-24  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn this follow-up to the original classic, you are once again a member of Interpol's Rolling Thunder task force, and it's up to you to stop the return of the evil Geldra organization. Now known as Neo-Geldra and led by a newcomer named Gimdo, the bad guys are bent on destroying several valuable outer-space satellites. In this one- or two-player game, you can play as Leila or Albatross-both characters from the original-as you venture through several different levels, trying to put a stop to the nefarious efforts of Gimdo and the rest of Neo-Geldra. Use your bullets wisely and make Rolling Thunder proud.  i2007kNAMCO BANDAI Games America Inc.sGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00511na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002200005264001800027300002300045500028300068542002500351655002500376MBRJ00aRolling Thunder 2 1bNamcoc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aBullets whiz past you... You dive into piles of spent shell casings to avoid exploding grenades... Fingers numb from recoil, you slam your last clip into your pistol and take aim... You must destroy the terrorist organization called Geldra, or the world will never be the same !  i2014kNamcosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00514na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002200005264002100027300002300048500028300071542002500354655002500379MBRP00aRolling Thunder 2 1bNamcoc2007-12-7  a1 Wii optical disc  aBullets whiz past you... You dive into piles of spent shell casings to avoid exploding grenades... Fingers numb from recoil, you slam your last clip into your pistol and take aim... You must destroy the terrorist organization called Geldra, or the world will never be the same !  i2007kNamcosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00190na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002800005264001300033300002300046500000500069542001800074MBSJ00aDyna Brothers 2 Special 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00838na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264003100023300002300054500059100077542003500668655002500703MBTE00aAlien Soldier 1bSEGA of Americac2007-11-5  a1 Wii optical disc  aAs Epsilon-Eagle, you are an alien soldier who has been genetically engineered to produce maximum intelligence and strength. You were once a member of the criminal organization Scarlet, but when you decided to break from the group, you were forced into a showdown with Scarlet’s new leader Xi-Tiger, who kills a hostage in his attempt to destroy you. Now it’s up to you to take revenge against the bad guys in this side-scrolling action game! Choose from six different weapons and battle the bosses of Scarlet until you reach the final confrontation with the ultimate secret weapon!  i2007kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00393na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264001700023300002300040500017100063542002400234655002500258MBTJ00aAlien Soldier 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn the year 2015 the planet Sierra is in the grips of Xi-Tiger's Scarlet terrorists. All hope now lies with Epsilon-Eagle, a fearsame warrior with the lethal arsenal.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00396na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264002000023300002300043500017100066542002400237655002500261MBTP00aAlien Soldier 1bSegac2007-11-2  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn the year 2015 the planet Sierra is in the grips of Xi-Tiger's Scarlet terrorists. All hope now lies with Epsilon-Eagle, a fearsame warrior with the lethal arsenal.  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00636na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001900005264003200024300002300056500030800079542003500387655002500422655002800447655002700475MBUE00aSonic 3D Blast 1bSEGA of Americac2007-11-19  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe evil Dr. Eggman (AKA Dr. Robotnik) stumbles upon an alternate dimension where some odd birds called Flickies have the ability to travel anywhere. In order to get help in his search for the Chaos Emeralds, Dr. Eggman transforms the Flickies into robots that will help him track down his coveted gems.  i2007kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00447na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001900005264001700024300002300041500018500064542002400249655002500273655002700298MBUJ00aSonic 3D Blast 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aYour favorite superhero is back... and the greatest 3D graphic sensation ever to hit 16-bit gaming. Find, free and guide the Flickies to safety in 7 massive action-packed 3D zones.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00462na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003100005264002000036300002300056500018500079542002400264655002500288655002700313MBUP00aSonic 3D: Flickies' Island 1bSegac2007-11-2  a1 Wii optical disc  aYour favorite superhero is back... and the greatest 3D graphic sensation ever to hit 16-bit gaming. Find, free and guide the Flickies to safety in 7 massive action-packed 3D zones.  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00184na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002200005264001300027300002300040500000500063542001800068MBVJ00aJuso Kihei Leynos 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00958na  a2200109   4500001000500000245003700005264003000042300002300072500069300095542003500788655002500823MBWE00aColumns III - Revenge of Columns 1bSEGA of Americac2008-2-4  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis single-player or multiplayer experience expands upon the game play of the original two Columns titles by giving players some extra attacks to spring on their opponents during the game. As in the original Columns, jewels fall into a bin, and you have to twist and manipulate them to form matches of three or more in a vertical, horizontal, or diagonal line to keep the jewels from stacking up and reaching the top. In Columns III, you can get special magical jewels that will do things like raising your opponent’s crush bar or lowering yours, adding an extra element of strategy to the game. This is a great game to play with friends, so download it today and jump into the action!  i2008kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00667na  a2200109   4500001000500000245004200005264001700047300002300064500042100087542002400508655002500532MBWJ00aColumns III - Taiketsu! Columns World 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis single-player or multi-player experience expands upon the gameplay of the two original Columns titles by giving players some extra attacks to spring on their opponents during gameplay. As in the original Columns, jewels fall into a bin and you have to twist and manipulate them to form matches of three or more in a vertical, horizontal or diagonal line to keep the jewels from stacking up and reaching the top.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00664na  a2200109   4500001000500000245003700005264001900042300002300061500042100084542002400505655002500529MBWM00aColumns III - Revenge of Columns 1bSegac2008-5-2  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis single-player or multi-player experience expands upon the gameplay of the two original Columns titles by giving players some extra attacks to spring on their opponents during gameplay. As in the original Columns, jewels fall into a bin and you have to twist and manipulate them to form matches of three or more in a vertical, horizontal or diagonal line to keep the jewels from stacking up and reaching the top.  i2008kSegasGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00757na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001300005264003200018300002300050500051100073542003500584655002800619MBXE00aEcco Jr. 1bSEGA of Americac2007-11-26  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe aquatic adventures of Ecco come to life for a younger generation of gamers! Perfect for kids, Ecco Jr. finds our young hero heading out to sea with a variety of tasks he must perform in order to get there. Along with his friends, Tara the baby orca and Kitnee the young Atlantic dolphin, Ecco Jr. will interact with sea lions, sea horses, and other aquatic life as he makes his journey to the Big Blue. Introduce your kids to the classic series of Ecco the Dolphin titles by downloading Ecco Jr. today!  i2007kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAdventure games2wiiext00471na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001300005264001700018300002300035500021400058542002400272655002500296655002800321MBXJ00aEcco Jr. 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe aquatic adventures of Ecco come to life for a younger generation of gamers! Perfect for kids, Ecco Jr. finds our young hero heading out to sea with a variety of tasks he must perform in order to get there.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00473na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001300005264001900018300002300037500021400060542002400274655002500298655002800323MBXM00aEcco Jr. 1bSegac2008-8-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe aquatic adventures of Ecco come to life for a younger generation of gamers! Perfect for kids, Ecco Jr. finds our young hero heading out to sea with a variety of tasks he must perform in order to get there.  i2008kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00826na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001900005264003200024300002300056500052100079542003500600655003100635655003800666MBYE00aLight Crusader 1bSEGA of Americac2007-12-31  a1 Wii optical disc  aEach day, more good townspeople of Green Row have been mysteriously disappearing, and beleaguered King Weeden summons the knight Sir David to investigate. Armed with his wits and his sword, Sir David must find the cause of this strange evil and save the citizens of Green Row before things get any worse. Take the role of the brave knight in this action RPG and get to the bottom of the mysteries of Green Row as you fight enemies, solve puzzles and use your best combination of brains and brawn to save the kingdom.  i2007kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aRole-playing games2wiiext 7aAction role-playing games2wiiext00426na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001900005264001700024300002300041500016000064542002400224655002500248655003100273MBYJ00aLight Crusader 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aFight your way through a dungeon of evil! Innocent people are vanishing, victims of horrifying magic. You, a master swordsman, are challenged to save them!  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00429na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001900005264002000024300002300044500016000067542002400227655002500251655003100276MBYP00aLight Crusader 1bSegac2007-12-7  a1 Wii optical disc  aFight your way through a dungeon of evil! Innocent people are vanishing, victims of horrifying magic. You, a master swordsman, are challenged to save them!  i2007kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00826na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002200005264003100027300002300058500057300081542003500654655002700689MBZE00aEternal Champions 1bSEGA of Americac2007-12-3  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis 2-D fighting game introduces a cast of different characters that met untimely deaths in their lives on Earth. Now they have been given a chance to compete against each other, with the winner taking on the Eternal Champion, the ultimate fighter in the universe. The reward for defeating the Eternal Champion is a return to Earth for the opportunity to avenge death and restore balance to the universe. Choose from nine unique characters with a variety of fighting styles, and bring your best moves to defeat all comers in your quest to topple the Eternal Champion!  i2007kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00272na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002200005264001700027300002300044500004400067542002400111655002700135MBZJ00aEternal Champions 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aPrepare for the ultimate fighting game!  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00275na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002200005264002000027300002300047500004400070542002400114655002700138MBZP00aEternal Champions 1bSegac2008-2-15  a1 Wii optical disc  aPrepare for the ultimate fighting game!  i2008kSegasGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00707na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002000005264002600025300002300051500043000074542002900504655002500533655002700558MC2E00aEarthworm Jim 2 1bInterplayc2009-12-14  a1 Wii optical disc  aSuperhero annelid Jim and his new sidekick Snott are back for an off-the-wall sequel in Earthworm Jim 2. Containing more action than your standard platformer of this era, each stage has a different style and mission that draws on game play from different genres, including mazes, trivia contests, and arcade game style levels. Features game music composed by Tommy Tallarico. Do you have what it takes to rescue the Princess?  i2009kInterplaysGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00322na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002000005264002200025300002300047500004900070542002900119655002500148655002700173MC2J00aEarthworm Jim 2 1bInterplayc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aTwo times the fun! Two times the excitement!  i2014kInterplaysGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00325na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002000005264002500025300002300050500004900073542002900122655002500151655002700176MC2P00aEarthworm Jim 2 1bInterplayc2009-12-4  a1 Wii optical disc  aTwo times the fun! Two times the excitement!  i2009kInterplaysGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00657na  a2200133   4500001000500000245005000005264002000055300002300075500032400098542002400422655002500446655002700471655002500498MC3E00aSuper Street Fighter II - The New Challengers 1bSEGAc2012-4-26  a1 Wii optical disc  aYour fearless street fighters are now available in the classic Mega Drive version of Super Street Fighter II: The New Challengers. Battle in elimination tournaments with Ryu’s new flaming fireball and Ken’s new Dragon Punch. Fight head-to-head locally and compete against other challengers in heated online battles.  i2012kSEGAsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext00376na  a2200109   4500001000500000245005000005264002100055300002300076500011400099542002600213655002700239MC3J00aSuper Street Fighter II - The New Challengers 1bCapcomc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aWhen Super Street Fighter II - The New Challengers debuted, the fighting game genre would be changed forever.  i2014kCapcomsGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00376na  a2200109   4500001000500000245004900005264002200054300002300076500011400099542002600213655002700239MC3P00aSuper Street Fighter II: The New Challengers 1bCapcomc2008-1-25  a1 Wii optical disc  aWhen Super Street Fighter II - The New Challengers debuted, the fighting game genre would be changed forever.  i2008kCapcomsGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00725na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001200005264003100017300002300048500044700071542003500518655002500553655002500578MC4E00aStrider 1bSEGA of Americac2012-2-16  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe year is 2048. The Striders, ninja-like agents and the last defenders of justice on Earth, are the only hope to stop Grandmaster Meio from ruling the world. Hiryu, the youngest Strider to achieve Class A ranking, embarks on a mission to assassinate the evil Grandmaster with his plasma sword, called a Cypher. Guide Hiryu as he jumps, slides and hangs throughout the Eastern European nation of Kazafu in a battle to find the evil dictator.  i2012kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext00728na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264002800023300002300051500044700074542003500521655002500556655002500581MC4J00aStrider Hiryu 1bSEGA of Americac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe year is 2048. The Striders, ninja-like agents and the last defenders of justice on Earth, are the only hope to stop Grandmaster Meio from ruling the world. Hiryu, the youngest Strider to achieve Class A ranking, embarks on a mission to assassinate the evil Grandmaster with his plasma sword, called a Cypher. Guide Hiryu as he jumps, slides and hangs throughout the Eastern European nation of Kazafu in a battle to find the evil dictator.  i2014kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext00742na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001200005264002000017300002300037500044700060542002400507655002500531655002500556655002700581MC4P00aStrider 1bSEGAc2012-3-15  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe year is 2048. The Striders, ninja-like agents and the last defenders of justice on Earth, are the only hope to stop Grandmaster Meio from ruling the world. Hiryu, the youngest Strider to achieve Class A ranking, embarks on a mission to assassinate the evil Grandmaster with his plasma sword, called a Cypher. Guide Hiryu as he jumps, slides and hangs throughout the Eastern European nation of Kazafu in a battle to find the evil dictator.  i2012kSEGAsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00811na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001600005264001800021300002300039500055300062542002300615655002500638655002600663MCAJ00aGley Lancer 1bNCSc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn the year 2025, a war breaks out between humans and a hostile alien race, and 16-year-old Lucia and the rest of the starfighter pilots in the Earth Federation must join the battle. When Lucia’s father, Ken, is kidnapped by the aliens, Lucia decides to take action and hijacks a brand-new prototype starfighter, the “Gley Lancer,” in order to try to save her father. In this side-scrolling shooter, step into the cockpit of the Gley Lancer as Lucia, rescue your father, and destroy the evil aliens that are bent on destroying the human race!  i2014kNCSsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00618na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001600005264002000021300002300041500035700064542002400421655002500445655002600470MCAL00aGley Lancer 1bSegac2008-5-16  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn the year 2025, a war breaks out between humans and a hostile alien race, and 16-year-old Lucia and the rest of the starfighter pilots in the Earth Federation must join the battle. When Lucia’s father is kidnapped by the aliens, she decides to take action and hijacks a brand new prototype starfighter, the Gley Lancer, in order to try to save him.  i2008kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00812na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001600005264001900021300002300040500055300063542002300616655002500639655002600664MCAN00aGley Lancer 1bNCSc2008-7-21  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn the year 2025, a war breaks out between humans and a hostile alien race, and 16-year-old Lucia and the rest of the starfighter pilots in the Earth Federation must join the battle. When Lucia’s father, Ken, is kidnapped by the aliens, Lucia decides to take action and hijacks a brand-new prototype starfighter, the “Gley Lancer,” in order to try to save her father. In this side-scrolling shooter, step into the cockpit of the Gley Lancer as Lucia, rescue your father, and destroy the evil aliens that are bent on destroying the human race!  i2008kNCSsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00726na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001400005264002000019300002300039500050500062542002400567655002500591MCBE00aPowerball 1bNBGIc2008-3-24  a1 Wii optical disc  aEight different teams representing various nations are vying to become the POWERBALL champions, and you control one of the eight in your quest for the championship. A hybrid of games like rugby and football, POWERBALL is played on a 100-yard field. Try to score by either carrying the ball into your opponent’s end zone or kicking it into your opponent’s net for points. This one- or two-player game offers both exhibition and league play. Jump into a game of POWERBALL and try a brand-new sport!  i2008kNBGIsGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext00725na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001600005264001700021300002300038500050500061542002400566655002500590MCBJ00aWrestleball 1bNBGIc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aEight different teams representing various nations are vying to become the POWERBALL champions, and you control one of the eight in your quest for the championship. A hybrid of games like rugby and football, POWERBALL is played on a 100-yard field. Try to score by either carrying the ball into your opponent’s end zone or kicking it into your opponent’s net for points. This one- or two-player game offers both exhibition and league play. Jump into a game of POWERBALL and try a brand-new sport!  i2014kNBGIsGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext00888na  a2200109   4500001000500000245004400005264003100049300002300080500060900103542003500712655003100747MCCE00aPhantasy Star III - Generations of Doom 1bSEGA of Americac2008-4-21  a1 Wii optical disc  aAs Rhys, the crown prince of the Orakian kingdom of Landen, you are engaged to be married to Maia, a woman from a rival kingdom. But Maia is kidnapped on your wedding day, setting you on a quest filled with twists and turns that will reintroduce you to people and places from previous Phantasy Star games. This epic spans several generations of characters, and your choices will dramatically impact the way the story unfolds, which makes it a great game to play all the way through more than once. In Phantasy Star III, things aren’t always what they seem—check it out and watch the mysteries unfold!  i2008kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00371na  a2200109   4500001000500000245004300005264001700048300002300065500011800088542002400206655003100230MCCJ00aToki no Keishousha - Phantasy Star III 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aIt's been a millenium since Laya's hordes battled Orakio's cyborg armies. And civilized man was almost destroyed.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00375na  a2200109   4500001000500000245004400005264002000049300002300069500011800092542002400210655003100234MCCP00aPhantasy Star III - Generations of Doom 1bSegac2008-4-18  a1 Wii optical disc  aIt's been a millenium since Laya's hordes battled Orakio's cyborg armies. And civilized man was almost destroyed.  i2008kSegasGameTDB 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00338na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264003100026300002300057500004900080542003500129655002500164655002700189MCDE00aSonic & Knuckles 1bSEGA of Americac2010-2-15  a1 Wii optical disc  aSonic must defeat doctor Robotnik yet again!  i2010kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00350na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264001700026300002300043500008600066542002400152655002500176655002700201MCDJ00aSonic & Knuckles 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aSonic & Knuckles join forces to defeat Dr.Robotnik in this massive new adventure.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00353na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264002000026300002300046500008600069542002400155655002500179655002700204MCDP00aSonic & Knuckles 1bSegac2010-2-12  a1 Wii optical disc  aSonic & Knuckles join forces to defeat Dr.Robotnik in this massive new adventure.  i2010kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00450na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002300005264001700028300002300045500018500068542002400253655002500277655002600302MCEJ00aSuper Fantasy Zone 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe Fantasy Zone is once again under siege! Dark Menon is back, and his forces are stronger than ever! Guide Opa-Opa through hosts of creepy creatures and stop the Menons for good!  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00837na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002300005264002300028300002300051500056300074542002700637655002500664655002600689MCEN00aSuper Fantasy Zone 1bSunsoftc2008-7-21  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe last entry in the Fantasy Zone series, this side-scrolling shooter puts you in the shoes of main character Opa-Opa, who is on a mission to avenge the death of his father. To do so, you’ll have to battle a variety of Enemy Generators to clear out the various levels and finish off the Menon Guardian at the end of the level. Eliminating your enemies will let you rack up some gold, which you can use to buy even better weapons, upgrades, and other equipment. Spend your gold wisely, as each different boss you need to defeat presents a unique challenge!  i2008kSunsoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00453na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002300005264002000028300002300048500018500071542002400256655002500280655002600305MCEP00aSuper Fantasy Zone 1bSegac2008-6-27  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe Fantasy Zone is once again under siege! Dark Menon is back, and his forces are stronger than ever! Guide Opa-Opa through hosts of creepy creatures and stop the Menons for good!  i2008kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00333na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001200005264003400017300002300051500000500074542003800079655002500117655002600142655003100168MCFJ00aPhelios 1bNamco Bandai Gamesc2009-7-28  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2009kNamco Bandai GamessGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext 7aShoot 'em up games2wiiext01179na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002100005264002300026300002300049500094600072542002601018655002501044MCGE00aForgotten Worlds 1bCapcomc2008-11-17  a1 Wii optical disc  aFORGOTTEN WORLDS is a one- to two-player simultaneous side-scrolling shooter made by CAPCOM CO., LTD. It was one of the first games to incorporate 360-degree aiming and shooting. This SEGA GENESIS version provides the same impact and intensity of the classic arcade game. The time: the 29th century. Without warning, warships broke through the sky, loaded with fiendish aliens. They rained down fire, bombs, missiles, and napalm, making it barren and inhospitable. Humanity was enslaved, and Earth became known as the Forgotten World. In a hidden place, a group of brave humans raised two male children in secret. They brought up the young men as warriors, training them for battle. The two warriors emerged as armed machines of might, strength, and super power—the Nameless Ones. Fight the hateful invaders as the powerful Nameless Ones! Collect Zenny to upgrade your weapons and satellite, and free the planet that was once called Earth.  i2008kCapcomsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00534na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264001900026300002300045500026700068542002600335655002500361655002600386MCGJ00aForgotten Worlds 1bCapcomc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe planet used to be beautiful, with gorgeous cities ans gleaming countrysides. Until the Aliens attacked! With fire, bombs, and napalm they devastated the world! They made the planet so abominable that it became an outcast in the universe, the Forgotten World.  i2014kCapcomsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00537na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264002200026300002300048500026700071542002600338655002500364655002600389MCGP00aForgotten Worlds 1bCapcomc2008-8-28  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe planet used to be beautiful, with gorgeous cities ans gleaming countrysides. Until the Aliens attacked! With fire, bombs, and napalm they devastated the world! They made the planet so abominable that it became an outcast in the universe, the Forgotten World.  i2008kCapcomsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00872na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001500005264002600020300002300046500060000069542003000669655002500699655002600724MCHE00aM.U.S.H.A. 1bNaxat Softc2009-1-19  a1 Wii optical disc  aMUSHA is a SEGA GENESIS game that is a fan favorite among shooter fans for its intense and exciting gameplay. The player controls Terri, a girl who pilots a MUSHA (Metallic Uniframe Super Hybrid Armor). Terri’s goal is to eliminate Dire 51, an Intellicomputer that has gone out of control and is planning an offensive attack upon humanity. Use special weapons like the Vanishing Buster, Blazing Beam, and Defensive Detonator, along with offensive options that allow six types of formation fire, to battle through seven exhilarating levels to finally reach and destroy Dire 51 once and for all!  i2009kNaxat SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00364na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001500005264002500020300002300045500009300068542003000161655002500191655002600216MCHJ00aM.U.S.H.A. 1bNaxat Softc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aOur solar system is under siege from Dire 51, the MUSHA Team is the only hope we've got!  i2014kNaxat SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00365na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001500005264002600020300002300046500009300069542003000162655002500192655002600217MCHM00aM.U.S.H.A. 1bNaxat Softc2009-7-17  a1 Wii optical disc  aOur solar system is under siege from Dire 51, the MUSHA Team is the only hope we've got!  i2009kNaxat SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00173na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001100005264001300016300002300029500000500052542001800057MCIJ00aGynoug 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00665na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002000005264001900025300002300044500043900067542002400506655002500530MCJE00aSplatterhouse 2 1bNBGIc2008-8-4  a1 Wii optical disc  aSPLATTERHOUSE 2 is the sequel to SPLATTERHOUSE, released only on the SEGA GENESIS. A few months after escaping from the first mansion in SPLATTERHOUSE, the main character, Rick, once again encounters the Terror Mask and must use its powers to rescue his beloved Jennifer. Rick will need to punch, slash, smash, and even chainsaw his way through a haunted mansion against unspeakable horrors and terrifying bosses to make it out alive.  i2008kNBGIsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00525na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001800005264001700023300002300040500022200063542002400285655002500309655002700334655003000361MCJJ00aSplatterhouse 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aYour girlfriend Jennifer is trapped in a living nightmare and it's up to you to save her. The only option is to don the terror mask to transform into a buffed out mayhem machine ready to smash and bash a path freedom.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext00529na  a2200133   4500001000500000245002000005264001900025300002300044500022200067542002400289655002500313655002700338655003000365MCJP00aSplatterhouse 2 1bSegac2008-8-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aYour girlfriend Jennifer is trapped in a living nightmare and it's up to you to save her. The only option is to don the terror mask to transform into a buffed out mayhem machine ready to smash and bash a path freedom.  i2008kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext00890na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002100005264003200026300002300058500063300081542003500714655003100749MCKE00aPhantasy Star IV 1bSEGA of Americac2008-12-22  a1 Wii optical disc  aPhantasy Star IV is the fourth released game from SEGA's epic Phantasy Star series, one of SEGA's biggest RPGs on the SEGA GENESIS. In the year AW 2284, planet Motavia is once again plagued by strange biocreatures, and it’s up to the brave men and women of the Hunters Guild to exterminate them. You are Chaz Ashley, a rookie Hunter straight out of training who is supported by Alys Brangwin—a crafty veteran whose good looks and prowess with the blade have earned her an awesome reputation. These two Hunters, along with a cast of supporting characters, will go beyond Motavia to unwittingly save their entire solar system.  i2008kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00414na  a2200109   4500001000500000245003800005264001700043300002300060500016600083542002400249655003100273MCKJ00aPhantasy Star - Sennenki no Owari 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aLaunch yourself into the biggest RPG ever! This is the explosive finale to the incredible Phantasy Star saga. An ancient Dark Force stalks the Algol star system.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00401na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002100005264002100026300002300047500016600070542002400236655003100260MCKP00aPhantasy Star IV 1bSegac2008-11-14  a1 Wii optical disc  aLaunch yourself into the biggest RPG ever! This is the explosive finale to the incredible Phantasy Star saga. An ancient Dark Force stalks the Algol star system.  i2008kSegasGameTDB 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00913na  a2200109   4500001000500000245004900005264002300054300002300077500065000100542002600750655002700776MCLE00aStreet Fighter II - Special Champion Edition 1bCapcomc2010-10-13  a1 Wii optical disc  aSTREET FIGHTER II': SPECIAL CHAMPION EDITION was the first Street Fighter game released on the SEGA GENESIS. The Street Fighter series can be considered one of the first fighting games to popularize competitive video-game fighting. This version of the game contains both the CHAMPION and HYPER rule sets, from the two editions released in the arcades. It also introduced an exclusive Group Battle mode that is now a general feature in most fighting games. Play as one of twelve different characters, each with their own distinctive fighting style, either fight in single-player mode or challenge a friend in this legendary classic fighting game.  i2010kCapcomsGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00482na  a2200109   4500001000500000245005100005264001900056300002300075500022100098542002600319655002700345MCLJ00aStreet Fighter II Dash Plus - Champion Edition 1bCapcomc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aFrom the comers of the globe come twelve of the toughest fighters to ever prowl the streets. Choose your champion and step into the arena as one of the eight original challengers or as one of the four Grand Masters !  i2014kCapcomsGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00484na  a2200109   4500001000500000245004900005264002300054300002300077500022100100542002600321655002700347MCLP00aStreet Fighter II - Special Champion Edition 1bCapcomc2008-10-17  a1 Wii optical disc  aFrom the comers of the globe come twelve of the toughest fighters to ever prowl the streets. Choose your champion and step into the arena as one of the eight original challengers or as one of the four Grand Masters !  i2008kCapcomsGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00205na  a2200097   4500001000500000245004300005264001300048300002300061500000500084542001800089MCMJ00aLord Monarch - Tokoton Sentou Densetsu 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00217na  a2200097   4500001000500000245005500005264001300060300002300073500000500096542001800101MCNJ00aHokuto no Ken - Shin Seikimatsu Kyuseishu Densetsu 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00176na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001400005264001300019300002300032500000500055542001800060MCOJ00aSorcerian 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00866na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264002600023300002300049500063000072542002900702655002500731MCPE00aEarthworm Jim 1bInterplayc2008-10-27  a1 Wii optical disc  aJim was an ordinary earthworm who did very earthworm-like things, such as flee from crows and eat dirt. One day, during an outer-space fight, a suit drops to Earth and falls around Jim. It mutates him into a large and intelligent (at least by earthworm standards) superhero. Play as Jim in this SEGA GENESIS classic! When Jim learns of the evil plans of Psy-Crow and Queen Slug-for-a-Butt, he decides to rescue Princess What's-Her-Name. Run, gun, swing on hooks by your head, and launch cows at the interesting characters you meet along the way, such as Major Mucus, Chuck and Fifi, Evil the Cat, and Bob the Killer Goldfish.  i2008kInterplaysGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00521na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264002300023300002300046500024800069542003000317655002500347655002700372MCPJ00aEarthworm Jim 1b Interplayc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aJim, just an ordinary earthworm caught in a suit he doesn't understand. Faced with the daunting task of keeping the super-powered suit out of the evil clutches of his vicious enemies, you'll have to use every weapon and power at your disposal.  i2014k InterplaysGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00524na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264002600023300002300049500024800072542003000320655002500350655002700375MCPP00aEarthworm Jim 1b Interplayc2008-10-3  a1 Wii optical disc  aJim, just an ordinary earthworm caught in a suit he doesn't understand. Faced with the daunting task of keeping the super-powered suit out of the evil clutches of his vicious enemies, you'll have to use every weapon and power at your disposal.  i2008k InterplaysGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00811na  a2200109   4500001000500000245004300005264002600048300002300074500055000097542002900647655002500676MCQE00aBoogerman - A Pick and Flick Adventure 1bInterplayc2008-11-24  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn this top pick from the Sega Genesis, play as Boogerman, the heroic alter ego of Snotty Ragsdale. While investigating Professor Stinkbaum’s lab, Boogerman stumbles upon a strange machine that opens a portal to another dimension. Boogerman has a nose for adventure, but has he met his match in this sticky situation? Journey through dangerous worlds while battling wicked enemies like Fly Boy and Deodor Ant. Deal them a blow with Boogerman’s super abilities: pick and flick with deadly precision, belch, and use his deadly signature stomp.  i2008kInterplaysGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00439na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001400005264004000019300002300059500014000082542004300222655002500265655002700290MCQP00aBoogerman 1bInterplay Entertainmentc2008-12-12  a1 Wii optical disc  aBogey on down to the pick of the action games, as our hero, the Boogerman, tries to clean up the world against the evil Booger Meister.  i2008kInterplay EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00868na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003600005264003000041300002300071500056600094542003500660655002500695655002600720MCRE00aMercs - Wolf of the Battlefield 1bSEGA of Americac2009-2-9  a1 Wii optical disc  aFollowing a rash of terrorism outbreaks and increasing opposition using guerilla warfare, the U.S. Government has decided to hire a group of professional mercenaries to undergo secret missions battling through enemy lines; to go where no ordinary soldier would dare to go. Based on the popular arcade game, MERCS for the SEGA GENESIS lets you play as a MERC and also adds an original mode, allowing players to choose from five different characters. Take no prisoners as you shoot, drive jeeps and tanks, and clash against huge bosses to accomplish your mission!  i2009kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00413na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002400005264001900029300002300048500018300071542002400254655002500278MCRJ00aSenjou no Ōkami II 1bSegac2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aYou are a "Merc", a professional mercenary. Now you must run secret missions for the U.S. government in areas where fighting is so intense, no ordinary soldier would dare to go !  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00426na  a2200109   4500001000500000245003600005264002000041300002300061500018300084542002400267655002500291MCRP00aWolf of the Battlefield - MERCS 1bSegac2009-2-20  a1 Wii optical disc  aYou are a "Merc", a professional mercenary. Now you must run secret missions for the U.S. government in areas where fighting is so intense, no ordinary soldier would dare to go !  i2009kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00548na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003400005264001700039300002300056500027100079542002400350655002500374655002700399MCSJ00aWonder Boy III - Monster Lair 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThy're ferocious, beastly, wicked, you name it. That's right. The monsters from the far ends of the universe have invaded! They've pillaged Xenobia and now they're heading for your town! Join Leo and Priscilla and destroy them before it's too late to save the world!  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00829na  a2200109   4500001000500000245003400005264003100039300002300070500056300093542003500656655002800691MCSN00aWonder Boy III - Monster Lair 1bSEGA of Americac2009-4-20  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe once quiet town of Xenobia is under attack by fierce and gruesome monsters, and no one can stop them. As Leo, it is up to you to save Xenobia and the world from danger as you navigate through a series of worlds in a race against time to reach your goal. Battle your foes with your sword and jumping abilities. Look out for power-ups that will increase your health and add to the amount of time you have to complete your missions. Play alone or even play co-op with a friend who can take the role of Priscilla. Do you have what it takes to save the world?  i2009kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAdventure games2wiiext00550na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003400005264001900039300002300058500027100081542002400352655002500376655002700401MCSP00aWonder Boy III - Monster Lair 1bSegac2009-3-6  a1 Wii optical disc  aThy're ferocious, beastly, wicked, you name it. That's right. The monsters from the far ends of the universe have invaded! They've pillaged Xenobia and now they're heading for your town! Join Leo and Priscilla and destroy them before it's too late to save the world!  i2009kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00573na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001700005264003900022300002300061500030900084542004300393655002700436MCTE00aClay Fighter 1bInterplay Entertainmentc2009-5-25  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn this zany 2D fighter, it's just another average day for a humble traveling circus troupe - until a meteor crash lands in their camp! This otherwordly orb, made entirely out of interstellar clay, contaminates all of the circus employees, turning them into bizarrely superpowered versions of themselves!  i2009kInterplay EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00507na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001700005264003800022300002300060500024400083542004300327655002700370MCTP00aClay Fighter 1bInterplay Entertainmentc2009-2-6  a1 Wii optical disc  aSticks and stones might make him groan, but Clay really ticks him off! Bad Mister Frosty is the name, and action is the game. Fists ans feet will fly (and other parts) as Frosty and his friends smack it out in head-to-head fighting action.  i2009kInterplay EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00196na  a2200097   4500001000500000245003400005264001300039300002300052500000500075542001800080MCUJ00aDragon Slayer - Eiyu Densetsu 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00870na  a2200109   4500001000500000245003400005264002600039300002300065500061700088542003000705655002500735MCVE00aPitfall - The Mayan Adventure 1bActivisionc2009-4-13  a1 Wii optical disc  aPitfall: The Mayan Adventure is a side-scrolling action game in which you play adventurer Pitfall Harry Jr. in search of his father, Pitfall Harry. Pitfall Harry has been taken captive by the dreaded warrior spirit Zakelua: Lord of Evil. Armed with only a trusty sling and his father's journal, young Harry Jr. must now venture into the unknown to rescue him...before it's too late! Bungee jump and boomerang your way to safety as you battle through treacherous Mayan jungles, waterfalls, and deserted mines. With 13 levels of fast, gripping action, you will need to be attentive and quick—or prepare to die...  i2009kActivisionsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00541na  a2200133   4500001000500000245003400005264002300039300002300062500021200085542003000297655002500327655002800352655002700380MCVJ00aPitfall - The Mayan Adventure 1bActivisionc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aA vast labyrinth of interconnected levels guards the fabulous secrets of the Mayans. Hollywood produced sound effects and revolutionary animation technology create un intense journey of excitement discovery.  i2014kActivisionsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00544na  a2200133   4500001000500000245003400005264002600039300002300065500021200088542003000300655002500330655002800355655002700383MCVP00aPitfall - The Mayan Adventure 1bActivisionc2009-5-15  a1 Wii optical disc  aA vast labyrinth of interconnected levels guards the fabulous secrets of the Mayans. Hollywood produced sound effects and revolutionary animation technology create un intense journey of excitement discovery.  i2009kActivisionsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00822na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002000005264003100025300002300056500053500079542003500614655002500649655002600674MCWE00aGalaxy Force II 1bSEGA of Americac2009-5-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aGalaxy Force II is an arcade shooter with a 3-D view from behind your spaceship. Fly through five different planets, taking on enemies in environments that range from a peaceful garden to lands made of fire or ice. Navigate treacherous landscapes by flying low over the planet surface and blowing up enemy robots, ships, and turrets then flying through a tunnel to destroy the alien stronghold on each planet. It is your duty as part of the Galaxy Force to defend against the alien invasion and maintain peace in the solar system.  i2009kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00422na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002000005264001700025300002300042500016000065542002400225655002500249655002600274MCWJ00aGalaxy Force II 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aJunos, a solar system located at the end of the Milky Way, has come under attack. The unprovoked assault is led by Halcyon, sovereign of the Fourth Empire.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00424na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002000005264001900025300002300044500016000067542002400227655002500251655002600276MCWP00aGalaxy Force II 1bSegac2009-5-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aJunos, a solar system located at the end of the Milky Way, has come under attack. The unprovoked assault is led by Halcyon, sovereign of the Fourth Empire.  i2009kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00205na  a2200097   4500001000500000245004300005264001300048300002300061500000500084542001800089MCXJ00aDragon Slayer: The Legend of Heroes II 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00812na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002700005264003100032300002300063500055600086542003500642655002500677MCYE04aThe Revenge of Shinobi 1bSEGA of Americac2009-8-17  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn this classic SEGA Genesis platformer, play as Joe Musashi a ninja out to avenge the evil Neo Zeed and his criminal empire. A sequel to the arcade favorite Shinobi, you once again traverse through various districts ranging from the bamboo forests of Japan to the urban streets of New York City, fighting incoming enemies by throwing Shurikens, performing special ninjutsu moves, and slashing a katana sword. Win your battles against unique bosses at the last stage of each district and make your way up to the final match with your nemesis Neo Zeed.  i2009kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00382na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002200005264001700027300002300044500011700067542002400184655002500208655002700233MCYJ04aThe Super Shinobi 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aYou are Musashi, master ninja. You are one of the mystic warriors, who see and know all things. You are deadly !  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00389na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002700005264001900032300002300051500011700074542002400191655002500215655002700240MCYP04aThe Revenge of Shinobi 1bSegac2009-8-7  a1 Wii optical disc  aYou are Musashi, master ninja. You are one of the mystic warriors, who see and know all things. You are deadly !  i2009kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00849na  a2200109   4500001000500000245003100005264003100036300002300067500059000090542003500680655002400715MCZE00aShanghai II - Dragon's Eye 1bSEGA of Americac2010-1-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe ancient pastime of Mahjong solitaire is reinvented as an interactive video game where each tile you remove may be your last! Discover enchanting music, fun animation and exciting obstacles that are built in to this intriguing board game that will keep you engaged for hours. This classic title challenges you to clear the board by removing matching pairs of tiles. Play the traditional Shanghai® II or take the game to a new dimension with Dragon’s Eye! Don't let the simple rules deceive you - the depth and intricacy of this challenge will become your new obsession very soon!  i2010kSEGA of AmericasGameTDB 7aBoard games2wiiext00412na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003100005264002700036300002300063500012500086542003000211655002400241655002500265MCZP00aShanghai II - Dragon's Eye 1bActivisionc2009-11-27  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe ancient pastime of Mah-Jongg is reinvented as an interactive video game where each tile you remove may be your last!  i2009kActivisionsGameTDB 7aBoard games2wiiext 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00182na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002000005264001300025300002300038500000500061542001800066PA2J00aYokai Douchuuki 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00177na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001500005264001300020300002300033500000500056542001800061PA3J00aSalamander 1bc2012--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2012sGameTDB00180na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001800005264001300023300002300036500000500059542001800064PA4J00aParasol Stars 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00956na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001600005264002200021300002300043500069100066542002600757655002500783655002600808PA6E00aBloody Wolf 1bG-Modec2007-6-18  a1 Wii optical disc  aEnter alone, deep into enemy territory to rescue the kidnapped President in this overhead-view action shooter. Take on the role of a commando in a Special Forces team and face your enemies with an onslaught of weapons, including machine guns and grenades. Earn valuable information, weapons, and items by rescuing POWs. Fight your way to the end of each stage and defeat the boss by effectively using your weapons and equipment. This port of the insanely popular arcade game features refined graphics, story, and cut-scenes, making this action game a must-have. This new and enhanced version includes the never-been-told second half of the story that was left out of the arcade version.  i2007kG-ModesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00370na  a2200121   4500001000500000245004200005264001900047300002300066500008200089542002600171655002500197655002600222PA6J00aNarazumono Sentou Butai - Bloody Wolf 1bG-modec2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aTake out the enemies who stand in your way and rescue the abducted President.  i2014kG-modesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00347na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001600005264002200021300002300043500008200066542002600148655002500174655002600199PA6P00aBloody Wolf 1bG-modec2007-6-29  a1 Wii optical disc  aTake out the enemies who stand in your way and rescue the abducted President.  i2007kG-modesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00403na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001600005264002800021300002300049500016400072542003100236655002600267PA7E00aAlien Crush 1bHUDSON SOFTc2006-12-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aAlien Crush features a science fiction theme reminiscent of the film Alien. Essentially, the player is "fighting" against the aliens with their pinball skills.  i2006kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aPinball games2wiiext00517na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001600005264002400021300002300045500028200068542003100350655002600381PA7J00aAlien Crush 1bHudson Softc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aAlien Crush is a fan-favorite pinball game that features a sinister sci-fi theme. Play through a two-level playing field that comes to life with pulsating alien creatures. Rack up a high enough score, clear the board of these extraterrestrials and discover secret bonus stages.  i2014kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aPinball games2wiiext00604na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001600005264005100021300002300072500028200095542005400377655002500431655002600456PA7P00aAlien Crush 1bHudson Soft / Hudson Entertainmentc2006-12-15  a1 Wii optical disc  aAlien Crush is a fan-favorite pinball game that features a sinister sci-fi theme. Play through a two-level playing field that comes to life with pulsating alien creatures. Rack up a high enough score, clear the board of these extraterrestrials and discover secret bonus stages.  i2006kHudson Soft / Hudson EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aArcade games2wiiext 7aPinball games2wiiext01040na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001100005264004600016300002300062500073100085542005100816655002500867655002600892PA8E00aOrdyne 1bNAMCO BANDAI Games America Inc.c2007-5-7  a1 Wii optical disc  aOrdyne is a port of the popular side-scrolling arcade shooter that includes simultaneous two-player co-op play as well as impressive visuals and catchy background music. The evil Kubota has kidnapped Dr. Tomari’s fiancée, Kana, and taken the colossal nuclear reactor Ordyne. In order to reclaim them, Dr. Tomari and his assistant Felix take to their battleships and head off in pursuit. Avoid enemies and advance through seven different levels that take place on land, sea, and air. Collect crystals from defeated enemies and use them to buy items or upgrades for your ship at the Space Inn. Do you have what it takes to defeat the boss at the end of each level and ultimately reach Kubota in the final stage, Kubota World?  i2007kNAMCO BANDAI Games America Inc.sGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext01038na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001100005264004400016300002300060500073100083542005100814655002500865655002600890PA8J00aOrdyne 1bNAMCO BANDAI Games America Inc.c2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aOrdyne is a port of the popular side-scrolling arcade shooter that includes simultaneous two-player co-op play as well as impressive visuals and catchy background music. The evil Kubota has kidnapped Dr. Tomari’s fiancée, Kana, and taken the colossal nuclear reactor Ordyne. In order to reclaim them, Dr. Tomari and his assistant Felix take to their battleships and head off in pursuit. Avoid enemies and advance through seven different levels that take place on land, sea, and air. Collect crystals from defeated enemies and use them to buy items or upgrades for your ship at the Space Inn. Do you have what it takes to defeat the boss at the end of each level and ultimately reach Kubota in the final stage, Kubota World?  i2014kNAMCO BANDAI Games America Inc.sGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext01209na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264002700023300002300050500097000073542003101043655002501074PA9E00aSplatterhouse 1bHUDSON SOFTc2007-3-19  a1 Wii optical disc  aRick and Jennifer, both parapsychology students at the local university, are visiting West Mansion, site of the research lab where the famed Dr. West conducted some of his most gruesome experiments. A sudden storm forces them to find shelter inside the mansion. Once inside, they are attacked by monsters! Jennifer is kidnapped and Rick is knocked unconscious! Hours later, Rick awakes to find himself covered in blood with the Terror Mask stuck to his face. His only hope is to depend on the ancient powers of the mask to give him the strength and courage to find Jennifer. Now Rick’s fight has begun! Splatter your way through 7 stages of side-scrolling horror action. Armed with cleavers and shotguns, Rick must fight his way through the monsters of West Mansion and defeat the bosses at the end of every stage. The creepy music, gruesome monsters, flying blood, gory action, and shocking events leading up to the finale will keep you on the edge of your seat!  i2007kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00678na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001800005264003100023300002300054500034700077542003800424655002500462655002700487655003000514PA9J00aSplatterhouse 1bNamco Bandai Gamesc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe forces of evil are abroad - ghastly, slimy creatures from the depths of your very worst nightmares. And as if that wasn't bad enough, they've captured your girlfriend! You've got to go to rescue her, so climb into your blue boiler-suit, put on your fearsome ice hockey mask and go kick the butts of those things that go bump in the night.  i2014kNamco Bandai GamessGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext00681na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001800005264003400023300002300057500034700080542003800427655002500465655002700490655003000517PA9P00aSplatterhouse 1bNamco Bandai Gamesc2007-3-16  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe forces of evil are abroad - ghastly, slimy creatures from the depths of your very worst nightmares. And as if that wasn't bad enough, they've captured your girlfriend! You've got to go to rescue her, so climb into your blue boiler-suit, put on your fearsome ice hockey mask and go kick the butts of those things that go bump in the night.  i2007kNamco Bandai GamessGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext00944na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264002800023300002300051500070400074542003100778655002500809PAAE00aBomberman '93 1bHUDSON SOFTc2006-11-22  a1 Wii optical disc  aBomberman '93 is the exciting, powered-up version that followed the original Bomberman! With 6 rounds, each containing 8 stages, the single-player Normal Mode provides all the fun you can handle in its 48 different stages! Blast all of your enemies and find the hidden exit within the time limit to progress to the next stage. The "kick" function appears for the first time in this version of Bomberman, and you can really start using cunning tactics in your game play! Make the most of the traps and the new items to clock the game with a perfect record! Up to 5 players can play in the Battle Game, and all the new tricks and devices (like the conveyor belt) are sure to guarantee a heated battle!  i2006kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00301na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264005000023300002300073500001600096542005400112655002500166PAAP00aBomberman '93 1bHudson Soft / Hudson Entertainmentc2006-12-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aNORMAL GAME  i2006kHudson Soft / Hudson EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00893na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002100005264005100026300002300077500060400100542005400704655002500758PABE00aBonk's Adventure 1bHudson Soft / Hudson Entertainmentc2006-11-22  a1 Wii optical disc  aAn old-school side-scrolling action game! Gameplay is simple: just headbutt your enemies as you progress through each stage. You receive damage when you get hit by an enemy or when you touch something hazardous. Chow down on meat you find along the way to power-up Bonk by 2 levels. Headbutt the ground after Bonk has transformed to unleash a powerful explosion! The earth will tremble and your enemies will be stunned! That's Bonk power! The power of his mighty rock-hard head! The game is loaded with bonus games and hidden stages! And, just like any great action game, there are big boss battles!  i2006kHudson Soft / Hudson EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00554na  a2200121   4500001000500000245004300005264002400048300002300072500025400095542003100349655002500380655002700405PABJ00aPC Genjin - Pithecanthropus Computerus 1bHudson Softc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aSet in prehistoric times, this Wonderboy-style scrolling platform game has the hero, a slap-head baldy called PC Kid, running and jumping his way through many levels, head butting an unbelievably weird load of beasts who run, hop and fly around him.  i2014kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00581na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264005000026300002300076500025400099542005400353655002500407655002700432PABP00aBonk's Adventure 1bHudson Soft / Hudson Entertainmentc2006-12-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aSet in prehistoric times, this Wonderboy-style scrolling platform game has the hero, a slap-head baldy called PC Kid, running and jumping his way through many levels, head butting an unbelievably weird load of beasts who run, hop and fly around him.  i2006kHudson Soft / Hudson EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext01044na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264004900026300002300075500071400098542005400812655002500866655003100891PACE00aDungeon Explorer 1bHudson Soft / Hudson Entertainmentc2007-1-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aDungeon Explorer is a multiplayer action/role-playing game where up to five players can play at the same time. The story takes place in underground dungeons. Players can choose from eight different character types: Fighter, Thief, Warlock, Witch, Bishop, Elf, Bard or Knome. Depending on the character, the types of magic, attack strength and movement will all vary. To survive, players must know all about their enemies' weaknesses. Players also must know about the special attributes of each magic spell and use them to their greatest advantage. In team-play games, working together is the key to victory. Any combination of Wii Remotes and Nintendo GameCube™ controllers can be used in multiplayer games.  i2007kHudson Soft / Hudson EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00351na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264002400026300002300050500006900073542003100142655002500173655003100198PACJ00aDungeon Explorer 1bHudson Softc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aAfter leaving the tavern, gather information from the villagers.  i2014kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00400na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264005000026300002300076500006900099542005400168655002500222655003100247PACP00aDungeon Explorer 1bHudson Soft / Hudson Entertainmentc2006-12-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aAfter leaving the tavern, gather information from the villagers.  i2006kHudson Soft / Hudson EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aRole-playing games2wiiext01130na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001100005264002800016300002300044500085900067542003100926655002500957655002600982PADE00aR-Type 1bHUDSON SOFTc2006-12-25  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis is a completely faithful port - right down to the character details - of the famous shooting-game masterpiece R-TYPE. Destroy the POW armor and one of six different units will appear, which players can then use to power up the R-9. Equip Bits and obtain Laser Units to make the Force appear and to power it up. The Force can then be integrated into or separated from the R-9. Make the most of weapons, including the Reflecting Laser Beams, Air-to-Surface and Antiaircraft Lasers. Keep pressing the fire button to fire blasts from the Beam Cannon. Press and hold the fire button to charge the Beam Gauge, then release it to fire a devastating Wave Cannon blast. The longer players hold it, the stronger the blast. The ultimate highlights are the bosses that await at the end of each stage, including a stage that pits players against a giant warship.  i2006kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00645na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001100005264002400016300002300040500037800063542003100441655002500472655002600497PADJ00aR-Type 1bHudson Softc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aPitted against the Bydo Empire, the "R-Type" class ship is humanity's last hope of thwarting the impending invasion. Equipped with a sphere like object, called the "Force," this weapon contains the only form of energy strong enough to destroy the Bydo. Unfortunately, you've been chosen as the delivery system for this weapon - so it rests upon you to complete the mission.  i2014kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00649na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001100005264002800016300002300044500037800067542003100445655002500476655002600501PADP00aR-Type 1bHudson Softc2006-12-29  a1 Wii optical disc  aPitted against the Bydo Empire, the "R-Type" class ship is humanity's last hope of thwarting the impending invasion. Equipped with a sphere like object, called the "Force," this weapon contains the only form of energy strong enough to destroy the Bydo. Unfortunately, you've been chosen as the delivery system for this weapon - so it rests upon you to complete the mission.  i2006kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00842na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002300005264002800028300002300056500055900079542003100638655002500669655002600694PAEE00aSuper Star Soldier 1bHUDSON SOFTc2006-11-27  a1 Wii optical disc  aSuper Star Soldier is a classic, vertically scrolling shooting game. In addition to the NORMAL GAME, there are 2-minute and 5-minute Time Attack Modes, and a mode where high scores can be checked. A NORMAL GAME is made up of 8 different stages, and in each stage (except Stage 7), a boss awaits you at the end. The Special Attack Squad, led by the Mother Brain, has launched an all-out invasion of the Earth. Take your small-scale fighter, the Neo Caesar, with its arsenal of 4 regular weapons and 2 special weapons, and send them back where they belong!  i2006kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00593na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002300005264002400028300002300052500031400075542003100389655002500420655002600445PAEJ00aSuper Star Soldier 1bHudson Softc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aSuper Star Soldier is a classic vertical-scrolling shooting game. In addition to the Normal Game mode, there are 2-minute and 5-minute Time Attack modes and a mode where high-scores can be checked. Normal Game is made up of 8 different stages, and in each stage (except Stage 7), a boss awaits you at the end.  i2014kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00642na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002300005264005000028300002300078500031400101542005400415655002500469655002600494PAEP00aSuper Star Soldier 1bHudson Soft / Hudson Entertainmentc2006-12-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aSuper Star Soldier is a classic vertical-scrolling shooting game. In addition to the Normal Game mode, there are 2-minute and 5-minute Time Attack modes and a mode where high-scores can be checked. Normal Game is made up of 8 different stages, and in each stage (except Stage 7), a boss awaits you at the end.  i2006kHudson Soft / Hudson EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext01042na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001600005264002700021300002300048500080500071542003100876655002500907PAFE00aVictory Run 1bHUDSON SOFTc2006-12-4  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe game is made up of 8 different Special Stages, including highways, deserts, savannahs, and coastlines. Cross the finish line within the allotted stage time (plus any extra time) to successfully clear each stage. If the total time elapsed is less than the set stage time, you can progress to the next stage. Parts such as tires, gears, engines, suspension systems, and brakes can be custom fitted to the car to suit each type of race. Driving on rough courses and hitting obstacles will cause damage to individual parts, so making repairs is key. This means that making the right choices when customizing parts is very important, and incorporates a great simulation element into the game. Race from Paris to Dakar, while replacing parts at checkpoints along the way, in the Victory Run rally game.  i2006kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext00436na  a2200109   4500001000500000245003600005264002400041300002300065500018200088542003100270655002500301PAFJ00aVictory Run - Eikou no 13,000KM 1bHudson Softc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aWhen Victory Run made its way to the Turbo Grafx-16 in late 1980s, it stood out among racing games for gameplay that dove deeper than the arcade action of Rad Racer and Out Run.  i2014kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext00419na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001600005264002700021300002300048500018200071542003100253655002500284PAFP00aVictory Run 1bHudson Softc2006-12-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aWhen Victory Run made its way to the Turbo Grafx-16 in late 1980s, it stood out among racing games for gameplay that dove deeper than the arcade action of Rad Racer and Out Run.  i2006kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext00828na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264002400023300002300047500059200070542003100662655002500693PAGJ00aBomberman '94 1bHUDSON SOFTc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aBOMBERMAN has arrived to restore peace on the planet, which has been split into five parts by an evil hand! In addition to the nine members of the Bomber Family, the character ROOI shows up to lend a hand. Jump on the EGGS that appear from destroyed SOFT BLOCKS, and you can ride one of five types of ROOI. Each ROOI has different special abilities—use these well and you’ll ride to victory! Bombs that turn according to arrows and other new gimmicks have been added to BATTLE GAME, increased to ten stages. Tag-team matches are now possible, ensuring that this game will be a blast!  i2014kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00255na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264002700023300002300050500001600073542003100089655002500120PAGL00aBomberman '94 1bHudson Softc2009-7-10  a1 Wii optical disc  aNORMAL GAME  i2009kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00831na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264002700023300002300050500059200073542003100665655002500696PAGN00aBomberman '94 1bHUDSON SOFTc2009-3-23  a1 Wii optical disc  aBOMBERMAN has arrived to restore peace on the planet, which has been split into five parts by an evil hand! In addition to the nine members of the Bomber Family, the character ROOI shows up to lend a hand. Jump on the EGGS that appear from destroyed SOFT BLOCKS, and you can ride one of five types of ROOI. Each ROOI has different special abilities—use these well and you’ll ride to victory! Bombs that turn according to arrows and other new gimmicks have been added to BATTLE GAME, increased to ten stages. Tag-team matches are now possible, ensuring that this game will be a blast!  i2009kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00571na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002300005264002700028300002300055500032700078542003100405655002500436PAHE00aBattle Lode Runner 1bHUDSON SOFTc2007-4-23  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis upgraded edition to the famous Lode Runner series includes a 5-player versus mode. Gold funds have been stolen from the Time Machine Research Center, and the group responsible used a time machine to escape and hide the gold throughout time. The center sends an elite team of “Runners” to go and retrieve the gold.  i2007kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00295na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002300005264002400028300002300052500001700075542003100092655002500123655002500148PAHJ00aBattle Lode Runner 1bHudson Softc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aPuzzle mode:  i2014kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00344na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002300005264005000028300002300078500001700101542005400118655002500172655002500197PAHP00aBattle Lode Runner 1bHudson Soft / Hudson Entertainmentc2007-4-27  a1 Wii optical disc  aPuzzle mode:  i2007kHudson Soft / Hudson EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00634na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002500005264002700030300002300057500038500080542003100465655002800496PAIE00aNew Adventure Island 1bHUDSON SOFTc2007-2-19  a1 Wii optical disc  aWhile Master Higgins and Tina are leaving the church after getting married, a shadowy figure called Baron Bronsky and six of his underlings kidnap Tina and some of island children. The player controls Higgins through six stages with four areas each (the fourth area being a boss battle) to rescue the children, and then finally defeat Baron Bronsky in his fortress to rescue Tina.  i2007kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAdventure games2wiiext00704na  a2200121   4500001000500000245004100005264002400046300002300070500040600093542003100499655002500530655002700555PAIJ00aTakahashi Meijin no Shin Bouken Jima 1bHudson Softc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aSomewhere on the peaceful Adventure Island, Master Higgins weds Tina, the new Miss Island. Everyone who was invited to the wedding begins to celebrate when, suddenly, the evil Baron Bronsky appears and snatches Tina away, while his henchmen take the six children away. To reach his castle and rescue Tina, Master Higgins must first rescue the six children, each of whom is hidden on a separate island.  i2014kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00691na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002500005264002700030300002300057500040600080542003100486655002500517655002700542PAIP00aNew Adventure Island 1bHudson Softc2007-2-16  a1 Wii optical disc  aSomewhere on the peaceful Adventure Island, Master Higgins weds Tina, the new Miss Island. Everyone who was invited to the wedding begins to celebrate when, suddenly, the evil Baron Bronsky appears and snatches Tina away, while his henchmen take the six children away. To reach his castle and rescue Tina, Master Higgins must first rescue the six children, each of whom is hidden on a separate island.  i2007kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00187na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002500005264001300030300002300043500000500066542001800071PAJJ00aJaseiken Necromancer 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB01091na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001900005264002600024300002300050500080900073542003100882655002500913655003100938PAKE00aDragon's Curse 1bHUDSON SOFTc2007-4-2  a1 Wii optical disc  aAfter defeating the Mecha Dragon in the depths of the Dragon Castle, the wounded beast casts a spell on the hero, turning him into an ugly creature. To return to human form, he must find the Salamander Cross, which can break any curse. This side-scrolling action role-playing game is nonlinear, allowing players to venture freely. Collect gold and items while upgrading equipment and powering up stats. The hero starts as Lizard-Man but, upon defeating the dragon bosses, is changed into other creatures such as Mouse-Man, Piranha-Man, Tiger-Man and Hawk-Man. Each creature possesses distinct abilities such as the ability to fly, swim, walk on ceilings or cling to walls. Players use each creature's special skills to widen your search for the Salamander Cross and bring the hero back to his human form!  i2007kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00400na  a2200133   4500001000500000245002100005264002400026300002300050500008200073542003100155655002500186655002800211655002700239PAKJ00aAdventure Island 1bHudson Softc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe hero has been cursed and transformed into a creature by the Mecha Dragon.  i2014kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00447na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001900005264005000024300002300074500008200097542005400179655002500233655002800258655002700286PAKP00aDragon's Curse 1bHudson Soft / Hudson Entertainmentc2007-3-30  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe hero has been cursed and transformed into a creature by the Mecha Dragon.  i2007kHudson Soft / Hudson EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext01113na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264002600023300002300049500083700072542003100909655002500940655002600965PALE00aSoldier Blade 1bHUDSON SOFTc2007-1-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aA new shooter in the "Star Soldier" tradition. Players play as an SIA (Special Interception Airforce) pilot flying the heavy assault fighter "Soldier Blade." Players face the Zeograd invasion force with weapon attacks that change each time they grab a power-up item. Players can unleash three different kinds of attack depending on the color of the power-up item. New features, such as the "Gunbody" option for avoiding enemy attacks and the "Burst Out" system (which has a different effect depending on the power-up level), add a strategic element that requires players to make snap decisions about which items to grab and when to use special attacks. Awesome boss battles await players at the end of each operation. Playing in "CHALLENGE" mode requires players to try to get as many points as they can in a limited amount of time.  i2007kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext01111na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264002400023300002300047500083700070542003100907655002500938655002600963PALJ00aSoldier Blade 1bHudson Softc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aA new shooter in the "Star Soldier" tradition. Players play as an SIA (Special Interception Airforce) pilot flying the heavy assault fighter "Soldier Blade." Players face the Zeograd invasion force with weapon attacks that change each time they grab a power-up item. Players can unleash three different kinds of attack depending on the color of the power-up item. New features, such as the "Gunbody" option for avoiding enemy attacks and the "Burst Out" system (which has a different effect depending on the power-up level), add a strategic element that requires players to make snap decisions about which items to grab and when to use special attacks. Awesome boss battles await players at the end of each operation. Playing in "CHALLENGE" mode requires players to try to get as many points as they can in a limited amount of time.  i2014kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext01160na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264005000023300002300073500083700096542005400933655002500987655002601012PALP00aSoldier Blade 1bHudson Soft / Hudson Entertainmentc2007-1-26  a1 Wii optical disc  aA new shooter in the "Star Soldier" tradition. Players play as an SIA (Special Interception Airforce) pilot flying the heavy assault fighter "Soldier Blade." Players face the Zeograd invasion force with weapon attacks that change each time they grab a power-up item. Players can unleash three different kinds of attack depending on the color of the power-up item. New features, such as the "Gunbody" option for avoiding enemy attacks and the "Burst Out" system (which has a different effect depending on the power-up level), add a strategic element that requires players to make snap decisions about which items to grab and when to use special attacks. Awesome boss battles await players at the end of each operation. Playing in "CHALLENGE" mode requires players to try to get as many points as they can in a limited amount of time.  i2007kHudson Soft / Hudson EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext01023na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001300005264002700018300002300045500074600068542003100814655002500845655003100870PAME00aNeutopia 1bHUDSON SOFTc2007-8-20  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn this action role-playing game, you take control of a brave boy who sets off on a journey to rescue the kidnapped princess and reclaim the eight medallions that were stolen by the evil demon, Dirth. You'll need to rely on your magic compass and information you've gathered to find entrances to labyrinths and defeat the bosses in them. Solve puzzles, avoid traps, move blocks and destroy walls to uncover secret rooms in the labyrinths. Carefully use your map to uncover hidden treasure and powerful equipment. Travel the land, underground, sea and sky on your quest to recover the medallions. With a save function, the right difficulty level and a system that doesn't include experience points, this is truly an RPG that anyone can enjoy.  i2007kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00395na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002800005264002400033300002300057500010600080542003100186655002500217655003100242PAMJ00aNeutopia - Frey no Shou 1bHudson Softc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aTake back the 8 medallions that were taken by the evil demon Dirth and rescue the kidnapped princess!  i2014kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00429na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001300005264005000018300002300068500010600091542005400197655002500251655003100276PAMP00aNeutopia 1bHudson Soft / Hudson Entertainmentc2007-8-24  a1 Wii optical disc  aTake back the 8 medallions that were taken by the evil demon Dirth and rescue the kidnapped princess!  i2007kHudson Soft / Hudson EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00881na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002100005264002800026300002300054500063600077542003100713655002700744PANE00aMilitary Madness 1bHUDSON SOFTc2006-12-18  a1 Wii optical disc  aMilitary Madness is a futuristic simulation game that throws the player into the middle of a war on the moon's surface. The rules are simple, making it easy for newcomers to enjoy the thrills of this war-strategy game. Players can see easy-to-understand, detailed instructions from the Title screen. Military Madness is also turn-based, allowing players to devise their strategy before they move. To top it off, the units players have for each stage are already decided, allowing them to concentrate on commanding. Use the terrain and surround enemies to claim victory. Fight through all 16 stages and thwart the enemy's ambitions!  i2006kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aStrategy games2wiiext00318na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001300005264002400018300002300042500008500065542003100150655002700181PANJ00aNectaris 1bHudson Softc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aYou start out with units (troops) and control them to progress through the game.  i2014kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aStrategy games2wiiext00330na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002100005264002800026300002300054500008500077542003100162655002700193PANP00aMilitary Madness 1bHudson Softc2006-12-22  a1 Wii optical disc  aYou start out with units (troops) and control them to progress through the game.  i2006kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aStrategy games2wiiext01013na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264002400023300002300047500073900070542003100809655002500840655002600865PAOJ00aFinal Soldier 1bHUDSON SOFTc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aA vertically scrolling shooter from the well-known Soldier series. In the 23rd century, invaders from the future suddenly attack Earth. Controlling a fighter created by the world’s scientists, you rise to meet the enemy. Collect power-up units, such as LASER, E-BEAM, FIRE, and MISSILE, and then equip them in Options to launch a variety of attacks. For each of these weapons, you can freely select from three different types in SET-UP. Anticipate enemies’ strikes and deftly switch between weapons to defeat the invaders! In addition to NORMAL GAME, there are also 2 MINUTE GAME and 5 MINUTE GAME score-attack modes. The most perfect blend and balance of any game in the series, Final Soldier is a title you don’t want to miss.  i2014kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00409na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264004900023300002300072500008700095542005400182655002500236655002600261PAOL00aFinal Soldier 1bHudson Soft / Hudson Entertainmentc2008-5-2  a1 Wii optical disc  aMove through the levels defeating enemies. Clear the level by destroying the boss.  i2008kHudson Soft / Hudson EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext01015na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264002600023300002300049500073900072542003100811655002500842655002600867PAON00aFinal Soldier 1bHUDSON SOFTc2008-9-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aA vertically scrolling shooter from the well-known Soldier series. In the 23rd century, invaders from the future suddenly attack Earth. Controlling a fighter created by the world’s scientists, you rise to meet the enemy. Collect power-up units, such as LASER, E-BEAM, FIRE, and MISSILE, and then equip them in Options to launch a variety of attacks. For each of these weapons, you can freely select from three different types in SET-UP. Anticipate enemies’ strikes and deftly switch between weapons to defeat the invaders! In addition to NORMAL GAME, there are also 2 MINUTE GAME and 5 MINUTE GAME score-attack modes. The most perfect blend and balance of any game in the series, Final Soldier is a title you don’t want to miss.  i2008kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00176na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001400005264001300019300002300032500000500055542001800060PAPJ00aR-Type II 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00174na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001200005264001300017300002300030500000500053542001800058PAQJ00aGradius 1bc2012--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2012sGameTDB00899na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264002100026300002300047500063000070542002600700655002500726655002600751PARJ00aDetana!! TwinBee 1bKonamic2012-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aIt’s the popular vertical-scrolling shooter renowned for its cute and comical world. Here come Twinbee and Winbee on a mission to save the planet from evil alien invaders! Standing in their way are six stages full of goofy enemies! Play as Twinbee in one-player mode, or team up with Winbee in two-player-cooperative mode. With powerful attacks like Big Shot, or Twin Attack and Burst Attack in two-player mode, there’s plenty of sting in their arsenal! Use your Shot to transform Bells that appear in stages into items with various effects. Stock up on these bad boys to expand your attack range and really have a blast!  i2012kKonamisGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00365na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264002200026300002300048500009500071542002600166655002500192655002600217PARL00aDetana!! TwinBee 1bKonamic2009-7-24  a1 Wii optical disc  aOne day, an SOS from a distant planet arrives at the island where Twinbee and Winbee live.  i2009kKonamisGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00900na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264002200026300002300048500063000071542002600701655002500727655002600752PARN00aDetana!! TwinBee 1bKonamic2009-3-23  a1 Wii optical disc  aIt’s the popular vertical-scrolling shooter renowned for its cute and comical world. Here come Twinbee and Winbee on a mission to save the planet from evil alien invaders! Standing in their way are six stages full of goofy enemies! Play as Twinbee in one-player mode, or team up with Winbee in two-player-cooperative mode. With powerful attacks like Big Shot, or Twin Attack and Burst Attack in two-player mode, there’s plenty of sting in their arsenal! Use your Shot to transform Bells that appear in stages into items with various effects. Stock up on these bad boys to expand your attack range and really have a blast!  i2009kKonamisGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00173na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001100005264001300016300002300029500000500052542001800057PASJ00aCadash 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00178na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001600005264001300021300002300034500000500057542001800062PATJ00aKiKi KaiKai 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00195na  a2200097   4500001000500000245003100005264001500036300002300051500000500074542001800079PAUJ00aKaizou Choujin Shubibinman 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00880na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001400005264002600019300002300045500064600068542003100714655002500745PAVE00aVigilante 1bHUDSON SOFTc2007-2-5  a1 Wii optical disc  aBrave the streets of New York City in this side-scrolling beat-'em-up game. Thugs kidnap the beloved Madonna, and it's up to players to become vigilantes. Players fight their way into enemy territory to get her back. Enemies attack with weapons like iron pipes, chains, guns and motorcycles. To fight back, players can punch, kick or use the "nunchaku" item that appears in the stage. Players must use each of the attacks effectively to defeat their enemies. To clear a stage, defeat the boss that waits at the end. Players fight their way through exciting stages that include the City Streets, Junkyard, Brooklyn Bridge and the Backstreets.  i2007kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00704na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001400005264002600019300002300045500038700068542003300455655002500488655002700513655003000540PAVJ00aVigilante 1bIrem Softwarec2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aBrave the streets of New York City in this side-scrolling beat-'em-up game. Thugs kidnap the beloved Madonna, and it's up to players to become vigilantes. Players fight their way into enemy territory to get her back. Enemies attack with weapons like iron pipes, chains, guns and motorcycles. To fight back, players can punch, kick or use the nunchaku item that appears in the stage.  i2014kIrem SoftwaresGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext00706na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001400005264002800019300002300047500038700070542003300457655002500490655002700515655003000542PAVP00aVigilante 1bIrem Softwarec2007-2-9  a1 Wii optical disc  aBrave the streets of New York City in this side-scrolling beat-'em-up game. Thugs kidnap the beloved Madonna, and it's up to players to become vigilantes. Players fight their way into enemy territory to get her back. Enemies attack with weapons like iron pipes, chains, guns and motorcycles. To fight back, players can punch, kick or use the nunchaku item that appears in the stage.  i2007kIrem SoftwaresGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext00937na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001500005264001900020300002300039500067800062542002400740655002500764655002600789PAWE00aGalaga '90 1bNBGIc2007-8-6  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis is an updated version of the classic arcade shooter Galaga. Set in the vast reaches of space, you will fight your way through all 29 rounds to reach the enemies' stronghold on Planet Galaga. Game levels consist of a few rounds with changing enemies and backgrounds. To top it off, the nostalgic "Galactic Dancing" lives on to mark the end of each level. With the new addition of dimensions, you can choose your attack route. Collect capsules and open dimension warps at branch sections to take on even tougher enemies. GALAGA '90's inclusion of the triple fighter, scrolling backgrounds, boss Galaga and even new system effects make it nothing less than a masterpiece.  i2007kNBGIsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00365na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001500005264003100020300002300051500008000074542003800154655002500192655002600217PAWJ00aGalaga '88 1bNamco Bandai Gamesc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aDrive back the continuous onslaught of The Galaga Corps with your missiles.  i2014kNamco Bandai GamessGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00368na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001500005264003400020300002300054500008000077542003800157655002500195655002600220PAWP00aGalaga '90 1bNamco Bandai Gamesc2007-8-10  a1 Wii optical disc  aDrive back the continuous onslaught of The Galaga Corps with your missiles.  i2007kNamco Bandai GamessGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00187na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002500005264001300030300002300043500000500066542001800071PAYJ00aValkyrie no Densetsu 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00182na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002000005264001300025300002300038500000500061542001800066PAZJ00aGenpei Toumaden 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00987na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001600005264002700021300002300048500070700071542003100778655002500809655003100834PB2E00aNeutopia II 1bHUDSON SOFTc2007-9-10  a1 Wii optical disc  aExperience improved graphics and controls in this exciting sequel to the action RPG Neutopia. Take on the role of the main hero’s son and watch as the story begins with the apparent revival of Dirth, the evil demon. Once again you’ll need to rely on your magic compass and the information you’ve gathered to find entrances to labyrinths and defeat the bosses in them. Make your way through the field, which can be tricky at times, to search for and find hidden information and items, or move blocks and destroy walls to uncover secret rooms. Like the original, this game has a save function, a finely tuned difficulty level, and a fast-paced story, making it truly an RPG that everyone can enjoy.  i2007kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00759na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001600005264002400021300002300045500048200068542003100550655002500581655003100606PB2J00aNeutopia II 1bHudson Softc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aSome years have passed since the brave hero Jazeta destroyed Dirth, the Emperor of Darkness. Peace has returned to the land of Neutopia. But there are still monsters roaming the countryside, and some of them were spotted near Yurius Shrine. Jazeta went there to find out what exactly had happened. But he didn't return. You are Jazeta's son, and you must first of all find your missing father! Can it be that the shadow of Emperor of Darkness threatens the peaceful land again?  i2014kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00762na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001600005264002700021300002300048500048200071542003100553655002500584655003100609PB2P00aNeutopia II 1bHudson Softc2007-9-14  a1 Wii optical disc  aSome years have passed since the brave hero Jazeta destroyed Dirth, the Emperor of Darkness. Peace has returned to the land of Neutopia. But there are still monsters roaming the countryside, and some of them were spotted near Yurius Shrine. Jazeta went there to find out what exactly had happened. But he didn't return. You are Jazeta's son, and you must first of all find your missing father! Can it be that the shadow of Emperor of Darkness threatens the peaceful land again?  i2007kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00852na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264002700023300002300050500057500073542003100648655002500679655002600704PB3E00aDevil's Crush 1bHUDSON SOFTc2007-7-23  a1 Wii optical disc  aDevil's Crush is the exciting sequel to the hit pinball game Alien Crush and features even smoother ball movement and enhanced special effects. Shoot the ball onto the board with the Devil Shooter, then use flippers and nudging to keep it in play and rack up a high score. Complete certain conditions to play up to six different bonus stages. Get a "Perfect Clear" on those to earn a huge amount of points. The game's ominous theme is enhanced by its enemies: wandering skeleton knights, sorcerers and even a giant face that changes from a goddess to a sinister serpent.  i2007kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aArcade games2wiiext 7aPinball games2wiiext00847na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001600005264002400021300002300045500057500068542003100643655002500674655002600699PB3J00aDevil Crash 1bHudson Softc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aDevil's Crush is the exciting sequel to the hit pinball game Alien Crush and features even smoother ball movement and enhanced special effects. Shoot the ball onto the board with the Devil Shooter, then use flippers and nudging to keep it in play and rack up a high score. Complete certain conditions to play up to six different bonus stages. Get a "Perfect Clear" on those to earn a huge amount of points. The game's ominous theme is enhanced by its enemies: wandering skeleton knights, sorcerers and even a giant face that changes from a goddess to a sinister serpent.  i2014kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aArcade games2wiiext 7aPinball games2wiiext00898na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264005000023300002300073500057500096542005400671655002500725655002600750PB3P00aDevil's Crush 1bHudson Soft / Hudson Entertainmentc2007-7-27  a1 Wii optical disc  aDevil's Crush is the exciting sequel to the hit pinball game Alien Crush and features even smoother ball movement and enhanced special effects. Shoot the ball onto the board with the Devil Shooter, then use flippers and nudging to keep it in play and rack up a high score. Complete certain conditions to play up to six different bonus stages. Get a "Perfect Clear" on those to earn a huge amount of points. The game's ominous theme is enhanced by its enemies: wandering skeleton knights, sorcerers and even a giant face that changes from a goddess to a sinister serpent.  i2007kHudson Soft / Hudson EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aArcade games2wiiext 7aPinball games2wiiext00182na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002000005264001300025300002300038500000500061542001800066PB5J00aNinja Ryukenden 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB01007na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001500005264002700020300002300047500077100070542003100841655002500872PB6E00aCratermaze 1bHUDSON SOFTc2007-8-13  a1 Wii optical disc  aCratermaze is a comical action game set in a parallel world. While on a trip through time, you and your friends are confronted by Kublai, henchman to the evil Zenzombie. He traps your friends at separate points in the space-time continuum. Now you must fight your way through 60 rounds of mazes to save your friends. Dinosaurs, ninjas, robots and other enemies lurk within the mazes, spanning from primitive times to the future. Escape the enemies by digging holes to trap them in and then filling the holes to finish them off. Collect all the chests within the time limit to get the key and exit to the next round. With special items such as shovels and spring platforms, Cratermaze takes its game play to new heights, making for an unforgettable gaming experience.  i2007kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00379na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001500005264002700020300002300047500014300070542003100213655002500244PB6P00aCratermaze 1bHudson Softc2007-8-17  a1 Wii optical disc  aWhile on a journey through time on a "magic carpet ship", you and your friends are suddenly attacked by "Kublai", a minion of "Zenzombie".  i2007kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00182na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002000005264001300025300002300038500000500061542001800066PB7J00aSengoku Mahjong 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00975na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001900005264002700024300002300051500069700074542003100771655002500802655002600827PB8E00aBlazing Lazers 1bHUDSON SOFTc2007-5-21  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe player takes control of the Gunhed Star Fighter through nine vertically-scrolling areas. The player's mission is to destroy the Dark Squadron and its eight enemy Super Weapons. Every area contains one or more bosses, all of which must be destroyed before continuing in the game. Players lose a life if they are hit by an enemy or projectile, with the game continuing at a previously–crossed checkpoint. The game ends when all lives have been lost, but the game awards 1-ups when the player scores a particular number of points. The game provides four continues in which players can restart the game at that level in which their previous game ended provided the system is not turned off.  i2007kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00364na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001900005264002400024300002300048500008900071542003100160655002500191655002600216PB8J00aBlazing Lazers 1bHudson Softc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aControl your ship and use power-up weapons and bombs to get to the end of each area.  i2014kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00367na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001900005264002700024300002300051500008900074542003100163655002500194655002600219PB8P00aBlazing Lazers 1bHudson Softc2007-5-25  a1 Wii optical disc  aControl your ship and use power-up weapons and bombs to get to the end of each area.  i2007kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00927na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002900005264002700034300002300061500064000084542003100724655002500755655002500780PB9E00aWorld Sports Competition 1bHUDSON SOFTc2007-6-18  a1 Wii optical disc  aPlay through a total of 18 Olympic events in this action/sports title. Players compete in six categories of events that include shooting, archery, rowing, swimming and track and field. The game features Olympics mode, where you play all the events over the course of a few days, and Training mode, where you can choose individual events to play. After practicing in Training mode, go for the gold in Olympics mode and break world records. Depending on your play time and ability, you can enjoy the game a number of different ways. Gather friends and play in competitions with up to five players to get even more out of this great game.  i2007kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aSports games2wiiext00516na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001700005264002400022300002300046500028100069542003100350655002500381PB9J00aPower Sports 1bHudson Softc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aOriginally released in 1992, World Sports Competition brought the spirit of the summer Olympic games home to the TurboGrafx-16. Featuring 6 different sports, and over 18 events, World Sports Competition offers a unique compilation of diverse, exciting summer games and sports.  i2014kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext00530na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002900005264002600034300002300060500028100083542003100364655002500395PB9P00aWorld Sports Competition 1bHudson Softc2007-6-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aOriginally released in 1992, World Sports Competition brought the spirit of the summer Olympic games home to the TurboGrafx-16. Featuring 6 different sports, and over 18 events, World Sports Competition offers a unique compilation of diverse, exciting summer games and sports.  i2007kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext01058na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264001900023300002300042500079600065542002400861655002500885655002600910PBAE00aDragon Spirit 1bNBGIc2007-7-2  a1 Wii optical disc  aA fantastic world of adventure unfolds in this vertical-scrolling shooter. Sealed away by the gods long ago, the Evil Demon of Darkness, Zawell, seeks to rise again and unleash a new reign of evil. The brave warrior Amur races to rescue Princess Alicia from the demon's wretched clutches. Amur takes the form of the legendary Blue Dragon and fights his way through the legions of monsters that await in the sky. Battle your way through eight different areas, using your Dragon Breath to bring down airborne targets and Fireballs to wipe out targets on the ground. Destroy flashing enemies and smash Eggs to uncover different kinds of power-up items. Boost your firepower by increasing the number of heads your dragon has, and defeat all the bosses as you make your way to Zawell's dark lair.  i2007kNBGIsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00370na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264003100023300002300054500008200077542003800159655002500197655002600222PBAJ00aDragon Spirit 1bNamco Bandai Gamesc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe player controls Amur, a brave warrior who transformed into a Blue Dragon.  i2014kNamco Bandai GamessGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00372na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264003300023300002300056500008200079542003800161655002500199655002600224PBAP00aDragon Spirit 1bNamco Bandai Gamesc2007-7-6  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe player controls Amur, a brave warrior who transformed into a Blue Dragon.  i2007kNamco Bandai GamessGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00178na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001600005264001300021300002300034500000500057542001800062PBCJ00aWonder-Momo 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB01052na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002000005264002700025300002300052500080500075542003100880655003100911PBDE00aDouble Dungeons 1bHUDSON SOFTc2007-3-12  a1 Wii optical disc  aDouble Dungeons is a dungeon role-playing game that features smooth-scrolling 3-D game play. Two players can play at the same time, which makes this game truly stand out from the rest. There are 22 unique scenarios, spread out among six levels. The higher the level is, the harder the scenario. Because each scenario is independent, players can choose to start the game from any scenario other than the final one. Players defeat monsters in each dungeon to gain experience while searching for the "key" that opens the door to the room with the boss. They buy equipment at the shop, team up with characters and defeat the boss to clear a scenario. Players must conquer all 21 scenarios from levels 1 through 5 to obtain passwords. If they obtain all of them, they make their way to the final scenario!  i2007kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00312na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002000005264002400025300002300049500006800072542003100140655003100171PBDJ00aDouble Dungeons 1bHudson Softc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aRaise your level by exploring the DUNGEON and slaying monsters.  i2014kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00314na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002000005264002600025300002300051500006800074542003100142655003100173PBDP00aDouble Dungeons 1bHudson Softc2007-3-9  a1 Wii optical disc  aRaise your level by exploring the DUNGEON and slaying monsters.  i2007kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00950na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001600005264002700021300002300048500071300071542003100784655002500815PBEE00aMoto Roader 1bHUDSON SOFTc2007-1-15  a1 Wii optical disc  aMoto Roader is a futuristic racing game that allows up to five players to compete against each other. Players use the cash earned when they win a race to power up their machine. Not only can they change the "TIRE" and "BODY" of their vehicles, but they also can add "SPECIAL" parts. Jump over tall obstacles with a "HOPPER" and blast past rivals at incredible speeds with "NITRO." What multiplayer game would be complete without attack items? Use a forward-launching "GRENADE" or a backward-dropping "BOMBER" to blow up and knock away rivals. Outmaneuver rivals in all eight heats to become the champion. Any combination of Wii Remote™ and Nintendo GameCube™ controllers can be used in multiplayer games.  i2007kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext00314na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001600005264002400021300002300045500008000068542003100148655002500179PBEJ00aMoto Roader 1bHudson Softc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aCompete in all 8 races while powering up your vehicle with different parts.  i2014kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext00316na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001600005264002600021300002300047500008000070542003100150655002500181PBEP00aMoto Roader 1bHudson Softc2007-1-5  a1 Wii optical disc  aCompete in all 8 races while powering up your vehicle with different parts.  i2007kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext00202na  a2200097   4500001000500000245004000005264001300045300002300058500000500081542001800086PBFJ00aFire ProWrestling - Combination Tag 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB01048na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001900005264005000024300002300074500076200097542005400859655002500913PBHE00aBonk's Revenge 1bHudson Soft / Hudson Entertainmentc2007-4-16  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe "hardheaded” hero is back for more in the 2nd installment of the Bonk series. Taking place in the Monster Kingdom, Bonk the Caveman makes his way toward King Drool III. Bonk’s Revenge is a side-scrolling action game in which you Jump and “Bonk” (headbutt) your enemies while you make your way to the goal at the end of each stage. Double, even triple, your attack power by eating the meat that appears in a stage. There are 8 different hidden bonus stages, and the Dinosaur Train that appears after you defeat a boss will change depending on how many Smileys you’ve collected. With new actions such as the Triangle Jump and the ability to climb trees, as well as 7 variety–packed stages, Bonk’s Revenge will keep you playing over and over.  i2007kHudson Soft / Hudson EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00606na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001600005264002400021300002300045500033300068542003100401655002500432655002700457PBHJ00aPC Genjin 2 1bHudson Softc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn this follow-up to Bonk's Adventure, Bonk must again battle King Drool and save the moon and Princess Za, but this time in a land infested with Chikkuns, the egg shell-helmeted enemies. The game featured brighter and more cartoony graphics and sound, more in line with the comic strip, and greatly influences later Bonk games.  i2014kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00658na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001900005264005000024300002300074500033300097542005400430655002500484655002700509PBHP00aBonk's Revenge 1bHudson Soft / Hudson Entertainmentc2007-4-13  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn this follow-up to Bonk's Adventure, Bonk must again battle King Drool and save the moon and Princess Za, but this time in a land infested with Chikkuns, the egg shell-helmeted enemies. The game featured brighter and more cartoony graphics and sound, more in line with the comic strip, and greatly influences later Bonk games.  i2007kHudson Soft / Hudson EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext01017na  a2200109   4500001000500000245003400005264002600039300002300065500076300088542003100851655002500882PBIE00aBonk 3 - Bonk's Big Adventure 1bHUDSON SOFTc2007-9-3  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe hard-headed hero is back for more side-scrolling action in the third installment of the popular Bonk series. It's up to Bonk once again to thwart the plans of the relentless evil King Drool. There are seven rounds scattered throughout the Dinosaur Kingdom, each one filled with fun contraptions and comical enemies. Grab a Flower Copter or exchange 16 Smileys at the end of each round to play up to eight different bonus stages. Or you can change the size of Bonk by grabbing the new red or blue candy items. Depending on the situation, you can change your size to bonk your way through a dead end or to get a hard-to-reach item. And if that's not enough, you can grab a friend and put your heads together to defeat King Drool in the new two-player mode.  i2007kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00357na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001600005264002400021300002300045500008400068542003100152655002500183655002700208PBIJ00aPC Genjin 3 1bHudson Softc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn the Dinosaur Kingdom, the moon, which had been previously restored, has been  i2014kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00378na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003400005264002700039300002300066500008400089542003100173655002500204655002700229PBIP00aBonk 3 - Bonk's Big Adventure 1bHudson Softc2007-8-31  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn the Dinosaur Kingdom, the moon, which had been previously restored, has been  i2007kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00994na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264002100023300002300044500076800067542002400835655002500859PBJE00aSamurai Ghost 1bNBGIc2007-10-29  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis action platformer features a samurai ghost, back from the depths of the underworld. In a past war, Kagekiyo managed to defeat the shogun Yoritomo and his clan. However, their evil spirits were not completely destroyed, and now, in the world known as Dark Side, they seek the time of their rebirth. In order to shatter those ambitions, Kagekiyo must make his way across seven zones and head for “The Heart of the Darkside” where Yoritomo lies in wait. Use spirit weapons to power up your sword or other items, such as candles to recover health, and defeat the endless hordes of enemies. Each zone is not only protected by a boss but also includes demons as well as real samurai from 12th-century Japan! Get ready for some intense one-on-one combat action!  i2007kNBGIsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00757na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003200005264003100037300002300068500045400091542003800545655002500583655002700608PBJJ00aGenpei Toumaden - Kan no Ni 1bNamco Bandai Gamesc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis action platformer features a samurai ghost from the depths of the underworld. In a past war, Kagekiyo managed to defeat the shogun Yoritomo and his clan. However, their evil spirits were not completely destroyed, and now, in the world known as Dark Side, they seek the time of their rebirth. In order to shatter those ambitions, Kagekiyo must make his way across seven zones and head for "The Heart of the Darkside" where Yoritomo lies in wait.  i2014kNamco Bandai GamessGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00746na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264003400023300002300057500045400080542003800534655002500572655002700597PBJP00aSamurai Ghost 1bNamco Bandai Gamesc2007-11-2  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis action platformer features a samurai ghost from the depths of the underworld. In a past war, Kagekiyo managed to defeat the shogun Yoritomo and his clan. However, their evil spirits were not completely destroyed, and now, in the world known as Dark Side, they seek the time of their rebirth. In order to shatter those ambitions, Kagekiyo must make his way across seven zones and head for "The Heart of the Darkside" where Yoritomo lies in wait.  i2007kNamco Bandai GamessGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00857na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002500005264002000030300002300050500062500073542002400698655002500722PBME00aLegend of Hero Tonma 1bIREMc2007-9-24  a1 Wii optical disc  aLEGEND OF HERO TONMA is an action game that puts players in control of the magic user Tonma whose role--as was typical for game heroes of the day--is to travel to another world and save the princess. Fight your way through seven stages using Tonma’s jump ability and shot power. Collect power-ups and barriers to grow in strength and pummel your enemies. Bring that strength to the end of each stage to face off against and defeat the menacing bosses that aim to keep you from the princess. This well-detailed game’s comic visuals and feel will have players wanting to come back for more frantic and exciting action.  i2007kIREMsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00408na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002500005264002600030300002300056500012200079542003300201655002500234655002700259PBMJ00aLegend of Hero Tonma 1bIrem Softwarec2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aOne day, "Tonma", a pupil under the tutelage of the magician "Merlin", hears the voice of a princess asking for help.  i2014kIrem SoftwaresGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00411na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002500005264002900030300002300059500012200082542003300204655002500237655002700262PBMP00aLegend of Hero Tonma 1bIrem Softwarec2007-9-28  a1 Wii optical disc  aOne day, "Tonma", a pupil under the tutelage of the magician "Merlin", hears the voice of a princess asking for help.  i2007kIrem SoftwaresGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext01011na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001700005264002000022300002300042500078700065542002400852655002500876PBNE00aNinja Spirit 1bIREMc2007-5-14  a1 Wii optical disc  aNinja Spirit is a side-scrolling action game that amazed the gaming world with its precision graphics and quality game play. Play as the ninja Moonlight and engage in a fierce battle to avenge his father’s death and unlock the secrets of his birth. Select between the original ARCADE MODE and PC-ENGINE MODE, which includes a life gauge. Use four types of weapons: katana, shuriken, bombs and chain and sickles to battle your way through the enemies. Pick up power-up items and switch between weapons to give you the advantage. You’ll need to consider the enemy attacks and your weapon’s abilities in order to deftly make it through all seven stages. Use your skills and attacks to get through the game’s boundless enemies and traps. That’s what ninja action is all about.  i2007kIREMsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00638na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003500005264002600040300002300066500034200089542003300431655002500464655002700489PBNJ00aSaigo no Nindou - Ninja Spirit 1bIrem Softwarec2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aNinja Spirit is a side-scrolling action game that amazed the gaming world with its precision graphics and quality game play. Play as the ninja Moonlight and engage in a fierce battle to avenge his father's death and unlock the secrets of his birth. Select between the original arcade mode and PC Engine mode, which includes a life gauge.  i2014kIrem SoftwaresGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00623na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001700005264002900022300002300051500034200074542003300416655002500449655002700474PBNP00aNinja Spirit 1bIrem Softwarec2007-5-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aNinja Spirit is a side-scrolling action game that amazed the gaming world with its precision graphics and quality game play. Play as the ninja Moonlight and engage in a fierce battle to avenge his father's death and unlock the secrets of his birth. Select between the original arcade mode and PC Engine mode, which includes a life gauge.  i2007kIrem SoftwaresGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext01017na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001600005264002700021300002300048500074300071542003100814655002500845655002500870PBSE00aChew-Man-Fu 1bHUDSON SOFTc2007-2-26  a1 Wii optical disc  aA novel action-puzzle game set in the sacred towers taken over by the evil sorcerer, Chew Man Fu. It's up to you as an apprentice female monk to free the towers and lift Chew's curse to bring peace and fried rice back to the land once ruled by the Egg Roll Dynasty. The rules are simple! Your objective is to clear each round by pushing or pulling four colored orbs onto their matching colored tiles. Beware the sorcerer's minions in the tower who stand in your way! Kick the orbs to take your enemies out or to break down walls! Overcome the obstacles and place the orbs on their respective tiles! Chew Man Fu also features the 2-player Kick Ball minigame, as well as an Edit Mode for creating your own unique stages! The fun is endless!  i2007kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00460na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001200005264002600017300002300043500022800066542003100294655002500325PBSJ00aBe Ball 1bHudson Softc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe sacred towers containing the treasures of the Master Monk have been taken over by the mysterious sorcerer Chew Man Fu. To reclaim them from the sorcerer's control, two apprentice monks must make their way up the towers.  i2014kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00464na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001600005264002600021300002300047500022800070542003100298655002500329PBSP00aChew-Man-Fu 1bHudson Softc2007-3-2  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe sacred towers containing the treasures of the Master Monk have been taken over by the mysterious sorcerer Chew Man Fu. To reclaim them from the sorcerer's control, two apprentice monks must make their way up the towers.  i2007kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00923na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264002700023300002300050500068400073542003100757655002500788PBTE00aChina Warrior 1bHUDSON SOFTc2007-6-25  a1 Wii optical disc  aChina Warrior is a side-scrolling action game that was released around the same time as the TurboGrafx16 in Japan. It's up to the kung fu master Wang to defeat the Dark Emperor, who stands atop the kung fu world in China. Punch, kick and jump-kick enemies along the path that lies between you and the three bosses of each stage. Skillfully fight your way through all four stages, and be sure not to miss recovery items while dodging enemy attacks. China Warrior boasts character size and detail that rivaled all other games at the time of its release. Exciting one-on-one fights against the game's realistic bosses will make you feel like you're in the middle of a kung fu movie.  i2007kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00380na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001600005264002400021300002300045500006500068542003100133655002500164655002700189655003000216PBTJ04aThe Kung Fu 1bHudson Softc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aYou're a Kung Fu master out to defeat the evil Dark Emperor.  i2014kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext00431na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001800005264005000023300002300073500006500096542005400161655002500215655002700240655003000267PBTP00aChina Warrior 1bHudson Soft / Hudson Entertainmentc2007-6-22  a1 Wii optical disc  aYou're a Kung Fu master out to defeat the evil Dark Emperor.  i2007kHudson Soft / Hudson EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext00997na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001300005264002600018300002300044500076400067542003100831655002500862PBUE00aBravoman 1bHUDSON SOFTc2007-4-9  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe village of Nitta has been invaded by the army of Dr. Bomb, an evil scientist who is plotting to take over the world. Facing this crisis is Bravoman, who received his powers from Alpha Man to stand up against Dr. Bomb in the name of justice. The village of Nitta consists of 22 stages - action stages that take place on the ground and shooting stages that take place underwater. Action stages use a unique control system in which the height of a jump and the distance of an attack changes depending on how long players hold down the button. Players collect the Luck Symbols that appear when they defeat enemies and give them to Lottery Man to get recovery and power-up items. Stop Dr. Bomb and bring peace to the village of Nitta and the rest of the world.  i2007kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext01011na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002900005264002400034300002300058500076400081542003100845655002500876PBUJ00aChouzetsurinjin Bravoman 1bHUDSON SOFTc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe village of Nitta has been invaded by the army of Dr. Bomb, an evil scientist who is plotting to take over the world. Facing this crisis is Bravoman, who received his powers from Alpha Man to stand up against Dr. Bomb in the name of justice. The village of Nitta consists of 22 stages - action stages that take place on the ground and shooting stages that take place underwater. Action stages use a unique control system in which the height of a jump and the distance of an attack changes depending on how long players hold down the button. Players collect the Luck Symbols that appear when they defeat enemies and give them to Lottery Man to get recovery and power-up items. Stop Dr. Bomb and bring peace to the village of Nitta and the rest of the world.  i2014kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00180na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001800005264001300023300002300036500000500059542001800064PBVJ00aBenkei Gaiden 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB01024na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001300005264002600018300002300044500075300067542003100820655002500851655002600876PBWE00aAir Zonk 1bHUDSON SOFTc2007-7-9  a1 Wii optical disc  aAir “Zonk” is a spin-off of the popular Bonk’s Adventure series. This side-scrolling shooter retains the same cartoonish style of Bonk, but is set in a cyberpunkesque future. The powered-up Zonk gathers his friends to form Team Cool, and they set out to stop King Drool’s plan to conquer the world. Choose from 3 levels of difficulty and 3 types of Friend Modes. Shoot King Drool's cyber robots and avoid their attacks while collecting the Air Bones to unleash a variety of attacks. Enjoy unique moves such as combining with a friend to create an invincible hybrid form or blasting enemies with a charged attack. Air “Zonk” is filled with humor, like its wacky theme song that plays when you post a huge score or when your game is over.  i2007kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00312na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003100005264002400036300002300060500002500083542003100108655002500139655002600164PBWJ00aPC Denjin - Punkic Cyborgs 1bHudson Softc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe year is 2999 AD.  i2014kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00297na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001300005264002700018300002300045500002500068542003100093655002500124655002600149PBWP00aAir Zonk 1bHudson Softc2007-7-13  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe year is 2999 AD.  i2007kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext01033na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001300005264002700018300002300045500076100068542003100829655002500860655002600885PBXE00aShockman 1bHUDSON SOFTc2007-4-30  a1 Wii optical disc  aIt's been two years since Arnold and Sonya were made into Shockmen. A message from the professor to return to their bodies has them head to his laboratory, but they are ambushed by a mysterious enemy along the way. After narrowly defeating the enemy, they catch a TV news flash announcing the Ryo Empire invasion. They find that the professor has been abducted and set out to rescue him. Shockman is a side-view action shooter that has eight stages, including Action Stages, where you jump and use special techniques, and side-scrolling Shooting Stages. This game expands on the well-paced story from the previous version and contains cooperative elements like shared life and a powerful Team Shockbeam that can be used during two-player simultaneous play.  i2007kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00737na  a2200133   4500001000500000245005000005264002400055300002300079500039200102542003100494655002500525655002700550655002600577PBXJ00aKaizou Choujin Shubibinman 2 - Aratanaru Teki 1bHudson Softc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aIt's been two years since Arnold and Sonya were made into Shockmen. A message from the professor to return to their bodies has them head to his laboratory, but they are ambushed by a mysterious enemy along the way. After narrowly defeating the enemy, they catch a TV news flash announcing the Ryo Empire invasion. They find that the professor has been abducted and set out to rescue him.  i2014kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00748na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001300005264004900018300002300067500039200090542005400482655002500536655002700561655002600588PBXP00aShockman 1bHudson Soft / Hudson Entertainmentc2007-5-4  a1 Wii optical disc  aIt's been two years since Arnold and Sonya were made into Shockmen. A message from the professor to return to their bodies has them head to his laboratory, but they are ambushed by a mysterious enemy along the way. After narrowly defeating the enemy, they catch a TV news flash announcing the Ryo Empire invasion. They find that the professor has been abducted and set out to rescue him.  i2007kHudson Soft / Hudson EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00175na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001300005264001300018300002300031500000500054542001800059PBYJ00aOut Live 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB01014na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001600005264005000021300002300071500073100094542005400825655002500879PBZE00aJ.J. & Jeff 1bHudson Soft / Hudson Entertainmentc2007-5-28  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis comical action game features two bungling detectives, J.J. and JEFF, as they travel through a total of six fields. One day, a request comes into their office to take a case that requires them to "rescue a wealthy man who's been kidnapped." Choose between the two characters and set off alone to outwit your partner and save the day. Each field is broken down into four areas, where enemies, as well as your partner, will try to keep you from your goal. There are many items throughout each area. Kick around in various locations to make them appear. Jump and spray-paint your way toward your goal. If you find a hidden room, you can regain health while being completely entertained by its short sketch and surreal allure.  i2007kHudson Soft / Hudson EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00552na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001600005264005000021300002300071500023000094542005400324655002500378655002700403PBZP00aJ.J. & Jeff 1bHudson Soft / Hudson Entertainmentc2007-6-15  a1 Wii optical disc  aWelcome to the world of the two bungling detectives, "J.J." and "JEFF". "J.J." and "JEFF" receive a phone call to take a case that requires them to "rescue a wealthy man who's been kidnapped" and quickly head out to save him.  i2007kHudson Soft / Hudson EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00985na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001500005264002100020300002300041500072400064542002500788655002500813655002500838PC2E00aChase H.Q. 1bTaitoc2008-7-28  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis is a different style of racing game, in which you attempt to catch criminals by chasing them and ramming their car off the road. Playing as two cops from the NYPD special “CHASE H.Q.” unit, the first half of each stage involves you maneuvering your unmarked car in a heated chase, followed by an action sequence in the latter half. Once you reach the target vehicle, you flip on your lights and siren, then try to stop the culprit by repeatedly colliding with them. Use your different gears wisely as you make your way through streets and around corners, and be careful not to hit objects or other cars, or you’ll lose speed. Also at your disposal are turbo units for temporary extra speed and ramming power.  i2008kTaitosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aRacing games2wiiext00506na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001500005264001800020300002300038500024800061542002500309655002500334655002500359PC2J00aChase H.Q. 1bTaitoc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aNew York City crime is as diverse as its inhabitants. In order to pursue and apprehend criminals on the run, a certain precinct of the New York City Police Department based in Manhattan has formed a special unit to hunt them down: "CHASE H.Q."  i2014kTaitosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aRacing games2wiiext00508na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001500005264002000020300002300040500024800063542002500311655002500336655002500361PC2P00aChase H.Q. 1bTaitoc2008-9-5  a1 Wii optical disc  aNew York City crime is as diverse as its inhabitants. In order to pursue and apprehend criminals on the run, a certain precinct of the New York City Police Department based in Manhattan has formed a special unit to hunt them down: "CHASE H.Q."  i2008kTaitosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aRacing games2wiiext00178na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001600005264001300021300002300034500000500057542001800062PC3J00aDarius Plus 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00198na  a2200097   4500001000500000245003600005264001300041300002300054500000500077542001800082PC4J00aSpace Invaders - Fukkatsu no Hi 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00179na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001700005264001300022300002300035500000500058542001800063PC5J00aDragon Saber 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00180na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001800005264001300023300002300036500000500059542001800064PC6J00aFinal Blaster 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00185na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002300005264001300028300002300041500000500064542001800069PC7J00aMizubaku Daibouken 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00184na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002200005264001300027300002300040500000500063542001800068PC8J04aThe Ninjawarriors 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00187na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002500005264001300030300002300043500000500066542001800071PC9J04aThe NewZealand Story 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB01029na  a2200133   4500001000500000245002100005264002700026300002300053500069800076542003100774655002500805655002600830655003900856PCAE00aSilent Debuggers 1bHUDSON SOFTc2007-7-16  a1 Wii optical disc  aMake your way through a dungeon-like space station and defeat the prowling monsters in this real-time first-person shooter. You're a member of the elite Debuggers, a group of warriors who are jacks-of-all-trades. Assigned to inspect an unmanned space station, you have exactly 100 minutes to get in, destroy the monsters lurking in each block, make your way to the lowest level and deactivate the automatic detonator placed there. With each monster that slips by you, the core block becomes harder to survive in, so speed is key in preserving the facility and each separate block. Experience the thrill of survival as the timer ticks away and you uncover the truth of the events that occurred.  i2007kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext 7aFirst-person shooter games2wiiext00484na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264001900026300002300045500021700068542002600285655002500311655002600336PCAJ00aSilent Debuggers 1bG-modec2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aMake your way through a dungeon-like space station and defeat the prowling monsters in this real-time first-person shooter. You're a member of the elite Debuggers, a group of warriors who are jacks-of-all-trades.  i2014kG-modesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00487na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264002200026300002300048500021700071542002600288655002500314655002600339PCAP00aSilent Debuggers 1bG-modec2007-7-20  a1 Wii optical disc  aMake your way through a dungeon-like space station and defeat the prowling monsters in this real-time first-person shooter. You're a member of the elite Debuggers, a group of warriors who are jacks-of-all-trades.  i2007kG-modesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext01075na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001400005264002200019300002300041500081100064542002700875655002500902655002600927PCBE00aDead Moon 1bNatsumec2007-6-4  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis side-scrolling shooter includes a total of six scenes spanning areas from Earth to the moon. The story begins with a comet discovered in the vicinity of Pluto that is headed on a sudden collision course with Earth. Mankind narrowly succeeds in diverting the comet's course, and it crashes into the moon. However, investigations into the damage uncover that what hit the moon was not a comet, but a gigantic mother ship. Power up your ship, destroy enemies and fight your way through the bosses in an attempt to reach the moon's core and protect Earth from alien invasion. Enjoy the unique world of Dead Moon, including various stages with beautiful backgrounds, a power-up system that increases your attack as well as your defense and bosses that have you altering your ship's direction to fight them.  i2007kNatsumesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00446na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003700005264002000042300002300062500016100085542002700246655002500273655002600298PCBJ00aDead Moon - Getsu Sekai no Akumu 1bNatsumec2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aA comet is discovered in the vicinity of Pluto. While investigations are being conducted, the comet changes course and heads towards a collision with Earth.  i2014kNatsumesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00425na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001400005264002200019300002300041500016100064542002700225655002500252655002600277PCBP00aDead Moon 1bNatsumec2007-6-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aA comet is discovered in the vicinity of Pluto. While investigations are being conducted, the comet changes course and heads towards a collision with Earth.  i2007kNatsumesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00188na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002600005264001300031300002300044500000500067542001800072PCCJ00aMakai Hakkenden Shada 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00183na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002100005264001300026300002300039500000500062542001800067PCDJ00aAppare! Gateball 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00981na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001500005264002700020300002300047500071000070542003100780655002500811655002300836PCEE00aPower Golf 1bHUDSON SOFTc2007-11-5  a1 Wii optical disc  aPower Golf sports a perfect combination of simple-yet-realistic controls and beautiful graphics. Swing away on 18 lush holes in one of three different game modes: the single player STROKE PLAY mode and the multiplayer MATCH PLAY and COMPETITION modes. Enter tournaments as one of three different characters—beginner, intermediate, and advanced. Wind strength and the slope of the green add extra challenges to each hole. Compete against other players in the standard NORMAL MATCH or ante up one of your clubs in the unique CLUB MATCH. Up to three players can play in COMPETITION mode, and a handicap feature is included to help novice players pull off breathtaking shots just like their advanced rivals.  i2007kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aGolf games2wiiext00524na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001500005264002400020300002300044500025600067542003100323655002500354655002300379PCEJ00aPower Golf 1bHudson Softc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aPower Golf sports a perfect combination of simple-yet-realistic controls and beautiful graphics. Swing away on 18 lush holes in one of three different game modes: the single-player STROKE PLAY mode and the multiplayer MATCH PLAY and COMPETITION modes.  i2014kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aGolf games2wiiext00527na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001500005264002700020300002300047500025600070542003100326655002500357655002300382PCEP00aPower Golf 1bHudson Softc2007-11-9  a1 Wii optical disc  aPower Golf sports a perfect combination of simple-yet-realistic controls and beautiful graphics. Swing away on 18 lush holes in one of three different game modes: the single-player STROKE PLAY mode and the multiplayer MATCH PLAY and COMPETITION modes.  i2007kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aGolf games2wiiext00920na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001300005264002200018300002300040500069600063542002600759655002500785PCHE00aDrop Off 1bG-Modec2007-7-30  a1 Wii optical disc  aBrave five rounds of haunting, nightmarish dreams in this take on the classic arcade puzzler. To save his dearly beloved from the malicious demon that controls her dreams and holds her captive, our brave hero plunges himself into the nightmare to vanquish this evil foe. Deftly use the arrow items and control the angle of the ball to shatter the blocks that descend from the top of the screen. Set your sights on the joints holding the blocks together and knock off multiple blocks in one exhilarating blow. As you drop more and more blocks, their shapes will change, allowing you to earn bonus points. You must use your concentration and reflexes to defeat the demon and save your beloved.  i2007kG-ModesGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00315na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002400005264001900029300002300048500008300071542002600154655002500180PCHJ00aDrop Rock Hora Hora 1bG-modec2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aOne night, "something" suddenly crept into the dream of TAKASHI's lover IZUMI.  i2014kG-modesGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00306na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001300005264002100018300002300039500008300062542002600145655002500171PCHP00aDrop Off 1bG-modec2007-8-3  a1 Wii optical disc  aOne night, "something" suddenly crept into the dream of TAKASHI's lover IZUMI.  i2007kG-modesGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00175na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001300005264001300018300002300031500000500054542001800059PCJJ00aOverride 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00176na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001400005264001300019300002300032500000500055542001800060PCKJ00aGai Flame 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00190na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002800005264001300033300002300046500000500069542001800074PCMC00aGokuraku! Chuuka Taisen 1bc2020--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2020sGameTDB00188na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002600005264001300031300002300044500000500067542001800072PCMJ00aMr. Heli no Daibouken 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00179na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001700005264001300022300002300035500000500058542001800063PCNJ00aWinning Shot 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB01025na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001400005264002600019300002300045500075400068542003000822655002500852655002600877PCOE00aPsychosis 1bNaxat Softc2008-2-25  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis is a side-scrolling shooter played in a world created from the mind of a twisted demon. Your soul has suddenly wandered into that evil world that exists in every person's heart. The only way out is to blast your way past the grotesque creatures that block your path in five "causes" (stages). You must face the dangers of this psychedelic world by making full use of three shot types and the satellite option. With power-ups, you can change your shots to a wide-coverage beam, a satellite-generated laser and more. Each shot type can be powered up to three levels. You can also block enemy fire by rotating the satellites to a desired position. How you use these features will be the key to successfully escaping this strange and surreal world.  i2008kNaxat SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00575na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001300005264002300018300002300041500030800064542003000372655002500402655002600427PCOJ00aParanoia 1bNaxat softc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis is a side-scrolling shooter played in a world created from the mind of a twisted demon. Your soul has suddenly wandered into that evil world that exists in every person’s heart. The only way out is to blast your way past the grotesque creatures that block your path in five “causes” (stages).  i2014kNaxat softsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00579na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001400005264002600019300002300045500030800068542003000376655002500406655002600431PCOP00aPsychosis 1bNaxat softc2008-2-29  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis is a side-scrolling shooter played in a world created from the mind of a twisted demon. Your soul has suddenly wandered into that evil world that exists in every person’s heart. The only way out is to blast your way past the grotesque creatures that block your path in five “causes” (stages).  i2008kNaxat softsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00179na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001700005264001300022300002300035500000500058542001800063PCPJ00aPower Eleven 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00180na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001800005264001300023300002300036500000500059542001800064PCQJ00aPsycho Chaser 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00914na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001300005264002300018300002300041500064500064542003000709655002500739655002800764PCRJ00aBreak In 1bNaxat Softc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aGather up to four players for an authentic game of pool right in your own home! Choose from six billiards games, such as 9 Ball, Rotation, and Carom (a game played without pockets). Use Simulation mode to calculate the perfect shot, or select Action mode and check out what went wrong with your missed shots. With all that to choose from, Break In gives players--from beginners to experts--all the elements necessary to enjoy a great game of pool! But it doesn’t stop there. Select Technique to practice your angles or even go for a trick shot! Get some help from the CPU and hone your skills. With Break In, you’ll be a pro in no time!  i2014kNaxat SoftsGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aBilliards games2wiiext00295na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001300005264002500018300002300043500002400066542003000090655002500120655002800145PCRL00aBreak In 1bNaxat softc2008-5-9  a1 Wii optical disc  a1. Choose your game  i2008kNaxat softsGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aBilliards games2wiiext00917na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001300005264002600018300002300044500064500067542003000712655002500742655002800767PCRN00aBreak In 1bNaxat Softc2008-8-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aGather up to four players for an authentic game of pool right in your own home! Choose from six billiards games, such as 9 Ball, Rotation, and Carom (a game played without pockets). Use Simulation mode to calculate the perfect shot, or select Action mode and check out what went wrong with your missed shots. With all that to choose from, Break In gives players--from beginners to experts--all the elements necessary to enjoy a great game of pool! But it doesn’t stop there. Select Technique to practice your angles or even go for a trick shot! Get some help from the CPU and hone your skills. With Break In, you’ll be a pro in no time!  i2008kNaxat SoftsGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aBilliards games2wiiext01053na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264002300023300002300046500078200069542003000851655002500881655002500906PCSJ00aDigital Champ 1bNaxat Softc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aSet in the near future, DIGITAL CHAMP is a first-person-perspective boxing title that plunges players into the raw intensity of the ring! Determined to thwart Mother Computer’s plot to conquer mankind, you infiltrate the enemy’s domain, using your boxing skills to vanquish your foes. Each round is three minutes, with a total of twelve rounds to a match. Advance to the next contest through either a KO or by flattening an opponent three times in a round for a TKO. Utilize an arsenal of left and right jabs, hooks, power-charged crosses, and three different kinds of “Devastator” punches. Deftly block and slip your opponent’s attacks, and look for your chance to lay them out. Master these techniques and take down the greatest opponent of them all, DIGITAL CHAMP!  i2014kNaxat SoftsGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aBoxing games2wiiext00450na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003200005264002600037300002300063500016200086542003000248655002500278655002500303PCSL00aDigital Champ Battle Boxing 1bNaxat softc2008-5-16  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn the year 20XX, Mother Computer compiles the data from past boxing champions to create the ultimate boxer, "DIGITAL CHAMP", in a plot to subjugate mankind.  i2008kNaxat softsGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aBoxing games2wiiext01071na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003200005264002700037300002300064500078200087542003000869655002500899655002500924PCSN00aDigital Champ Battle Boxing 1bNaxat Softc2008-10-20  a1 Wii optical disc  aSet in the near future, DIGITAL CHAMP is a first-person-perspective boxing title that plunges players into the raw intensity of the ring! Determined to thwart Mother Computer’s plot to conquer mankind, you infiltrate the enemy’s domain, using your boxing skills to vanquish your foes. Each round is three minutes, with a total of twelve rounds to a match. Advance to the next contest through either a KO or by flattening an opponent three times in a round for a TKO. Utilize an arsenal of left and right jabs, hooks, power-charged crosses, and three different kinds of “Devastator” punches. Deftly block and slip your opponent’s attacks, and look for your chance to lay them out. Master these techniques and take down the greatest opponent of them all, DIGITAL CHAMP!  i2008kNaxat SoftsGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aBoxing games2wiiext00179na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001700005264001300022300002300035500000500058542001800063PCTJ00aPower Tennis 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00193na  a2200097   4500001000500000245003100005264001300036300002300049500000500072542001800077PCUJ00aFire ProWrestling 2nd Bout 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB01041na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002500005264002700030300002300057500075600080542003100836655002500867655002700892PCVE00aWorld Class Baseball 1bHUDSON SOFTc2007-9-17  a1 Wii optical disc  aAcclaimed for its steady game play, World Class Baseball is the definitive baseball game on the TurboGrafx. Battle the computer in OPEN MODE or play a friend in VERSUS MODE. Customize your team in EDIT MODE or even watch a game between two computer opponents in WATCH MODE. WCB offers the complete baseball gaming experience. Of course there’s also plenty of single-player action! The main feature is PENNANT MODE, where the player chooses a team from one of the world’s leagues and strives to win their team’s league. Beat league rivals and save your progress with passwords on your way to becoming league champions. After winning your league, get ready to the face the other league’s champion in the heated series for the world championship!  i2007kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aBaseball games2wiiext00565na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002500005264002700030300002300057500028000080542003100360655002500391655002700416PCVP00aWorld Class Baseball 1bHudson Softc2007-9-21  a1 Wii optical disc  aAcclaimed for its steady game play, World Class Baseball is the definitive baseball game on the TurboGrafx16. Battle the computer in OPEN MODE or play a friend in VERSUS MODE. Customize your team in EDIT MODE or even watch a game between two computer opponents in WATCH MODE.  i2007kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aBaseball games2wiiext00178na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001600005264001300021300002300034500000500057542001800062PCWJ00aImage Fight 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00182na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002000005264001300025300002300038500000500061542001800066PCXJ00aPower League IV 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00207na  a2200097   4500001000500000245004500005264001300050300002300063500000500086542001800091PCYJ00aWallaby!! Usagi no Kuni no Kangaroo Race 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00202na  a2200097   4500001000500000245004800005264000900053300002300062500000500085542001400090PDAJ00aNekketsu Koukou Dodgeball Bu - PC Bangaihen 1bc--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  isGameTDB00180na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001800005264001300023300002300036500000500059542001800064PDCJ00aDai Makaimura 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00174na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001200005264001300017300002300030500000500053542001800058PDDJ00aVolfied 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00206na  a2200097   4500001000500000245004400005264001300049300002300062500000500085542001800090PDEJ00aS.C.I. - Special Criminal Investigation 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00182na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001800005264001500023300002300038500000500061542001800066PDFJ00aJigoku Meguri 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00200na  a2200097   4500001000500000245003800005264001300043300002300056500000500079542001800084PDGJ00aFire ProWrestling 3 - Legend Bout 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00181na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001900005264001300024300002300037500000500060542001800065PDHJ00aRastan Saga II 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00186na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002200005264001500027300002300042500000500065542001800070PDIJ00aChampion Wrestler 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB01002na  a2200109   4500001000500000245004600005264001900051300002300070500074600093542002600839655002700865PDJJ00aStreet Fighter II Dash - Champion Edition 1bCapcomc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis is the classic PCEngine (TurboGrafx16) version of the two-player fighting game that started it all. For the port, a large capacity HuCARD was used at the time, allowing the faithful recreation of the dynamic arcade game and its features including bonus stages and sound effects. In the game, players select one of twelve characters and face opponents in a no-holds-barred battle to decide the top fighter. Master a character’s special moves and combos to defeat your rivals around the world! In “V.S. BATTLE” mode, there’s a convenient handicap feature. Using this feature to adjust a character’s performance, a novice player can be evenly matched against a seasoned player to enjoy an intense, head-to-head combat experience!  i2014kCapcomsGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00364na  a2200109   4500001000500000245004100005264002300046300002300069500010900092542002600201655002700227PDJL00aStreet Fighter II - Champion Edition 1bCapcomc2009-12-18  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis is the classic PCEngine (TurboGrafx16) version of the two-player fighting game that started it all.  i2009kCapcomsGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext01001na  a2200109   4500001000500000245004100005264002300046300002300069500074600092542002600838655002700864PDJN00aStreet Fighter II - Champion Edition 1bCapcomc2009-11-16  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis is the classic PCEngine (TurboGrafx16) version of the two-player fighting game that started it all. For the port, a large capacity HuCARD was used at the time, allowing the faithful recreation of the dynamic arcade game and its features including bonus stages and sound effects. In the game, players select one of twelve characters and face opponents in a no-holds-barred battle to decide the top fighter. Master a character’s special moves and combos to defeat your rivals around the world! In “V.S. BATTLE” mode, there’s a convenient handicap feature. Using this feature to adjust a character’s performance, a novice player can be evenly matched against a seasoned player to enjoy an intense, head-to-head combat experience!  i2009kCapcomsGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00213na  a2200097   4500001000500000245004900005264001500054300002300069500000500092542001800097QA2J00aNekketsu Koukou Dodgeball Bu - CD Soccer Hen 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB01183na  a2200109   4500001000500000245003200005264005000037300002300087500088000110542005400990655002901044QA3E00aSimEarth: The Living Planet 1bHudson Soft / Hudson Entertainmentc2009-6-22  a1 Wii optical disc  aAn entire planet becomes your laboratory in this large-scale simulation game. Players help foster new life and promote its evolution into life-forms of higher intelligence. Guide civilization along the path of evolution until it can achieve Exodus, the ultimate goal of settling on another planet. The basic challenge of the game is to maintain a comfortable environment for the life-forms by adjusting atmospheric and geological parameters. Small organisms called Prokaryote and Trichordate will grow and evolve into a multitude of life-forms. Making a drastic change is a recipe for disaster. The key to success is to make small adjustments and watch how the life-forms react. SimEarth also includes planets with environments different from Earth, such as Mars and Venus. Try your hand at terraforming these planets with harsh conditions into a world where life can thrive.  i2009kHudson Soft / Hudson EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aSimulation games2wiiext00928na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001300005264005000018300002300068500059900091542005400690655002900744655003300773QA3J00aSimEarth 1bHudson Soft / Hudson Entertainmentc2009-5-12  a1 Wii optical disc  aAn entire planet becomes your laboratory in this large-scale simulation game. Players help foster new life and promote its evolution into life forms of higher intelligence. Guide civilization along the path of evolution until it can achieve Exodus, the ultimate goal of settling on another planet. The basic challenge of the game is to maintain a comfortable environment for the life forms by adjusting atmospheric and geological parameters. Small organisms called Prokaryote and Trichordate will grow and evolve into a multitude of life forms. Making a drastic change is a recipe for disaster.  i2009kHudson Soft / Hudson EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aSimulation games2wiiext 7aEducational software2wiiext00947na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003200005264005000037300002300087500059900110542005400709655002900763655003300792QA3P00aSimEarth: The Living Planet 1bHudson Soft / Hudson Entertainmentc2009-6-26  a1 Wii optical disc  aAn entire planet becomes your laboratory in this large-scale simulation game. Players help foster new life and promote its evolution into life forms of higher intelligence. Guide civilization along the path of evolution until it can achieve Exodus, the ultimate goal of settling on another planet. The basic challenge of the game is to maintain a comfortable environment for the life forms by adjusting atmospheric and geological parameters. Small organisms called Prokaryote and Trichordate will grow and evolve into a multitude of life forms. Making a drastic change is a recipe for disaster.  i2009kHudson Soft / Hudson EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aSimulation games2wiiext 7aEducational software2wiiext00183na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001900005264001500024300002300039500000500062542001800067QA4J00aSuper Darius 2 1bc2012-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2012sGameTDB00203na  a2200097   4500001000500000245003900005264001500044300002300059500000500082542001800087QA5J00aSpace Invaders - The Original Game 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00179na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001700005264001300022300002300035500000500058542001800063QA6J00aSuper Darius 1bc2012--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2012sGameTDB00190na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002800005264001300033300002300046500000500069542001800074QA7J00aKaze no Densetsu Xanadu 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00182na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002000005264001300025300002300038500000500061542001800066QA8J00aSpriggan Mark 2 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00193na  a2200097   4500001000500000245003100005264001300036300002300049500000500072542001800077QA9J00aKaze no Densetsu Xanadu II 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB01052na  a2200121   4500001000500000245004100005264002800046300002300074500075100097542003100848655002500879655002600904QAAE00aSuper Air Zonk - Rockabilly-Paradise 1bHUDSON SOFTc2007-11-19  a1 Wii optical disc  aZonk is back in Super Air Zonk, the sequel to the shooting game spin-off of the Bonk series, Air “Zonk”. Now moving to a rockabilly beat and able to transform into nine different characters, Zonk lets loose through seven action-packed stages in another battle against his archnemesis, SandroVitch. Power up Zonk with the classic Meat item, eventually turning him into the champion of justice, Ultra Zonk, or the fearsome Tyrano Zonk in the latter stages of the game. After rescuing his friends from enemies, Zonk can also morph with them to combine powers. Fight enemies with killer tunes belted out from a trusty microphone! Hurl freshly made sushi at them! With its variety of wacky attacks, Super Air Zonk has a sense of humor all its own.  i2007kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00763na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003500005264002400040300002300064500047200087542003100559655002500590655002600615QAAJ00aCD Denjin - Rockabilly Tengoku 1bHudson Softc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aZonk is back in Super Air Zonk, the sequel to the shooting game spin-off of the Bonk series, Air "Zonk." Now moving to a rockabilly beat and able to transform into nine different characters, Zonk lets loose through seven action-packed stages in another battle against his arch nemesis, SandroVitch. Power up Zonk with the classic Meat item, eventually turning him into the champion of justice, Ultra Zonk, or the fearsome Tyrano Zonk in the latter stages of the game.  i2014kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00772na  a2200121   4500001000500000245004000005264002800045300002300073500047200096542003100568655002500599655002600624QAAP00aSuper Air Zonk: Rockabilly-Paradise 1bHudson Softc2007-10-26  a1 Wii optical disc  aZonk is back in Super Air Zonk, the sequel to the shooting game spin-off of the Bonk series, Air "Zonk." Now moving to a rockabilly beat and able to transform into nine different characters, Zonk lets loose through seven action-packed stages in another battle against his arch nemesis, SandroVitch. Power up Zonk with the classic Meat item, eventually turning him into the champion of justice, Ultra Zonk, or the fearsome Tyrano Zonk in the latter stages of the game.  i2007kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext01031na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264002800026300002300054500074400077542003200821655002500853655003100878QABE00aYs - Book I & II 1bNIHON FALCOMc2008-8-25  a1 Wii optical disc  aYs Book I & II chronicles the first adventures of Adol Christin, a young, red-haired swordsman, on his quest to unlock the secrets of an ancient kingdom. As Adol, you search the island of Esteria, gathering clues to unravel the mystery of Ys. Fight monsters that lurk in caves and towers with physical or magical attacks, and use your brain to make your way through dangerous areas filled with traps. In Ys Book I & II, the first titles in the Ys series were put together as a single TurboGrafx CD-ROM. They awed players with their gripping story lines accompanied by fully orchestrated sound tracks, wonderful voice acting, and amazing special effects. Don’t miss out on your chance to experience this wonderful piece of gaming history.  i2008kNIHON FALCOMsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00684na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264002400026300002300050500040200073542003100475655002500506655003100531QABJ00aYs - Book I & II 1bHudson Softc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aYs Book I & II chronicles the first adventures of Adol Christin, a young, red-haired swordsman on a quest to unlock the secrets of an ancient kingdom. As Adol, you search the island of Esteria, gathering clues to unravel the mystery of Ys. Fight monsters that lurk in caves and towers with physical or magical attacks, and use your brain to make your way through dangerous areas filled with traps.  i2014kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00730na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001900005264004900024300002300073500040200096542005400498655002500552655003100577QABP00aYs Book I & II 1bHudson Soft / Hudson Entertainmentc2008-9-5  a1 Wii optical disc  aYs Book I & II chronicles the first adventures of Adol Christin, a young, red-haired swordsman on a quest to unlock the secrets of an ancient kingdom. As Adol, you search the island of Esteria, gathering clues to unravel the mystery of Ys. Fight monsters that lurk in caves and towers with physical or magical attacks, and use your brain to make your way through dangerous areas filled with traps.  i2008kHudson Soft / Hudson EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00904na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001400005264002600019300002300045500063200068542003100700655002500731655002600756QACJ00aCho Aniki 1bHUDSON SOFTc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe odd world in this shooter made for quite the conversation piece in its day. Players control either Idaten or Benten, celestial warriors out to bring an end to the tyrannical rule of the emperor of Planet Builder, who holds muscular prowess to be the supreme virtue of the universe. Aided by able-bodied muscle-head options Adon and Samson, they must battle to defeat the emperor’s army across five stages. Use the buttons to fire away and lay into the Builder forces! Power up your character and options with protein from defeated enemies to have them "bulk up" with a yell, and take their macho battle to the next level!  i2014kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00406na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001400005264002600019300002300045500013400068542003100202655002500233655002600258QACL00aCho Aniki 1bHudson Softc2008-5-9  a1 Wii optical disc  aDespite having dominated the Galactic Bodybuilding Contest for the past 10 years, the emperor of Planet Builder felt ill at ease.  i2008kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00904na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001400005264002600019300002300045500063200068542003100700655002500731655002600756QACN00aCho Aniki 1bHUDSON SOFTc2008-9-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe odd world in this shooter made for quite the conversation piece in its day. Players control either Idaten or Benten, celestial warriors out to bring an end to the tyrannical rule of the emperor of Planet Builder, who holds muscular prowess to be the supreme virtue of the universe. Aided by able-bodied muscle-head options Adon and Samson, they must battle to defeat the emperor’s army across five stages. Use the buttons to fire away and lay into the Builder forces! Power up your character and options with protein from defeated enemies to have them "bulk up" with a yell, and take their macho battle to the next level!  i2008kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00905na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003200005264001900037300002300056500062700079542002600706655002500732655002600757QADJ00aGradius II - Gofer no Yabou 1bKonamic2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis shooter is the sequel to the seminal masterpiece, GRADIUS. Two years after its last epic battle, the GRADIUS army recommissions the VIC VIPER superdimensional warplane to combat the invasion of a new nemesis known as GOFER. Piloting the latest model of the VIC VIPER, players can select between multiple WEAPON MODULES and SHIELDS to tackle the varying stages and enemy attack patterns they come up against. With a total of nine stages, this perfect port of the original boasts one of the longest adventures in the series and features more of its trademark fast-paced background music to accompany the intense action!  i2014kKonamisGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00579na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003200005264002100037300002300058500029900081542002600380655002500406655002600431QADL00aGradius II - Gofer no Yabou 1bKonamic2008-5-2  a1 Wii optical disc  aIt's been two years since the VIC VIPER super-dimensional warship led the GRADIUS army to victory against a swarm of alien invaders. Having been attacked by Special Forces Unit GOFER, the GRADIUS army now faces a new crisis. VIC VIPER once again takes off for the stars to stop GOFER's assault.  i2008kKonamisGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00909na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003200005264002300037300002300060500062700083542002600710655002500736655002600761QADN00aGradius II - Gofer no Yabou 1bKonamic2008-10-20  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis shooter is the sequel to the seminal masterpiece, GRADIUS. Two years after its last epic battle, the GRADIUS army recommissions the VIC VIPER superdimensional warplane to combat the invasion of a new nemesis known as GOFER. Piloting the latest model of the VIC VIPER, players can select between multiple WEAPON MODULES and SHIELDS to tackle the varying stages and enemy attack patterns they come up against. With a total of nine stages, this perfect port of the original boasts one of the longest adventures in the series and features more of its trademark fast-paced background music to accompany the intense action!  i2008kKonamisGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00308na  a2200109   4500001000500000245003300005264005100038300002300089500000500112542005400117655002700171QAEJ00aA.III.: A-Ressha de Ikou III 1bHudson Soft / Hudson Entertainmentc2007-11-20  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2007kHudson Soft / Hudson EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aStrategy games2wiiext01032na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002200005264002700027300002300054500074600077542003100823655002500854655003100879QAFE04aThe Dynastic Hero 1bHUDSON SOFTc2007-12-3  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe Dynastic Hero is an action RPG featuring a cast of insect characters. The story begins with the invasion of their peaceful homeland of Tarron by the evil Drilkor Empire. Rushing to the insects’ aid is Dyna, the prince of Beetras! Take control of Dyna as he battles through action-filled stages. Equip weapons and items to vanquish the relentless foes, and acquire special items that enable you to brave the journey across the perilous desert or open sea. But it’s not just all action. Correctly answer multiple-choice quizzes, and play the ocarina to find the right melody to open doors. Plus, there are countless traps and other puzzles packed into this fun game to keep you entertained and ensure you continue coming back for more!  i2007kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00687na  a2200145   4500001000500000245004000005264002600045300002300071500030500094542003100399655002500430655002800455655003100483655002700514QAFJ00aChou Eiyuu Densetsu - Dynastic Hero 1bHudson Softc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe Dynastic Hero is an action RPG featuring a cast of insect characters. The story begins with the invasion of their peaceful homeland of Tarron by the evil Drilkor Empire. Rushing to the insects’ aid is Dyna, the prince of Beetras! Take control of Dyna as he battles through action-filled stages.  i2014kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext 7aRole-playing games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00671na  a2200145   4500001000500000245002200005264002800027300002300055500030500078542003100383655002500414655002800439655003100467655002700498QAFP04aThe Dynastic Hero 1bHudson Softc2007-11-30  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe Dynastic Hero is an action RPG featuring a cast of insect characters. The story begins with the invasion of their peaceful homeland of Tarron by the evil Drilkor Empire. Rushing to the insects’ aid is Dyna, the prince of Beetras! Take control of Dyna as he battles through action-filled stages.  i2007kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext 7aRole-playing games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext01032na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002000005264002800025300002300053500075200076542003100828655002500859655002600884QAGE00aGate of Thunder 1bHUDSON SOFTc2007-10-15  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe legendary sci-fi shooter is back! Gate of Thunder is a horizontal side-scrolling shooter that places you in control of special undercover agent Hawk, whose mission is to stop the deadly army of Obbellon fighters. Jump into the action as Hawk gets aboard his ship, the Hunting Dog, and heads out toward the enemy. Blast through stages while effectively using all three of the weapons at your disposal and receiving support from ally Wild Cat ships. Switch through equippable power-up options on the fly to change the direction of your attack. You’ll have to blast in front of and behind you to survive all seven stages. Hard-core shooting-game fans looking for a challenge can select HARD or DEVIL mode to experience even more intense action!  i2007kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00453na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002000005264002400025300002300049500017700072542003100249655002500280655002600305QAGJ00aGate of Thunder 1bHudson Softc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a"Don Jingi" leads a deadly army of "Obbellon" fighters in an attack that aims to seize the powerful source of energy known as "Starlight" from the peaceful planet of Aries.  i2014kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00457na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002000005264002800025300002300053500017700076542003100253655002500284655002600309QAGP00aGate of Thunder 1bHudson Softc2007-10-19  a1 Wii optical disc  a"Don Jingi" leads a deadly army of "Obbellon" fighters in an attack that aims to seize the powerful source of energy known as "Starlight" from the peaceful planet of Aries.  i2007kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00195na  a2200097   4500001000500000245003300005264001300038300002300051500000500074542001800079QAHJ00aKawa no Nushi Tsuni Shizenha 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00183na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001900005264001500024300002300039500000500062542001800067QAJJ00aImage Fight II 1bc2012-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2012sGameTDB00179na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001700005264001300022300002300035500000500058542001800063QAKJ00aAi Cho Aniki 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00198na  a2200097   4500001000500000245003600005264001300041300002300054500000500077542001800082QALJ04aThe Atlas - Renaissance Voyager 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00179na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001700005264001300022300002300035500000500058542001800063QANJ00aNeo Nectaris 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00186na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002400005264001300029300002300042500000500065542001800070QAOJ00aDungeon Explorer II 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00589na  a2200109   4500001000500000245003800005264001900043300002300062500034300085542002600428655002500454QAPJ00aAkumajou Dracula X - Chi no Rondo 1bKonamic2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis is the tenth action-packed installment in the ever-popular Castlevania series, which depicts the epic struggle between the Belmont clan and the dark forces of Count Dracula! An instant classic, this title is recognized far and wide for its beautifully rendered world, outstanding game balance, and its haunting CD-quality game music!  i2014kKonamisGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00497na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003200005264002200037300002300059500021500082542002600297655002500323655002700348QAPL00aCastlevania: Rondo of Blood 1bKonamic2010-3-19  a1 Wii optical disc  aYou play as RICHTER, a descendant in the long line of Belmont Vampire Killers. The evil Count Dracula has risen again, and it's up to you to rescue the maidens he's abducted and to destroy him once and for all!  i2010kKonamisGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00626na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003300005264002200038300002300060500034300083542002600426655002500452655002700477QAPN00aCastlevania - Rondo of Blood 1bKonamic2010-3-15  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis is the tenth action-packed installment in the ever-popular Castlevania series, which depicts the epic struggle between the Belmont clan and the dark forces of Count Dracula! An instant classic, this title is recognized far and wide for its beautifully rendered world, outstanding game balance, and its haunting CD-quality game music!  i2010kKonamisGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00586na  a2200109   4500001000500000245003200005264002200037300002300059500034300082542002600425655002500451QAPP00aCastlevania: Rondo of Blood 1bKonamic2010-3-19  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis is the tenth action-packed installment in the ever-popular Castlevania series, which depicts the epic struggle between the Belmont clan and the dark forces of Count Dracula! An instant classic, this title is recognized far and wide for its beautifully rendered world, outstanding game balance, and its haunting CD-quality game music!  i2010kKonamisGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00196na  a2200097   4500001000500000245003400005264001300039300002300052500000500075542001800080QAQJ00aDragon Slayer - Eiyu Densetsu 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00177na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001500005264001300020300002300033500000500056542001800061QARJ00aBlood Gear 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB01094na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264002700026300002300053500081400076542003100890655002500921655002600946QASE00aLords of Thunder 1bHUDSON SOFTc2008-2-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aLords of Thunder is a side-scrolling shooter that has you take on the role of a legendary warrior, blasting enemies to heavy-metal tunes. Your enemies are plotting to revive Zaggart, “The Dark One,” who was sealed beneath the six continents of Mistral. It’s up to Landis, descendant of the heroic Dyu, to stop them. Choose the order in which to attack the six stages. Before each stage, select one of four magic armors and use crystals you’ve collected during your battles to buy items. Selecting the right armor for each stage is the key to your ultimate victory. Then get ready to face awesome enemies like a fire-spewing sea serpent or a giant insect. Whether it’s the fast-paced shooting or breaking into the fortress of a stage boss, you’ll be blown away by the intensity of Lords of Thunder.  i2008kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00655na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264002400026300002300050500037800073542003100451655002500482655002600507QASJ00aWinds of Thunder 1bHudson Softc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aLords of Thunder is a side-scrolling shooter that has you take on the role of a legendary warrior, blasting enemies to heavy-metal tunes. Your enemies are plotting to revive Zaggart, “The Dark One,” who was sealed beneath the six continents of Mistral. It’s up to Landis, descendant of the heroic Dyu, to stop them. Choose the order in which to attack the six stages.  i2014kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00657na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264002600026300002300052500037800075542003100453655002500484655002600509QASP00aLords of Thunder 1bHudson Softc2008-2-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aLords of Thunder is a side-scrolling shooter that has you take on the role of a legendary warrior, blasting enemies to heavy-metal tunes. Your enemies are plotting to revive Zaggart, “The Dark One,” who was sealed beneath the six continents of Mistral. It’s up to Landis, descendant of the heroic Dyu, to stop them. Choose the order in which to attack the six stages.  i2008kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext01000na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001400005264002700019300002300046500076500069542003100834655002500865QATE00aRiot Zone 1bHUDSON SOFTc2008-1-14  a1 Wii optical disc  aRiot Zone is a side-scrolling fighting game that follows two heroes as they fight to take down an evil organization. The crime syndicate Dragon Zone has kidnapped Hawk’s girlfriend and it’s up to him and his partner detective, Tony, to get her back. Join them as they jump “fists first” into the grim Kowloon district. Play as Hawk or Tony and fight through all five stages in the deadly Kowloon district. Smash down the Dragon Zone goons in areas like the Harbor, Abandoned Warehouse, and the Ghetto. Both characters have unique skills and attacks. Hawk is a master of karate, while Tony is a hard-hitter. That being said, both guys are massive and possess killer techniques. The hard-boiled action is enhanced by the game’s realistic sound effects.  i2008kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00640na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001800005264002400023300002300047500032300070542003100393655002500424655002700449655003000476QATJ00aCrest of Wolf 1bHudson Softc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aRiot Zone is a side-scrolling fighting game that follows two heroes as they fight to take down an evil organization. The crime syndicate Dragon Zone has kidnapped Hawk's girlfriend and it's up to him and his partner detective, Tony, to get her back. Join them as they jump "fists first" into the grim Kowloon district.  i2014kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext00639na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001400005264002700019300002300046500032300069542003100392655002500423655002700448655003000475QATP00aRiot Zone 1bHudson Softc2008-1-18  a1 Wii optical disc  aRiot Zone is a side-scrolling fighting game that follows two heroes as they fight to take down an evil organization. The crime syndicate Dragon Zone has kidnapped Hawk's girlfriend and it's up to him and his partner detective, Tony, to get her back. Join them as they jump "fists first" into the grim Kowloon district.  i2008kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext01040na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001700005264002800022300002300050500076300073542003100836655002500867655002600892QAUE00aMonster Lair 1bHUDSON SOFTc2007-12-17  a1 Wii optical disc  aJoin young Adam and Laura as they embark on a fantastic adventure in this comical action/shooting game. Featuring beautiful music brought to life by the power of the CD-ROM, the game consists of 14 rounds packed with cute monster enemies. Players can either play alone as Adam (or play with a friend controlling Laura) as they battle their way through round after round. The first half of each round is the action scene, where players must avoid obstacles and pits. Use your Power Boost weapons against enemies, and restore your Life Force with food as you head for the gate at the end. The second half is the exhilarating shooting scene, where players must shoot down flying enemies. Take out the boss at the end to clear the round and move to the next one!  i2007kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00379na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003400005264002400039300002300063500008900086542003100175655002500206655002600231QAUJ00aWonder Boy III - Monster Lair 1bHudson Softc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe legend of the brave heroes again unfolds in the land once tormented by Monsters.  i2014kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00366na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001700005264002800022300002300050500008900073542003100162655002500193655002600218QAUP00aMonster Lair 1bHudson Softc2007-12-21  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe legend of the brave heroes again unfolds in the land once tormented by Monsters.  i2007kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00191na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002900005264001300034300002300047500000500070542001800075QAVJ00aBomberman - Panic Bomber 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00989na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264002400023300002300047500071500070542003100785655002500816655002600841QAWJ00aStar Parodier 1bHUDSON SOFTc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aStar Parodier is the hilarious spoof of the classic Hudson shooter Star Soldier. In this parody, there are three playable ships for players to choose from: the ingratiating PAROCEASER, the hot-headed BOMBERMAN, and the ever-so-introverted PC-ENGINE. Players control one of these unique and original ships and set off to blast their way through eight stages on the planet PAROSON! The comical characters take the color and flavor of the Soldier series to the next level and are guaranteed to leave players mesmerized. In addition to the normal game mode, there are also the familiar 2-minute and 5-minute attack modes, making Star Parodier the complete package that is sure to have players coming back for more.  i2014kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00419na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264002700023300002300050500014200073542003100215655002500246655002600271QAWL00aStar Parodier 1bHudson Softc2008-5-16  a1 Wii optical disc  aA "cute'em-up" top-down shooter that lampoons the Star Soldier games by replacing most sci-fi elements with humorous graphics and sounds.  i2008kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00992na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264002700023300002300050500071500073542003100788655002500819655002600844QAWN00aStar Parodier 1bHUDSON SOFTc2008-8-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aStar Parodier is the hilarious spoof of the classic Hudson shooter Star Soldier. In this parody, there are three playable ships for players to choose from: the ingratiating PAROCEASER, the hot-headed BOMBERMAN, and the ever-so-introverted PC-ENGINE. Players control one of these unique and original ships and set off to blast their way through eight stages on the planet PAROSON! The comical characters take the color and flavor of the Soldier series to the next level and are guaranteed to leave players mesmerized. In addition to the normal game mode, there are also the familiar 2-minute and 5-minute attack modes, making Star Parodier the complete package that is sure to have players coming back for more.  i2008kHUDSON SOFTsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00183na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002100005264001300026300002300039500000500062542001800067QAXJ00aMartial Champion 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00189na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002700005264001300032300002300045500000500068542001800073QAYJ00aSeirei Senshi Spriggan 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00211na  a2200097   4500001000500000245004900005264001300054300002300067500000500090542001800095QAZJ00aEikan wa Kimi ni - Koko Yakyu Zenkoku Taikai 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00172na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001000005264001300015300002300028500000500051542001800056QBAJ00aL-Dis 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00778na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002000005264002200025300002300047500054500070542002600615655002700641QBBE00aFighting Street 1bCapcomc2009-11-2  a1 Wii optical disc  aA port of the arcade version of “STREET FIGHTER”, the legendary fighting game that started it all. Players control RYU or KEN and battle against unique fighters from all over the world. The first fighter to knock out their opponent and win two rounds is the winner. Power up your attack to three different levels—the longer you hold a button, the stronger your attack. Input commands to perform special attacks and deal serious damage to your opponent! Combine your normal and special attacks effectively to fight your way to victory!  i2009kCapcomsGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00386na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002000005264001900025300002300044500015600067542002600223655002700249QBBJ00aFighting Street 1bCapcomc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aBattle your way through 10 formidable fighters from 5 countries - Japan, USA, China, England, and Thailand - in elimination matches to come out on top.  i2014kCapcomsGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00389na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002000005264002200025300002300047500015600070542002600226655002700252QBBP00aFighting Street 1bCapcomc2009-11-6  a1 Wii optical disc  aBattle your way through 10 formidable fighters from 5 countries - Japan, USA, China, England, and Thailand - in elimination matches to come out on top.  i2009kCapcomsGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00348na  a2200109   4500001000500000245006200005264004200067300002300109500003200132542004900164655002500213SP4V00aCastlevania: Rondo of Blood - English Translation Version 1bBurnt Lasagna, Shortfilms.tk 2012c--  a1 Wii optical disc  aEnglish Translation Version  ikBurnt Lasagna, Shortfilms.tk 2012sGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext01053na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001700005264002900022300002300051500081100074542003300885655002500918EA2E00aMetal Slug 2 1bD4 Enterprisec2008-12-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased in 1998 by SNK, Metal Slug 2 is a side-scrolling military-action game. Players choose from Marco, Tarma, Eri, and Fio and then set their sights on wiping out Morden's newly remobilized Rebellion Army. Just like the original Metal Slug, players blaze a trail by shooting and jumping, but Metal Slug 2 adds a new arsenal for you to command, including a heavy machine gun, a shotgun, and even a laser gun, providing players a battle rich with variety to enjoy. Not only that, but battle effects are packed in as well--players turn into mummies after getting caught in poison gas coughed up by mummies. Characters also turn fat, but get an attack-strength upgrade, after picking up too many food items. Naturally, as two-player action is supported, players can have a blast with their friends as well.  i2008kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext01141na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001700005264003400022300002300056500081100079542003900890655002500929655002700954655002600981EA2J00aMetal Slug 2 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased in 1998 by SNK, Metal Slug 2 is a side-scrolling military-action game. Players choose from Marco, Tarma, Eri, and Fio and then set their sights on wiping out Morden's newly remobilized Rebellion Army. Just like the original Metal Slug, players blaze a trail by shooting and jumping, but Metal Slug 2 adds a new arsenal for you to command, including a heavy machine gun, a shotgun, and even a laser gun, providing players a battle rich with variety to enjoy. Not only that, but battle effects are packed in as well--players turn into mummies after getting caught in poison gas coughed up by mummies. Characters also turn fat, but get an attack-strength upgrade, after picking up too many food items. Naturally, as two-player action is supported, players can have a blast with their friends as well.  i2014kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext01143na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001700005264003600022300002300058500081100081542003900892655002500931655002700956655002600983EA2P00aMetal Slug 2 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2008-11-28  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased in 1998 by SNK, Metal Slug 2 is a side-scrolling military-action game. Players choose from Marco, Tarma, Eri, and Fio and then set their sights on wiping out Morden's newly remobilized Rebellion Army. Just like the original Metal Slug, players blaze a trail by shooting and jumping, but Metal Slug 2 adds a new arsenal for you to command, including a heavy machine gun, a shotgun, and even a laser gun, providing players a battle rich with variety to enjoy. Not only that, but battle effects are packed in as well--players turn into mummies after getting caught in poison gas coughed up by mummies. Characters also turn fat, but get an attack-strength upgrade, after picking up too many food items. Naturally, as two-player action is supported, players can have a blast with their friends as well.  i2008kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00200na  a2200097   4500001000500000245003800005264001300043300002300056500000500079542001800084EA3J00aGalaxy Fight - Universal Warriors 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00904na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002400005264002800029300002300057500065400080542003300734655002700767EA4E00aSamurai Shodown III 1bD4 Enterprisec2010-9-7  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis is a fighting game released in 1995 as a sequel to the previous year's release of Samurai Shodown II. Though this is the third installment in the series, the story takes place between the first and second installments. Players can choose from 12 samurai seeking to defeat Zankuro Minazuki. Along with minor upgrades from the last version, such as the ability to press buttons to fill your rage gauge and the ability to defend in midair, you can also select from slash and bust personality types for each character. Each type has its own set of special moves you can take advantage of, effectively doubling the amount of characters you can play.  i2010kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00917na  a2200109   4500001000500000245003900005264002600044300002300070500065400093542003300747655002700780EA4J00aSamurai Spirits - Zankuro Musouken 1bD4 Enterprisec2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis is a fighting game released in 1995 as a sequel to the previous year's release of Samurai Shodown II. Though this is the third installment in the series, the story takes place between the first and second installments. Players can choose from 12 samurai seeking to defeat Zankuro Minazuki. Along with minor upgrades from the last version, such as the ability to press buttons to fill your rage gauge and the ability to defend in midair, you can also select from slash and bust personality types for each character. Each type has its own set of special moves you can take advantage of, effectively doubling the amount of characters you can play.  i2014kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00904na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002400005264002800029300002300057500065400080542003300734655002700767EA4P00aSamurai Shodown III 1bD4 Enterprisec2010-9-3  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis is a fighting game released in 1995 as a sequel to the previous year's release of Samurai Shodown II. Though this is the third installment in the series, the story takes place between the first and second installments. Players can choose from 12 samurai seeking to defeat Zankuro Minazuki. Along with minor upgrades from the last version, such as the ability to press buttons to fill your rage gauge and the ability to defend in midair, you can also select from slash and bust personality types for each character. Each type has its own set of special moves you can take advantage of, effectively doubling the amount of characters you can play.  i2010kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext01218na  a2200109   4500001000500000245004500005264002900050300002300079500094600102542003301048655002701081EA5E00aFatal Fury 3 - Road to the Final Victory 1bD4 Enterprisec2010-10-4  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased in 1995, this is the fourth title in the Fatal Fury series of beat 'em up games. Previous releases in the Fatal Fury series utilized a two-plane battle system allowing you to move and fight between the foreground and background planes on-screen. This has been revamped from previous Fatal Fury titles to a three-plane format (foreground, background and main plane) known as the Oversway System. Characters will automatically move back to the main line after a certain period of time in the foreground or background planes. Other new features include Combination Arts (the ability to execute combo attacks with simple rhythmic button taps), Hidden Abilities (superior versions of the popular Special Moves and Super Special Moves from previous installments), and minor tweaks to all of the characters' Special Moves. This combination of features gives this episode the deepest strategies and tactics in the Fatal Fury series to date.  i2010kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext01219na  a2200109   4500001000500000245004900005264002600054300002300080500094600103542003301049655002701082EA5J00aGarou Densetsu 3 - Road to the Final Victory 1bD4 Enterprisec2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased in 1995, this is the fourth title in the Fatal Fury series of beat 'em up games. Previous releases in the Fatal Fury series utilized a two-plane battle system allowing you to move and fight between the foreground and background planes on-screen. This has been revamped from previous Fatal Fury titles to a three-plane format (foreground, background and main plane) known as the Oversway System. Characters will automatically move back to the main line after a certain period of time in the foreground or background planes. Other new features include Combination Arts (the ability to execute combo attacks with simple rhythmic button taps), Hidden Abilities (superior versions of the popular Special Moves and Super Special Moves from previous installments), and minor tweaks to all of the characters' Special Moves. This combination of features gives this episode the deepest strategies and tactics in the Fatal Fury series to date.  i2014kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext01254na  a2200121   4500001000500000245004400005264002900049300002300078500094600101542003301047655002501080655002701105EA5P00aFatal Fury 3: Road to the Final Victory 1bD4 Enterprisec2010-8-20  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased in 1995, this is the fourth title in the Fatal Fury series of beat 'em up games. Previous releases in the Fatal Fury series utilized a two-plane battle system allowing you to move and fight between the foreground and background planes on-screen. This has been revamped from previous Fatal Fury titles to a three-plane format (foreground, background and main plane) known as the Oversway System. Characters will automatically move back to the main line after a certain period of time in the foreground or background planes. Other new features include Combination Arts (the ability to execute combo attacks with simple rhythmic button taps), Hidden Abilities (superior versions of the popular Special Moves and Super Special Moves from previous installments), and minor tweaks to all of the characters' Special Moves. This combination of features gives this episode the deepest strategies and tactics in the Fatal Fury series to date.  i2010kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext00580na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002900005264001600034300002300050500031500073542001800388655002500406655002700431EA6E04aThe King of Fighters '96 1bc2012-7-12  a1 Wii optical disc  aOriginally released in 1996, this is the third installment in The King of Fighters game series. The series features an SNK all-star lineup, with characters from games like Fatal Fury, Ikari Warriors, Psycho Soldier and Art of Fighting competing with each other for the title of the world’s strongest fighter.  i2012sGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext00577na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002900005264001300034300002300047500031500070542001800385655002500403655002700428EA6J04aThe King of Fighters '96 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aOriginally released in 1996, this is the third installment in The King of Fighters game series. The series features an SNK all-star lineup, with characters from games like Fatal Fury, Ikari Warriors, Psycho Soldier and Art of Fighting competing with each other for the title of the world’s strongest fighter.  i2014sGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext00581na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002900005264001700034300002300051500031500074542001800389655002500407655002700432EA6P04aThe King of Fighters '96 1bc2012-11-22  a1 Wii optical disc  aOriginally released in 1996, this is the third installment in The King of Fighters game series. The series features an SNK all-star lineup, with characters from games like Fatal Fury, Ikari Warriors, Psycho Soldier and Art of Fighting competing with each other for the title of the world’s strongest fighter.  i2012sGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext00432na  a2200121   4500001000500000245004300005264002900048300002300077500012500100542003300225655002500258655002700283EA7E00aSamurai Shodown IV - Amakusa's Revenge 1bD4 Enterprisec2012-3-15  a1 Wii optical disc  aSamurai Shodown IV: Amakusa’s Revenge is the fourth installment in the Samurai Shodown series, which launched in 1996.  i2012kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext00423na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003700005264002600042300002300068500012500091542003300216655002500249655002700274EA7J00aSamurai Spirits - Amakusa Kourin 1bD4 Enterprisec2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aSamurai Shodown IV: Amakusa’s Revenge is the fourth installment in the Samurai Shodown series, which launched in 1996.  i2014kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext00429na  a2200121   4500001000500000245004300005264002600048300002300074500012500097542003300222655002500255655002700280EA7P00aSamurai Shodown IV - Amakusa's Revenge 1bD4 Enterprisec2012--  a1 Wii optical disc  aSamurai Shodown IV: Amakusa’s Revenge is the fourth installment in the Samurai Shodown series, which launched in 1996.  i2012kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext01319na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001300005264002800018300002300046500104400069542003301113655002501146655002601171EA8E00aIronclad 1bD4 Enterprisec2010-4-5  a1 Wii optical disc  aIron Clad is a side-scrolling shoot ‘em up developed by SAURUS in 1996. You operate a war ship and team with the mighty Iron Clad in order to fight the Iron Mask Republic and save the Kingdom of Chop. The biggest appeal of this game comes from discovering all the ways you can attack your enemies. Your weaponry includes three main blast weapons upgradable by collecting more items, a charged attack you can use when Iron Clad is attached to your ship, three types of melee weapons you can brandish to show off your strength in close-range combat, a bomber that clears all enemy bullets, and finally shooting patterns that change based on whether the Iron Clad is attached or disconnected from your ship. And not surprisingly, a vast array of weaponry lies in wait to be part of your arsenal. You can even select the stages you want, feeding your hunger for combat and allowing you to see different endings for each play through! You can have a blast playing over and over again to see all the endings and variety this game has to offer.  i2010kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext01338na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003200005264002800037300002300065500104400088542003301132655002501165655002601190EA8J00aIRONCLAD Chotetsu Brikinger 1bD4 Enterprisec2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aIron Clad is a side-scrolling shoot ‘em up developed by SAURUS in 1996. You operate a war ship and team with the mighty Iron Clad in order to fight the Iron Mask Republic and save the Kingdom of Chop. The biggest appeal of this game comes from discovering all the ways you can attack your enemies. Your weaponry includes three main blast weapons upgradable by collecting more items, a charged attack you can use when Iron Clad is attached to your ship, three types of melee weapons you can brandish to show off your strength in close-range combat, a bomber that clears all enemy bullets, and finally shooting patterns that change based on whether the Iron Clad is attached or disconnected from your ship. And not surprisingly, a vast array of weaponry lies in wait to be part of your arsenal. You can even select the stages you want, feeding your hunger for combat and allowing you to see different endings for each play through! You can have a blast playing over and over again to see all the endings and variety this game has to offer.  i2014kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext01320na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001300005264002900018300002300047500104400070542003301114655002501147655002601172EA8M00aIronclad 1bD4 Enterprisec2010-3-12  a1 Wii optical disc  aIron Clad is a side-scrolling shoot ‘em up developed by SAURUS in 1996. You operate a war ship and team with the mighty Iron Clad in order to fight the Iron Mask Republic and save the Kingdom of Chop. The biggest appeal of this game comes from discovering all the ways you can attack your enemies. Your weaponry includes three main blast weapons upgradable by collecting more items, a charged attack you can use when Iron Clad is attached to your ship, three types of melee weapons you can brandish to show off your strength in close-range combat, a bomber that clears all enemy bullets, and finally shooting patterns that change based on whether the Iron Clad is attached or disconnected from your ship. And not surprisingly, a vast array of weaponry lies in wait to be part of your arsenal. You can even select the stages you want, feeding your hunger for combat and allowing you to see different endings for each play through! You can have a blast playing over and over again to see all the endings and variety this game has to offer.  i2010kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00178na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001600005264001300021300002300034500000500057542001800062EA9J00aWaku Waku 7 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB01042na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001500005264002900020300002300049500080000072542003300872655002700905EAAE00aFatal Fury 1bD4 Enterprisec2007-10-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased in 1991 and one of the longest-running series in the fighting-game genre, this title introduced players to Terry Bogard, Andy Bogard, and Joe Higashi. Select one of the three and visit many locations as your chosen fighter engages in numerous street fights around the fictional city of South Town. If you’re good enough, you’ll eventually take on Billy Kane and then his boss, the notorious crime lord Geese Howard. Use each fighter’s own finishing maneuver and battle in two different planes on the screen, one in the foreground and the other farther away in the background. The game also features a two-player mode that is well known for its unique setup, which allows fighters to both fight and help each other. Do you have what it takes to win the King of Fighters tournament?  i2007kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext01104na  a2200121   4500001000500000245004100005264002800046300002300074500080000097542003300897655002500930655002700955EAAJ00aGarou Densetsu - Shukumei no Tatakai 1bD4 Enterprisec2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased in 1991 and one of the longest-running series in the fighting-game genre, this title introduced players to Terry Bogard, Andy Bogard, and Joe Higashi. Select one of the three and visit many locations as your chosen fighter engages in numerous street fights around the fictional city of South Town. If you’re good enough, you’ll eventually take on Billy Kane and then his boss, the notorious crime lord Geese Howard. Use each fighter’s own finishing maneuver and battle in two different planes on the screen, one in the foreground and the other farther away in the background. The game also features a two-player mode that is well known for its unique setup, which allows fighters to both fight and help each other. Do you have what it takes to win the King of Fighters tournament?  i2014kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext01079na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001500005264002900020300002300049500080000072542003300872655002500905655002700930EAAP00aFatal Fury 1bD4 Enterprisec2007-10-5  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased in 1991 and one of the longest-running series in the fighting-game genre, this title introduced players to Terry Bogard, Andy Bogard, and Joe Higashi. Select one of the three and visit many locations as your chosen fighter engages in numerous street fights around the fictional city of South Town. If you’re good enough, you’ll eventually take on Billy Kane and then his boss, the notorious crime lord Geese Howard. Use each fighter’s own finishing maneuver and battle in two different planes on the screen, one in the foreground and the other farther away in the background. The game also features a two-player mode that is well known for its unique setup, which allows fighters to both fight and help each other. Do you have what it takes to win the King of Fighters tournament?  i2007kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext01017na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001700005264002900022300002300051500077300074542003300847655002700880EABE00aWorld Heroes 1bD4 Enterprisec2007-10-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aA fighting game released in 1992 featuring eight characters, including Hanzo, Janne, and Rasputin, modeled on historical figures from throughout the ages. The fighters compete against each other to become the world’s toughest combatant, with players using a setup consisting of only three buttons (one each for punching, kicking, and throwing). Adding to this unique system is the fact that the strength of your offensive blow depends on how long the button is pressed and held. Along with regular match styles, Death Match mode is also available and features mines, electrified ropes, and other dangerous objects in the battle arena that can change conditions during the fight or damage players. Enjoy the wide range of combat forms as you take on history’s best!  i2007kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext01028na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001700005264003400022300002300056500077300079542003900852655002700891EABJ00aWorld Heroes 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aA fighting game released in 1992 featuring eight characters, including Hanzo, Janne, and Rasputin, modeled on historical figures from throughout the ages. The fighters compete against each other to become the world’s toughest combatant, with players using a setup consisting of only three buttons (one each for punching, kicking, and throwing). Adding to this unique system is the fact that the strength of your offensive blow depends on how long the button is pressed and held. Along with regular match styles, Death Match mode is also available and features mines, electrified ropes, and other dangerous objects in the battle arena that can change conditions during the fight or damage players. Enjoy the wide range of combat forms as you take on history’s best!  i2014kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext01030na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001700005264003600022300002300058500077300081542003900854655002700893EABP00aWorld Heroes 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2007-10-12  a1 Wii optical disc  aA fighting game released in 1992 featuring eight characters, including Hanzo, Janne, and Rasputin, modeled on historical figures from throughout the ages. The fighters compete against each other to become the world’s toughest combatant, with players using a setup consisting of only three buttons (one each for punching, kicking, and throwing). Adding to this unique system is the fact that the strength of your offensive blow depends on how long the button is pressed and held. Along with regular match styles, Death Match mode is also available and features mines, electrified ropes, and other dangerous objects in the battle arena that can change conditions during the fight or damage players. Enjoy the wide range of combat forms as you take on history’s best!  i2007kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext01083na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264003000023300002300053500083900076542003300915655002500948EACE00aMagician Lord 1bD4 Enterprisec2007-10-29  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased in 1990 and one of the NEOGEO’s earliest signature games, this side-scrolling platformer mixes action with the mystical world of fantasy. A magician named Elta, last descendant of the famed Magician Lord, takes on an epic adventure to save the world from the evil Gul-Agieze. Elta must battle through eight stages, collecting the eight tomes of power that are the key to defeating Gul-Agieze and his evil plans. By obtaining orbs in one of three colors (elements) that appear during the progress of the game, Elta’s offensive powers and jumping abilities can be strengthened. The effect varies considerably depending on the combination of elements though, and Elta can transform into six different forms (Waterman, Dragon Warrior, Shinobi, Samurai, Raijin, or Poseidon). Can you help Elta to become the new Magician Lord?  i2007kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext01132na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264003400023300002300057500083900080542003900919655002500958655002700983EACJ00aMagician Lord 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased in 1990 and one of the NEOGEO’s earliest signature games, this side-scrolling platformer mixes action with the mystical world of fantasy. A magician named Elta, last descendant of the famed Magician Lord, takes on an epic adventure to save the world from the evil Gul-Agieze. Elta must battle through eight stages, collecting the eight tomes of power that are the key to defeating Gul-Agieze and his evil plans. By obtaining orbs in one of three colors (elements) that appear during the progress of the game, Elta’s offensive powers and jumping abilities can be strengthened. The effect varies considerably depending on the combination of elements though, and Elta can transform into six different forms (Waterman, Dragon Warrior, Shinobi, Samurai, Raijin, or Poseidon). Can you help Elta to become the new Magician Lord?  i2014kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext01134na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264003600023300002300059500083900082542003900921655002500960655002700985EACP00aMagician Lord 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2007-10-26  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased in 1990 and one of the NEOGEO’s earliest signature games, this side-scrolling platformer mixes action with the mystical world of fantasy. A magician named Elta, last descendant of the famed Magician Lord, takes on an epic adventure to save the world from the evil Gul-Agieze. Elta must battle through eight stages, collecting the eight tomes of power that are the key to defeating Gul-Agieze and his evil plans. By obtaining orbs in one of three colors (elements) that appear during the progress of the game, Elta’s offensive powers and jumping abilities can be strengthened. The effect varies considerably depending on the combination of elements though, and Elta can transform into six different forms (Waterman, Dragon Warrior, Shinobi, Samurai, Raijin, or Poseidon). Can you help Elta to become the new Magician Lord?  i2007kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext01229na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002000005264002900025300002300054500098200077542003301059655002701092EADE00aArt of Fighting 1bD4 Enterprisec2007-10-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis fighting game, released in 1992, began the story of the Sakazaki family and Robert Garcia, further developed in two later sequels. Yuri Sakazaki has been abducted by Mr. Big to punish her father, Takuma, and her brother, Ryo. To rescue her, Ryo and Robert must take on numerous enemies around South Town, eventually reaching the mysterious Mr. Karate. The passion of the game’s creators is evident in the unique game play elements introduced. These include an energy gauge that is depleted every time a fighter uses a special maneuver, Desperation Attacks that are usable only when a fighter’s health is low, and camera zooming that adjusts on the fly as fighters move around the stage. All these features ensure that players use strategy and tactics, rather than simply mash buttons. Adding to the mix are little touches such as characters showing cuts when they are injured and voice-over samples during cut scenes. Can you perfect the art of fighting and save Yuri?  i2007kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext01238na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264003400023300002300057500098200080542003901062655002701101EADJ00aRyuuko no Ken 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis fighting game, released in 1992, began the story of the Sakazaki family and Robert Garcia, further developed in two later sequels. Yuri Sakazaki has been abducted by Mr. Big to punish her father, Takuma, and her brother, Ryo. To rescue her, Ryo and Robert must take on numerous enemies around South Town, eventually reaching the mysterious Mr. Karate. The passion of the game’s creators is evident in the unique game play elements introduced. These include an energy gauge that is depleted every time a fighter uses a special maneuver, Desperation Attacks that are usable only when a fighter’s health is low, and camera zooming that adjusts on the fly as fighters move around the stage. All these features ensure that players use strategy and tactics, rather than simply mash buttons. Adding to the mix are little touches such as characters showing cuts when they are injured and voice-over samples during cut scenes. Can you perfect the art of fighting and save Yuri?  i2014kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext01241na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002000005264003500025300002300060500098200083542003901065655002701104EADP00aArt of Fighting 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2007-11-2  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis fighting game, released in 1992, began the story of the Sakazaki family and Robert Garcia, further developed in two later sequels. Yuri Sakazaki has been abducted by Mr. Big to punish her father, Takuma, and her brother, Ryo. To rescue her, Ryo and Robert must take on numerous enemies around South Town, eventually reaching the mysterious Mr. Karate. The passion of the game’s creators is evident in the unique game play elements introduced. These include an energy gauge that is depleted every time a fighter uses a special maneuver, Desperation Attacks that are usable only when a fighter’s health is low, and camera zooming that adjusts on the fly as fighters move around the stage. All these features ensure that players use strategy and tactics, rather than simply mash buttons. Adding to the mix are little touches such as characters showing cuts when they are injured and voice-over samples during cut scenes. Can you perfect the art of fighting and save Yuri?  i2007kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext01309na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002000005264002900025300002300054500106200077542003301139655002701172EAEE00aSamurai Shodown 1bD4 Enterprisec2008-6-16  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis first entry in the extremely popular and revolutionary fighting-game series was released in 1993. Choose from twelve swordsmen with highly individualistic characteristics and fight furiously, ultimately confronting the evil Amakusa Shiro Tokisada. Each character wields his/her own specific weapon, but you must be careful not to lose it during the heat of battle. Some of the fighters also bring an animal companion into the fray, offering a unique aspect to the quick-paced action. Another significant feature of the game is the anger gauge, which indicates the level of anger felt by each of the combatants as repeated injuries are suffered. If the anger reaches its maximum level, the attacking ability of the character increases, leading to even more intense confrontations. Through it all, the refined camera system smoothly zooms in and out of the playing field, presenting the frenzy of the battle while showcasing the lively background (watch as the referee scores hits!). Awake the samurai spirit within and get ready for a new kind of fight!  i2008kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext01322na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002000005264003500025300002300060500106200083542004001145655002701185EAEJ00aSamurai Spirits 1b D4 Enterprise, Inc.c2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis first entry in the extremely popular and revolutionary fighting-game series was released in 1993. Choose from twelve swordsmen with highly individualistic characteristics and fight furiously, ultimately confronting the evil Amakusa Shiro Tokisada. Each character wields his/her own specific weapon, but you must be careful not to lose it during the heat of battle. Some of the fighters also bring an animal companion into the fray, offering a unique aspect to the quick-paced action. Another significant feature of the game is the anger gauge, which indicates the level of anger felt by each of the combatants as repeated injuries are suffered. If the anger reaches its maximum level, the attacking ability of the character increases, leading to even more intense confrontations. Through it all, the refined camera system smoothly zooms in and out of the playing field, presenting the frenzy of the battle while showcasing the lively background (watch as the referee scores hits!). Awake the samurai spirit within and get ready for a new kind of fight!  i2014k D4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext01323na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002000005264003600025300002300061500106200084542004001146655002701186EAEP00aSamurai Shodown 1b D4 Enterprise, Inc.c2008-5-30  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis first entry in the extremely popular and revolutionary fighting-game series was released in 1993. Choose from twelve swordsmen with highly individualistic characteristics and fight furiously, ultimately confronting the evil Amakusa Shiro Tokisada. Each character wields his/her own specific weapon, but you must be careful not to lose it during the heat of battle. Some of the fighters also bring an animal companion into the fray, offering a unique aspect to the quick-paced action. Another significant feature of the game is the anger gauge, which indicates the level of anger felt by each of the combatants as repeated injuries are suffered. If the anger reaches its maximum level, the attacking ability of the character increases, leading to even more intense confrontations. Through it all, the refined camera system smoothly zooms in and out of the playing field, presenting the frenzy of the battle while showcasing the lively background (watch as the referee scores hits!). Awake the samurai spirit within and get ready for a new kind of fight!  i2008k D4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext01169na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001900005264003000024300002300054500092400077542003301001655002501034EAFE00aBlue's Journey 1bD4 Enterprisec2007-11-12  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe planet of Raguy has been invaded by the Daruma tribe, changing it from a beautiful and peaceful place into one filled with pollution. This horizontally scrolling action game, released in 1991, tells the story of an insectarian named Blue and his quest to save the planet and keep its inhabitants from being turned into slaves. Use Blue’s main weapon, a leaf, to flip enemies onto their heads and then throw them at other members of the Daruma tribe, defeating anyone in your way. Additional weapons, such as bombs and boomerangs, are also available, or you can collect flowers as you progress to purchase other special items like honey or swim fins. Blue also has the special ability to change his size at will—if he’s too big to fit in a particular area, then shrink him! The bright, colorful graphics—combined with lots of hidden items to find—ensure an enjoyable experience with plenty of replay value.  i2007kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext01193na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001000005264002600015300002300041500092400064542003100988655002501019655002701044EAFJ00aRaguy 1bHudson Softc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe planet of Raguy has been invaded by the Daruma tribe, changing it from a beautiful and peaceful place into one filled with pollution. This horizontally scrolling action game, released in 1991, tells the story of an insectarian named Blue and his quest to save the planet and keep its inhabitants from being turned into slaves. Use Blue’s main weapon, a leaf, to flip enemies onto their heads and then throw them at other members of the Daruma tribe, defeating anyone in your way. Additional weapons, such as bombs and boomerangs, are also available, or you can collect flowers as you progress to purchase other special items like honey or swim fins. Blue also has the special ability to change his size at will—if he’s too big to fit in a particular area, then shrink him! The bright, colorful graphics—combined with lots of hidden items to find—ensure an enjoyable experience with plenty of replay value.  i2014kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext01203na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001900005264002700024300002300051500092400074542003100998655002501029655002701054EAFP00aBlue's Journey 1bHudson Softc2007-11-9  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe planet of Raguy has been invaded by the Daruma tribe, changing it from a beautiful and peaceful place into one filled with pollution. This horizontally scrolling action game, released in 1991, tells the story of an insectarian named Blue and his quest to save the planet and keep its inhabitants from being turned into slaves. Use Blue’s main weapon, a leaf, to flip enemies onto their heads and then throw them at other members of the Daruma tribe, defeating anyone in your way. Additional weapons, such as bombs and boomerangs, are also available, or you can collect flowers as you progress to purchase other special items like honey or swim fins. Blue also has the special ability to change his size at will—if he’s too big to fit in a particular area, then shrink him! The bright, colorful graphics—combined with lots of hidden items to find—ensure an enjoyable experience with plenty of replay value.  i2007kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext01292na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002900005264002800034300002300062500103700085542003301122655002701155EAGE04aThe King of Fighters '94 1bD4 Enterprisec2008-1-7  a1 Wii optical disc  aAs the first game in the long-running King of Fighters series, The King of Fighters ’94 brought together popular characters from other well-known franchises and pitted them against each other. Match warriors from Fatal Fury against favorites from its sister series, Art of Fighting. Or see if the casts of the Ikari Warriors and Psycho Soldier series better suit your fighting style. Plus, there’s a set of brand- new characters, exclusive to the KOF series, that are willing to join the fray. But there’s a twist—instead of the standard best best-two- out- of- three- rounds fight setup, players choose one of eight teams, each made up of three teammates. To win, all members of the other team must be eliminated before your fighters are knocked out. Use the game’s power gauge to inflict maximum damage and end the round with a devastating finishing move. It’s a battle royal unlike anything else—a game whose inspiration is easily seen in the fighting games that followed it. Can your team be the last one standing?  i2008kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext01304na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002900005264003400034300002300068500103700091542003901128655002701167EAGJ04aThe King of Fighters '94 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aAs the first game in the long-running King of Fighters series, The King of Fighters ’94 brought together popular characters from other well-known franchises and pitted them against each other. Match warriors from Fatal Fury against favorites from its sister series, Art of Fighting. Or see if the casts of the Ikari Warriors and Psycho Soldier series better suit your fighting style. Plus, there’s a set of brand- new characters, exclusive to the KOF series, that are willing to join the fray. But there’s a twist—instead of the standard best best-two- out- of- three- rounds fight setup, players choose one of eight teams, each made up of three teammates. To win, all members of the other team must be eliminated before your fighters are knocked out. Use the game’s power gauge to inflict maximum damage and end the round with a devastating finishing move. It’s a battle royal unlike anything else—a game whose inspiration is easily seen in the fighting games that followed it. Can your team be the last one standing?  i2014kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext01306na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002900005264003600034300002300070500103700093542003901130655002701169EAGP04aThe King of Fighters '94 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2007-11-23  a1 Wii optical disc  aAs the first game in the long-running King of Fighters series, The King of Fighters ’94 brought together popular characters from other well-known franchises and pitted them against each other. Match warriors from Fatal Fury against favorites from its sister series, Art of Fighting. Or see if the casts of the Ikari Warriors and Psycho Soldier series better suit your fighting style. Plus, there’s a set of brand- new characters, exclusive to the KOF series, that are willing to join the fray. But there’s a twist—instead of the standard best best-two- out- of- three- rounds fight setup, players choose one of eight teams, each made up of three teammates. To win, all members of the other team must be eliminated before your fighters are knocked out. Use the game’s power gauge to inflict maximum damage and end the round with a devastating finishing move. It’s a battle royal unlike anything else—a game whose inspiration is easily seen in the fighting games that followed it. Can your team be the last one standing?  i2007kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext01135na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264003000026300002300056500084900079542003300928655002500961655002700986EAHE00aBaseball Stars 2 1bD4 Enterprisec2007-12-10  a1 Wii optical disc  aLace up your cleats, and step onto the diamond with the pros of Baseball Stars 2. You’ll find everything you’d expect in a classic game of baseball, but with an arcade feel and intense action that distinguish it from the pack. Pick one of six unique teams from cities around the world, and then get ready for nine innings of excitement, whether you’re taking on the computer in a 15-game tournament or squaring off against a friend. There are two modes of game play, so even the most inexperienced player can compete at the major-league level (with a little computer-aided fielding). Watch as the game develops through split-screen views and close-up shots worthy of any highlight film, and see if you can catch the numerous over-the-top animations of the large and detailed player models. Think you have what it takes to win the pennant?  i2007kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aBaseball games2wiiext01145na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264003400026300002300060500084900083542003900932655002500971655002700996EAHJ00aBaseball Stars 2 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aLace up your cleats, and step onto the diamond with the pros of Baseball Stars 2. You’ll find everything you’d expect in a classic game of baseball, but with an arcade feel and intense action that distinguish it from the pack. Pick one of six unique teams from cities around the world, and then get ready for nine innings of excitement, whether you’re taking on the computer in a 15-game tournament or squaring off against a friend. There are two modes of game play, so even the most inexperienced player can compete at the major-league level (with a little computer-aided fielding). Watch as the game develops through split-screen views and close-up shots worthy of any highlight film, and see if you can catch the numerous over-the-top animations of the large and detailed player models. Think you have what it takes to win the pennant?  i2014kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aBaseball games2wiiext01147na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264003600026300002300062500084900085542003900934655002500973655002700998EAHP00aBaseball Stars 2 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2007-11-30  a1 Wii optical disc  aLace up your cleats, and step onto the diamond with the pros of Baseball Stars 2. You’ll find everything you’d expect in a classic game of baseball, but with an arcade feel and intense action that distinguish it from the pack. Pick one of six unique teams from cities around the world, and then get ready for nine innings of excitement, whether you’re taking on the computer in a 15-game tournament or squaring off against a friend. There are two modes of game play, so even the most inexperienced player can compete at the major-league level (with a little computer-aided fielding). Watch as the game develops through split-screen views and close-up shots worthy of any highlight film, and see if you can catch the numerous over-the-top animations of the large and detailed player models. Think you have what it takes to win the pennant?  i2007kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aBaseball games2wiiext01206na  a2200109   4500001000500000245003100005264003000036300002300066500094900089542003301038655002501071EAIE00aTop Hunter - Roddy & Cathy 1bD4 Enterprisec2007-12-31  a1 Wii optical disc  aTake on the role of either Roddy or Cathy, bounty hunters in this side-scrolling action game set far in the future when humans have colonized space. But all is not well: Space pirates called the Klaptons are making their way through the galaxies, wiping out peaceful settlements along their path. This disgraceful behavior leads to them having a price on their heads, so now Roddy and Cathy must travel through four distinct worlds on a mission to defeat their leader, Captain Klapton. Both characters have retractable arms-used to grab enemies or other objects in the scenery-that can then be thrown at others to destroy them. Also, be on the lookout for rings or levers to pull, as this might reveal special bonuses. Further adding to the mix, the game uses a unique system where the action happens on two planes, with the player switching between them at will. Can you prove yourself worthy of the Top Hunter name and help save the universe?  i2007kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext01216na  a2200109   4500001000500000245003100005264003400036300002300070500094900093542003901042655002501081EAIJ00aTop Hunter - Roddy & Cathy 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aTake on the role of either Roddy or Cathy, bounty hunters in this side-scrolling action game set far in the future when humans have colonized space. But all is not well: Space pirates called the Klaptons are making their way through the galaxies, wiping out peaceful settlements along their path. This disgraceful behavior leads to them having a price on their heads, so now Roddy and Cathy must travel through four distinct worlds on a mission to defeat their leader, Captain Klapton. Both characters have retractable arms-used to grab enemies or other objects in the scenery-that can then be thrown at others to destroy them. Also, be on the lookout for rings or levers to pull, as this might reveal special bonuses. Further adding to the mix, the game uses a unique system where the action happens on two planes, with the player switching between them at will. Can you prove yourself worthy of the Top Hunter name and help save the universe?  i2014kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext01218na  a2200109   4500001000500000245003100005264003600036300002300072500094900095542003901044655002501083EAIP00aTop Hunter - Roddy & Cathy 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2007-12-14  a1 Wii optical disc  aTake on the role of either Roddy or Cathy, bounty hunters in this side-scrolling action game set far in the future when humans have colonized space. But all is not well: Space pirates called the Klaptons are making their way through the galaxies, wiping out peaceful settlements along their path. This disgraceful behavior leads to them having a price on their heads, so now Roddy and Cathy must travel through four distinct worlds on a mission to defeat their leader, Captain Klapton. Both characters have retractable arms-used to grab enemies or other objects in the scenery-that can then be thrown at others to destroy them. Also, be on the lookout for rings or levers to pull, as this might reveal special bonuses. Further adding to the mix, the game uses a unique system where the action happens on two planes, with the player switching between them at will. Can you prove yourself worthy of the Top Hunter name and help save the universe?  i2007kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext01073na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001500005264002900020300002300049500083300072542003300905655002500938EAJE00aMetal Slug 1bD4 Enterprisec2008-5-26  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased in 1996 by SNK, Metal Slug is a side-scrolling military-action game. Players control Marco and Tarma, both members of the special-ops force Team Peregrine Falcon (commonly known as Team PF), and battle their way through stage after stage of intense action. The goal is to try to overthrow General Morden and win back the stolen weapon, the Metal Slug. Players must blast through waves of enemies and machines (while also jumping over any obstacles in the way) to advance through the stages. It's not as hopeless as it might sound, though—weapons such as heavy machine guns, shotguns, rocket launchers and flamethrowers, as well as the Metal Slug itself (which appears frequently in the game), will make the battle easier. Take on General Morden with a friend to lighten your load and ramp up the excitement even more.  i2008kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext01161na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001500005264003400020300002300054500083300077542003900910655002500949655002700974655002601001EAJJ00aMetal Slug 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased in 1996 by SNK, Metal Slug is a side-scrolling military-action game. Players control Marco and Tarma, both members of the special-ops force Team Peregrine Falcon (commonly known as Team PF), and battle their way through stage after stage of intense action. The goal is to try to overthrow General Morden and win back the stolen weapon, the Metal Slug. Players must blast through waves of enemies and machines (while also jumping over any obstacles in the way) to advance through the stages. It's not as hopeless as it might sound, though—weapons such as heavy machine guns, shotguns, rocket launchers and flamethrowers, as well as the Metal Slug itself (which appears frequently in the game), will make the battle easier. Take on General Morden with a friend to lighten your load and ramp up the excitement even more.  i2014kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext01161na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001500005264003400020300002300054500083300077542003900910655002500949655002700974655002601001EAJP00aMetal Slug 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2008-5-9  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased in 1996 by SNK, Metal Slug is a side-scrolling military-action game. Players control Marco and Tarma, both members of the special-ops force Team Peregrine Falcon (commonly known as Team PF), and battle their way through stage after stage of intense action. The goal is to try to overthrow General Morden and win back the stolen weapon, the Metal Slug. Players must blast through waves of enemies and machines (while also jumping over any obstacles in the way) to advance through the stages. It's not as hopeless as it might sound, though—weapons such as heavy machine guns, shotguns, rocket launchers and flamethrowers, as well as the Metal Slug itself (which appears frequently in the game), will make the battle easier. Take on General Morden with a friend to lighten your load and ramp up the excitement even more.  i2008kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext01317na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264002900023300002300052500107400075542003301149655002501182EAKE00aBurning Fight 1bD4 Enterprisec2008-6-23  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased in 1991 by SNK, BURNING FIGHT is a side-scrolling hand-to-hand-combat action game. In pursuit of Casterora, leader of a huge syndicate that has escaped from New York to Osaka, the protagonists are three detectives—Duke, Ryu, and Billy. Each character fights using a combination of punches, kicks, and jumps, and his own particular special move, activated by simultaneously pressing the jump and attack buttons. These lethal techniques have enormous destructive force, but they also consume a great deal of energy. For this reason, players must use their special moves with skillful timing. Luckily for the detectives, new weapons and additional health can be found by breaking things like phone booths and street signs along the way. A boss, who must be defeated in order to continue the mission, awaits at the end of each stage. You can also take on the gang with a friend, but beware that the attacks by one player can damage the other—so keep an eye on where your partner is in the heat of the battle. End Casterora’s reign of terror once and for all!  i2008kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext01409na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001800005264003400023300002300057500107400080542003901154655002501193655002701218655003001245EAKJ00aBurning Fight 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased in 1991 by SNK, BURNING FIGHT is a side-scrolling hand-to-hand-combat action game. In pursuit of Casterora, leader of a huge syndicate that has escaped from New York to Osaka, the protagonists are three detectives—Duke, Ryu, and Billy. Each character fights using a combination of punches, kicks, and jumps, and his own particular special move, activated by simultaneously pressing the jump and attack buttons. These lethal techniques have enormous destructive force, but they also consume a great deal of energy. For this reason, players must use their special moves with skillful timing. Luckily for the detectives, new weapons and additional health can be found by breaking things like phone booths and street signs along the way. A boss, who must be defeated in order to continue the mission, awaits at the end of each stage. You can also take on the gang with a friend, but beware that the attacks by one player can damage the other—so keep an eye on where your partner is in the heat of the battle. End Casterora’s reign of terror once and for all!  i2014kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext01410na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001800005264003500023300002300058500107400081542003901155655002501194655002701219655003001246EAKP00aBurning Fight 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2008-5-30  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased in 1991 by SNK, BURNING FIGHT is a side-scrolling hand-to-hand-combat action game. In pursuit of Casterora, leader of a huge syndicate that has escaped from New York to Osaka, the protagonists are three detectives—Duke, Ryu, and Billy. Each character fights using a combination of punches, kicks, and jumps, and his own particular special move, activated by simultaneously pressing the jump and attack buttons. These lethal techniques have enormous destructive force, but they also consume a great deal of energy. For this reason, players must use their special moves with skillful timing. Luckily for the detectives, new weapons and additional health can be found by breaking things like phone booths and street signs along the way. A boss, who must be defeated in order to continue the mission, awaits at the end of each stage. You can also take on the gang with a friend, but beware that the attacks by one player can damage the other—so keep an eye on where your partner is in the heat of the battle. End Casterora’s reign of terror once and for all!  i2008kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext01311na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002200005264002900027300002300056500106200079542003301141655002701174EALE00aArt of Fighting 2 1bD4 Enterprisec2008-7-28  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased in 1994 by SNK, ART OF FIGHTING 2 sees 12 characters compete for the title in the toughest fighting contest of them all: King of Fighters. Each character has a range of deadly techniques in his/her arsenal, and players must use these lethal techniques to fight their opponents. As in the original ART OF FIGHTING, however, using a deadly technique lowers a character’s mental-energy gauge. For this reason, players must use these techniques carefully. Meanwhile, players can taunt an opponent to exhaust his/her mental energy, and even suppress the opponent’s techniques if successful. This type of mental-energy offense and defense gives ART OF FIGHTING 2 a uniquely enjoyable spin on the fighting-game genre. Further adding to the strategy required to win, an attack will become stronger or weaker depending on exactly when the button is pressed. And even if a player is thrown, defensive action is possible with the timely press of a button. All of this adds up to an intense and nail-biting fighting-game experience not found anywhere else!  i2008kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext01320na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002000005264003400025300002300059500106200082542003901144655002701183EALJ00aRyuuko no Ken 2 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased in 1994 by SNK, ART OF FIGHTING 2 sees 12 characters compete for the title in the toughest fighting contest of them all: King of Fighters. Each character has a range of deadly techniques in his/her arsenal, and players must use these lethal techniques to fight their opponents. As in the original ART OF FIGHTING, however, using a deadly technique lowers a character’s mental-energy gauge. For this reason, players must use these techniques carefully. Meanwhile, players can taunt an opponent to exhaust his/her mental energy, and even suppress the opponent’s techniques if successful. This type of mental-energy offense and defense gives ART OF FIGHTING 2 a uniquely enjoyable spin on the fighting-game genre. Further adding to the strategy required to win, an attack will become stronger or weaker depending on exactly when the button is pressed. And even if a player is thrown, defensive action is possible with the timely press of a button. All of this adds up to an intense and nail-biting fighting-game experience not found anywhere else!  i2014kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext01323na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002200005264003500027300002300062500106200085542003901147655002701186EALP00aArt of Fighting 2 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2008-7-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased in 1994 by SNK, ART OF FIGHTING 2 sees 12 characters compete for the title in the toughest fighting contest of them all: King of Fighters. Each character has a range of deadly techniques in his/her arsenal, and players must use these lethal techniques to fight their opponents. As in the original ART OF FIGHTING, however, using a deadly technique lowers a character’s mental-energy gauge. For this reason, players must use these techniques carefully. Meanwhile, players can taunt an opponent to exhaust his/her mental energy, and even suppress the opponent’s techniques if successful. This type of mental-energy offense and defense gives ART OF FIGHTING 2 a uniquely enjoyable spin on the fighting-game genre. Further adding to the strategy required to win, an attack will become stronger or weaker depending on exactly when the button is pressed. And even if a player is thrown, defensive action is possible with the timely press of a button. All of this adds up to an intense and nail-biting fighting-game experience not found anywhere else!  i2008kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext01080na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001700005264002800022300002300050500083900073542003300912655002500945EAME00aNinja Combat 1bD4 Enterprisec2008-6-2  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased in 1990, Ninja Combat is a side-scrolling combat-action game. Take control of the ninjas Joe (one player) and Hayabusa (two players), and enter into battle against a group of evil ninjas called the Kage Ichizoku. Make your way into their home fortress, Ninja Tower, which dominates a big city of the near future. Fight using normal attacks, jumps, special movements, and ninja materials that deliver damaging blows to all enemies on the screen. In addition, you’ll find weapons and items to aid you along the way. Even better, as you progress in the game, reliable allies such as Musashi, Kagero, and Gembu will emerge to fight alongside you, allowing you to choose a new character in each stage. Ninja Combat also supports simultaneous play with two players, so you can grab a friend and defeat the Kage Ichizoku together!  i2008kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext01173na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001700005264003400022300002300056500083900079542003900918655002500957655002700982655003001009EAMJ00aNinja Combat 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased in 1990, Ninja Combat is a side-scrolling combat-action game. Take control of the ninjas Joe (one player) and Hayabusa (two players), and enter into battle against a group of evil ninjas called the Kage Ichizoku. Make your way into their home fortress, Ninja Tower, which dominates a big city of the near future. Fight using normal attacks, jumps, special movements, and ninja materials that deliver damaging blows to all enemies on the screen. In addition, you’ll find weapons and items to aid you along the way. Even better, as you progress in the game, reliable allies such as Musashi, Kagero, and Gembu will emerge to fight alongside you, allowing you to choose a new character in each stage. Ninja Combat also supports simultaneous play with two players, so you can grab a friend and defeat the Kage Ichizoku together!  i2014kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext01174na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001700005264003500022300002300057500083900080542003900919655002500958655002700983655003001010EAMP00aNinja Combat 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2008-6-13  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased in 1990, Ninja Combat is a side-scrolling combat-action game. Take control of the ninjas Joe (one player) and Hayabusa (two players), and enter into battle against a group of evil ninjas called the Kage Ichizoku. Make your way into their home fortress, Ninja Tower, which dominates a big city of the near future. Fight using normal attacks, jumps, special movements, and ninja materials that deliver damaging blows to all enemies on the screen. In addition, you’ll find weapons and items to aid you along the way. Even better, as you progress in the game, reliable allies such as Musashi, Kagero, and Gembu will emerge to fight alongside you, allowing you to choose a new character in each stage. Ninja Combat also supports simultaneous play with two players, so you can grab a friend and defeat the Kage Ichizoku together!  i2008kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext01302na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001700005264002900022300002300051500105800074542003301132655002701165EANE00aFatal Fury 2 1bD4 Enterprisec2008-6-30  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased in 1992 by SNK, FATAL FURY 2 is the second installment of the renowned fighting-game series. In addition to Terry, Andy, and Joe, who appeared in the original game, another five distinctive fighters gather from around the world to compete for the championship title. Also newly added are stage-specific hazards and the ability to perform desperation attacks when a character’s strength is low. These particularly deadly techniques create the chance for a come-from-behind victory achieved with a single strike. Moreover, the innovative two-line battle, which proved popular in the previous version, has also been radically enhanced. Pressing the weak attack and strong attack buttons simultaneously enables a player to move their fighter to another line themselves, or to launch an attack that pushes the opponent back to another line. This game mechanic, unique to this title in the series, allows the player to take advantage of the depth of the screen and create even more exciting bouts. Can you prove yourself the king of fighters again?  i2008kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext01337na  a2200109   4500001000500000245004100005264003400046300002300080500105800103542003901161655002701200EANJ00aGarou Densetsu 2 - Aratanaru Tatakai 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased in 1992 by SNK, FATAL FURY 2 is the second installment of the renowned fighting-game series. In addition to Terry, Andy, and Joe, who appeared in the original game, another five distinctive fighters gather from around the world to compete for the championship title. Also newly added are stage-specific hazards and the ability to perform desperation attacks when a character’s strength is low. These particularly deadly techniques create the chance for a come-from-behind victory achieved with a single strike. Moreover, the innovative two-line battle, which proved popular in the previous version, has also been radically enhanced. Pressing the weak attack and strong attack buttons simultaneously enables a player to move their fighter to another line themselves, or to launch an attack that pushes the opponent back to another line. This game mechanic, unique to this title in the series, allows the player to take advantage of the depth of the screen and create even more exciting bouts. Can you prove yourself the king of fighters again?  i2014kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext01351na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001700005264003500022300002300057500105800080542003901138655002501177655002701202EANP00aFatal Fury 2 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2010-6-13  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased in 1992 by SNK, FATAL FURY 2 is the second installment of the renowned fighting-game series. In addition to Terry, Andy, and Joe, who appeared in the original game, another five distinctive fighters gather from around the world to compete for the championship title. Also newly added are stage-specific hazards and the ability to perform desperation attacks when a character’s strength is low. These particularly deadly techniques create the chance for a come-from-behind victory achieved with a single strike. Moreover, the innovative two-line battle, which proved popular in the previous version, has also been radically enhanced. Pressing the weak attack and strong attack buttons simultaneously enables a player to move their fighter to another line themselves, or to launch an attack that pushes the opponent back to another line. This game mechanic, unique to this title in the series, allows the player to take advantage of the depth of the screen and create even more exciting bouts. Can you prove yourself the king of fighters again?  i2010kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext01094na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002500005264002800030300002300058500084500081542003300926655002500959EAOE00aKing of the Monsters 1bD4 Enterprisec2008-7-7  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased by SNK in 1991, King of the Monsters is an action/fighting game that features city-destroying battles between huge monsters. Choose one of six monsters and travel around Japan, stopping to fight in various famous cities, with the aim of becoming the ultimate winner. In addition to punches, kicks, and other regular moves, each character has the ability to use more devastating maneuvers, like throwing flames and shooting laser beams, to defeat opponents. Wrestling elements are also incorporated, as you must completely exhaust your opponent and get a three-count to pin him and be victorious. Along with the player-versus-computer game, multiplayer options allow you and a friend to enjoy one-on-one matches and two-on-two tag-team matches against the computer. Take on the challenge and claim the title of King of the Monsters!  i2008kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext01108na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002500005264003400030300002300064500084500087542003900932655002700971EAOJ00aKing of the Monsters 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased by SNK in 1991, King of the Monsters is an action/fighting game that features city-destroying battles between huge monsters. Choose one of six monsters and travel around Japan, stopping to fight in various famous cities, with the aim of becoming the ultimate winner. In addition to punches, kicks, and other regular moves, each character has the ability to use more devastating maneuvers, like throwing flames and shooting laser beams, to defeat opponents. Wrestling elements are also incorporated, as you must completely exhaust your opponent and get a three-count to pin him and be victorious. Along with the player-versus-computer game, multiplayer options allow you and a friend to enjoy one-on-one matches and two-on-two tag-team matches against the computer. Take on the challenge and claim the title of King of the Monsters!  i2014kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext01109na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002500005264003500030300002300065500084500088542003900933655002700972EAOP00aKing of the Monsters 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2008-6-27  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased by SNK in 1991, King of the Monsters is an action/fighting game that features city-destroying battles between huge monsters. Choose one of six monsters and travel around Japan, stopping to fight in various famous cities, with the aim of becoming the ultimate winner. In addition to punches, kicks, and other regular moves, each character has the ability to use more devastating maneuvers, like throwing flames and shooting laser beams, to defeat opponents. Wrestling elements are also incorporated, as you must completely exhaust your opponent and get a three-count to pin him and be victorious. Along with the player-versus-computer game, multiplayer options allow you and a friend to enjoy one-on-one matches and two-on-two tag-team matches against the computer. Take on the challenge and claim the title of King of the Monsters!  i2008kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext01262na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001900005264002900024300002300053500098000076542003301056655002501089655002601114EAPE00aNinja Commando 1bD4 Enterprisec2008-7-14  a1 Wii optical disc  aNINJA COMMANDO is a vertically scrolling action game released by ADK in 1992. Players choose from among three ninjas—Joe, descended from the Koga ninja; Rayar, a woman who has learned the ways of the Iga ninja; and Ryu, descendant of the famous ninja Fuma Kotaro—as they pursue the merchant of death known as Spider, who plans to use a time machine to bring havoc to the world. The battle spans seven time periods, including the Stone Age, the Egyptian era, and the Japanese Civil War era. Each hero features a variety of attack options in addition to their own normal attack, including a deadly attack that inflicts damage on all enemies on the screen, special ninja-arts attacks performed by inputting specific commands, and finally, a powerful attack unleashed by taking on the “shape of the beast” when three scrolls have been collected. Also supporting two-player cooperative play, you’re welcome to bring a friend and enjoy taking on the evil Spider together.  i2008kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext01235na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001900005264003400024300002300058500098000081542003901061655002501100EAPJ00aNinja Commando 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aNINJA COMMANDO is a vertically scrolling action game released by ADK in 1992. Players choose from among three ninjas—Joe, descended from the Koga ninja; Rayar, a woman who has learned the ways of the Iga ninja; and Ryu, descendant of the famous ninja Fuma Kotaro—as they pursue the merchant of death known as Spider, who plans to use a time machine to bring havoc to the world. The battle spans seven time periods, including the Stone Age, the Egyptian era, and the Japanese Civil War era. Each hero features a variety of attack options in addition to their own normal attack, including a deadly attack that inflicts damage on all enemies on the screen, special ninja-arts attacks performed by inputting specific commands, and finally, a powerful attack unleashed by taking on the “shape of the beast” when three scrolls have been collected. Also supporting two-player cooperative play, you’re welcome to bring a friend and enjoy taking on the evil Spider together.  i2014kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext01224na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001900005264002900024300002300053500098000076542003301056655002501089EAPP00aNINJA COMMANDO 1bD4 Enterprisec2008-7-10  a1 Wii optical disc  aNINJA COMMANDO is a vertically scrolling action game released by ADK in 1992. Players choose from among three ninjas—Joe, descended from the Koga ninja; Rayar, a woman who has learned the ways of the Iga ninja; and Ryu, descendant of the famous ninja Fuma Kotaro—as they pursue the merchant of death known as Spider, who plans to use a time machine to bring havoc to the world. The battle spans seven time periods, including the Stone Age, the Egyptian era, and the Japanese Civil War era. Each hero features a variety of attack options in addition to their own normal attack, including a deadly attack that inflicts damage on all enemies on the screen, special ninja-arts attacks performed by inputting specific commands, and finally, a powerful attack unleashed by taking on the “shape of the beast” when three scrolls have been collected. Also supporting two-player cooperative play, you’re welcome to bring a friend and enjoy taking on the evil Spider together.  i2008kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00990na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001900005264002900024300002300053500070700076542003300783655002500816655002700841EAQE00aWorld Heroes 2 1bD4 Enterprisec2013-1-10  a1 Wii optical disc  aWorld Heroes 2 is a fighting game released in 1993 by ADK, featuring characters based on heroes throughout history like Hanzou, Janne and Captain Kidd - there are 14 characters in all from which to choose. Some gameplay features of this game include, the ability to throw back and reflect projectiles, making it a simple yet in-depth play system. One unusual aspect is the introduction of two game modes, each with different sets of rules. Normal Mode is the standard best-of-two bouts type match, and Death Match Mode is more extreme then that of the previous title, with a 10 count, sudden death system. These two modes make for thrilling and fervent battles that will keep you playing over and over!  i2013kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext00987na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001900005264002600024300002300050500070700073542003300780655002500813655002700838EAQJ00aWorld Heroes 2 1bD4 Enterprisec2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aWorld Heroes 2 is a fighting game released in 1993 by ADK, featuring characters based on heroes throughout history like Hanzou, Janne and Captain Kidd - there are 14 characters in all from which to choose. Some gameplay features of this game include, the ability to throw back and reflect projectiles, making it a simple yet in-depth play system. One unusual aspect is the introduction of two game modes, each with different sets of rules. Normal Mode is the standard best-of-two bouts type match, and Death Match Mode is more extreme then that of the previous title, with a 10 count, sudden death system. These two modes make for thrilling and fervent battles that will keep you playing over and over!  i2014kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext00991na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001900005264003000024300002300054500070700077542003300784655002500817655002700842EAQP00aWorld Heroes 2 1bD4 Enterprisec2012-12-27  a1 Wii optical disc  aWorld Heroes 2 is a fighting game released in 1993 by ADK, featuring characters based on heroes throughout history like Hanzou, Janne and Captain Kidd - there are 14 characters in all from which to choose. Some gameplay features of this game include, the ability to throw back and reflect projectiles, making it a simple yet in-depth play system. One unusual aspect is the introduction of two game modes, each with different sets of rules. Normal Mode is the standard best-of-two bouts type match, and Death Match Mode is more extreme then that of the previous title, with a 10 count, sudden death system. These two modes make for thrilling and fervent battles that will keep you playing over and over!  i2012kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext00879na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264002900026300002300055500059800078542003300676655002500709655002300734EARE00aNeo Turf Masters 1bD4 Enterprisec2008-8-18  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis is a golf game that was first released in 1996. The player picks one of six available golfers and competes on a number of golf courses around the world, including Japan (Fujiyama Oriental Golf Club), America (Grand Canyon Golf Course), Australia (Blue Lagoon Golf Course), and Germany (Baden Golf Course). The game features two modes of play. The first is Stroke Play, in which the player attempts to get the best score by playing all 18 holes. The second is Match Play, in which two players compete to see who can win more of the 18 holes. Grab a friend and get ready to hit the fairway!  i2008kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aGolf games2wiiext00890na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264003400026300002300060500059800083542003900681655002500720655002300745EARJ00aNeo Turf Masters 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis is a golf game that was first released in 1996. The player picks one of six available golfers and competes on a number of golf courses around the world, including Japan (Fujiyama Oriental Golf Club), America (Grand Canyon Golf Course), Australia (Blue Lagoon Golf Course), and Germany (Baden Golf Course). The game features two modes of play. The first is Stroke Play, in which the player attempts to get the best score by playing all 18 holes. The second is Match Play, in which two players compete to see who can win more of the 18 holes. Grab a friend and get ready to hit the fairway!  i2014kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aGolf games2wiiext00891na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264003500026300002300061500059800084542003900682655002500721655002300746EARP00aNeo Turf Masters 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2008-7-25  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis is a golf game that was first released in 1996. The player picks one of six available golfers and competes on a number of golf courses around the world, including Japan (Fujiyama Oriental Golf Club), America (Grand Canyon Golf Course), Australia (Blue Lagoon Golf Course), and Germany (Baden Golf Course). The game features two modes of play. The first is Stroke Play, in which the player attempts to get the best score by playing all 18 holes. The second is Match Play, in which two players compete to see who can win more of the 18 holes. Grab a friend and get ready to hit the fairway!  i2008kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aGolf games2wiiext00911na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002300005264002900028300002300057500066100080542003300741655002700774EASE00aSamurai Shodown II 1bD4 Enterprisec2008-8-25  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis is a fighting game released in 1994 that follows 15 samurai in their individual quests. The rage system, which was popular in the first game, has been further enhanced. Not only does attack power rise when the gauge is full, the player can also use a special technique that can break the opponent's weapon and force the opponent to fight unarmed. The game also allows for more movement techniques such as back-stepping, rushing forward, and ducking, allowing for even more strategies. A fun and important detail of this game is that one of the new characters, Cham Cham, was voiced by voice actress Reiko Chiba, who is an idol in the gaming community.  i2008kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00924na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002500005264003400030300002300064500066100087542003900748655002700787EASJ00aShin Samurai Spirits 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis is a fighting game released in 1994 that follows 15 samurai in their individual quests. The rage system, which was popular in the first game, has been further enhanced. Not only does attack power rise when the gauge is full, the player can also use a special technique that can break the opponent's weapon and force the opponent to fight unarmed. The game also allows for more movement techniques such as back-stepping, rushing forward, and ducking, allowing for even more strategies. A fun and important detail of this game is that one of the new characters, Cham Cham, was voiced by voice actress Reiko Chiba, who is an idol in the gaming community.  i2014kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00922na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002300005264003400028300002300062500066100085542003900746655002700785EASP00aSamurai Shodown II 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2008-8-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis is a fighting game released in 1994 that follows 15 samurai in their individual quests. The rage system, which was popular in the first game, has been further enhanced. Not only does attack power rise when the gauge is full, the player can also use a special technique that can break the opponent's weapon and force the opponent to fight unarmed. The game also allows for more movement techniques such as back-stepping, rushing forward, and ducking, allowing for even more strategies. A fun and important detail of this game is that one of the new characters, Cham Cham, was voiced by voice actress Reiko Chiba, who is an idol in the gaming community.  i2008kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext01087na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002300005264002900028300002300057500080000080542003300880655002500913655002700938EATE00aWorld Heroes 2 Jet 1bD4 Enterprisec2013-2-14  a1 Wii optical disc  aWorld Heroes 2 Jet, initially released in 1994, is the 3rd in the prolific fighting game series. Choose from 16 historical or well-known heroes, villains and fighters and battle your way to the top to become the world's greatest warrior! There are two types of modes in this version, "Tournament of Titans Mode", where you fight three bouts in one day, and if you are successful you move on to the next day, and "World Heroes Training Mode", where you can fight with any opponent. Furthermore, the addition of dash and back step, which were not in the previous version, as well as a countering system that ushers in a more speedy way of fighting, makes World Heroes 2 Jet even more enjoyable to play. There are also four competition types to choose from, allowing for even more in-depth battles.  i2013kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext01084na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002300005264002600028300002300054500080000077542003300877655002500910655002700935EATJ00aWorld Heroes 2 Jet 1bD4 Enterprisec2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aWorld Heroes 2 Jet, initially released in 1994, is the 3rd in the prolific fighting game series. Choose from 16 historical or well-known heroes, villains and fighters and battle your way to the top to become the world's greatest warrior! There are two types of modes in this version, "Tournament of Titans Mode", where you fight three bouts in one day, and if you are successful you move on to the next day, and "World Heroes Training Mode", where you can fight with any opponent. Furthermore, the addition of dash and back step, which were not in the previous version, as well as a countering system that ushers in a more speedy way of fighting, makes World Heroes 2 Jet even more enjoyable to play. There are also four competition types to choose from, allowing for even more in-depth battles.  i2014kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext01086na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002300005264002800028300002300056500080000079542003300879655002500912655002700937EATP00aWorld Heroes 2 Jet 1bD4 Enterprisec2013-5-9  a1 Wii optical disc  aWorld Heroes 2 Jet, initially released in 1994, is the 3rd in the prolific fighting game series. Choose from 16 historical or well-known heroes, villains and fighters and battle your way to the top to become the world's greatest warrior! There are two types of modes in this version, "Tournament of Titans Mode", where you fight three bouts in one day, and if you are successful you move on to the next day, and "World Heroes Training Mode", where you can fight with any opponent. Furthermore, the addition of dash and back step, which were not in the previous version, as well as a countering system that ushers in a more speedy way of fighting, makes World Heroes 2 Jet even more enjoyable to play. There are also four competition types to choose from, allowing for even more in-depth battles.  i2013kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext00187na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002500005264001300030300002300043500000500066542001800071EAUJ00aTwinkle Star Sprites 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB01069na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002900005264002900034300002300063500081300086542003300899655002700932EAVE04aThe King of Fighters '95 1bD4 Enterprisec2010-4-26  a1 Wii optical disc  aKing of Fighters ’95 is a fighting game released in 1995 that features the main characters from the popular Fatal Fury, Ikari Warriors, Psycho Soldier and Art of Fighting games who engage in battle once again after the 1994 release of King of Fighters ’94. Kyo Kusanagi’s rival Iori Yagami has also joined the fight to leave his lasting mark on the continuing storyline and on Kyo, the game’s hero, so watch out! Three on three team battles, a power gauge that lets you store up energy to land a devastating blow, and the one-shot reversal super special moves unique to the series are all going strong just like in the ’94 release. On top of all that, this release also adds a new “Team Edit” ability, allowing you to enjoy bouts with a level of strategy like you’ve never experienced before.  i2010kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext01068na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002900005264002800034300002300062500081300085542003300898655002700931EAVJ04aThe King of Fighters '95 1bD4 Enterprisec2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aKing of Fighters ’95 is a fighting game released in 1995 that features the main characters from the popular Fatal Fury, Ikari Warriors, Psycho Soldier and Art of Fighting games who engage in battle once again after the 1994 release of King of Fighters ’94. Kyo Kusanagi’s rival Iori Yagami has also joined the fight to leave his lasting mark on the continuing storyline and on Kyo, the game’s hero, so watch out! Three on three team battles, a power gauge that lets you store up energy to land a devastating blow, and the one-shot reversal super special moves unique to the series are all going strong just like in the ’94 release. On top of all that, this release also adds a new “Team Edit” ability, allowing you to enjoy bouts with a level of strategy like you’ve never experienced before.  i2014kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext01068na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002900005264002800034300002300062500081300085542003300898655002700931EAVP04aThe King of Fighters '95 1bD4 Enterprisec2010-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aKing of Fighters ’95 is a fighting game released in 1995 that features the main characters from the popular Fatal Fury, Ikari Warriors, Psycho Soldier and Art of Fighting games who engage in battle once again after the 1994 release of King of Fighters ’94. Kyo Kusanagi’s rival Iori Yagami has also joined the fight to leave his lasting mark on the continuing storyline and on Kyo, the game’s hero, so watch out! Three on three team battles, a power gauge that lets you store up energy to land a devastating blow, and the one-shot reversal super special moves unique to the series are all going strong just like in the ’94 release. On top of all that, this release also adds a new “Team Edit” ability, allowing you to enjoy bouts with a level of strategy like you’ve never experienced before.  i2010kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00943na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002300005264002800028300002300056500069400079542003300773655002700806EAWE00aFatal Fury Special 1bD4 Enterprisec2010-3-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis is a fighting game released in 1993, pitting 15 different fighters against each other. The cast includes the original eight characters from Fatal Fury 2, as well as three new characters (Billy, Axel and Laurence) and a new boss (Wolfgang). Finally, three characters from the original Fatal Fury (Duck, Dan and Geese) have returned to the fight. By building on the appeal from the previous game with its two-line battles, special moves, and powerful finishers, and further improving on the series' formula, this game is truly worthy of the title "special." Also, if certain special conditions are met, special guest Ryuu Sakazaki will make an appearance, which in itself is noteworthy.  i2010kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00959na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002700005264003400032300002300066500069400089542003900783655002700822EAWJ00aGarou Densetsu Special 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis is a fighting game released in 1993, pitting 15 different fighters against each other. The cast includes the original eight characters from Fatal Fury 2, as well as three new characters (Billy, Axel and Laurence) and a new boss (Wolfgang). Finally, three characters from the original Fatal Fury (Duck, Dan and Geese) have returned to the fight. By building on the appeal from the previous game with its two-line battles, special moves, and powerful finishers, and further improving on the series' formula, this game is truly worthy of the title "special." Also, if certain special conditions are met, special guest Ryuu Sakazaki will make an appearance, which in itself is noteworthy.  i2014kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00993na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002300005264003500028300002300063500069400086542003900780655002500819655002700844EAWP00aFatal Fury Special 1bD4 Enterprise, Inc.c2010-3-26  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis is a fighting game released in 1993, pitting 15 different fighters against each other. The cast includes the original eight characters from Fatal Fury 2, as well as three new characters (Billy, Axel and Laurence) and a new boss (Wolfgang). Finally, three characters from the original Fatal Fury (Duck, Dan and Geese) have returned to the fight. By building on the appeal from the previous game with its two-line battles, special moves, and powerful finishers, and further improving on the series' formula, this game is truly worthy of the title "special." Also, if certain special conditions are met, special guest Ryuu Sakazaki will make an appearance, which in itself is noteworthy.  i2010kD4 Enterprise, Inc.sGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext00206na  a2200097   4500001000500000245004400005264001300049300002300062500000500085542001800090EAYJ00aKing of the Monsters 2 - The Next Thing 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00906na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002500005264002900030300002300059500061700082542003300699655002500732655002700757EAZE00aWorld Heroes Perfect 1bD4 Enterprisec2012-7-26  a1 Wii optical disc  a This is the fourth installment in the World Heroes fighting game series, released in 1995. In this game, 16 figures from across history fight for the title of the world’s strongest. In previous installments, the amount of time you held a button down determined the strength or weakness of an attack, but that system has been removed in this game. In addition to a more orthodox fighting-game approach that enables weak, middle and strong attacks using different buttons, this game includes new elements such as the Hero Gauge, Extra Attacks and Guard Breaker Attacks, adding an exciting new layer of strategy.  i2012kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext00903na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002500005264002600030300002300056500061700079542003300696655002500729655002700754EAZJ00aWorld Heroes Perfect 1bD4 Enterprisec2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a This is the fourth installment in the World Heroes fighting game series, released in 1995. In this game, 16 figures from across history fight for the title of the world’s strongest. In previous installments, the amount of time you held a button down determined the strength or weakness of an attack, but that system has been removed in this game. In addition to a more orthodox fighting-game approach that enables weak, middle and strong attacks using different buttons, this game includes new elements such as the Hero Gauge, Extra Attacks and Guard Breaker Attacks, adding an exciting new layer of strategy.  i2014kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext00484na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002500005264003000030300002300060500019400083542003300277655002500310655002700335EAZP00aWorld Heroes Perfect 1bD4 Enterprisec2012-10-18  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis is the fourth instalment in the World Heroes fighting game series, originally released in 1995. In this game, 16 figures from across history fight for the title of 'World's Strongest'.  i2012kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext00921na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003300005264001800038300002300056500064500079542002300724655002500747655002700772EB2E00aReal Bout Fatal Fury Special 1bSNKc2012-8-9  a1 Wii optical disc  aOriginally released in 1997, this fighting game is the sixth installment in the Fatal Fury series. With a system based on previous games in the series, the game introduced a more evolved two-line battle, improved the power gauge system and abolished the ring out system. These and other changes allow for greater strategic diversity. In addition to the 15 characters featured in previous games (Excluding Geese), this game includes Tung Fu Rue, Cheng Sinzan, Laurence Blood and Wolfgang Krauser for a roster of 19 characters, all truly suited to the name Special. They’ll duke it out here to see who will come out on top as the strongest.  i2012kSNKsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext00923na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003700005264001600042300002300058500064500081542002300726655002500749655002700774EB2J00aReal Bout Garou Densetsu Special 1bSNKc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aOriginally released in 1997, this fighting game is the sixth installment in the Fatal Fury series. With a system based on previous games in the series, the game introduced a more evolved two-line battle, improved the power gauge system and abolished the ring out system. These and other changes allow for greater strategic diversity. In addition to the 15 characters featured in previous games (Excluding Geese), this game includes Tung Fu Rue, Cheng Sinzan, Laurence Blood and Wolfgang Krauser for a roster of 19 characters, all truly suited to the name Special. They’ll duke it out here to see who will come out on top as the strongest.  i2014kSNKsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext00393na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003300005264002800038300002300066500009700089542003300186655002500219655002700244EB2P00aReal Bout Fatal Fury Special 1bD4 Enterprisec2012-9-6  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis is a fighting game released in 1997, and the sixth instalment in the Fatal Fury series.  i2012kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext00179na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001700005264001300022300002300035500000500058542001800063EB3J00aSoccer Brawl 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00189na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002700005264001300032300002300045500000500068542001800073EB4J00aASO II - Last Guardian 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB01017na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001900005264002800024300002300052500073500075542003300810655002500843655002700868EB5E04aThe Last Blade 1bD4 Enterprisec2012-6-7  a1 Wii optical disc  aOriginally released in 1997, The Last Blade is a fighting game set in the "Bakumatsu” period of Japanese history, where 10-plus swordsmen are fighting for different purposes. The game is similar to its predecessors from the Samurai Showdown series released by the same company, but it differs in allowing players to choose between two sword types; the damage-focused “Power” or “Speed,” which promotes speedy play. Other game elements include maneuvers like “Repel,” which allows players to deflect enemy attacks, and “Sublime Slash,” which cancels “Super Slice” and can be combined with “Super Secret Slice.” Don’t miss out on powerful -moves like "Super Secret Slice” and “Hidden Secret Slice.”  i2012kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext01045na  a2200121   4500001000500000245004900005264002600054300002300080500073500103542003300838655002500871655002700896EB5J00aBakumatsu Roman Daini Maku - Gekka no Kenshi 1bD4 Enterprisec2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aOriginally released in 1997, The Last Blade is a fighting game set in the "Bakumatsu” period of Japanese history, where 10-plus swordsmen are fighting for different purposes. The game is similar to its predecessors from the Samurai Showdown series released by the same company, but it differs in allowing players to choose between two sword types; the damage-focused “Power” or “Speed,” which promotes speedy play. Other game elements include maneuvers like “Repel,” which allows players to deflect enemy attacks, and “Sublime Slash,” which cancels “Super Slice” and can be combined with “Super Secret Slice.” Don’t miss out on powerful -moves like "Super Secret Slice” and “Hidden Secret Slice.”  i2014kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext00476na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001900005264002800024300002300052500019400075542003300269655002500302655002700327EB5P04aThe Last Blade 1bD4 Enterprisec2012-8-2  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe Last Blade is a fighting game originally released in 1997, which is set in the "Bakumatsu" period of Japanese history, where more than ten swordsmen are fighting for different purposes.  i2012kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext00857na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001700005264002900022300002300051500057700074542003300651655002500684655002600709EB6E00aMetal Slug 3 1bD4 Enterprisec2012-3-31  a1 Wii optical disc  aMetal Slug 3 is the fourth installment in the Metal Slug series, following Metal Slug, Metal Slug 2 and Metal Slug X. Marco and Tarma are back to blast their way through another action-packed adventure, picking up various weapons along the way. The Slugs are also back and more colorful than ever, with Slugmariners, Drill Slugs and Elephant Slugs joining the original Metal Slugs and Slugnoids. As with previous titles, there are hidden items to be found and POWs to be rescued, while a branching map lets players take a different route to the end with each play-through.  i2012kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00430na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001700005264002600022300002300048500019100071542003300262655002500295EB6J00aMetal Slug 3 1bD4 Enterprisec2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aJoin Marco, Tarma, Eri and Fio on their mission to stop this madman. The intense action builds in momentum with every level and leads to a staggering blaze of of unprecedented firepower.  i2014kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00433na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001700005264002900022300002300051500019100074542003300265655002500298EB6P00aMetal Slug 3 1bD4 Enterprisec2012-6-15  a1 Wii optical disc  aJoin Marco, Tarma, Eri and Fio on their mission to stop this madman. The intense action builds in momentum with every level and leads to a staggering blaze of of unprecedented firepower.  i2012kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00180na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001800005264001300023300002300036500000500059542001800064EB7J04aThe Super Spy 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00862na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001900005264003000024300002300054500057900077542003300656655002500689655002600714EB8E00aShock Troopers 1bD4 Enterprisec2012-10-25  a1 Wii optical disc  aShock Troopers is a military-themed action game that was first released in 1997. The characters are internationally renowned mercenaries assigned to rescue Dr. George and his granddaughter, who have been kidnapped by a terrorist group calling themselves the Bloody Scorpions. In the game you have the option of forming a team using three out of the eight total mercenaries, or going solo in Lone Wolf Mode. The route you choose at the beginning will affect the progress of the game, allowing you to enjoy original game play time after time. You can also play with 2 players.  i2012kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00860na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001900005264002800024300002300052500057900075542003300654655002500687655002600712EB8J00aShock Troopers 1bD4 Enterprisec2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aShock Troopers is a military-themed action game that was first released in 1997. The characters are internationally renowned mercenaries assigned to rescue Dr. George and his granddaughter, who have been kidnapped by a terrorist group calling themselves the Bloody Scorpions. In the game you have the option of forming a team using three out of the eight total mercenaries, or going solo in Lone Wolf Mode. The route you choose at the beginning will affect the progress of the game, allowing you to enjoy original game play time after time. You can also play with 2 players.  i2014kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00862na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001900005264002900024300002300053500058000076542003300656655002500689655002600714EB8P00aShock Troopers 1bD4 Enterprisec2012-11-8  a1 Wii optical disc  a	Shock Troopers is a military-themed action game that was first released in 1997. The characters are internationally renowned mercenaries assigned to rescue Dr. George and his granddaughter, who have been kidnapped by a terrorist group calling themselves the Bloody Scorpions. In the game you have the option of forming a team using three out of the eight total mercenaries, or going solo in Lone Wolf Mode. The route you choose at the beginning will affect the progress of the game, allowing you to enjoy original game play time after time. You can also play with 2 players.  i2012kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00174na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001200005264001300017300002300030500000500053542001800058EB9J00aPulstar 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB01231na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002000005264003000025300002300055500098500078542003301063655002501096EBAE00aMagical Drop II 1bD4 Enterprisec2010-11-29  a1 Wii optical disc  aPuzzle action game released by Data East in 1996. The rules are simple. Control the clown to pull in and throw back the balloons that appear on-screen. If you line up three or more balloons of the same color in a row vertically, they will burst. Some balloons feature unique characteristics. Special balloons, which come in all four colors, pop every balloon that share the same color as them. Arrow balloons burst everything in the direction their arrow is facing. Rainbow balloons have the same effect as special balloons, but can be thrown against a balloon of any color. And then there are bubble balloons, which simply get in your way. Together, these provide you with great chains and combos that make a puzzle game so much fun. Choose between VS CPU Mode, full of battles with a host of comical characters, and Puzzle Mode, where you’ll enjoy a one-player challenge. Both modes support player-versus-player action, meaning you can have a great time together with friends.  i2010kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext01226na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001900005264002600024300002300050500098500073542003301058655002501091EBAJ00aMagical Drop 2 1bD4 Enterprisec2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aPuzzle action game released by Data East in 1996. The rules are simple. Control the clown to pull in and throw back the balloons that appear on-screen. If you line up three or more balloons of the same color in a row vertically, they will burst. Some balloons feature unique characteristics. Special balloons, which come in all four colors, pop every balloon that share the same color as them. Arrow balloons burst everything in the direction their arrow is facing. Rainbow balloons have the same effect as special balloons, but can be thrown against a balloon of any color. And then there are bubble balloons, which simply get in your way. Together, these provide you with great chains and combos that make a puzzle game so much fun. Choose between VS CPU Mode, full of battles with a host of comical characters, and Puzzle Mode, where you’ll enjoy a one-player challenge. Both modes support player-versus-player action, meaning you can have a great time together with friends.  i2014kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext01227na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002000005264002600025300002300051500098500074542003301059655002501092EBAP00aMagical Drop II 1bD4 Enterprisec2010--  a1 Wii optical disc  aPuzzle action game released by Data East in 1996. The rules are simple. Control the clown to pull in and throw back the balloons that appear on-screen. If you line up three or more balloons of the same color in a row vertically, they will burst. Some balloons feature unique characteristics. Special balloons, which come in all four colors, pop every balloon that share the same color as them. Arrow balloons burst everything in the direction their arrow is facing. Rainbow balloons have the same effect as special balloons, but can be thrown against a balloon of any color. And then there are bubble balloons, which simply get in your way. Together, these provide you with great chains and combos that make a puzzle game so much fun. Choose between VS CPU Mode, full of battles with a host of comical characters, and Puzzle Mode, where you’ll enjoy a one-player challenge. Both modes support player-versus-player action, meaning you can have a great time together with friends.  i2010kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00940na  a2200109   4500001000500000245003100005264003000036300002300066500068100089542003300770655002700803EBBE00aFighter's History Dynamite 1bD4 Enterprisec2010-12-27  a1 Wii optical disc  aFIGHTER'S HISTORY DYNAMITE is a fighting game that was released in 1994. In this sequel to the well-loved FIGHTER'S HISTORY, the action takes place once again at the martial arts tournament the Great Grapple. This time, thirteen combatants have emerged to test their skills against the best of the best. Notable playing features include a wide range of secret attacks, a weak spot system that assigns a vulnerable area to each fighter, and the introduction of the original bosses Clown and Karlov as playable characters. The bull from the bonus stage of the Data East classic Karate Champ will also make a special appearance if you are able to clear certain secret conditions.  i2010kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00339na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003100005264002600036300002300062500004200085542003300127655002700160655003000187EBBJ00aFighter's History Dynamite 1bD4 Enterprisec2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aKarnov should stick to side-scrollers  i2014kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext 7a2D fighting games2wiiext00332na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264002900026300002300055500004200078542003300120655002700153655003000180EBBP00aKarnov's Revenge 1bD4 Enterprisec2010-12-3  a1 Wii optical disc  aKarnov should stick to side-scrollers  i2010kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext 7a2D fighting games2wiiext00184na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002200005264001300027300002300040500000500063542001800068EBCJ00aFlying Power Disc 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00665na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002100005264003000026300002300056500041800079542003300497655002500530EBDE00aMagical Drop III 1bD4 Enterprisec2010-12-27  a1 Wii optical disc  aPuzzle action game released by Data East in 1997. Control a clown to pull in and throw back balloons hurled from the top of the screen. If you line up three or more balloons of the same color in a row vertically they will burst, but if you’re not quick enough the balloons will squash the clown and it’s game over. Once you’ve caught the hang of bursting balloons, next you need to master combos and chains.  i2010kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00663na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002100005264002700026300002300053500041800076542003400494655002500528EBDJ00aMagical Drop III 1bD4 enterprisesc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aPuzzle action game released by Data East in 1997. Control a clown to pull in and throw back balloons hurled from the top of the screen. If you line up three or more balloons of the same color in a row vertically they will burst, but if you’re not quick enough the balloons will squash the clown and it’s game over. Once you’ve caught the hang of bursting balloons, next you need to master combos and chains.  i2014kD4 enterprisessGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00665na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002100005264002900026300002300055500041800078542003400496655002500530EBDP00aMagical Drop III 1bD4 enterprisesc2010-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aPuzzle action game released by Data East in 1997. Control a clown to pull in and throw back balloons hurled from the top of the screen. If you line up three or more balloons of the same color in a row vertically they will burst, but if you’re not quick enough the balloons will squash the clown and it’s game over. Once you’ve caught the hang of bursting balloons, next you need to master combos and chains.  i2010kD4 enterprisessGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext01022na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001600005264002900021300002300050500074000073542003300813655002500846655002900871EBEE00aStreet Slam 1bD4 Enterprisec2010-11-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis 3-on-3 street basketball game was released in 1994. Players choose from 10 teams vying for the position of the strongest street basketball team in America. The excitement of this game comes from the players’ ability to enjoy an exhilarating game of street basketball. In addition to pulling off fancy slam dunks, players can enjoy the thrill of basketball with simple controls that allow them to make passes to players in midair to throw down a slam dunk or dunk when rebounding the ball. Additionally, if players charge up their gauges, they’ll be able to make an earth-shattering super shot that can break any defense. This game successfully combines adherence to the basics of basketball with some outrageous special moves.  i2010kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aBasketball games2wiiext01018na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001500005264002600020300002300046500074000069542003300809655002500842655002900867EBEJ00aDunk Dream 1bD4 Enterprisec2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis 3-on-3 street basketball game was released in 1994. Players choose from 10 teams vying for the position of the strongest street basketball team in America. The excitement of this game comes from the players’ ability to enjoy an exhilarating game of street basketball. In addition to pulling off fancy slam dunks, players can enjoy the thrill of basketball with simple controls that allow them to make passes to players in midair to throw down a slam dunk or dunk when rebounding the ball. Additionally, if players charge up their gauges, they’ll be able to make an earth-shattering super shot that can break any defense. This game successfully combines adherence to the basics of basketball with some outrageous special moves.  i2014kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aBasketball games2wiiext01021na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001600005264002800021300002300049500074000072542003300812655002500845655002900870EBEP00aStreet Hoop 1bD4 Enterprisec2010-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis 3-on-3 street basketball game was released in 1994. Players choose from 10 teams vying for the position of the strongest street basketball team in America. The excitement of this game comes from the players’ ability to enjoy an exhilarating game of street basketball. In addition to pulling off fancy slam dunks, players can enjoy the thrill of basketball with simple controls that allow them to make passes to players in midair to throw down a slam dunk or dunk when rebounding the ball. Additionally, if players charge up their gauges, they’ll be able to make an earth-shattering super shot that can break any defense. This game successfully combines adherence to the basics of basketball with some outrageous special moves.  i2010kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aBasketball games2wiiext01115na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001600005264003000021300002300051500087300074542003300947655002500980EBFE00aSpin Master 1bD4 Enterprisec2010-11-22  a1 Wii optical disc  aSPIN MASTER is a side-scrolling action game that was released in 1993. Take on the role of an adventurer named Johnny. Dr. De Playne has stolen your piece of a treasure map and kidnapped your girlfriend Mary. Now you must set off and get them both back. Make your way through five different stages, each of which features a unique and colorful boss at the final turn. After clearing each stage, you will obtain a piece of the treasure map. Put all the pieces together and you’re in for one big surprise! Make full use of jumps and standard attacks to advance through the game. To experience really explosive and invigorating combat, however, be sure to employ the wide range of special attacks that are also available. These include spirit charges, sliding attacks, and super bomb attacks. On top of that, another player can also join in the action at the same time!  i2010kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext01117na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002200005264002600027300002300053500087300076542003300949655002500982EBFJ00aMiracle Adventure 1bD4 Enterprisec2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aSPIN MASTER is a side-scrolling action game that was released in 1993. Take on the role of an adventurer named Johnny. Dr. De Playne has stolen your piece of a treasure map and kidnapped your girlfriend Mary. Now you must set off and get them both back. Make your way through five different stages, each of which features a unique and colorful boss at the final turn. After clearing each stage, you will obtain a piece of the treasure map. Put all the pieces together and you’re in for one big surprise! Make full use of jumps and standard attacks to advance through the game. To experience really explosive and invigorating combat, however, be sure to employ the wide range of special attacks that are also available. These include spirit charges, sliding attacks, and super bomb attacks. On top of that, another player can also join in the action at the same time!  i2014kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext01111na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001600005264002600021300002300047500087300070542003300943655002500976EBFP00aSpin Master 1bD4 Enterprisec2010--  a1 Wii optical disc  aSPIN MASTER is a side-scrolling action game that was released in 1993. Take on the role of an adventurer named Johnny. Dr. De Playne has stolen your piece of a treasure map and kidnapped your girlfriend Mary. Now you must set off and get them both back. Make your way through five different stages, each of which features a unique and colorful boss at the final turn. After clearing each stage, you will obtain a piece of the treasure map. Put all the pieces together and you’re in for one big surprise! Make full use of jumps and standard attacks to advance through the game. To experience really explosive and invigorating combat, however, be sure to employ the wide range of special attacks that are also available. These include spirit charges, sliding attacks, and super bomb attacks. On top of that, another player can also join in the action at the same time!  i2010kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00530na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002900005264002800034300002300062500023800085542003300323655002500356655002700381EBGE04aThe King of Fighters '97 1bD4 Enterprisec2012-3-8  a1 Wii optical disc  a The King of Fighters ’97 is the fourth game in The King of Fighters series, once again allowing players to combat opponents with popular characters from games such as Fatal Fury, Ikari Warriors, Psycho Soldier and Art of Fighting.  i2012kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext00528na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002900005264002600034300002300060500023800083542003300321655002500354655002700379EBGJ04aThe King of Fighters '97 1bD4 Enterprisec2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a The King of Fighters ’97 is the fourth game in The King of Fighters series, once again allowing players to combat opponents with popular characters from games such as Fatal Fury, Ikari Warriors, Psycho Soldier and Art of Fighting.  i2014kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext00492na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002900005264002800034300002300062500023700085542003300322655002700355EBGP04aThe King of Fighters '97 1bD4 Enterprisec2012-2-9  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe King of Fighters ’97 is the fourth game in the King of Fighters series, once again allowing players to combat opponents with popular characters from Fatal Fury, Ikari Warriors, Psycho Soldier, Art of Fighting and other titles.  i2012kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00178na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001600005264001300021300002300034500000500057542001800062EBKJ00aLast Resort 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00194na  a2200097   4500001000500000245003200005264001300037300002300050500000500073542001800078EBLJ00aTsuukai GanGan Koushinkyoku 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00178na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001600005264001300021300002300034500000500057542001800062EBMJ00aFire Suplex 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00203na  a2200097   4500001000500000245003900005264001500044300002300059500000500082542001800087EBNJ00aFu'un Mokushiroku - Kakutou Sousei 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00189na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002700005264001300032300002300045500000500068542001800073EBOJ00aFu'un Super Tag Battle 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00181na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001900005264001300024300002300037500000500060542001800065EBPJ00aLeague Bowling 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00911na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264002900023300002300052500063200075542003200707655002500739655002500764EBQE00aNinja Masters 1bSNK Playmorec2012-11-22  a1 Wii optical disc  aFirst released in 1996, “Ninja Master's”, is set in the fictional land of "Zipangu". Players can select from 10 different ninjas and warriors with which to test their might. The main feature of this game is the ability for each character to use a wide variety of weapons. Also, as each character’s Super Attacks change depending on whether they are armed or unarmed, the player needs to respond differently according to the situation. Damage increases with respect to the Super Power Gauge. There are also many must-see deadly techniques like "Super Death Blow", "Ultimate Super Mode", "Dark Super Power" and "Dark Combo!  i2012kSNK PlaymoresGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext00925na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003600005264002500041300002300066500063200089542003200721655002500753655002500778EBQJ00aNinja Master's Haou Ninpou-chou 1bSNK Playmorec2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aFirst released in 1996, “Ninja Master's”, is set in the fictional land of "Zipangu". Players can select from 10 different ninjas and warriors with which to test their might. The main feature of this game is the ability for each character to use a wide variety of weapons. Also, as each character’s Super Attacks change depending on whether they are armed or unarmed, the player needs to respond differently according to the situation. Damage increases with respect to the Super Power Gauge. There are also many must-see deadly techniques like "Super Death Blow", "Ultimate Super Mode", "Dark Super Power" and "Dark Combo!  i2014kSNK PlaymoresGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext00952na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001900005264002900024300002300053500063200076542003300708655002500741655002700766655002500793EBQP00aNinja Master's 1bD4 Enterprisec2013-1-10  a1 Wii optical disc  aFirst released in 1996, “Ninja Master's”, is set in the fictional land of "Zipangu". Players can select from 10 different ninjas and warriors with which to test their might. The main feature of this game is the ability for each character to use a wide variety of weapons. Also, as each character’s Super Attacks change depending on whether they are armed or unarmed, the player needs to respond differently according to the situation. Damage increases with respect to the Super Power Gauge. There are also many must-see deadly techniques like "Super Death Blow", "Ultimate Super Mode", "Dark Super Power" and "Dark Combo!  i2013kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext00178na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001600005264001300021300002300034500000500057542001800062EBRJ00aJoy Joy Kid 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00996na  a2200133   4500001000500000245002200005264002900027300002300056500067300079542003300752655002500785655002700810655002500837EBSE00aArt of Fighting 3 1bD4 Enterprisec2013-3-21  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased in 1996, Art of Fighting 3: The Path of the Warrior is a fighting game set in Grasshill Valley, where drama and battles unfold among various fighters. Aside from the protagonists Ryo and Robert, this installment has all-new characters. Art of Fighting 3: The Path of the Warrior features powerful airborne combos, more efficient parrying maneuvers, the ability to inflict damage to downed opponents, and the Ultimate K.O., which allows characters to win a match in just one round. Furthermore, the graphics are based off of motion capture technology rendering them smoother than ever before, making it one of the most innovative 2D fighting games at the time.  i2013kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext01018na  a2200133   4500001000500000245004700005264002600052300002300078500067300101542003300774655002500807655002700832655002500859EBSJ04aThe Art of Fighting - Ryuuko no Ken Gaiden 1bD4 Enterprisec2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased in 1996, Art of Fighting 3: The Path of the Warrior is a fighting game set in Grasshill Valley, where drama and battles unfold among various fighters. Aside from the protagonists Ryo and Robert, this installment has all-new characters. Art of Fighting 3: The Path of the Warrior features powerful airborne combos, more efficient parrying maneuvers, the ability to inflict damage to downed opponents, and the Ultimate K.O., which allows characters to win a match in just one round. Furthermore, the graphics are based off of motion capture technology rendering them smoother than ever before, making it one of the most innovative 2D fighting games at the time.  i2014kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext00449na  a2200133   4500001000500000245002200005264002900027300002300056500012600079542003300205655002500238655002700263655002500290EBSP00aArt of Fighting 3 1bD4 Enterprisec2013-6-13  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased in 1996, this is a fighting game set in Grasshill Valley, where drama and battles unfold among various fighters.  i2013kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext00181na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001900005264001300024300002300037500000500060542001800065EBTJ00aCrossed Swords 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB01028na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002400005264002700029300002300056500074300079542003200822655002500854655002700879EBUE00a2020 Super Baseball 1bD4Enterprisec2012-7-5  a1 Wii optical disc  aOriginally released in 1991, this is not your typical baseball game. In the near future, there are two leagues with a total of 12 teams for players to choose from. Pick your team and go for the championship. The games are held at the exclusive Cyber Egg Stadium, where the home run zone is alarmingly small and the fair zone is unusually wide. There is even a stop zone to stop any ball that lands there. As the game progresses Crackers (mines) are installed. During games, armor can be purchased to reinforce your players. All this makes for a unique baseball experience. You may be a bit perplexed at first, but once you get used to it and begin devising a strategy, you might even start enjoying all the curveballs being thrown at you.  i2012kD4EnterprisesGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aBaseball games2wiiext01026na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002400005264002500029300002300054500074300077542003200820655002500852655002700877EBUJ00aSuper Baseball 2020 1bD4Enterprisec2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aOriginally released in 1991, this is not your typical baseball game. In the near future, there are two leagues with a total of 12 teams for players to choose from. Pick your team and go for the championship. The games are held at the exclusive Cyber Egg Stadium, where the home run zone is alarmingly small and the fair zone is unusually wide. There is even a stop zone to stop any ball that lands there. As the game progresses Crackers (mines) are installed. During games, armor can be purchased to reinforce your players. All this makes for a unique baseball experience. You may be a bit perplexed at first, but once you get used to it and begin devising a strategy, you might even start enjoying all the curveballs being thrown at you.  i2014kD4EnterprisesGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aBaseball games2wiiext00539na  a2200133   4500001000500000245002400005264002800029300002300057500021600080542003200296655002500328655002500353655002700378EBUP00a2020 Super Baseball 1bD4Enterprisec2012-8-23  a1 Wii optical disc  aOriginally released in 1991, this is not your typical baseball game. In the near future, there are two leagues with a total of twelve teams the player can choose from; pick your team and go for the championship.  i2012kD4EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aSports games2wiiext 7aBaseball games2wiiext00178na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001600005264001300021300002300034500000500057542001800062EBVJ00aShin-Oh-Ken 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB01078na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001200005264003700017300002300054500078500077542004100862655002500903655002800928EBWE00aSengoku 1bD4Enterprise Co., Ltdc2013-4-25  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn this side scrolling action game set in Washington City, which was initially released in 1991, the player takes the role of a super warrior who must battle against ghosts from the past bent on taking over the present. The main feature of this title is the ability to change characters in mid-play. If you release an incarcerated character while fighting against the enemy, that character becomes available for you to use. The key to a successful strategy is adeptly switching among the ninja dog, samurai or ninja according to the situation. You can also pick up items like weapons and orbs that give you magical attacks. Not only is there adventure to be had in the regular world, but also in a parallel universe, where stages change at a hectic pace, with never a dull moment.  i2013kD4Enterprise Co., LtdsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext01083na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002000005264003400025300002300059500078500082542004100867655002500908655002800933EBWJ00aSengoku Denshou 1bD4Enterprise Co., Ltdc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn this side scrolling action game set in Washington City, which was initially released in 1991, the player takes the role of a super warrior who must battle against ghosts from the past bent on taking over the present. The main feature of this title is the ability to change characters in mid-play. If you release an incarcerated character while fighting against the enemy, that character becomes available for you to use. The key to a successful strategy is adeptly switching among the ninja dog, samurai or ninja according to the situation. You can also pick up items like weapons and orbs that give you magical attacks. Not only is there adventure to be had in the regular world, but also in a parallel universe, where stages change at a hectic pace, with never a dull moment.  i2014kD4Enterprise Co., LtdsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext01155na  a2200145   4500001000500000245001200005264003700017300002300054500078600077542004100863655002500904655002800929655002700957655002500984EBWP00aSengoku 1bD4Enterprise Co., Ltdc2013-7-25  a1 Wii optical disc  a	In this side scrolling action game set in Washington City, which was initially released in 1991, the player takes the role of a super warrior who must battle against ghosts from the past bent on taking over the present. The main feature of this title is the ability to change characters in mid-play. If you release an incarcerated character while fighting against the enemy, that character becomes available for you to use. The key to a successful strategy is adeptly switching among the ninja dog, samurai or ninja according to the situation. You can also pick up items like weapons and orbs that give you magical attacks. Not only is there adventure to be had in the regular world, but also in a parallel universe, where stages change at a hectic pace, with never a dull moment.  i2013kD4Enterprise Co., LtdsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext00911na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001400005264002900019300002300048500063500071542003300706655002500739655002500764EBXE00aSengoku 2 1bD4 Enterprisec2012-11-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aOriginally released in 1993, Sengoku 2 is a belt-scrolling beat-'em-up game. The characters are warriors who have been summoned by a sorceress princess to take down a dark lord while battling through various epochs. As in the previous version, you can transform your characters, but unlike its predecessor, you don't have to save your ally to be able to transform into them, but rather you can change among the Ninja, Tengu and Ninja Dog freely right from the beginning. Furthermore, one of the new elements to this version is the incorporation of build up attacks and defense, giving a more tactical twist to this action brawler.  i2012kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext00916na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002200005264002600027300002300053500063500076542003300711655002500744655002500769EBXJ00aSengoku Denshou 2 1bD4 Enterprisec2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aOriginally released in 1993, Sengoku 2 is a belt-scrolling beat-'em-up game. The characters are warriors who have been summoned by a sorceress princess to take down a dark lord while battling through various epochs. As in the previous version, you can transform your characters, but unlike its predecessor, you don't have to save your ally to be able to transform into them, but rather you can change among the Ninja, Tengu and Ninja Dog freely right from the beginning. Furthermore, one of the new elements to this version is the incorporation of build up attacks and defense, giving a more tactical twist to this action brawler.  i2014kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext00949na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001400005264002800019300002300047500063500070542003300705655002500738655002700763655002500790EBXP00aSengoku 2 1bD4 Enterprisec2013-2-7  a1 Wii optical disc  aOriginally released in 1993, Sengoku 2 is a belt-scrolling beat-'em-up game. The characters are warriors who have been summoned by a sorceress princess to take down a dark lord while battling through various epochs. As in the previous version, you can transform your characters, but unlike its predecessor, you don't have to save your ally to be able to transform into them, but rather you can change among the Ninja, Tengu and Ninja Dog freely right from the beginning. Furthermore, one of the new elements to this version is the incorporation of build up attacks and defense, giving a more tactical twist to this action brawler.  i2013kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext00847na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002500005264003000030300002300060500059400083542003300677655002700710EBZE00aReal Bout Fatal Fury 1bD4 Enterprisec2012-12-13  a1 Wii optical disc  aReal Bout Fatal Fury was first released in 1995, and is the 5th installment in the fighting game series. While based on the previous games, this version saw the incorporation of an independent Sway Button, and the introduction of a more evolved Combination Attack system and the Ring Out component, making for speedier and more enjoyable gameplay. Real Bout Fatal Fury features 16 playable fighters including, the Qin brothers (the boss characters from the previous installment), as well as user-favorites Billy Cane and Duck King. Cut through the ruthless competition and aim for the top!  i2012kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00847na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002900005264002600034300002300060500059400083542003300677655002700710EBZJ00aReal Bout Garou Densetsu 1bD4 Enterprisec2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aReal Bout Fatal Fury was first released in 1995, and is the 5th installment in the fighting game series. While based on the previous games, this version saw the incorporation of an independent Sway Button, and the introduction of a more evolved Combination Attack system and the Ring Out component, making for speedier and more enjoyable gameplay. Real Bout Fatal Fury features 16 playable fighters including, the Qin brothers (the boss characters from the previous installment), as well as user-favorites Billy Cane and Duck King. Cut through the ruthless competition and aim for the top!  i2014kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00920na  a2200133   4500001000500000245002500005264002900030300002300059500059400082542003300676655002500709655002700734655002500761EBZP00aReal Bout Fatal Fury 1bD4 Enterprisec2013-4-25  a1 Wii optical disc  aReal Bout Fatal Fury was first released in 1995, and is the 5th installment in the fighting game series. While based on the previous games, this version saw the incorporation of an independent Sway Button, and the introduction of a more evolved Combination Attack system and the Ring Out component, making for speedier and more enjoyable gameplay. Real Bout Fatal Fury features 16 playable fighters including, the Qin brothers (the boss characters from the previous installment), as well as user-favorites Billy Cane and Duck King. Cut through the ruthless competition and aim for the top!  i2013kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext01116na  a2200109   4500001000500000245004300005264002900048300002300077500084600100542003300946655002700979ECAE00aReal Bout Fatal Fury 2 - The Newcomers 1bD4 Enterprisec2012-9-27  a1 Wii optical disc  a"Real Bout Fatal Fury 2: The Newcomers" is the 7th installment in the Fatal Fury fighting game franchise, and was first released in 1998. Based on the same game mechanics as previous installments, "Real Bout Fatal Fury 2: The Newcomers" boasts an evolved version of the 2-line battle, as well as many new features such as: "Break Shot" - a guard cancel system that is available for several moves; also, when a character continues walking, their sway line accumulates; and when a character is knocked down, if the player expertly times the gauge and button action, the character will swiftly get back on their feet. This time around 2 newcomers have been introduced: Li Xiang Fei the Kung-Fu master and a boxer by the name of Rick Strowd. And Geese Howard makes reappearance as playable character. Choose from 22 fighters and test your might!  i2012kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext01117na  a2200109   4500001000500000245004700005264002600052300002300078500084600101542003300947655002700980ECAJ00aReal Bout Garou Densetsu 2 - The Newcomers 1bD4 Enterprisec2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a"Real Bout Fatal Fury 2: The Newcomers" is the 7th installment in the Fatal Fury fighting game franchise, and was first released in 1998. Based on the same game mechanics as previous installments, "Real Bout Fatal Fury 2: The Newcomers" boasts an evolved version of the 2-line battle, as well as many new features such as: "Break Shot" - a guard cancel system that is available for several moves; also, when a character continues walking, their sway line accumulates; and when a character is knocked down, if the player expertly times the gauge and button action, the character will swiftly get back on their feet. This time around 2 newcomers have been introduced: Li Xiang Fei the Kung-Fu master and a boxer by the name of Rick Strowd. And Geese Howard makes reappearance as playable character. Choose from 22 fighters and test your might!  i2014kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00448na  a2200121   4500001000500000245004200005264002900047300002300076500014200099542003300241655002500274655002700299ECAP00aReal Bout Fatal Fury 2: The Newcomers 1bD4 Enterprisec2012-10-4  a1 Wii optical disc  aReal Bout Fatal Fury 2: The Newcomers is the seventh instalment in the Fatal Fury fighting game franchise and was first released in 1998.  i2012kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext00835na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001700005264002900022300002300051500055500074542003300629655002500662655002600687ECCE00aMetal Slug X 1bD4 Enterprisec2012-8-23  a1 Wii optical disc  a This game is an improved version of Metal Slug 2, adding the new “Iron Lizard” weapon that chases enemies and the “Drop Shot” weapon whose shots bounce. It also adds many new enemies and allows players to adjust the game’s difficulty level by changing the position of bosses and other things. It includes several arranged production features such as changed backgrounds and some rearranged BGM. It’s a solidly enjoyable game-play experience that offers Metal Slug 2 fans some new discoveries if they look for differences while they play.  i2012kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00832na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001700005264002600022300002300048500055500071542003300626655002500659655002600684ECCJ00aMetal Slug X 1bD4 Enterprisec2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a This game is an improved version of Metal Slug 2, adding the new “Iron Lizard” weapon that chases enemies and the “Drop Shot” weapon whose shots bounce. It also adds many new enemies and allows players to adjust the game’s difficulty level by changing the position of bosses and other things. It includes several arranged production features such as changed backgrounds and some rearranged BGM. It’s a solidly enjoyable game-play experience that offers Metal Slug 2 fans some new discoveries if they look for differences while they play.  i2014kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00491na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001700005264002900022300002300051500021100074542003300285655002500318655002600343ECCP00aMetal Slug X 1bD4 Enterprisec2012-9-13  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis game is an improved version of Metal Slug 2. While based on Metal Slug 2, it includes the new 'Iron Lizard' weapon (which homes in on enemies) and the 'Drop Shot' weapon (which fires bouncing bullets).  i2012kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00209na  a2200097   4500001000500000245004700005264001300052300002300065500000500088542001800093ECDJ00aStakes Winner - G1 Kanzen Seihahe no Michi 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00994na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002100005264003000026300002300056500074700079542003300826655002500859ECEE04aThe Last Blade 2 1bD4 Enterprisec2012-10-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe Last Blade 2, originally released in 1998, is the sequel to the fighting game, The Last Blade, which was released a year before. It picks up where the previous title left off and takes the story of battling at the gates of hell to its climax. This time around, there are 16 unique swordsmen from which to choose. Choose from 2 sword types (Strength and Attack). Deflect your enemy's attacks with "Repel". You can also cancel game-changing special moves like "Super Secret Slice" or "Hidden Secret Slice" with a "Sublime Slash", which connects to Super Secret Slice - just like in the previous title. And there are even some new features like aerial repels, aerial guards and knockdown recovery. Take your battles to a whole 'nother level!  i2012kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext01058na  a2200109   4500001000500000245008700005264002800092300002300120500074700143542003300890655002500923ECEJ00aBakumatsu Roman Daini Maku - Gekka no Kenshi - Tsuki ni Saku Hana, Chiri Yuku Hana 1bD4 Enterprisec2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe Last Blade 2, originally released in 1998, is the sequel to the fighting game, The Last Blade, which was released a year before. It picks up where the previous title left off and takes the story of battling at the gates of hell to its climax. This time around, there are 16 unique swordsmen from which to choose. Choose from 2 sword types (Strength and Attack). Deflect your enemy's attacks with "Repel". You can also cancel game-changing special moves like "Super Secret Slice" or "Hidden Secret Slice" with a "Sublime Slash", which connects to Super Secret Slice - just like in the previous title. And there are even some new features like aerial repels, aerial guards and knockdown recovery. Take your battles to a whole 'nother level!  i2014kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00990na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002100005264002600026300002300052500074700075542003300822655002500855ECEP04aThe Last Blade 2 1bD4 Enterprisec2012--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe Last Blade 2, originally released in 1998, is the sequel to the fighting game, The Last Blade, which was released a year before. It picks up where the previous title left off and takes the story of battling at the gates of hell to its climax. This time around, there are 16 unique swordsmen from which to choose. Choose from 2 sword types (Strength and Attack). Deflect your enemy's attacks with "Repel". You can also cancel game-changing special moves like "Super Secret Slice" or "Hidden Secret Slice" with a "Sublime Slash", which connects to Super Secret Slice - just like in the previous title. And there are even some new features like aerial repels, aerial guards and knockdown recovery. Take your battles to a whole 'nother level!  i2012kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00179na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001700005264001300022300002300035500000500058542001800063ECFJ00aBlazing Star 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00859na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003100005264003000036300002300066500056400089542003300653655002500686655002600711ECGE00aShock Troopers - 2nd Squad 1bD4 Enterprisec2012-12-27  a1 Wii optical disc  aShock Troopers: 2nd Squad is a military-themed action game, first released in 1998. In order to stop a large corporation from running amok, choose one of four mercenaries and battle through by shooting, using different weapons and jumping. The highly praised scoring system from the previous game has been left intact, but the characters are all new. Furthermore, some major changes include, the ability to operate vehicles and choosing different routes only at important junctures in the game, making the play system even easier to manage and more intuitive.  i2012kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00855na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003100005264002600036300002300062500056400085542003300649655002500682655002600707ECGJ00aShock Troopers - 2nd Squad 1bD4 Enterprisec2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aShock Troopers: 2nd Squad is a military-themed action game, first released in 1998. In order to stop a large corporation from running amok, choose one of four mercenaries and battle through by shooting, using different weapons and jumping. The highly praised scoring system from the previous game has been left intact, but the characters are all new. Furthermore, some major changes include, the ability to operate vehicles and choosing different routes only at important junctures in the game, making the play system even easier to manage and more intuitive.  i2014kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00574na  a2200133   4500001000500000245003100005264002800036300002300064500024400087542003300331655002500364655002600389655002500415ECGP00aShock Troopers - 2nd Squad 1bD4 Enterprisec2013-4-4  a1 Wii optical disc  aShock Troopers: 2nd Squad is a military-themed action game, first released in 1998. In order to stop a large corporation from running amok, choose one of four mercenaries and battle through by shooting, using different weapons and jumping.  i2013kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext00897na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002900005264002800034300002300062500060500085542003300690655002500723655002700748ECHE04aThe King of Fighters '98 1bD4 Enterprisec2013-3-7  a1 Wii optical disc  aKing of Fighters '98 is the 5th installment in the fighting game series released as a compilation after the dust settled from the epic Orochi Sage. King of Fighters '98 features a total of 38 characters, which can be broken down into 12 teams plus 2 individual characters. This time around, we see the long-awaited return of the Sports Team. The gameplay follows the same idea as its predecessor, '97, where players can select either advanced or extra modes to match their individual styles. Some minor changes include higher customizability, much to the fans' rejoice, and better fighting mechanics.  i2013kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext00897na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002900005264002800034300002300062500060500085542003300690655002500723655002700748ECHJ04aThe King of Fighters '98 1bD4 Enterprisec2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aKing of Fighters '98 is the 5th installment in the fighting game series released as a compilation after the dust settled from the epic Orochi Sage. King of Fighters '98 features a total of 38 characters, which can be broken down into 12 teams plus 2 individual characters. This time around, we see the long-awaited return of the Sports Team. The gameplay follows the same idea as its predecessor, '97, where players can select either advanced or extra modes to match their individual styles. Some minor changes include higher customizability, much to the fans' rejoice, and better fighting mechanics.  i2014kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext00475na  a2200133   4500001000500000245002900005264002900034300002300063500014500086542003300231655002500264655002700289655002500316ECHP04aThe King of Fighters '98 1bD4 Enterprisec2013-5-30  a1 Wii optical disc  aKing of Fighters '98 is the fifth instalment in the fighting game series that was released after the dust settled from the epic Orochi Saga.  i2013kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext00883na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001700005264003800022300002300060500058500083542004200668655002500710655002600735ECIE00aMetal Slug 4 1bD4Enterprise Co., Ltd.c2013-1-31  a1 Wii optical disc  aMetal Slug 4 is the fifth installment in the Metal Slug series. Choose from four different mercenaries and battle against the terrorist group "Amadeus". Skillfully jump and shoot your way through enemies while picking up items to replenish your weapons. Like in the previous games, you can ride vehicles and fight rigorously against enemies. Furthermore, Metal Slug 4 introduces the all-new Metallish System, an interesting bonus scoring system that puts a new spin on things. Additionally, there are new items and characters, creating a fresh new take on the Metal Slug universe.  i2013kD4Enterprise Co., Ltd.sGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00880na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001700005264003500022300002300057500058500080542004200665655002500707655002600732ECIJ00aMetal Slug 4 1bD4Enterprise Co., Ltd.c2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aMetal Slug 4 is the fifth installment in the Metal Slug series. Choose from four different mercenaries and battle against the terrorist group "Amadeus". Skillfully jump and shoot your way through enemies while picking up items to replenish your weapons. Like in the previous games, you can ride vehicles and fight rigorously against enemies. Furthermore, Metal Slug 4 introduces the all-new Metallish System, an interesting bonus scoring system that puts a new spin on things. Additionally, there are new items and characters, creating a fresh new take on the Metal Slug universe.  i2014kD4Enterprise Co., Ltd.sGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00961na  a2200145   4500001000500000245001700005264003700022300002300059500058500082542004200667655002500709655002600734655003000760655002500790ECIP00aMetal Slug 4 1bD4Enterprise Co., Ltd.c2013-7-3  a1 Wii optical disc  aMetal Slug 4 is the fifth installment in the Metal Slug series. Choose from four different mercenaries and battle against the terrorist group "Amadeus". Skillfully jump and shoot your way through enemies while picking up items to replenish your weapons. Like in the previous games, you can ride vehicles and fight rigorously against enemies. Furthermore, Metal Slug 4 introduces the all-new Metallish System, an interesting bonus scoring system that puts a new spin on things. Additionally, there are new items and characters, creating a fresh new take on the Metal Slug universe.  i2013kD4Enterprise Co., Ltd.sGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext 7aRun and gun games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext01103na  a2200133   4500001000500000245002900005264003700034300002300071500075700094542004100851655002500892655002700917655002500944ECJE04aThe King of Fighters '99 1bD4Enterprise Co., Ltdc2013-5-16  a1 Wii optical disc  aOriginally released in 1999, this is the 6th installment in the King of Fighters series. This time, there is a new protagonist with an all-new story. Instead of the previous 3-member team format, now teams have 4 members, where 3 members actually fight and 1 member is designated as a "Striker". As in previous versions, you can unleash Super Special Moves when the gauges fill up. However, a new feature has been introduced whereby using 3 power stocks allows you to execute either Counter Mode, which increases offensive strength, or Armor Mode, which increases defensive strength. Tactics that apply to each situation have also been powered up. King of Fighters 99 boasts 32 playable characters. Do you think you have what it takes to reach the top?  i2013kD4Enterprise Co., LtdsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext01102na  a2200133   4500001000500000245002900005264003600034300002300070500075700093542004100850655002500891655002700916655002500943ECJJ04aThe King of Fighters '99 1bD4Enterprise Co., Ltdc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aOriginally released in 1999, this is the 6th installment in the King of Fighters series. This time, there is a new protagonist with an all-new story. Instead of the previous 3-member team format, now teams have 4 members, where 3 members actually fight and 1 member is designated as a "Striker". As in previous versions, you can unleash Super Special Moves when the gauges fill up. However, a new feature has been introduced whereby using 3 power stocks allows you to execute either Counter Mode, which increases offensive strength, or Armor Mode, which increases defensive strength. Tactics that apply to each situation have also been powered up. King of Fighters 99 boasts 32 playable characters. Do you think you have what it takes to reach the top?  i2014kD4Enterprise Co., LtdsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext01102na  a2200133   4500001000500000245002900005264003600034300002300070500075700093542004100850655002500891655002700916655002500943ECJP04aThe King of Fighters '99 1bD4Enterprise Co., Ltdc2013-7-4  a1 Wii optical disc  aOriginally released in 1999, this is the 6th installment in the King of Fighters series. This time, there is a new protagonist with an all-new story. Instead of the previous 3-member team format, now teams have 4 members, where 3 members actually fight and 1 member is designated as a "Striker". As in previous versions, you can unleash Super Special Moves when the gauges fill up. However, a new feature has been introduced whereby using 3 power stocks allows you to execute either Counter Mode, which increases offensive strength, or Armor Mode, which increases defensive strength. Tactics that apply to each situation have also been powered up. King of Fighters 99 boasts 32 playable characters. Do you think you have what it takes to reach the top?  i2013kD4Enterprise Co., LtdsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext00884na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001300005264002800018300002300046500057700069542003300646655002000679655002500699655002600724ECKE00aNAM-1975 1bD4 Enterprisec2013-4-4  a1 Wii optical disc  aInitially released in 1990, NAM 1975 is a third-person “shoot 'em up”, action game. The player takes the role of an American Special Forces soldier fighting through a harsh battlefield while moving left and right in front of the screen as enemies in the background shoot fiercely at the protagonist. Essentially, you fight with machine guns and other firearms, as well as hand grenades and the like; however, you can pick up new weapons from items. Not to mention, you can move at high speed while dashing, enabling you to get out of sticky situations if used adeptly.  i2013kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aFantasy2wiiext 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00882na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001300005264002600018300002300044500057700067542003300644655002500677655002000702655002600722ECKJ00aNAM-1975 1bD4 Enterprisec2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aInitially released in 1990, NAM 1975 is a third-person “shoot 'em up”, action game. The player takes the role of an American Special Forces soldier fighting through a harsh battlefield while moving left and right in front of the screen as enemies in the background shoot fiercely at the protagonist. Essentially, you fight with machine guns and other firearms, as well as hand grenades and the like; however, you can pick up new weapons from items. Not to mention, you can move at high speed while dashing, enabling you to get out of sticky situations if used adeptly.  i2014kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFantasy2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00884na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001300005264002800018300002300046500057700069542003300646655002000679655002500699655002600724ECKP00aNAM-1975 1bD4 Enterprisec2013-4-4  a1 Wii optical disc  aInitially released in 1990, NAM 1975 is a third-person “shoot 'em up”, action game. The player takes the role of an American Special Forces soldier fighting through a harsh battlefield while moving left and right in front of the screen as enemies in the background shoot fiercely at the protagonist. Essentially, you fight with machine guns and other firearms, as well as hand grenades and the like; however, you can pick up new weapons from items. Not to mention, you can move at high speed while dashing, enabling you to get out of sticky situations if used adeptly.  i2013kD4 EnterprisesGameTDB 7aFantasy2wiiext 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00182na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002000005264001300025300002300038500000500061542001800066ECLJ00aStakes Winner 2 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00195na  a2200097   4500001000500000245003300005264001300038300002300051500000500074542001800079ECMJ00aTokuten Oh - Honoo no Libero 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00984na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001400005264003600019300002300055500069300078542004100771655002500812655002500837ECNE00aSengoku 3 1bD4Enterprise Co., Ltdc2013-6-6  a1 Wii optical disc  aSengoku 3 is a side scrolling action game first released in 2001. Choose one of the 4 initial characters to play with and set off on an adventure around the world destroying evil spirits that were awoken by the red moon. This sequel takes on a new gaming dynamic from its predecessors by incorporating a ninja (shinobi) gauge which when filled allows you to launch several different Ninja Art attacks against your enemies. The new system allows you to use both armed and unarmed attacks to adeptly execute and link combos, increasing your characters attack power. Use high-powered ninja arts and combos to decimate your enemies in this action-packed final installment of this epic series.  i2013kD4Enterprise Co., LtdsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext00993na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002500005264003400030300002300064500069300087542004100780655002500821655002500846ECNJ00aSengoku Denshou 2001 1bD4Enterprise Co., Ltdc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aSengoku 3 is a side scrolling action game first released in 2001. Choose one of the 4 initial characters to play with and set off on an adventure around the world destroying evil spirits that were awoken by the red moon. This sequel takes on a new gaming dynamic from its predecessors by incorporating a ninja (shinobi) gauge which when filled allows you to launch several different Ninja Art attacks against your enemies. The new system allows you to use both armed and unarmed attacks to adeptly execute and link combos, increasing your characters attack power. Use high-powered ninja arts and combos to decimate your enemies in this action-packed final installment of this epic series.  i2014kD4Enterprise Co., LtdsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext00984na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001400005264003600019300002300055500069300078542004100771655002500812655002500837ECNP00aSengoku 3 1bD4Enterprise Co., Ltdc2013-9-5  a1 Wii optical disc  aSengoku 3 is a side scrolling action game first released in 2001. Choose one of the 4 initial characters to play with and set off on an adventure around the world destroying evil spirits that were awoken by the red moon. This sequel takes on a new gaming dynamic from its predecessors by incorporating a ninja (shinobi) gauge which when filled allows you to launch several different Ninja Art attacks against your enemies. The new system allows you to use both armed and unarmed attacks to adeptly execute and link combos, increasing your characters attack power. Use high-powered ninja arts and combos to decimate your enemies in this action-packed final installment of this epic series.  i2013kD4Enterprise Co., LtdsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext00585na  a2200121   4500001000500000245000900005264002200014300002300036500032700059542002600386655002500412655002600437E52E00a1942 1bcapcomc2011-1-24  a1 Wii optical disc  a1942 is a shooter that puts you in command of a U.S. aircraft deal with Japanese fleets. At the beginning of each level you take off your aircraft carriers to fly over land and sea to destroy entire formations of enemy planes, that allow you to gain bonuses to your weapons. This version is the arcade version of the game.  i2011kcapcomsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00375na  a2200121   4500001000500000245000900005264002300014300002300037500011600060542002600176655002500202655002600227E52J00a1942 1bCapcomc2010-12-21  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis classic vertically-scrolling shoot 'em up is perhaps Capcom's finest moment in the pre-Street Fighter era.  i2010kCapcomsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00585na  a2200121   4500001000500000245000900005264002200014300002300036500032700059542002600386655002500412655002600437E52P00a1942 1bCapcomc2011-1-21  a1 Wii optical disc  a1942 is a shooter that puts you in command of a U.S. aircraft