l disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00180na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001800005264001300023300002300036500000500059542001800064E6GJ00aNamco Quester 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00175na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001300005264001300018300002300031500000500054542001800059E6HJ00aFace Off 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00177na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001500005264001300020300002300033500000500056542001800061E6IJ00aTank Force 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00199na  a2200097   4500001000500000245003700005264001300042300002300055500000500078542001800083E6JJ00aBakutotsu Kijuutei - Baraduke II 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00197na  a2200097   4500001000500000245003500005264001300040300002300053500000500076542001800081E6KJ00aChouzetsu Rinjin - Berabow Man 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00180na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001800005264001300023300002300036500000500059542001800064E6LJ00aMaerchen Maze 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00948na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001500005264002000020300002300040500068600063542002500749655002500774655002700799E6ME00aTecmo Bowl 1bTecmoc2009-8-3  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased in 1987, the football game that took America by storm is back. This arcade version required a custom-made dual-screen cabinet, and was popular for its large characters and intense graphics. Players take control of receivers and running backs. The game is filled with great action, like quickly moving the controller to break a tackle. Play alone, or with up to four players in a two-on-two match. Experience the best moments of both competitive and cooperative play, finding holes in your opponent's defense, then savor the thrill of receiving a pass thrown by your teammate. In addition, game options such as play time, team division and difficulty level can be adjusted.  i2009kTecmosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aFootball games2wiiext00946na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001500005264001800020300002300038500068600061542002500747655002500772655002700797E6MJ00aTecmo Bowl 1bTecmoc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aReleased in 1987, the football game that took America by storm is back. This arcade version required a custom-made dual-screen cabinet, and was popular for its large characters and intense graphics. Players take control of receivers and running backs. The game is filled with great action, like quickly moving the controller to break a tackle. Play alone, or with up to four players in a two-on-two match. Experience the best moments of both competitive and cooperative play, finding holes in your opponent's defense, then savor the thrill of receiving a pass thrown by your teammate. In addition, game options such as play time, team division and difficulty level can be adjusted.  i2014kTecmosGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aFootball games2wiiext00679na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264002200023300002300045500041400068542002500482655002500507655002500532E6NE00aSolomon's Key 1bTecmoc2009-11-30  a1 Wii optical disc  aTo save the world from demons that threaten him, Dana embarks on a quest to find the Key of Solomon to seal the passage borrowed by the monsters. Audacious mix between an action game and a giant puzzle. The player must use his logic and reflexes to uncover all the mysteries of each piece. Good players will certainly do that to find some secrets, but only the best will come to see all the different endings.  i2009kTecmosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00675na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264001800023300002300041500041400064542002500478655002500503655002500528E6NJ00aSolomon's Key 1bTecmoc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aTo save the world from demons that threaten him, Dana embarks on a quest to find the Key of Solomon to seal the passage borrowed by the monsters. Audacious mix between an action game and a giant puzzle. The player must use his logic and reflexes to uncover all the mysteries of each piece. Good players will certainly do that to find some secrets, but only the best will come to see all the different endings.  i2014kTecmosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00678na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264002100023300002300044500041400067542002500481655002500506655002500531E6NP00aSolomon's Key 1bTecmoc2009-9-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aTo save the world from demons that threaten him, Dana embarks on a quest to find the Key of Solomon to seal the passage borrowed by the monsters. Audacious mix between an action game and a giant puzzle. The player must use his logic and reflexes to uncover all the mysteries of each piece. Good players will certainly do that to find some secrets, but only the best will come to see all the different endings.  i2009kTecmosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00178na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001400005264001500019300002300034500000500057542001800062E6OJ00aBomb Jack 1bc2012-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2012sGameTDB00902na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001700005264002200022300002300044500063800067542002500705655002500730655002500755E6PE00aNinja Gaiden 1bTecmoc2009-12-21  a1 Wii optical disc  aTake control of a ninja, master of the Five Ninja Fighting Arts of assassination passed down since the chaotic times of feudal Japan, and enter "Jungle," a terrifying American city, to crush waves of foes that are part of an assassination syndicate. Use three buttons to execute exciting moves like the Flying Neck Throw, the Hang Kick, and the Triple Blow Combination. Each stage is based around popular Western misconceptions about ninja and Japan, making the game world a fantastic mix of ninja and American pop culture. Game settings such as the starting number of player characters and the difficulty level can also be adjusted.  i2009kTecmosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext00903na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002000005264001800025300002300043500063800066542002500704655002500729655002700754E6PJ00aNinja Ryukenden 1bTecmoc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aTake control of a ninja, master of the Five Ninja Fighting Arts of assassination passed down since the chaotic times of feudal Japan, and enter "Jungle," a terrifying American city, to crush waves of foes that are part of an assassination syndicate. Use three buttons to execute exciting moves like the Flying Neck Throw, the Hang Kick, and the Triple Blow Combination. Each stage is based around popular Western misconceptions about ninja and Japan, making the game world a fantastic mix of ninja and American pop culture. Game settings such as the starting number of player characters and the difficulty level can also be adjusted.  i2014kTecmosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00904na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001700005264002200022300002300044500063800067542002500705655002500730655002700755E6PP00aNinja Gaiden 1bTecmoc2009-11-13  a1 Wii optical disc  aTake control of a ninja, master of the Five Ninja Fighting Arts of assassination passed down since the chaotic times of feudal Japan, and enter "Jungle," a terrifying American city, to crush waves of foes that are part of an assassination syndicate. Use three buttons to execute exciting moves like the Flying Neck Throw, the Hang Kick, and the Triple Blow Combination. Each stage is based around popular Western misconceptions about ninja and Japan, making the game world a fantastic mix of ninja and American pop culture. Game settings such as the starting number of player characters and the difficulty level can also be adjusted.  i2009kTecmosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext01042na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001000005264002200015300002300037500082200060542002500882655002500907E6QE00aRygar 1bTecmoc2009-10-19  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe year is 19XX A.D. and the human race has been brought to its knees by the resurrected ancient Beast Lord. The people then brought back to life Rygar, a legendary warrior, in order to fight to save the Human race. Armed with a weapon which extends out (Diskarmor), you'll also make full use of your jumping abilities to venture through and clear all 27 stages. Making its appearance in arcades in 1986 as a side-scrolling action game, the game received high acclaim for its beautifully rendered graphics, such as a setting sun and waterfalls. There are also many bonus features such as collecting the 5 Powers of Indra to obtain special bonuses or gaining 1,000,000 bonus points for finding hidden items (Indra’s Book of Secrets). Aside from those, the number of lives and the difficulty settings can be altered.  i2009kTecmosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext01089na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002000005264002000025300002300045500082200068542002500890655002500915655002700940E6QJ00aArgus no Senshi 1bTecmoc2012-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe year is 19XX A.D. and the human race has been brought to its knees by the resurrected ancient Beast Lord. The people then brought back to life Rygar, a legendary warrior, in order to fight to save the Human race. Armed with a weapon which extends out (Diskarmor), you'll also make full use of your jumping abilities to venture through and clear all 27 stages. Making its appearance in arcades in 1986 as a side-scrolling action game, the game received high acclaim for its beautifully rendered graphics, such as a setting sun and waterfalls. There are also many bonus features such as collecting the 5 Powers of Indra to obtain special bonuses or gaining 1,000,000 bonus points for finding hidden items (Indra’s Book of Secrets). Aside from those, the number of lives and the difficulty settings can be altered.  i2012kTecmosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext01080na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001000005264002100015300002300036500082200059542002500881655002500906655002700931E6QP00aRygar 1bTecmoc2009-9-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe year is 19XX A.D. and the human race has been brought to its knees by the resurrected ancient Beast Lord. The people then brought back to life Rygar, a legendary warrior, in order to fight to save the Human race. Armed with a weapon which extends out (Diskarmor), you'll also make full use of your jumping abilities to venture through and clear all 27 stages. Making its appearance in arcades in 1986 as a side-scrolling action game, the game received high acclaim for its beautifully rendered graphics, such as a setting sun and waterfalls. There are also many bonus features such as collecting the 5 Powers of Indra to obtain special bonuses or gaining 1,000,000 bonus points for finding hidden items (Indra’s Book of Secrets). Aside from those, the number of lives and the difficulty settings can be altered.  i2009kTecmosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00178na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001600005264001300021300002300034500000500057542001800062E6SJ00aNew Rally-X 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB01235na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001100005264002000016300002300036500094200059542002401001655002501025655002601050655002501076E6VE00aZaxxon 1bSEGAc2010-4-12  a1 Wii optical disc  aTravel back to a time when a lovable alien phoned home, gas cost a mere 90 cents a gallon, and everyone was wearing high-tops, leg warmers and had big hair. This was the early 80s, and this was when video gamers nationwide were wowed by the cutting edge graphics and sound effects of the first three-dimensional-like intergalactic arcade shooter: Zaxxon. Touted as the first game to put video display in perspective, Zaxxon featured “looks” and “sounds” like actual aircraft flight, allowing the player to command his ship just like a real fighter pilot. Dive, bank, fly left and right, and up and down—Zaxxon had it all. Fly through heavily armored space fortresses, strafing fuel tanks, dodging walls, and blowing up enemy missiles and gunnery. This game is littered with explosions. Then take the fight to the enemy fighter fleet and destroy the aggressor ships with extreme prejudice. Blasting pixels has never been so fun.  i2010kSEGAsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext 7aArcade games2wiiext00481na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001100005264001700016300002300033500022800056542002400284655002500308655002600333E6VJ00aZaxxon 1bSegac2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aTouted as the first isometric shooter, Zaxxon featured the looks and sounds of an actual aircraft flight, allowing the player to command their ship just like a real fighter pilot. Dive, climb and bank – Zaxxon had it all!  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00483na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001100005264001900016300002300035500022800058542002400286655002500310655002600335E6VP00aZaxxon 1bSegac2010-3-5  a1 Wii optical disc  aTouted as the first isometric shooter, Zaxxon featured the looks and sounds of an actual aircraft flight, allowing the player to command their ship just like a real fighter pilot. Dive, climb and bank – Zaxxon had it all!  i2010kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00814na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001500005264002100020300002300041500059100064542002400655655002500679E6WE00aGolden Axe 1bSEGAc2009-10-26  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn this original arcade game that launched the popular series, the evil Death Adder has invaded your land and taken the king and princess prisoner. Three mighty warriors step forward to bring the villain to justice. The powerful fighter, Ax Battler, the female amazon, Tyris Flare, and the mighty dwarf, Gilius Thunderhead, will use their weapons and magic to fight their way through Death Adder's hordes. Along the way, they'll mount fearsome, fire-spitting beasts to help even the odds. Team up with a friend and enjoy two-player simultaneous gameplay for a better chance of survival.  i2009kSEGAsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00658na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001500005264001900020300002300039500043700062542002400499655002500523E6WJ00aGolden Axe 1bSegac2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe villainous Death Adder has taken the king and his daughter prisoner and only three brave warriors have stepped forward to oppose him. The powerful barbarian, Ax Battler, the skilled Amazon warrior Tyris Flare and the mighty dwarf, Gilius Thunderhead. They must all use their weapons and magic to fight their way through Death Adder's evil hordes! Along the way they'll mount fearsome fire-breathing beasts to help even the odds.  i2014kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00659na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001500005264002000020300002300040500043700063542002400500655002500524E6WP00aGolden Axe 1bSegac2009-9-18  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe villainous Death Adder has taken the king and his daughter prisoner and only three brave warriors have stepped forward to oppose him. The powerful barbarian, Ax Battler, the skilled Amazon warrior Tyris Flare and the mighty dwarf, Gilius Thunderhead. They must all use their weapons and magic to fight their way through Death Adder's evil hordes! Along the way they'll mount fearsome fire-breathing beasts to help even the odds.  i2009kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00440na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264002000023300002300043500021500066542002400281655002500305E6XE00aAltered Beast 1bSEGAc2009-9-28  a1 Wii optical disc  a"Rise from your grave!" When Zeus, the legendary Greek god, brings you back to life with those famous words, you set forth on a mission to rescue his daughter Athena from the wicked God of the Underworld, Neff.  i2009kSEGAsGameTDB 7aArcade games2wiiext00434na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001200005264002000017300002300037500021500060542002400275655002500299E6XJ00aJyuouki 1bSEGAc2009-9-28  a1 Wii optical disc  a"Rise from your grave!" When Zeus, the legendary Greek god, brings you back to life with those famous words, you set forth on a mission to rescue his daughter Athena from the wicked God of the Underworld, Neff.  i2009kSEGAsGameTDB 7aArcade games2wiiext00440na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264002000023300002300043500021500066542002400281655002500305E6XP00aAltered Beast 1bSegac2009-6-26  a1 Wii optical disc  a"Rise from your grave!" When Zeus, the legendary Greek god, brings you back to life with those famous words, you set forth on a mission to rescue his daughter Athena from the wicked God of the Underworld, Neff.  i2009kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00181na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001900005264001300024300002300037500000500060542001800065E6YJ00aSpace Invaders 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00831na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001500005264002100020300002300041500056900064542002500633655002500658655002600683E6ZE00aStar Force 1bTecmoc2009-3-25  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe classic vertical-scrolling shooter and a huge nationwide hit! Exhilarating play in which you can shoot down enemy units one after another with a single button. Hidden special bonuses scattered in all 25 areas. 1,000,000 bonus points for solving the biggest mystery. Rapid fir gained by docking with an ally unit, the PURSER. With various elements and rapid-fire play requiring strong and agile finger control, this is the mother of all shooters! Various settings (customizing the starting number of Final Stars, the difficulty of the game, etc.) are available!  i2009kTecmosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00830na  a2200121   450