9-5-19  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2009kNamco Bandai Games Inc.sGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext 7aRun and gun games2wiiext00182na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002000005264001300025300002300038500000500061542001800066E7WJ00aNuman Athletics 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00183na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002100005264001300026300002300039500000500062542001800067E7XJ00aYoukai Douchuuki 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00174na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001200005264001300017300002300030500000500053542001800058E7YJ00aSky Kid 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00870na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002400005264002000029300002300049500063900072542002400711655002500735E7ZE04aThe Tower of Druaga 1bNBGIc2009-3-25  a1 Wii optical disc  aControl Gil, the hero, as he climbs the tower starting from the first floor. Pick up the key inside each maze and go through the door to advance to the next floor. To clear the game, you must defeat Druaga, the ruler of the tower, then advance to the top floor and save your beloved Ki. Lives can be lost in numerous ways, including (but not limited to) taking damage from enemies, failing to block a spell attack with your shield, touching fire, and running out of time. Once you run out of lives, the game is over. Note: Not all enemies will kill you instantly; some will need to land several hits before causing you to lose a life.  i2009kNBGIsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00932na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264003100023300002300054500063900077542003800716655002500754655003100779E7ZJ00aDruaga no Tou 1bNamco Bandai Gamesc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aControl Gil, the hero, as he climbs the tower starting from the first floor. Pick up the key inside each maze and go through the door to advance to the next floor. To clear the game, you must defeat Druaga, the ruler of the tower, then advance to the top floor and save your beloved Ki. Lives can be lost in numerous ways, including (but not limited to) taking damage from enemies, failing to block a spell attack with your shield, touching fire, and running out of time. Once you run out of lives, the game is over. Note: Not all enemies will kill you instantly; some will need to land several hits before causing you to lose a life.  i2014kNamco Bandai GamessGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00941na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002400005264003400029300002300063500063900086542003800725655002500763655003100788E7ZP04aThe Tower of Druaga 1bNamco Bandai Gamesc2009-3-25  a1 Wii optical disc  aControl Gil, the hero, as he climbs the tower starting from the first floor. Pick up the key inside each maze and go through the door to advance to the next floor. To clear the game, you must defeat Druaga, the ruler of the tower, then advance to the top floor and save your beloved Ki. Lives can be lost in numerous ways, including (but not limited to) taking damage from enemies, failing to block a spell attack with your shield, touching fire, and running out of time. Once you run out of lives, the game is over. Note: Not all enemies will kill you instantly; some will need to land several hits before causing you to lose a life.  i2009kNamco Bandai GamessGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aRole-playing games2wiiext00659na  a2200121   4500001000500000245004100005264003200046300002300078500034700101542003600448655002500484655002800509C93E00aLast Ninja 2 - Back with a Vengeance 1bCommodore Gamingc2009-9-21  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe Ninja, known as the Mystic Shadow Warriors, were the elite fighting force of Ninth Century Feudal Japan. The evil Shogun Kunitoki has once been beaten but has gathered all his mystic powers to create a modern day tyranny in Manhattan.Encounter your arch-enemy Kunitoki within the urban jungle and conquer him with your Ninja style skills.  i2009kCommodore GamingsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00659na  a2200121   4500001000500000245004100005264003200046300002300078500034700101542003600448655002500484655002800509C93P00aLast Ninja 2 - Back with a Vengeance 1bCommodore Gamingc2008-6-13  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe Ninja, known as the Mystic Shadow Warriors, were the elite fighting force of Ninth Century Feudal Japan. The evil Shogun Kunitoki has once been beaten but has gathered all his mystic powers to create a modern day tyranny in Manhattan.Encounter your arch-enemy Kunitoki within the urban jungle and conquer him with your Ninja style skills.  i2008kCommodore GamingsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00535na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264003100023300002300054500024800077542003600325655002500361655002700386C94E00aTower Toppler 1bCommodore Gamingc2009-5-4  a1 Wii optical disc  aYou play a small green guy who needs to blow up eight towers, because their presence is somehow poisoning the water of planets which could potentially be ideal colonies. Unfortunately you need to get to the top of these towers to blow them up.  i2009kCommodore GamingsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00441na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001200005264003200017300002300049500015900072542003600231655002500267655002700292C94P00aNebulus 1bCommodore Gamingc2008-6-13  a1 Wii optical disc  aWeird things are happening on Planet Nebulus. Someone or something has begun building huge towers on the sea bottom without having a construction license.  i2008kCommodore GamingsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00628na  a2200133   4500001000500000245002300005264003200028300002300060500029500083542003600378655002500414655002800439655002700467C95P00aImpossible Mission 1bCommodore Gamingc2008-4-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aDuring the past three days, key military computer installations of every major world power have reported security failures. In each case, someone gained access to a primary missile attack computer. Only one person is capable of computer tampering on this scale - Professor Elvin Atombender.  i2008kCommodore GamingsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00680na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002000005264003600025300002300061500042100084542004000505655002500545C96E00aSummer Games II 1bAllied Kingdoms Inc.c2009-3-16  a1 Wii optical disc  aA thousand athletes. A hundred countries. Billions watching around the world as you enter the stadium, marching confidently among your nation's strongest, fastest and boldest young men and women. Your gaze sweeps the crowd as you realize the scope of your achievement. You are about to compete against the world's best athletes in a 3,000-year-old competition. The pinnacle of athletic achievement. The Summer Games.  i2009kAllied Kingdoms Inc.sGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext00672na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002000005264003200025300002300057500042100080542003600501655002500537C96P00aSummer Games II 1bCommodore Gamingc2008-6-27  a1 Wii optical disc  aA thousand athletes. A hundred countries. Billions watching around the world as you enter the stadium, marching confidently among your nation's strongest, fastest and boldest young men and women. Your gaze sweeps the crowd as you realize the scope of your achievement. You are about to compete against the world's best athletes in a 3,000-year-old competition. The pinnacle of athletic achievement. The Summer Games.  i2008kCommodore GamingsGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext00596na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002100005264003100026300002300057500034500080542003600425655002500461C97E00aCalifornia Games 1bCommodore Gamingc2009-7-6  a1 Wii optical disc  aWelcome to California. Home of the most radical sports in the world. Rad, bad and aggro. You're about to hit the beaches, parks and streets of the Golden State to go for trophies in everything from surfing to bike racing. California Games gives you the hottest sports. And the most aggro competition. You even have to pick your own sponsor.  i2009kCommodore GamingsGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext00597na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002100005264003200026300002300058500034500081542003600426655002500462C97P00aCalifornia Games 1bCommodore Gamingc2008-4-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aWelcome to California. Home of the most radical sports in the world. Rad, bad and aggro. You're about to hit the beaches, parks and streets of the Golden State to go for trophies in everything from surfing to bike racing. CALIFORNIA GAMES gives you the hottest sports. And the most aggro competition. You even have to pick your own sponsor.  i2008kCommodore GamingsGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext00443na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001400005264003200019300002300051500012300074542003600197655002500233655002600258655002500284C98P00aParadroid 1bCommodore Gamingc2008-5-23  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe droid crew of a galactic space freighter have turned against their masters and eradicated every human crew member!  i2008kCommodore GamingsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00461na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001200005264003200017300002300049500018000072542003600252655002500288655002600313C99P00aUridium 1bCommodore Gamingc2008-3-28  a1 Wii optical disc  a15 Super-Dreadnought ships have invaded your galaxy, each looking to steal a different precious metal. Destroy the dreadnought's defensive forces, then land to finish the job.  i2008kCommodore GamingsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00477na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001700005264003200022300002300054500022900077542003600306655002500342C9EP00aWinter Games 1bCommodore Gamingc2009-2-20  a1 Wii optical disc  aEpyx was known for their excellent sport games (mostly Olympic Games). Here's yet another of their sport games. This time we're taking you to Calgary, where the Jamaican bob-sled team (remember Cool Runnings) made its debut!  i2009kCommodore GamingsGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext00636na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002600005264003300031300002300064500033900087542003600426655002500462655002700487C9GP00aMayhem in Monsterland 1bCommodore Gamingc2008-10-17  a1 Wii optical disc  aMayhem is an unhappy dinosaur, as Monsterland is an unhappy place, due to an apprentice magic dinosaur who decided to practice some of his master's spells, after drinking too much cactus juice. Mayhem decides to change it back, with the help of Theo Saurus, the apprentice responsible for Monsterland being the gloomy place it is now.  i2008kCommodore GamingsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00591na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001700005264003100022300002300053500034400076542003600420655002500456C9HE00aBoulder Dash 1bCommodore Gamingc2009-6-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe hero of the game, whom the player controls, is the brave prospector "Rockford". He must dig through caves collecting gems and diamonds, while avoiding various types of dangerous creatures as well as obstacles like falling rocks and the constant danger of being crushed or trapped by an avalanche, or killed by an underground explosion.  i2009kCommodore GamingsGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00592na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001700005264003200022300002300054500034400077542003600421655002500457C9HP00aBoulder Dash 1bCommodore Gamingc2008-9-19  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe hero of the game, whom the player controls, is the brave prospector "Rockford". He must dig through caves collecting gems and diamonds, while avoiding various types of dangerous creatures as well as obstacles like falling rocks and the constant danger of being crushed or trapped by an avalanche, or killed by an underground explosion.  i2008kCommodore GamingsGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00529na  a2200109   4500001000500000245003700005264003200042300002300074500026100097542003600358655002500394C9IE00aCybernoid - The Fighting Machine 1bCommodore Gamingc2009-11-9  a1 Wii optical disc  aFederation storage depots have been raided by pirates, taking valuable minerals, jewels, ammunition and the latest battle weaponry. You have been commissioned by the Federation to retrieve the cargo and return it to a storage within a specified time limit.  i2009kCommodore GamingsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00567na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003700005264003200042300002300074500026100097542003600358655002500394655002600419C9IP00aCybernoid - The Fighting Machine 1bCommodore Gamingc2008-6-27  a1 Wii optical disc  aFederation storage depots have been raided by pirates, taking valuable minerals, jewels, ammunition and the latest battle weaponry. You have been commissioned by the Federation to retrieve the cargo and return it to a storage within a specified time limit.  i2008kCommodore GamingsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext00963na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001500005264003200020300002300052500071700075542003600792655002500828C9ME00aPitstop II 1bCommodore Gamingc2009-2-23  a1 Wii optical disc  aPitstop II was the first racing game that brought the thrill of battling an opponent, the excitement of fighting for the lead out on the track, and the suspense of struggling to be the first out of the pits to the computer screen. Third-person graphics and a split-screen display allowed up to two players to experience the challenge of head-to-head car racing. Six of the world’s toughest racetracks are waiting, from Brands Hatch and its hairpin turns to the mile-long straight of Vallelunga. You can practice against the computer, but nothing will compare to the fun of racing against another person. That’s the whole story behind Pitstop II. It’s simple—car racing was never meant to be a solo sport!  i2009kCommodore GamingsGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext00531na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001600005264002900021300002300050500028700073542003600360655002500396C9MJ00aPitstop Two 1bCommodore Gamingc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aA fun racing game. Race Formula-1 in several tracks while trying to beat a computer opponent. Featuring Dual player splitscreen graphics and gameplay, Pitstop 2 does give a nod to realism: it is necessary to drive into a pitstop to swap out burnt tires and refuel as you race along.  i2014kCommodore GamingsGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext00532na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001500005264003100020300002300051500028700074542003600361655002500397C9MP00aPitstop II 1bCommodore Gamingc2008-8-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aA fun racing game. Race Formula-1 in several tracks while trying to beat a computer opponent. Featuring Dual player splitscreen graphics and gameplay, Pitstop 2 does give a nod to realism: it is necessary to drive into a pitstop to swap out burnt tires and refuel as you race along.  i2008kCommodore GamingsGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext00317na  a2200109   4500001000500000245004300005264003300048300002300081500004000104542003600144655002700180C9PP00aLast Ninja 3 - Real Hatred is Timeless 1bCommodore Gamingc2008-12-12  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe third in the Last Ninja series.  i2008kCommodore GamingsGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00851na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001200005264003200017300002300049500056900072542003600641655002500677655002700702C9QP00aJumpman 1bCommodore Gamingc2008-9-19  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe object of the game is to defuse all bombs in a platform-filled screen. Jumpman defuses a bomb by touching it. According to the story, these are placed on Jupiter by terrorists. Jumpman can climb up and down ladders, and of course jump, and there are two kinds of rope each allowing a single direction of climbing only. Hazards include falling, 'smart darts' (small bullets that fly slowly across the screen, but when orthogonally lined up with Jumpman, greatly speed up and shoot straight in his direction) and other hazards that are unique to a certain level.  i2008kCommodore GamingsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00445na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002700005264003200032300002300064500018500087542003600272655002700308C9RP00aInternational Karate + 1bCommodore Gamingc2008-7-25  a1 Wii optical disc  aInternational Karate + ™ is a development of the original IK game, the main extra feature being that there are three fighting men on the screen at once (and five in pause mode!).  i2008kCommodore GamingsGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00424na  a2200133   4500001000500000245002600005264003400031300002300065500008500088542003700173655002500210655002800235655002700263C9SP00aImpossible Mission II 1b Commodore Gamingc2008-12-12  a1 Wii optical disc  aImpossible Mission II is a direct sequel to Epyx's 1984 game Impossible Mission.  i2008k Commodore GamingsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00428na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001900005264002500024300002300049500019200072542002900264655002500293C9XE04aThe Last Ninja 1bCommodorec2009-2-23  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe evil Shogun Kunitoki has long envied the powers of the Ninja brotherhood and would do anything to acquire their knowledge. To this end he has sworn an oath to their total destruction.  i2009kCommodoresGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00479na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001900005264002900024300002300053500019200076542003600268655002500304655002800329C9XJ04aThe Last Ninja 1bCommodore Gamingc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe evil Shogun Kunitoki has long envied the powers of the Ninja brotherhood and would do anything to acquire their knowledge. To this end he has sworn an oath to their total destruction.  i2014kCommodore GamingsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00482na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001900005264003200024300002300056500019200079542003600271655002500307655002800332C9XP04aThe Last Ninja 1bCommodore Gamingc2008-4-25  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe evil Shogun Kunitoki has long envied the powers of the Ninja brotherhood and would do anything to acquire their knowledge. To this end he has sworn an oath to their total destruction.  i2008kCommodore GamingsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00408na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002500005264003200030300002300062500015000085542003600235655002700271C9YE00aInternational Karate 1bCommodore Gamingc2009-2-23  a1 Wii optical disc  aINTERNATIONAL KARATE is a simulation of a Karate Tournament where two people can play against each other or one can compete against the computer.  i2009kCommodore GamingsGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00407na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002500005264003000030300002300060500015000083542003700233655002700270C9YJ00aInternational Karate 1b Commodore Gamingc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aINTERNATIONAL KARATE is a simulation of a Karate Tournament where two people can play against each other or one can compete against the computer.  i2014k Commodore GamingsGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00410na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002500005264003300030300002300063500015000086542003700236655002700273C9YP00aInternational Karate 1b Commodore Gamingc2008-3-28  a1 Wii optical disc  aINTERNATIONAL KARATE is a simulation of a Karate Tournament where two people can play against each other or one can compete against the computer.  i2008k Commodore GamingsGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00395na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001600005264003200021300002300053500014800076542003600224655002500260C9ZP00aWorld Games 1bCommodore Gamingc2008-4-25  a1 Wii optical disc  aLook out, world. Here we come! You're about to travel the globe with EPYX to compete in eight of the world's most glamorous and unusual sports.  i2008kCommodore GamingsGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext00171na  a2200097   4500001000500000245000900005264001300014300002300027500000500050542001800055XAAJ00aEggy 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00173na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001100005264001300016300002300029500000500052542001800057XABJ00aAleste 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00294na  a2200121   4500001000500000245004900005264001500054300002300069500000500092542001800097655002700115655003000142XADJ00aYie-Gah-koutei no Gyakush - Yie Ar Kung-Fu 2 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext00179na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001700005264001300022300002300035500000500058542001800063XAEJ00aSpace Manbow 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00177na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001500005264001300020300002300033500000500056542001800061XAFJ00aMetal Gear 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00179na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001700005264001300022300002300035500000500058542001800063XAGJ00aRoad Fighter 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00189na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002700005264001300032300002300045500000500068542001800073XAHJ00aYume Tairiku Adventure 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00173na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001100005264001300016300002300029500000500052542001800057XAIJ00aQuarth 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00202na  a2200097   4500001000500000245004000005264001300045300002300058500000500081542001800086XAKJ00aParodius - Tako wa Chikyou wo Sukou 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00173na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001100005264001300016300002300029500000500052542001800057XALJ00aContra 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00181na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001900005264001300024300002300037500000500060542001800065XAMJ00aMajou Densetsu 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00180na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001400005264001700019300002300036500000500059542001800064XANJ00aGradius 2 1bc2009-12-22  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2009sGameTDB00194na  a2200097   4500001000500000245003200005264001300037300002300050500000500073542001800078XAOJ00aGofer no Yabou - Episode II 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00195na  a2200097   4500001000500000245003100005264001500036300002300051500000500074542001800079XAPJ00aMetal Gear 2 - Solid Snake 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00177na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001500005264001300020300002300033500000500056542001800061XAQJ00aSalamander 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00178na  a2200097   45000010005000002450016000052640013000213000023000345000005000575420018000625NEA00aNWC24Editor 1bc2023--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2023sGameTDB00679na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264002500023300002300048500040500071542002800476655003200504655002100536HAAA00aPhoto Channel 1bNintendoc2007-12-10  a1 Wii optical disc  aBy using the SD Card Slot on the front of your Wii, you can view the pictures and movies you have taken with your digital camera or mobile phone on your TV screen. With the easy-to-use software, you can easily select, enlarge, and reduce the size of your photos. In addition, there is a full array of other ways to enjoy your photos, such as scribbling messages on them and turning them into puzzles.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aMultimedia software2wiiext 7aSoftware2wiiext00473na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002100005264002400026300002300050500024100073542002800314655002100342HABA00aWii Shop Channel 1bNintendoc2006-12-2  a1 Wii optical disc  aYour online experience with the Wii console begins here. Download a huge selection of new and classic games, and discover exciting Wii Channels. Find it all inside the Wii Shop Channel, when you connect your Wii console to the internet.  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aSoftware2wiiext00474na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002500005264002100030300002300051500024100074542002800315655002100343HABC00aWii Gòuwù Píndào 1bNintendoc2006--  a1 Wii optical disc  aYour online experience with the Wii console begins here. Download a huge selection of new and classic games, and discover exciting Wii Channels. Find it all inside the Wii Shop Channel, when you connect your Wii console to the internet.  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aSoftware2wiiext00474na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002500005264002100030300002300051500024100074542002800315655002100343HABK00aWii Shopping Channel 1bNintendoc2006--  a1 Wii optical disc  aYour online experience with the Wii console begins here. Download a huge selection of new and classic games, and discover exciting Wii Channels. Find it all inside the Wii Shop Channel, when you connect your Wii console to the internet.  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aSoftware2wiiext01284na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001600005264002300021300002300044500101700067542002801084655002901112655002101141HACA00aMii Channel 1bNintendoc2006-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe Mii Channel is a Nintendo-Proprietary Avatar Creator. It is designed to "Put yourself into the game" by allowing Miis to play in certain titles. For those titles that support Miis, each Mii can be used in that title, (ex Wii Sports, pick a Mii and play as it). This application was officially unveiled by Nintendo in September 2006. It is incorporated into Wii's operating system interface as the "Mii Channel". Users can select from pre-made caricatures or create their own by choosing custom facial shapes, colors, and positioning. Miis can interact with other Wii users by showing up on their Wii consoles through the WiiConnect24 feature or by talking with other Miis created by Wii owners all over the world. This feature is called Mii Parade. Early-created Miis as well as those encountered in Mii Parades may show up as spectators in some games. Miis can be stored on Wii Remotes and taken to other Wii consoles. The remote can hold up to a maximum amount of 10 Miis. The Wii itself can hold 100 Miis.  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aSimulation games2wiiext 7aSoftware2wiiext00429na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001600005264002100021300002300042500016400065542002800229655002900257655002100286HACC00aMii Channel 1bNintendoc2022--  a1 Wii optical disc  aA modification of the Mii Channel allowing users to enter custom symbols in their Miis' names, including ones specific to Mario Kart Wii for use in that title.  i2022kNintendosGameTDB 7aSimulation games2wiiext 7aSoftware2wiiext01251na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001600005264002300021300002300044500101700067542002801084655002901112HACK00aMii Channel 1bNintendoc2006-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe Mii Channel is a Nintendo-Proprietary Avatar Creator. It is designed to "Put yourself into the game" by allowing Miis to play in certain titles. For those titles that support Miis, each Mii can be used in that title, (ex Wii Sports, pick a Mii and play as it). This application was officially unveiled by Nintendo in September 2006. It is incorporated into Wii's operating system interface as the "Mii Channel". Users can select from pre-made caricatures or create their own by choosing custom facial shapes, colors, and positioning. Miis can interact with other Wii users by showing up on their Wii consoles through the WiiConnect24 feature or by talking with other Miis created by Wii owners all over the world. This feature is called Mii Parade. Early-created Miis as well as those encountered in Mii Parades may show up as spectators in some games. Miis can be stored on Wii Remotes and taken to other Wii consoles. The remote can hold up to a maximum amount of 10 Miis. The Wii itself can hold 100 Miis.  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aSimulation games2wiiext00685na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264002500026300002300051500040800074542002800482655003200510655002100542HADE00aInternet Channel 1bNintendoc2006-12-22  a1 Wii optical disc  aWith the Internet Channel, everyone in your family can browse the Internet with ease. A simple point of the Wii Remote controller brings email, news, and online video right to your living room. Plus-sized navigation buttons, and a handy zoom feature makes viewing websites a breeze without even leaving your couch. The Internet Channel is available to download from the Wii Shop Channel today, for free.  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aMultimedia software2wiiext 7aSoftware2wiiext00701na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264002400026300002300050500042500073542002800498655003200526655002100558HADJ00aInternet Channel 1bNintendoc2007-4-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aWith the Internet Channel, everyone in your family can browse the Internet with ease. A simple point of the Wii Remote™ controller brings email, news, and online video right to your living room. Plus-sized navigation buttons, and a handy zoom feature makes viewing websites a breeze—without even leaving your couch. The Internet Channel is available to download* from the Wii Shop Channel today, for 0 Wii Points™.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aMultimedia software2wiiext 7aSoftware2wiiext00701na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264002400026300002300050500042500073542002800498655003200526655002100558HADP00aInternet Channel 1bNintendoc2007-4-12  a1 Wii optical disc  aWith the Internet Channel, everyone in your family can browse the Internet with ease. A simple point of the Wii Remote™ controller brings email, news, and online video right to your living room. Plus-sized navigation buttons, and a handy zoom feature makes viewing websites a breeze—without even leaving your couch. The Internet Channel is available to download* from the Wii Shop Channel today, for 0 Wii Points™.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aMultimedia software2wiiext 7aSoftware2wiiext00551na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002100005264002100026300002300047500032200070542002800392655002100420HAFA00aForecast Channel 1bNintendoc2020--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis channel allows you to access local weather forecasts after turning on the Wii console. When connected to the Internet, the Wii automatically updates weather information from your local area and around the world. Use the Wii Remote to spin the globe and view weather reports from across town or across the planet!  i2020kNintendosGameTDB 7aSoftware2wiiext00555na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002100005264002500026300002300051500032200074542002800396655002100424HAFE00aForecast Channel 1bNintendoc2006-12-19  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis channel allows you to access local weather forecasts after turning on the Wii console. When connected to the Internet, the Wii automatically updates weather information from your local area and around the world. Use the Wii Remote to spin the globe and view weather reports from across town or across the planet!  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aSoftware2wiiext00553na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001900005264002500024300002300049500032200072542002800394655002100422HAFJ00aOtenki Channel 1bNintendoc2006-12-19  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis channel allows you to access local weather forecasts after turning on the Wii console. When connected to the Internet, the Wii automatically updates weather information from your local area and around the world. Use the Wii Remote to spin the globe and view weather reports from across town or across the planet!  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aSoftware2wiiext00555na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002100005264002500026300002300051500032200074542002800396655002100424HAFP00aForecast Channel 1bNintendoc2006-12-19  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis channel allows you to access local weather forecasts after turning on the Wii console. When connected to the Internet, the Wii automatically updates weather information from your local area and around the world. Use the Wii Remote to spin the globe and view weather reports from across town or across the planet!  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aSoftware2wiiext00492na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001700005264002400022300002300046500026400069542002800333655002100361HAGA00aNews Channel 1bNintendoc2007-1-26  a1 Wii optical disc  aCheck the news, even on a busy morning. Using the News Channel, you can select the news article you want to read from an easy to navigate list of headlines. Stay up to date with the latest news in any genre, both domestically and internationally, at any time.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aSoftware2wiiext00492na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001700005264002400022300002300046500026400069542002800333655002100361HAGE00aNews Channel 1bNintendoc2007-1-26  a1 Wii optical disc  aCheck the news, even on a busy morning. Using the News Channel, you can select the news article you want to read from an easy to navigate list of headlines. Stay up to date with the latest news in any genre, both domestically and internationally, at any time.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aSoftware2wiiext00492na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001700005264002400022300002300046500026400069542002800333655002100361HAGJ00aNews Channel 1bNintendoc2007-1-26  a1 Wii optical disc  aCheck the news, even on a busy morning. Using the News Channel, you can select the news article you want to read from an easy to navigate list of headlines. Stay up to date with the latest news in any genre, both domestically and internationally, at any time.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aSoftware2wiiext00492na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001700005264002400022300002300046500026400069542002800333655002100361HAGP00aNews Channel 1bNintendoc2007-1-26  a1 Wii optical disc  aCheck the news, even on a busy morning. Using the News Channel, you can select the news article you want to read from an easy to navigate list of headlines. Stay up to date with the latest news in any genre, both domestically and internationally, at any time.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aSoftware2wiiext00731na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002800005264002400033300002300057500045500080542002800535655002500563655002100588HAJE00aEverybody Votes Channel 1bNintendoc2007-2-13  a1 Wii optical disc  aEverybody Votes Channel works with WiiConnect24 to bring you all kinds of national and worldwide polls. Answer interesting questions that get the whole family talking. Up to six members of your family can vote - just choose an answer and check in later to see the results. You can even predict which answer will get the most votes and see how your predictions differ from other people across the country. But get ready to be surprised by the answers!  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aTrivia games2wiiext 7aSoftware2wiiext00732na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002900005264002400034300002300058500045500081542002800536655002500564655002100589HAJJ00aMinna de Touhyou Channel 1bNintendoc2007-2-13  a1 Wii optical disc  aEverybody Votes Channel works with WiiConnect24 to bring you all kinds of national and worldwide polls. Answer interesting questions that get the whole family talking. Up to six members of your family can vote - just choose an answer and check in later to see the results. You can even predict which answer will get the most votes and see how your predictions differ from other people across the country. But get ready to be surprised by the answers!  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aTrivia games2wiiext 7aSoftware2wiiext00731na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002800005264002400033300002300057500045500080542002800535655002500563655002100588HAJP00aEverybody Votes Channel 1bNintendoc2007-2-13  a1 Wii optical disc  aEverybody Votes Channel works with WiiConnect24 to bring you all kinds of national and worldwide polls. Answer interesting questions that get the whole family talking. Up to six members of your family can vote - just choose an answer and check in later to see the results. You can even predict which answer will get the most votes and see how your predictions differ from other people across the country. But get ready to be surprised by the answers!  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aTrivia games2wiiext 7aSoftware2wiiext00235na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002200005264002100027300002300048500000500071542002800076655002100104HAKC00aShǐyòng Xiéyì 1bNintendoc2006--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aSoftware2wiiext00237na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002000005264002500025300002300050500000500073542002800078655002100106HAKE00aUser Agreements 1bNintendoc2006-11-19  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aSoftware2wiiext00230na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001700005264002100022300002300043500000500066542002800071655002100099HAKJ00aRiyou Kiyaku 1bNintendoc2006--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aSoftware2wiiext00231na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264002100023300002300044500000500067542002800072655002100100HAKK00aIyong Yaggwan 1bNintendoc2006--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aSoftware2wiiext00239na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002200005264002500027300002300052500000500075542002800080655002100108HAKP00aAgreement/Contact 1bNintendoc2006-11-19  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2006kNintendosGameTDB 7aSoftware2wiiext00180na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001800005264001300023300002300036500000500059542001800064HALE00aRegion Select 1bc2020--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2020sGameTDB00180na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001800005264001300023300002300036500000500059542001800064HALJ00aRegion Select 1bc2020--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2020sGameTDB00180na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001800005264001300023300002300036500000500059542001800064HALK00aRegion Select 1bc2020--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2020sGameTDB00180na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001800005264001300023300002300036500000500059542001800064HALP00aRegion Select 1bc2020--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2020sGameTDB00751na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002600005264002500031300002300056500051300079542002800592655002100620HAPE00aCheck Mii Out Channel 1bNintendoc2007-11-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe Check Mii Out Channel is the place for Mii™ characters to mingle in fun and outrageous ways! Show off your best Mii creations, participate in Mii contests, and download Mii characters created by others. Import your favorite finds to your Wii console, and you can populate some of your favorite games with wacky new Mii characters created by the rest of the Check Mii Out Channel community. With Wii users from around the world joining in on the fun, there’s something new to see every time you visit!  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aSoftware2wiiext00749na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002400005264002500029300002300054500051300077542002800590655002100618HAPJ00aMii Contest Channel 1bNintendoc2007-11-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe Check Mii Out Channel is the place for Mii™ characters to mingle in fun and outrageous ways! Show off your best Mii creations, participate in Mii contests, and download Mii characters created by others. Import your favorite finds to your Wii console, and you can populate some of your favorite games with wacky new Mii characters created by the rest of the Check Mii Out Channel community. With Wii users from around the world joining in on the fun, there’s something new to see every time you visit!  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aSoftware2wiiext01024na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002400005264002500029300002300054500078800077542002800865655002100893HAPP00aMii Contest Channel 1bNintendoc2007-11-12  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe Mii Contest Channel works together with the Mii Channel, letting you share your favourite Miis with other Wii owners, and take part in fun, themed Contests. Visit the Posting Plaza to view the latest and most popular Miis, and post your own Miis for others to see. If any Miis catch your eye, simply save them to your Favourites list or even ‘take them home’ by importing them to the Mii Channel. And if you want to put your Mii-making talents to the test, or simply play judge, check out the Mii Contests. Contests are themed around a certain character or subject, and are updated regularly with fresh Mii-making challenges. You might even receive a souvenir photo of your Mii, simply by taking part. And who knows? Gain enough votes and you can become a Master Mii Artisan!  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aSoftware2wiiext00717na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002100005264002300026300002300049500048600072542002800558655002100586HATE00aNintendo Channel 1bNintendoc2008-5-7  a1 Wii optical disc  aFire up the Nintendo Channel for an exciting guide to what's new in the world of Nintendo. Watch gameplay videos, trailers, developer interviews, and much more. Download Nintendo DS game demos wirelessly. Find out detailed game information, and see which games Nintendo Channel users are playing the most. See what others think of the latest titles, or rate them yourself! A sleek navigation menu makes it easier than ever to find up-to-date game knowledge based on your interests.  i2008kNintendosGameTDB 7aSoftware2wiiext00692na  a2200109   4500001000500000245003000005264002500035300002300060500045000083542002800533655002100561HATJ00aMinna no Nintendo Channel 1bNintendoc2007-11-27  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe Nintendo Channel is an interactive guide to what's new in the world of Nintendo - and it is available for easy download to your Wii from the Wii Shop Channel. Watch trailers, mini-documentaries, product demonstrations, and gameplay videos. Gain useful information about your favorite games on Wii and Nintendo DS from reading the game guide pages. You can even click to buy straight from your Wii, if you have the Internet Channel installed.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aSoftware2wiiext00682na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002100005264002400026300002300050500045000073542002800523655002100551HATP00aNintendo Channel 1bNintendoc2008-5-30  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe Nintendo Channel is an interactive guide to what's new in the world of Nintendo - and it is available for easy download to your Wii from the Wii Shop Channel. Watch trailers, mini-documentaries, product demonstrations, and gameplay videos. Gain useful information about your favorite games on Wii and Nintendo DS from reading the game guide pages. You can even click to buy straight from your Wii, if you have the Internet Channel installed.  i2008kNintendosGameTDB 7aSoftware2wiiext00465na  a2200121   4500001000500000245004300005264002400048300002300072500017000095542002800265655002900293655002100322HAVJ00aKyou to Ashita no Uranai Lucky Channel 1bNintendoc2008-12-2  a1 Wii optical disc  aCheck your daily fortune and get hints on relationships, activities and even the types of food that your horoscope recommends with the free Today & Tomorrow Channel.  i2008kNintendosGameTDB 7aSimulation games2wiiext 7aSoftware2wiiext00420na  a2200109   4500001000500000245003200005264002300037300002300060500017000083542002800253655002900281HAVK00aJeulgeoun Halu Unse Channel 1bNintendoc2009-9-9  a1 Wii optical disc  aCheck your daily fortune and get hints on relationships, activities and even the types of food that your horoscope recommends with the free Today & Tomorrow Channel.  i2009kNintendosGameTDB 7aSimulation games2wiiext00449na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002900005264002300034300002300057500016900080542002800249655002900277655002100306HAVP00aToday & Tomorrow Channel 1bNintendoc2009-9-9  a1 Wii optical disc  aCheck your daily fortune and get hints on relationships, activities and even the types of food that your horoscope recommends with the free Today & Tomorrow Channel  i2009kNintendosGameTDB 7aSimulation games2wiiext 7aSoftware2wiiext00740na  a2200157   4500001000500000245003600005264002400041300002300065500032700088542002800415655002500443655002800468655002600496655003900522655002100561HAWE00aMetroid Prime 3 Preview Channel 1bNintendoc2007-8-10  a1 Wii optical disc  aFeel like gearing up for some out-of-this-world bounty hunting?, the much-anticipated first-person adventure for Wii, is nearly here! Download this exclusive preview and be one of the first to see the game in action. It's Nintendo's way of helping you get through these last few weeks before Samus's next adventure begins!  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext 7aFirst-person shooter games2wiiext 7aSoftware2wiiext00726na  a2200157   4500001000500000245003600005264002500041300002300066500031200089542002800401655002500429655002800454655002600482655003900508655002100547HAWP00aMetroid Prime 3 Preview Channel 1bNintendoc2007-10-15  a1 Wii optical disc  aMetroid Prime 3: Corruption, the much-anticipated first-person adventure for Wii, hits shops on 26th October. Download this exclusive preview and gear up for some out-of-this-world bounty hunting. It’s Nintendo’s way of helping you get through these last few weeks before Samus’ next adventure begins!  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext 7aFirst-person shooter games2wiiext 7aSoftware2wiiext00679na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264002500023300002300048500040500071542002800476655003200504655002100536HAYA00aPhoto Channel 1bNintendoc2007-12-10  a1 Wii optical disc  aBy using the SD Card Slot on the front of your Wii, you can view the pictures and movies you have taken with your digital camera or mobile phone on your TV screen. With the easy-to-use software, you can easily select, enlarge, and reduce the size of your photos. In addition, there is a full array of other ways to enjoy your photos, such as scribbling messages on them and turning them into puzzles.  i2007kNintendosGameTDB 7aMultimedia software2wiiext 7aSoftware2wiiext00682na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002500005264002100030300002300051500040500074542002800479655003200507655002100539HAYC00aXiàngpiàn Píndào 1bNintendoc2022--  a1 Wii optical disc  aBy using the SD Card Slot on the front of your Wii, you can view the pictures and movies you have taken with your digital camera or mobile phone on your TV screen. With the easy-to-use software, you can easily select, enlarge, and reduce the size of your photos. In addition, there is a full array of other ways to enjoy your photos, such as scribbling messages on them and turning them into puzzles.  i2022kNintendosGameTDB 7aMultimedia software2wiiext 7aSoftware2wiiext00675na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001800005264002100023300002300044500040500067542002800472655003200500655002100532HAYK00aPhoto Channel 1bNintendoc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aBy using the SD Card Slot on the front of your Wii, you can view the pictures and movies you have taken with your digital camera or mobile phone on your TV screen. With the easy-to-use software, you can easily select, enlarge, and reduce the size of your photos. In addition, there is a full array of other ways to enjoy your photos, such as scribbling messages on them and