2009-11-6  a1 Wii optical disc  aEvery week on the channel, there is a new theme for your Rabbid. Color, paint, and submit your outfits to customize your Rabbids for voting. You can also visit http://rabbids.com/izw to see the best Rabbids. At the end of the customization, there is an icon to submit your Rabbid to said website.  i2009kUbisoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aSoftware2wiiext00567na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002000005264002300025300002300048500030100071542002700372655002500399655002100424RGWX00aRabbids Channel 1bUbisoftc2009-11-5  a1 Wii optical disc  aEvery week on the channel, there is a new theme for your Rabbid. Color, paint, and submit your outfits to customize your Rabbids for voting. You can also visit http://rabbids.com/izw to see the best Rabbids. At the end of the customization, there is an icon to submit your Rabbid to said website.  i2009kUbisoftsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aSoftware2wiiext00481na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002300005264002400028300002300052500020100075542002800276655002500304655003000329RMCE00aMario Kart Channel 1bNintendoc2008-4-27  a1 Wii optical disc  aUsing WiiConnect24, you can download ghosts and send your ghost to friends. Also, you can get information about tournaments run through the Mario Kart Channel, as well as information about events.  i2008kNintendosGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext 7aKart racing games2wiiext00413na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002300005264002400028300002300052500013300075542002800208655002500236655003000261RMCJ00aMario Kart Channel 1bNintendoc2008-4-10  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe CTGP Revolution Channel is the new launcher and updater for CTGP Revolution, a custom track distribution for Mario Kart Wii.  i2008kNintendosGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext 7aKart racing games2wiiext00413na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002300005264002400028300002300052500013300075542002800208655002500236655003000261RMCK00aMario Kart Channel 1bNintendoc2009-4-30  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe CTGP Revolution Channel is the new launcher and updater for CTGP Revolution, a custom track distribution for Mario Kart Wii.  i2009kNintendosGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext 7aKart racing games2wiiext00598na  a2200157   4500001000500000245002300005264002400028300002300052500020100075542002800276655002500304655002400329655003000353655003600383655002100419RMCP00aMario Kart Channel 1bNintendoc2008-4-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aUsing WiiConnect24, you can download ghosts and send your ghost to friends. Also, you can get information about tournaments run through the Mario Kart Channel, as well as information about events.  i2008kNintendosGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext 7aParty games2wiiext 7aKart racing games2wiiext 7aMotorcycle racing games2wiiext 7aSoftware2wiiext00641na  a2200109   45000010005000002450013000052640026000183000023000445000413000675420029004806550022005099XGX00aSNES9xGX 1banumizterc2009-12-29  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe Super Nintendo Entertainment System (officially abbreviated the Super NES or SNES, and colloquially shortened to Super Nintendo) is a 16-bit home video game console developed by Nintendo that was first released in 1990 in Japan and South Korea. In Japan, the system is called the Super Famicom, or SFC for short. In South Korea, it is known as the Super Comboy and was distributed by Hyundai Electronics.  i2009kanumiztersGameTDB 7aEmulators2wiiext00545na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002000005264001300025300002300038500033500061542001800396655002100414D01A00aWiimmfi Patcher 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis app will attempt to patch the inserted disc so that it can use Wiimmfi, a replacement online service following the shutdown of Nintendo WFC. Wiimmfi was created primarily by Wiimm and Leseratte, with various input and help from many people who wanted to save Nintendo WFC. This app is heavily based off BrainSlug by Chadderz.  i2014sGameTDB 7aSoftware2wiiext00175na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001300005264001300018300002300031500000500054542001800059D02A00aEngine02 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00921na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001800005264001500023300002300038500074400061542001800805D03A00aBrainSlug Wii 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aBrainSlug is a specialised Wii disc loader which is designed to allow the loaded game to be patched. BrainSlug is designed to make the process of adding functionality to Wii games much easier and more enjoyable for all. The BrainSlug channel is still very simple, it lacks any sort of user interface or even configuration file. When it starts, BrainSlug immediately begins loading the disc in the drive. It then searches sd:/bslug/modules for .mod BrainSlug module files. It also searches sd:/bslug/symbols for .xml symbol information. Using all of this information it patches the game and boots it. If any error messages or warnings occur, you will need to press the RESET button on the Wii before it can be launched or the channel exits.  i2014sGameTDB00262na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002000005264001500025300002300040500008300063542001800146D05A00aBash the Castle 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aBash the Castle is a game where you destroy castles by throwing rocks at them.  i2014sGameTDB00346na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001700005264001500022300002300037500017000060542001800230D06A00aBit Streamer 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aBit Streamer is a game made for the Wii that is a mixture of Bit Rider and SFCave. Stream through the Bit Stream while avoiding all of the viruses that bar your way.  i2014sGameTDB00243na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001600005264001500021300002300036500006800059542001800127D07A00aBlisterBall 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aBlisterBall is a remake of an Apple II game with the same name.  i2014sGameTDB00673na  a2200097   4500001000500000245003200005264001500037300002300052500048200075542001800557D08A00aBlob Wars: Metal Blob Solid 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aSince their world was invaded by an alien race, the Blobs have faced a lifetime of war. But now they have a chance to win the war once and for all. In Blob Wars: Metal Blob Solid, you take on the role of a fearless Blob agent, Bob. Bob’s mission is to infiltrate the various enemy bases around the Blobs’ homeworld and rescue as many MIAs as possible. But standing in his way are many vicious aliens, other Blobs who have been assimilated and the evil alien leader, Galdov.  i2014sGameTDB00476na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002400005264001500029300002300044500029300067542001800360D09A00aBlobby Volley 2 Wii 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aBlobby Volley 2 Wii is a really fun and addictive Volleyball game. Basically you are a little blob that plays Volleyball. You sort of look like a squishy jellybean. Each player (Blob) can be controlled either by the player or the CPU. So you can play against an AI, opponent, or a friend.  i2014sGameTDB00188na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002400005264001500029300002300044500000500067542001800072D0AA00aMPlayer Wii YouTube 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00178na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001600005264001300021300002300034500000500057542001800062D0BA00aMPlayer Wii 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00174na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001200005264001300017300002300030500000500053542001800058D0CA00aOcarina 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00189na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002700005264001300032300002300045500000500068542001800073D0DA00aMPlayer DVDLib Edition 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00191na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002700005264001500032300002300047500000500070542001800075D0EA00aMPlayer