1  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00557na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001500005264001300020300002300033500035100056542001800407655002200425DVXA00aVectrexWii 1bc2011--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe Vectrex was a Videogame system of the 1980’s that competed with Atari 2600 and Colecovision. Unlike other video game consoles, which connected to televisions and rendered raster graphics, the Vectrex had an integrated vector monitor which displayed vector graphics. The monochrome Vectrex used screen overlays to give the illusion of color.  i2011sGameTDB 7aEmulators2wiiext00177na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001500005264001300020300002300033500000500056542001800061DW1A00aIntuitwars 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00172na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001000005264001300015300002300028500000500051542001800056DW5A00aMarel 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00177na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001300005264001500018300002300033500000500056542001800061DW6A00aWiicraft 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00175na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001300005264001300018300002300031500000500054542001800059DW7A00aRavewild 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00388na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001300005264001500018300002300033500021600056542001800272DWAA00aWiiApple 1bc2009-1-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis is an Apple II emulator for the Wii based on the AppleWin/LinApple. You must have a USB keyboard to be able to use this application. You can use Gamecube controller as joystick for games requiring joystick.  i2009sGameTDB00278na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001600005264001600021300002300037500006800060542001800128655002200146DWBA00aWiirtualBoy 1bc2011-6-16  a1 Wii optical disc  aWiirtualBoy is a Wii port of the Mednafen Virtual Boy Emulator.  i2011sGameTDB 7aEmulators2wiiext00471na  a2200097   4500001000500000245003000005264001500035300002300050500028200073542001800355DWCA00aWiiFlow Channel Installer 1bc2013-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aWiiflow Channel Installer is an app that installs a channel on your Wii Menu so you can boot Wiiflow without going to the Homebrew Channel every time. If you have a Wii U, this app installs a vWii compatible channel. This tool also installs a hidden channel that loads Wiiflow.  i2013sGameTDB00270na  a2200097   4500001000500000245003000005264001500035300002300050500008100073542001800154DWDA00aWiiFlow Banner Downloader 1bc2013-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aWiiFlow Banner Downloader is a tool that downloads banners for custom games.  i2013sGameTDB00487na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001300005264001500018300002300033500023700056542002200293655002500315655002500340DWEA00aWiiEarth 1bKonamic--  a1 Wii optical disc  aWiiEarth allows you to use your Wiimote to navigate (and zoom-in on) the Earth, using Google Maps and similar services. You can switch between viewing with OpenStreetMap, Live (Maps, Satellite) and Google (Maps, Satellite, Terrain).  ikKonamisGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aSoccer games2wiiext00185na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001200005264001500017300002300032500001400055542001800069DWFA00aWiiFlow 1bc2010-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aFeatures:  i2010sGameTDB00304na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001600005264001600021300002300037500012800060542001800188DWHA00aWiiHandySDL 1bc2009-1-18  a1 Wii optical disc  aWiiHandy is a port of the Handy 0.95 Atari Lynx emulator developed by Keith Wilkins. Additional changes by the SDLEmu team.  i2009sGameTDB00172na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001000005264001300015300002300028500000500051542001800056DWJA00aJewel 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00177na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001500005264001300020300002300033500000500056542001800061DWKA00aWiibreaker 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00482na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001400005264001500019300002300034500030900057542001800366DWLA00aWii-Linux 1bc2008-8-4  a1 Wii optical disc  aWii-Linux or GC-Linux is a port of the Linux kernel and related GNU userspace utilities to the Nintendo Wii video game console. Many distributions of GNU/Linux are available for the Wii. All current distributions use a version of the "gc-linux" kernel, a port of the Linux kernel by the GC-Linux project.  i2008sGameTDB00386na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001600005264002200021300002300043500019300066542002900259DWMA00aWAD Manager 1bWaninkokoc2010--  a1 Wii optical disc  aWad Manager allows you to install or uninstall .wad files to and from your Nintendo Wii. You can install from USB or SD card. Also allows you to install .wad files to an emulated wii nand.  i2010kWaninkokosGameTDB00174na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001200005264001300017300002300030500000500053542001800058DWNA00aNwancat 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00301na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001500005264001500020300002300035500012700058542001800185DWPA00aWiiPhysics 1bc2013-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aWiiPhysics is a physics playground for the Wii, much like Crayon Physics or PocketPhysics. It uses Box2D and libwiisprite.  i2013sGameTDB00446na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001300005264000900018300002300027500024000050542001400290655003200304DWRA00aWiiRadio 1bc--  a1 Wii optical disc  aWiiRadio is a SHOUTcast stream player, which can read from thousands of internet radio streams and play them back on the Wii.  It has multiple built-in visualizers, it is able to be skinned, and is built on Tantric’s SDL Wii project.  isGameTDB 7aMultimedia software2wiiext00230na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001000005264004100015300002300056500000500079542004800084DWSA00aWiiSX 1bEmu_kidid, Sepp256 y TehPolac2010--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2010kEmu_kidid, Sepp256 y TehPolasGameTDB00283na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001200005264001300017300002300030500011400053542001800167DWTA00aWiituka 1bc2011--  a1 Wii optical disc  aWiituka is the first release of a fantastic emulator of the Amstrad CPC 8bit computer, developed by D_Skywalk  i2011sGameTDB00374na  a2200097   4500001000500000245000900005264001500014300002300029500020600052542001800258DWUA00aWufe 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aWith this tool you can insert any Wii DVD game and extract all the update files from the disc, e.g. System Menu WAD files and IOS files. The files are saved to an SD card inserted in the front SD slot.  i2014sGameTDB00674na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001600005264001500021300002300036500049900059542001800558DWWA00aWinters End 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aWinter's End is a simple winter themed game. You play as a snow person who is very slowly melting away. You can move around the map and collect snow to make yourself larger. When there is no snow left in the area you taken to the next level and when you complete the tenth level it will loop back to the first. Your movements are motion controlled (hold the wiimote sideways like an NES controller and tilt it in the direction you want to go) and you use the directional pad to turn the camera.  i2014sGameTDB00262na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001500005264000900020300002300029500006500052542001400117655002100131DWXA00aWiiXplorer 1bc--  a1 Wii optical disc  aA multi device file explorer for the Wii by dimok and r-win.  isGameTDB 7aSoftware2wiiext00199na  a2200097   4500001000500000245003500005264001500040300002300055500000500078542001800083DX3A00aMidway Space Invaders Emulator 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00283na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002200005264001500027300002300042500010200065542001800167DX4A00aBrawl DX Launcher 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis homebrew app does exactly what it says, it launches Brawl DX, a Super Smash Bros. Brawl Mod.  i2014sGameTDB00181na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001700005264001500022300002300037500000500060542001800065DX5A00aMP3+G Player 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00181na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001700005264001500022300002300037500000500060542001800065DX6A00aBuild Blocks 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00177na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001300005264001500018300002300033500000500056542001800061DX7A00aRoxoptr2 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00172na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001000005264001300015300002300028500000500051542001800056DX8A00aHexen 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00179na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001500005264001500020300002300035500000500058542001800063DX9A00aSand Traps 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00176na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001400005264001300019300002300032500000500055542001800060DXBA00aWiiX-Ball 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00177na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001300005264001500018300002300033500000500056542001800061DXCA00aCorsixTH 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00303na  a2200097   4500001000500000245000900005264001500014300002300029500013500052542001800187DXDA00aDVDX 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aDVDX used to be part of the Hackmii Installer, which allows you to play DVDs on your Wii. This only works with older Wii consoles.  i2014sGameTDB00179na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001500005264001500020300002300035500000500058542001800063DXEA00aSDExplorer 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00185na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002300005264001300028300002300041500000500064542001800069DXHA00aTexas Holdem Poker 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00177na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001500005264001300020300002300033500000500056542001800061DXIA00aPiixelator 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00416na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001000005264001500015300002300030500024700053542001800300DXLA00aWiiXL 1bc2009-2-7  a1 Wii optical disc  aWiiXL is a port of the Atari800 emulator 2.0.3 to the Wii developed by raz0red.  The Atari800 emulator is a free and portable Atari 800/XL/XE/5200 emulator, originally written by David Firth and now developed by the Atari800 Development Team.  i2009sGameTDB00178na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001600005264001300021300002300034500000500057542001800062DXNA00abootnetflix 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00259na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001600005264001500021300002300036500008400059542001800143DXPA00aXeempongwii 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aAction packed bat and ball excitement! Feel the action with the rumble feature!  i2014sGameTDB00174na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001200005264001300017300002300030500000500053542001800058DXQA00aQuadrax 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00181na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001900005264001300024300002300037500000500060542001800065DXSA00aSave Extractor 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00183na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001900005264001500024300002300039500000500062542001800067DXTA04aThe Lone Pixel 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00177na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001300005264001500018300002300033500000500056542001800061DXXA00aHexxagon 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00452na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001000005264001500015300002300030500028300053542001800336DXYA00axyzzy 1bc2013-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis tool is simple. It has one purpose. It dumps your Wii's keys at a click of a button to the root of your SD card in a file called keys.txt. The keys are a string of characters that is unique to your console, and they are useful to recover from bricks, and many other things.  i2013sGameTDB00175na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001300005264001300018300002300031500000500054542001800059DXZA00aMegaZeux 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00182na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001800005264001500023300002300038500000500061542001800066DY5A00aDarkcorp Lite 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00179na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001700005264001300022300002300035500000500058542001800063DY6A00aLiqwiid Wars 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00726na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001200005264002200017300002300039500054100062542002500603DY9A00aTetWiis 1bPemboc2009-11-18  a1 Wii optical disc  aTetWiis is a Nintendo Wii Tetris clone, shamelessly based on the Nintendo DS version of Tetris. The more lines you get, the higher the score rewarded, but the faster the game gets! More score can be gained by going for double triple or quad clearances, and you are rewarded highly if you successfully attempt the back to back quad clearance! This is the classic 'marathon' mode of Tetris - play till you drop or run out of luck! For every 10 lines you clear the level increases, along with the scores rewarded and the speed of the drop!  i2009kPembosGameTDB00177na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001500005264001300020300002300033500000500056542001800061DYAA00aSyasokoban 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00568na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001200005264001600017300002300033500039600056542001800452DYBA00aYabause 1bc2009-1-10  a1 Wii optical disc  aYabause Wii is the Wii version of Yabause, a Sega Saturn emulator, and is the first for Wii to emulate the complex processes of the Sega Saturn. The Wii port is not released officially. Some unofficial versions have been released. Note that the Wii port is in testable status, and won't be officially supported until a later date. You must not ask the Yabause Team about unofficial versions.  i2009sGameTDB00177na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001500005264001300020300002300033500000500056542001800061DYCA00aTetricycle 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00178na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001400005264001500019300002300034500000500057542001800062DYEA00aEpilepsii 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00500na  a2200097   4500001000500000245000800005264001500013300002300028500033300051542001800384DYGA00aYog 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe objective of Yog is to knock the ball in the hole with Pushers (A) and Bursts (-). If all else fails use the Magnet (B). The score is incremented at the end of the level for each Pusher and Burst left. The score is decremented when the Magnet is used. There is a Score bonus for quickly knocking the ball in into the target.  i2014sGameTDB00178na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001600005264001300021300002300034500000500057542001800062DYHA00aHypno Blast 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00173na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001100005264001300016300002300029500000500052542001800057DYIA00aChippy 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00269na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001000005264001500015300002300030500010000053542001800153DYMA00aYAWMM 1bc2013-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aYet Another Wad Manager is a mod of Wad Manager. It is based on Leathl's Wad Manager Multi Mod.  i2013sGameTDB00177na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001300005264001500018300002300033500000500056542001800061DYOA00aToy Wars 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00180na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001600005264001500021300002300036500000500059542001800064DYPA00