aZiip 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aZiip is a simple clone of Zoop.  i2014sGameTDB00174na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001200005264001300017300002300030500000500053542001800058DZPA00aPuzsion 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00172na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001000005264001300015300002300028500000500051542001800056DZQA00aQuizz 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00175na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001300005264001300018300002300031500000500054542001800059DZRA00aRezerwar 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00173na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001100005264001300016300002300029500000500052542001800057DZSA00aSzigoy 1bc2014--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00246na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001300005264001500018300002300033500004000056542001800096655002200114DZXA00aFBZX Wii 1bc2010-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aFBZX Wii is a ZX Spectrum emulator.  i2010sGameTDB 7aEmulators2wiiext00178na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001400005264001500019300002300034500000500057542001800062DZYA00aSnake Two 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00177na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001300005264001500018300002300033500000500056542001800061DZZA00aOpenJazz 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2014sGameTDB00949na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001700005264001500022300002300037500073900060542001800799655002200817FCEU00aFCE Ultra GX 1bc2008-9-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe Nintendo Entertainment System, commonly abbreviated as NES, is an 8-bit home video game console that was developed and manufactured by Nintendo. It was initially released in Japan in July of 1983 as the Family Computer, commonly known by the abbreviation Famicom, and was later released in New York City in 1985, and throughout the U.S as well as in Europe during 1986 and 1987, and Australia in 1987. The best-selling gaming console of its time, the NES helped revitalize the US video game industry following the North American video game crash of 1983. With the NES, Nintendo introduced a now-standard business model of licensing third-party developers, authorizing them to produce and distribute titles for Nintendo's platform.  i2008sGameTDB 7aEmulators2wiiext00427na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002400005264001700029300002300046500016400069542002200233655002900255655002100284HACS00aMii Channel Symbols 1bRoc2022-3-3  a1 Wii optical disc  aA modification of the Mii Channel allowing users to enter custom symbols in their Miis' names, including ones specific to Mario Kart Wii for use in that title.  i2022kRosGameTDB 7aSimulation games2wiiext 7aSoftware2wiiext00801na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002100005264002900026300002300055500055900078542003300637655002100670HAXX00aHomebrew Channel 1bTeam Twiizersc2008-5-24  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe Homebrew Channel is a channel for launching Wii homebrew applications without the need to run the Twilight Hack first. It will list apps stored and organised on an SD card in a nice little GUI, which you can very easily customise with descriptions and shiny little .png icons all by yourself if you want. You can also launch homebrew apps via TCP (with a correctly configured PC) or USB Gecko. Both of those built in options make it extremely convenient for testing out new code, as well as a general purpose homebrew launcher. You've seen the video,  i2008kTeam TwiizerssGameTDB 7aSoftware2wiiext00331na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001600005264001600021300002300037500015500060542001800215HWFL00aHackWiiFlow 1bc2010-1-29  a1 Wii optical disc  aHackWiiFlow is a customized version of WiiFlow designed to work best with the latest Cios Hermes V5 and have custom graphics and dedicated to hackwii.  i2010sGameTDB00801na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002100005264002900026300002300055500055900078542003300637655002100670JODI00aHomebrew Channel 1bTeam Twiizersc2009-9-30  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe Homebrew Channel is a channel for launching Wii homebrew applications without the need to run the Twilight Hack first. It will list apps stored and organised on an SD card in a nice little GUI, which you can very easily customise with descriptions and shiny little .png icons all by yourself if you want. You can also launch homebrew apps via TCP (with a correctly configured PC) or USB Gecko. Both of those built in options make it extremely convenient for testing out new code, as well as a general purpose homebrew launcher. You've seen the video,  i2009kTeam TwiizerssGameTDB 7aSoftware2wiiext00801na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002100005264002900026300002300055500055900078542003300637655002100670LULZ00aHomebrew Channel 1bTeam Twiizersc2012-12-7  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe Homebrew Channel is a channel for launching Wii homebrew applications without the need to run the Twilight Hack first. It will list apps stored and organised on an SD card in a nice little GUI, which you can very easily customise with descriptions and shiny little .png icons all by yourself if you want. You can also launch homebrew apps via TCP (with a correctly configured PC) or USB Gecko. Both of those built in options make it extremely convenient for testing out new code, as well as a general purpose homebrew launcher. You've seen the video,  i2012kTeam TwiizerssGameTDB 7aSoftware2wiiext00190na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002800005264001300033300002300046500000500069542001800074MAUI00aBackup Homebrew Channel 1bc2017--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2017sGameTDB00410na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001100005264001500016300002300031500024000054542001800294NK2O00aNeek2o 1bc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aSNEEK is a System Menu emulator, so this makes it possible to use your SD Card instead of the Wii's small 512 megabyte NAND. So if you have a lot of WiiWare games that you can not fit all into so little storage space, SNEEK is for you.  i2014sGameTDB00510na  a2200133   4500001000500000245003100005264003200036300002300068500016700091542003600258655002500294655002700319655003000346NZXM00aSuper Mario 64 Multiplayer 1bSkelux, Nintendoc2013-8-26  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe Mario Bros. have teamed up for the classic adventure of Super Mario 64! Grab a friend and set out to save Peach in the multiplayer modification of this title.  i2013kSkelux, NintendosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext 7a3D platform games2wiiext00802na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002100005264003000026300002300056500055900079542003300638655002100671OHBC00aHomebrew Channel 1bTeam Twiizersc2016-11-22  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe Homebrew Channel is a channel for launching Wii homebrew applications without the need to run the Twilight Hack first. It will list apps stored and organised on an SD card in a nice little GUI, which you can very easily customise with descriptions and shiny little .png icons all by yourself if you want. You can also launch homebrew apps via TCP (with a correctly configured PC) or USB Gecko. Both of those built in options make it extremely convenient for testing out new code, as well as a general purpose homebrew launcher. You've seen the video,  i2016kTeam TwiizerssGameTDB 7aSoftware2wiiext00331na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001100005264001300016300002300029500016300052542001800215PLUS00aWiiMC+ 1bc2013--  a1 Wii optical disc  aA very useful enhancement to WiiMC. It adds many features to the application, including savable playlists, extra online features, and other various additions.  i2013sGameTDB00569na  a2200121   4500001000500000245003700005264002500042300002300067500027200090542003000362655002500392655003000417PXWE00aProject X:  Love Potion Disaster 1bKeryo Teamc2013-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aA freak accident in Delta Labs causes a pink cloud to cover all of Mobius, turning everyone into sex crazed maniacs. It's up to an elite group of mobians to fight their way through hordes of sex crazed monsters to reach the labs and stop this threat once and for all.  i2013kKeryo TeamsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7a2D platform games2wiiext00178na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001600005264001300021300002300034500000500057542001800062RIIV00aRiivolution 1bc2013--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2013sGameTDB00584na  a2200157   4500001000500000245002800005264004800033300002300081500013300104542005300237655002500290655002400315655003000339655003600369655002100405RMCX00aCTGP Revolution Channel 1bNintendo, MrBean35000vr, Chadderzc2014-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe CTGP Revolution Channel is the new launcher and updater for CTGP Revolution, a custom track distribution for Mario Kart Wii.  i2014kNintendo, MrBean35000vr, ChadderzsGameTDB 7aRacing games2wiiext 7aParty games2wiiext 7aKart racing games2wiiext 7aMotorcycle racing games2wiiext 7aSoftware2wiiext00838na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002000005264003100025300002300056500058900079542003800668655002200706SEGA00aGenesis Plus GX 1bJoWood Productionsc2012--  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe Sega Genesis, known as the Mega Drive in regions outside of North America, is a 16-bit home video game console developed and sold by Sega. The Genesis was Sega's third console and the successor to the Master System. The hardware was adapted from Sega's System 16 arcade board, centered on a Motorola 68000 processor as the CPU, a Zilog Z80 as a sound controller, and a video system supporting hardware sprites, tiles, and scrolling. The system plays a library of more than 900 games created by Sega and a wide array of third-party publishers and delivered on ROM-based cartridges.  i2012kJoWood ProductionssGameTDB 7aEmulators2wiiext00701na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002400005264002300029300002300052500046700075542002800542655002100570SMGX00aSaveGame Manager GX 1bDJ Skualc2010-1-2  a1 Wii optical disc  aSaveGame Manager GX is a Nintendo Wii© homebrew applications. It will list Saves and Miis stored in Wii memory as well than Saves, Miis & others files on an SD card or USB mass storage device in a nice little GUI, which you can very easily customise with integrated themes & languages features (powered by spiffy360.com). You can also launch applications via TCP (with a correctly configured PC) or through a dedicated browser; As download saves on wiisave.com.  i2010kDJ SkualsGameTDB 7aSoftware2wiiext00210na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001400005264001300019300002300032500000500055542001800060655002200078SNTX00aSnes9x TX 1bc2022--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2022sGameTDB 7aEmulators2wiiext00411na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002100005264002000026300002300046500014400069542002400213655002500237655002700262SOMA00aSonic Mania Plus 1bSegac2017-8-15  a1 Wii optical disc  aSonic Mania is an all-new adventure with Sonic, Tails, and Knuckles full of unique bosses, rolling 2D landscapes, and fun classic gameplay.  i2017kSegasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aPlatform games2wiiext00191na  a2200097   4500001000500000245002600005264001600031300002300047500000500070542001800075STUX00aSuper Tux Wii Edition 1bc2019-12-1  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2019sGameTDB00190na  a2200097   4500001000500000245001200005264002100017300002300038500000500061542002600066ULFW00auLoader 1bHermesc2009-4-9  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2009kHermessGameTDB00423na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001800005264003300023300002300056500017500079542003800254655002100292UNEO00aUSB Loader GX 1bUSB Loader GX Teamc2011-1-9  a1 Wii optical disc  aUSB Loader GX allows you to install your games to a USB storage device or SD card. You can then boot your games faster, download and use cheats, or apply various patches.  i2011kUSB Loader GX TeamsGameTDB 7aSoftware2wiiext00349na  a2200109   4500001000500000245002600005264001600031300002300047500012900070542001800199655002200217VBGX00aVisual Boy Advance GX 1bc2008-9-16  a1 Wii optical disc  aVisual Boy Advance GX is a Game Boy Advance / Game Boy emulator for the Wii based on VBA-M. The GUI is powered by libwiigui.  i2008sGameTDB 7aEmulators2wiiext00356na  a2200121   4500001000500000245001000005264001800015300002300033500010000056542002500156655003200181655002100213WIMC00aWiiMC 1bWiiMCc2010--  a1 Wii optical disc  aWiiMC (Wii Media Centre) is an open source media player for the Nintendo Wii. Features include:  i2010kWiiMCsGameTDB 7aMultimedia software2wiiext 7aSoftware2wiiext00336na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001700005264002900022300002300051500009300074542003400167655002500201WMH100aMother 1+2+3 1bBig John Gamesc2016-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aLead a lively little mouse on his hunt to collect the cheese in 100 challenging puzzles!  i2016kBig John GamessGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext00832na  a2200109   4500001000500000245001000005264002500015300002300040500060700063542003000670655002200700WN6400aWii64 1bTeam Wii64c2016-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe Nintendo 64, abbreviated to N64, is Nintendo's third home video game console for the international market. Named for its 64-bit central processing unit, it was released in June 1996 in Japan, September 1996 in North America and Brazil, March 1997 in Europe and Australia, September 1997 in France. It was the last major home console to use the cartridge as its primary storage format until Nintendo's seventh console, the Nintendo Switch, released in 2017. Though succeeded by Nintendo's MiniDVD-based GameCube in September 2001, the Nintendo 64 was sold until the system was retired in early 2002.  i2016kTeam Wii64sGameTDB 7aEmulators2wiiext00569na  a2200133   4500001000500000245001000005264004100015300002300056500022900079542004800308655002500356655002700381655002700408WPSX00aWiiSX 1bEmu_kidid, Sepp256 y TehPolac2010--  a1 Wii optical disc  aIntroducing a new kind of Pokémon challenge – exclusive to WiiWare! Pokémon Rumble is an action game in which you control Toy Pokémon and battle against waves of enemy Pokémon in order to be the last Pokémon standing!  i2010kEmu_kidid, Sepp256 y TehPolasGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aStrategy games2wiiext00475na  a2200121   4500001000500000245002600005264003500031300002300066500018300089542003800272655002500310655001800335XHMP00aArt of Balance (Demo) 1bShin'en Multimediac2010-12-17  a1 Wii optical disc  aThis is a demo version. It is possible that it does not support every feature of the full version. Please note that you cannot save the progress of your game in the demo version.  i2010kShin'en MultimediasGameTDB 7aPuzzle games2wiiext 7aDemos2wiiext00478na  a2200133   4500001000500000245003200005264003000037300002300067500014900090542003700239655002400276655002600300655001800326XJSP00aKaraoke Joysound Wii (Demo) 1bBrother Internationalc--  a1 Wii optical disc  aKARAOKE JOYSOUND DEMO is a demo version of KARAOKE JOYSOUND for the WiiWare.This demo version includes three (3) songs for you to enjoy KARAOKE.  ikBrother InternationalsGameTDB 7aMusic games2wiiext 7aKaraoke games2wiiext 7aDemos2wiiext00210na  a2200097   4500001000700000245002600007264002300033300002300056500000500079542002800084301E0100aGameCube Service Disc 1bNintendoc2013-1-1  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2013kNintendosGameTDB00234na  a2200097   4500001000700000245006000007264001700067300002300084500000500107542002400112D23J0100aGame Taikai Yuushou Kinen: Tokusei SmaBro DX Movie Disc 1bNintendoc--  a1 Wii optical disc  a  ikNintendosGameTDB00203na  a2200097   4500001000700000245002900007264001700036300002300053500000500076542002400081D24J0100aSmaBro DX Event-yo