kVivendi GamessGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext01095na  a2200109   4500001000700000245001500007264002900022300002300051500085300074542003300927655002500960GBDS7D00aBloodRayne 1bVivendi Gamesc2003-5-23  a1 Wii optical disc  aAs the vampiric agent BloodRayne, you'll travel through the eerie swamps of Louisiana, to Argentina and Germany in this battle-heavy, third-person thriller. The game features non-linear gameplay in more than 40 levels and three massive worlds, the ability to suck blood for health, and to use slow-motion, zoom and aura visions to aid in death dealing. Pull off fantastic acrobatic moves to bend the environment to your will and dispatch enemies with BloodRayne's blades and kicks for awesome in-your-face combat. BloodRayne can use and carry any weapon her enemy uses including guns, explosives and rocket launchers -- all in all there are more than 40 weapons in game. Fill the Bloodlust meter to activate Blood Rage for damaging over-the-top attacks to defeat Nazis, mutants, swamp creatures, ancient parasitic monsters and blood-sucking beasts.  i2003kVivendi GamessGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00546na  a2200121   4500001000700000245002200007264003300029300002300062500024900085542003800334655002500372655002700397GBFE7000aBackyard Football 1bAtari (Infogrames)c2002-9-8  a1 Wii optical disc  aAll 32 National Football League teams; 10 PRO players as kids or 30 Backyard Kids; Play Single Games or a whole season; Create and save custom players; Track player and team stats in Season play; Cool 3D environments and multiple camera angles;  i2002kAtari (Infogrames)sGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aFootball games2wiiext00617na  a2200121   4500001000700000245002500007264003200032300002300064500031800087542003700405655002500442655002800467GBGE5G00aBomberman Generation 1bMajesco Sales Incc2002-6-5  a1 Wii optical disc  aBomberman Generation, the next game in the series, will feature fully cel-shaded graphics similiar to Bomberman Online. Players will explore a huge 3D land, solving puzzles and fighting enormous boss foes. Using power-ups and bombs Bomberman will have to battle through 5 different worlds, holding 16 levels each.  i2002kMajesco Sales IncsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext00569na  a2200109   4500001000700000245002500007264002700032300002300059500031800082542003100400655002800431GBGJ1800aBomberman Generation 1bHudson Softc2002-6-27  a1 Wii optical disc  aBomberman Generation, the next game in the series, will feature fully cel-shaded graphics similiar to Bomberman Online. Players will explore a huge 3D land, solving puzzles and fighting enormous boss foes. Using power-ups and bombs Bomberman will have to battle through 5 different worlds, holding 16 levels each.  i2002kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aAdventure games2wiiext00594na  a2200109   4500001000700000245002500007264003900032300002300071500031900094542004300413655002800456GBGP7D00aBomberman Generation 1bVivendi Universal Gamesc2002-12-6  a1 Wii optical disc  aBomberman Generation , the next game in the series, will feature fully cel-shaded graphics similiar to Bomberman Online. Players will explore a huge 3D land, solving puzzles and fighting enormous boss foes. Using power-ups and bombs Bomberman will have to battle through 5 different worlds, holding 16 levels each.  i2002kVivendi Universal GamessGameTDB 7aAdventure games2wiiext00790na  a2200133   4500001000700000245001800007264002100025300002300046500048100069542002400550655002500574655002700599655003000626GBHDC800aMystic Heroes 1bKoeic2002-12-13  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn Mystic Heroes, it's up to you to find hidden Runes that will help you defeat an enemy army. As one of four main characters, you'll battle through Mt. Hoshin, Mt. Senkai, and The City of the Ancients. In each stage, you must equip your Runes strategically in order to defeat powerful enemies and bosses. The more Runes you gather, the more spells you unlock and levels you advance. There are 70 total Runes hidden throughout the single-player missions and multiplayer modes.  i2002kKoeisGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext00708na  a2200109   4500001000700000245001800007264002000025300002300045500048100068542002400549655002500573GBHEC800aMystic Heroes 1bKoeic2002-9-30  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn Mystic Heroes, it's up to you to find hidden Runes that will help you defeat an enemy army. As one of four main characters, you'll battle through Mt. Hoshin, Mt. Senkai, and The City of the Ancients. In each stage, you must equip your Runes strategically in order to defeat powerful enemies and bosses. The more Runes you gather, the more spells you unlock and levels you advance. There are 70 total Runes hidden throughout the single-player missions and multiplayer modes.  i2002kKoeisGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00790na  a2200133   4500001000700000245001800007264002100025300002300046500048100069542002400550655002500574655002700599655003000626GBHFC800aMystic Heroes 1bKoeic2002-12-13  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn Mystic Heroes, it's up to you to find hidden Runes that will help you defeat an enemy army. As one of four main characters, you'll battle through Mt. Hoshin, Mt. Senkai, and The City of the Ancients. In each stage, you must equip your Runes strategically in order to defeat powerful enemies and bosses. The more Runes you gather, the more spells you unlock and levels you advance. There are 70 total Runes hidden throughout the single-player missions and multiplayer modes.  i2002kKoeisGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext00709na  a2200109   4500001000700000245001900007264002000026300002300046500048100069542002400550655002500574GBHJC800aBattle Houshin 1bKoeic2002-3-29  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn Mystic Heroes, it's up to you to find hidden Runes that will help you defeat an enemy army. As one of four main characters, you'll battle through Mt. Hoshin, Mt. Senkai, and The City of the Ancients. In each stage, you must equip your Runes strategically in order to defeat powerful enemies and bosses. The more Runes you gather, the more spells you unlock and levels you advance. There are 70 total Runes hidden throughout the single-player missions and multiplayer modes.  i2002kKoeisGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00790na  a2200133   4500001000700000245001800007264002100025300002300046500048100069542002400550655002500574655002700599655003000626GBHPC800aMystic Heroes 1bKoeic2002-12-13  a1 Wii optical disc  aIn Mystic Heroes, it's up to you to find hidden Runes that will help you defeat an enemy army. As one of four main characters, you'll battle through Mt. Hoshin, Mt. Senkai, and The City of the Ancients. In each stage, you must equip your Runes strategically in order to defeat powerful enemies and bosses. The more Runes you gather, the more spells you unlock and levels you advance. There are 70 total Runes hidden throughout the single-player missions and multiplayer modes.  i2002kKoeisGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7aBeat 'em up games2wiiext00789na  a2200133   4500001000700000245001800007264002200025300002300047500047200070542002600542655002500568655002800593655003400621GBIE0800aResident Evil 1bCapcomc2002-4-30  a1 Wii optical disc  aRaccoon City has been completely overrun by mutant beasts and bloodthirsty zombies. You are a member of S.T.A.R.S.--a rescue squad sent into the community to investigate the ominous mansion at the core of the disaster. Take the role of operative Jill Valentine or Chris Redfield and uncover the secrets behind a radical, genetic research facility. With an array of weapons to master and horrors around every corner, the ultimate test may be just to make it out alive.  i2002kCapcomsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext 7aSurvival horror games2wiiext00785na  a2200133   4500001000700000245001400007264002200021300002300043500047200066542002600538655002500564655002800589655003400617GBIJ0800aBiohazard 1bCapcomc2002-3-22  a1 Wii optical disc  aRaccoon City has been completely overrun by mutant beasts and bloodthirsty zombies. You are a member of S.T.A.R.S.--a rescue squad sent into the community to investigate the ominous mansion at the core of the disaster. Take the role of operative Jill Valentine or Chris Redfield and uncover the secrets behind a radical, genetic research facility. With an array of weapons to master and horrors around every corner, the ultimate test may be just to make it out alive.  i2002kCapcomsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext 7aSurvival horror games2wiiext00743na  a2200121   4500001000700000245001800007264002200025300002300047500047200070542002600542655002500568655002800593GBIP0800aResident Evil 1bCapcomc2002-9-13  a1 Wii optical disc  aRaccoon City has been completely overrun by mutant beasts and bloodthirsty zombies. You are a member of S.T.A.R.S.--a rescue squad sent into the community to investigate the ominous mansion at the core of the disaster. Take the role of operative Jill Valentine or Chris Redfield and uncover the secrets behind a radical, genetic research facility. With an array of weapons to master and horrors around every corner, the ultimate test may be just to make it out alive.  i2002kCapcomsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aAdventure games2wiiext01054na  a2200121   4500001000700000245002200007264003300029300002300062500075700085542003800842655002500880655002700905GBKE7000aBackyard Baseball 1bAtari (Infogrames)c2003-4-9  a1 Wii optical disc  aMajor League Baseball pros join the Backyard Kids. Now, for the first time on the Sony PlayStation 2 computer entertainment system, young baseball fans can pick Alex Rodriguez, Alfonso Soriano and 14 other stars, all playing as kids. Choose lineups, team logos, and awesome fields and control every pitch. With outrageous power-ups and surprises, kids can smash homeruns, throw clutch strikeouts and have a one-of-a-kind Backyard Sports experience. Features include all 30 MLB team logos, customizable players, quick, single games and Season Play mode, Home Run Derby mini-game, full stats and standings in Season Play, multiple camera views and instant replay, unlockable fields and special players, tutorial mode, baseball darts and other mini-games.  i2003kAtari (Infogrames)sGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aBaseball games2wiiext00834na  a2200109   4500001000700000245002900007264002600036300002300062500058200085542003000667655002700697GBLE5200aBloody Roar: Primal Fury 1bActivisionc2002-3-19  a1 Wii optical disc  aPrimal Fury, called Bloody Roar Extreme in Japan, is a traditional 3D polygonal fighter that boasts a brawling style similar to that of Fighting Vipers. The twist is that each of the game's 16 characters can transform from human to beast shape and take on new fighting abilities. Bloody Roar: Primal Fury comes as an updated port to the PlayStation 2 released Bloody Roar 3, and is differentiated by enhanced, more detailed graphics, more rounded character models and a better framerate, among other additions. Developed by Eighting, the game is rated "T" for Teen by the ESRB.  i2002kActivisionsGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00833na  a2200109   4500001000700000245002900007264002500036300002300061500058200084542003000666655002700696GBLP5200aBloody Roar: Primal Fury 1bActivisionc2002-5-3  a1 Wii optical disc  aPrimal Fury, called Bloody Roar Extreme in Japan, is a traditional 3D polygonal fighter that boasts a brawling style similar to that of Fighting Vipers. The twist is that each of the game's 16 characters can transform from human to beast shape and take on new fighting abilities. Bloody Roar: Primal Fury comes as an updated port to the PlayStation 2 released Bloody Roar 3, and is differentiated by enhanced, more detailed graphics, more rounded character models and a better framerate, among other additions. Developed by Eighting, the game is rated "T" for Teen by the ESRB.  i2002kActivisionsGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00922na  a2200109   4500001000700000245002600007264002100033300002300054500068500077542002500762655002500787GBME7F00aBatman: Dark Tomorrow 1bKemcoc2003-3-25  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe storyline begins with the disappearance of Gotham City Police Commissioner James Gordon and the lockdown of Arkum Asylum. As Batman, players will have to infiltrate Arkum Asylum to find Gordon and uncover clues that reveal a bigger plot involving a criminal mastermind. Batman: Dark Tomorrow is a third-person action adventure game in which players will have to use a number Batman's skills in order to progress through the game. To aid him, Batman will also have access to plenty of traditional Bat-gadgets. The game will take place in a variety of locations in Gotham City, including Arkum Asylum, the docks, the sewer system, an abandoned steel factory, and Gazette Square.  i2003kKemcosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00922na  a2200109   4500001000700000245002600007264002100033300002300054500068500077542002500762655002500787GBMJ2800aBatman: Dark Tomorrow 1bKemcoc2003-3-21  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe storyline begins with the disappearance of Gotham City Police Commissioner James Gordon and the lockdown of Arkum Asylum. As Batman, players will have to infiltrate Arkum Asylum to find Gordon and uncover clues that reveal a bigger plot involving a criminal mastermind. Batman: Dark Tomorrow is a third-person action adventure game in which players will have to use a number Batman's skills in order to progress through the game. To aid him, Batman will also have access to plenty of traditional Bat-gadgets. The game will take place in a variety of locations in Gotham City, including Arkum Asylum, the docks, the sewer system, an abandoned steel factory, and Gazette Square.  i2003kKemcosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00922na  a2200109   4500001000700000245002600007264002100033300002300054500068500077542002500762655002500787GBMP7F00aBatman: Dark Tomorrow 1bKemcoc2003-4-11  a1 Wii optical disc  aThe storyline begins with the disappearance of Gotham City Police Commissioner James Gordon and the lockdown of Arkum Asylum. As Batman, players will have to infiltrate Arkum Asylum to find Gordon and uncover clues that reveal a bigger plot involving a criminal mastermind. Batman: Dark Tomorrow is a third-person action adventure game in which players will have to use a number Batman's skills in order to progress through the game. To aid him, Batman will also have access to plenty of traditional Bat-gadgets. The game will take place in a variety of locations in Gotham City, including Arkum Asylum, the docks, the sewer system, an abandoned steel factory, and Gazette Square.  i2003kKemcosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00337na  a2200133   4500001000700000245004000007264002100047300002300068500000500091542002500096655002500121655002700146655003000173GBNJC000aWarrior Blade: Rastan vs. Barbarian 1bTaitoc2003-3-27  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2003kTaitosGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aFighting games2wiiext 7a3D fighting games2wiiext00892na  a2200121   4500001000700000245001200007264002300019300002300042500062800065542002700693655002500720655002500745GBOE5100aBurnout 1bAcclaimc2002-4-30  a1 Wii optical disc  aBurnout is a street-racing game where you are put in the drivers seat racing across 14 circuits. Every dance with death earns you more 'Burn' power that you can use to tear up the road at turbo speeds. Smashing into traffic costs you time. You'll get bonus points for your near-misses, trying to actually win a race while the city bustles around you. Your opponents can be a pack of ruthless computer drivers, or you can turn up the aggression and battle against a friend in multiplayer races, ramming them into walls, steering them into oncoming traffic or causing pile-ups that they have to swerve around or dive through!  i2002kAcclaimsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aRacing games2wiiext00891na  a2200121   4500001000700000245001200007264002200019300002300041500062800064542002700692655002500719655002500744GBOP5100aBurnout 1bAcclaimc2002-5-3  a1 Wii optical disc  aBurnout is a street-racing game where you are put in the drivers seat racing across 14 circuits. Every dance with death earns you more 'Burn' power that you can use to tear up the road at turbo speeds. Smashing into traffic costs you time. You'll get bonus points for your near-misses, trying to actually win a race while the city bustles around you. Your opponents can be a pack of ruthless computer drivers, or you can turn up the aggression and battle against a friend in multiplayer races, ramming them into walls, steering them into oncoming traffic or causing pile-ups that they have to swerve around or dive through!  i2002kAcclaimsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aRacing games2wiiext00310na  a2200097   4500001000700000245007100007264005100078300002300129500000500152542005500157GBPJCM04aThe Baseball 2003: Battle Ball Park Sengen Perfect Play Pro Yakyuu 1bKonami Computer Entertainment Osakac2003-3-20  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2003kKonami Computer Entertainment OsakasGameTDB00836na  a2200109   4500001000700000245003200007264001900039300002300058500059700081542002300678655002500701GBQE7800aRocket Power: Beach Bandits 1bTHQc2002-9-24  a1 Wii optical disc  aSummer is just around the corner, and the kids from Ocean Shores look forward to the Annual Ocean Shores Surf Contest. But as Otto, Reggie, Twister, and Sam finally reach the beach, they make a startling discovery--most of the sand is missing, and the surf contest has been postponed. Now it's up to you to guide the kids through Ocean Shores, The Lakes, The Robot Factory, and Mondo Mountain in the effort to discover who stole the sand. In each area, you'll battle robot minions, use the new wave runner and zip-line glide, and play extreme sports, such as skateboarding and inline skating.  i2002kTHQsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00839na  a2200109   4500001000700000245003200007264001900039300002300058500059700081542002300678655002800701GBQP7800aRocket Power: Beach Bandits 1bTHQc2002-9-24  a1 Wii optical disc  aSummer is just around the corner, and the kids from Ocean Shores look forward to the Annual Ocean Shores Surf Contest. But as Otto, Reggie, Twister, and Sam finally reach the beach, they make a startling discovery--most of the sand is missing, and the surf contest has been postponed. Now it's up to you to guide the kids through Ocean Shores, The Lakes, The Robot Factory, and Mondo Mountain in the effort to discover who stole the sand. In each area, you'll battle robot minions, use the new wave runner and zip-line glide, and play extreme sports, such as skateboarding and inline skating.  i2002kTHQsGameTDB 7aAdventure games2wiiext00585na  a2200109   4500001000700000245002500007264002700032300002300059500033500082542003100417655002700448GBRJ1800aBloody Roar: Extreme 1bHudson Softc2002-4-25  a1 Wii optical disc  aBloody Roar: Extreme known as Bloody Roar: Primal Fury in North America and PAL territories is fighting game developed by Eighting/Raizing that boasts a brawling style similar to that of Fighting Vipers. The twist is that each of the game's 16 characters can transform from human to beast shape and take on new fighting abilities.  i2002kHudson SoftsGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00893na  a2200121   4500001000700000245004300007264002600050300002300076500058800099542003000687655002500717655002900742GBSE8P00aBeach Spikers: Virtua Beach Volleyball 1bSega Japanc2002-9-13  a1 Wii optical disc  aBeach Spikers is a simple, decidedly unsophisticated volleyball game, but it also happens to be a lot of fun. The title has enough gameplay modes and options to keep all of us busy for a long time and the AI character building elements even longer. I've spent some 10 hours just building various characters up to their full potentials and had a great time doing it. But there's more to the game than just these areas; there are entire other modes to explore, from the Point Kick matches to the highly entertaining Beach Countdown, in which the volleyball becomes a ticking time bomb.  i2002kSega JapansGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aVolleyball games2wiiext00881na  a2200121   4500001000700000245004300007264002000050300002300070500058800093542002400681655002500705655002900730GBSJ8P00aBeach Spikers: Virtua Beach Volleyball 1bSegac2002-7-19  a1 Wii optical disc  aBeach Spikers is a simple, decidedly unsophisticated volleyball game, but it also happens to be a lot of fun. The title has enough gameplay modes and options to keep all of us busy for a long time and the AI character building elements even longer. I've spent some 10 hours just building various characters up to their full potentials and had a great time doing it. But there's more to the game than just these areas; there are entire other modes to explore, from the Point Kick matches to the highly entertaining Beach Countdown, in which the volleyball becomes a ticking time bomb.  i2002kSegasGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aVolleyball games2wiiext00893na  a2200121   4500001000700000245004300007264002600050300002300076500058800099542003000687655002500717655002900742GBSP8P00aBeach Spikers: Virtua Beach Volleyball 1bSega Japanc2002-9-27  a1 Wii optical disc  aBeach Spikers is a simple, decidedly unsophisticated volleyball game, but it also happens to be a lot of fun. The title has enough gameplay modes and options to keep all of us busy for a long time and the AI character building elements even longer. I've spent some 10 hours just building various characters up to their full potentials and had a great time doing it. But there's more to the game than just these areas; there are entire other modes to explore, from the Point Kick matches to the highly entertaining Beach Countdown, in which the volleyball becomes a ticking time bomb.  i2002kSega JapansGameTDB 7aSports games2wiiext 7aVolleyball games2wiiext00704na  a2200109   4500001000700000245004500007264003400052300002300086500042000109542003800529655002700567GBTE7000aBeyblade VForce: Super Tournament Battle 1bAtari (Infogrames)c2003-9-24  a1 Wii optical disc  aBeyblade is a baffling game that is both so niche and so ill- executed that I can only recommended to the true fanatics out there who devour anything the franchise has to offer. Everyone else will be downright insulted by the simple, stupid game mechanics and horrendously outdated visual and audio presentations. This title does not look, sound or act any differently from its PS1 predecessor, which is a travesty.  i2003kAtari (Infogrames)sGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00280na  a2200109   4500001000700000245005900007264002300066300002300089500000500112542002600117655002700143GBTJA700aBakuten Shoot Beyblade 2002: Nettou! Magne Tag Battle! 1bTakarac2002-12-19  a1 Wii optical disc  a  i2002kTakarasGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00705na  a2200109   4500001000700000245004500007264003500052300002300087500042000110542003800530655002700568GBTP7000aBeyblade VForce: Super Tournament Battle 1bAtari (Infogrames)c2003-11-28  a1 Wii optical disc  aBeyblade is a baffling game that is both so niche and so ill- executed that I can only recommended to the true fanatics out there who devour anything the franchise has to offer. Everyone else will be downright insulted by the simple, stupid game mechanics and horrendously outdated visual and audio presentations. This title does not look, sound or act any differently from its PS1 predecessor, which is a travesty.  i2003kAtari (Infogrames)sGameTDB 7aFighting games2wiiext00964na  a2200109   4500001000700000245002200007264003900029300002300068500069600091542004200787655002500829GBVE4100aBatman: Vengeance 1bUbi Soft Entertainmentc2001-11-18  a1 Wii optical disc  aBatman Vengeance, developed by Ubi Soft Montreal, is a 3D action-adventure based on the animated television series. The game pits players as the Dark Knight himself on a quest to stop a mysterious crime wave in Gotham City. Batman has full freedom of movement to go anywhere within wide-open, sprawling 3D environments -- some that stretch up and up and up. The caped crusader can walk, run, sneak against walls, climb, glide through the air with his cape and engage in hand-to-hand combat. The game features 19 stages, 40 minutes of rendered cinematics, and plenty of Bat gadgets, like batarangs, batgrapples, flash bombs, remote charges, batcuffs, nets, the batlauncher, batscope and more.  i2001kUbi Soft EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext00962na  a2200109   4500001000700000245002200007264003700029300002300066500069600089542004200785655002500827GBVP4100aBatman: Vengeance 1bUbi Soft Entertainmentc2002-5-3  a1 Wii optical disc  aBatman Vengeance, developed by Ubi Soft Montreal, is a 3D action-adventure based on the animated television series. The game pits players as the Dark Knight himself on a quest to stop a mysterious crime wave in Gotham City. Batman has full freedom of movement to go anywhere within wide-open, sprawling 3D environments -- some that stretch up and up and up. The caped crusader can walk, run, sneak against walls, climb, glide through the air with his cape and engage in hand-to-hand combat. The game features 19 stages, 40 minutes of rendered cinematics, and plenty of Bat gadgets, like batarangs, batgrapples, flash bombs, remote charges, batcuffs, nets, the batlauncher, batscope and more.  i2002kUbi Soft EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext01000na  a2200133   4500001000700000245002900007264003800036300002300074500063600097542004300733655002500776655002600801655003900827GBWD6400aStar Wars: Bounty Hunter 1bLucasArts Entertainmentc2003-2-7  a1 Wii optical disc  aPublisher LucasArts takes players to period a long time ago in a galaxy far, far away. This time around, though, players don't assume the role of a powerful Jedi or an ambitious Rebel pilot, but rather a rough bounty hunter employed by the very enemies of Obi-Wan Kenobi and Yoda. Jango Fett, who won't think twice about killing anybody in his way -- good or bad, is brought to the digital arena third-person shooter-style. Armed with all the weapons and gadgets he can carry and a jetpack to boot, the character flies and shoots his way through a variety of gargantuan worlds and encounters recognizable creatures from the movies.  i2003kLucasArts EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext 7aThird-person shooter games2wiiext01001na  a2200133   4500001000700000245002900007264003900036300002300075500063600098542004300734655002500777655002600802655003900828GBWE6400aStar Wars: Bounty Hunter 1bLucasArts Entertainmentc2002-12-4  a1 Wii optical disc  aPublisher LucasArts takes players to period a long time ago in a galaxy far, far away. This time around, though, players don't assume the role of a powerful Jedi or an ambitious Rebel pilot, but rather a rough bounty hunter employed by the very enemies of Obi-Wan Kenobi and Yoda. Jango Fett, who won't think twice about killing anybody in his way -- good or bad, is brought to the digital arena third-person shooter-style. Armed with all the weapons and gadgets he can carry and a jetpack to boot, the character flies and shoots his way through a variety of gargantuan worlds and encounters recognizable creatures from the movies.  i2002kLucasArts EntertainmentsGameTDB 7aAction games2wiiext 7aShooter games2wiiext 7aT